{"raw": {"https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenured-Tenure-line-Positions-in-Interdisciplinary-Research--and--Quantum--ICDS-Co-hire-_REQ_0000083511-1": {"title": "Tenured/Tenure line Positions in Interdisciplinary Research \"and\" Quantum (ICDS Co-hire)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS) at The Pennsylvania State University is hiring multiple Tenure-track or Tenured faculty in Quantum Computing as part of an ambitious multi-year cluster hire in Quantum Science across multiple university units. The search is administered by the Quantum Hub within the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences. \u00a0 The focus of this year\u2019s search is on faculty with expertise in Quantum Computing with particular focus on Quantum Algorithms, Quantum Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning, and/or Quantum Security. \u00a0 The successful candidates will join a vibrant, interdisciplinary research community at Penn State and will have collaborative opportunities and access to extensive resources offered by Institutes within the Office of the Senior Vice President for Research (OSVPR). Faculty members in these positions will be expected to develop world-recognized research programs, create innovative graduate and undergraduate curricula in quantum computing, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, mentor graduate students, secure external funding to support research activities, and engage in collaborative, interdisciplinary research and scholarship at the University. As a joint appointment, successful candidates will be expected to contribute to both their tenure home units and to the institutes. Applicants should submit a single PDF through the application portal containing the following materials in this order: cover letter, teaching statement, research statement, the names and contact information for four references, and their curriculum vitae. The cover letter should explicitly specify the one position to which the applicant is applying (see below for information about calls for each department). Each applicant must apply to one position only. \u00a0 Applications received by January 3rd, 2027 , will be given full consideration. \u00a0 For Questions, contact ICDS director Guido Cervone (icds@psu.edu).\u00a0 \u00a0 Penn State Academic Ranks Defined: \u00a0 Assistant professors should show early promise in teaching or research through emerging scholarly or professional contributions.\u00a0 Associate professors should have a record of high-quality publications and demonstrate teaching excellence in their field.\u00a0 Full professors should demonstrate a distinguished record of advanced work and leadership, reflecting established excellence in teaching, mentoring, and/or research. \u00a0 Open positions include: \u00a0 Department of Computer Science and Engineering, College of Engineering, University Park, PA : An Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance quantum computing and quantum information science, with particular interest in quantum algorithms, quantum machine learning (QML), quantum software and systems, quantum architectures, and related areas. The department seeks to strengthen its research potential in quantum computing by building upon its strong existing research groups in quantum algorithms, theoretical computer science, computer architecture, and systems, which provide a rich foundation for interdisciplinary research. Candidates must possess a PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a closely related discipline, before their appointment start date. \u00a0 Department of Privacy and Cybersecurity Informatics (PCI), College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST), University Park, PA in conjunction with the National Security Institute (NSI) at Penn State: An Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance quantum security, post-quantum cybersecurity, and secure and trustworthy systems for the quantum era. The department seeks to build national leadership and research capacity at the intersection of quantum computing and cybersecurity, including security of quantum algorithms, post-quantum cryptography, quantum-safe critical infrastructure, and trustworthy, resilient, and policy-aware security for emerging quantum technologies. Candidates must possess a PhD in Computer Science, Informatics, Cybersecurity, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or a closely related discipline, before their appointment start date. \u00a0 Department of Mathematics, Eberly College of Science, University Park, PA : An Assistant or Associate Professor whose research and teaching advance the Mathematical Foundations and Analysis of Quantum Algorithms.\u00a0 The department seeks to strengthen its expertise in the mathematics of quantum computing and to foster collaborations with existing research areas, including numerical analysis, number theory, geometry, applied mathematics, and related disciplines within and outside the department. Candidates must possess a PhD in Mathematics or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date. \u00a0 About the Penn State Quantum HUB\u00a0 The Penn State Quantum Hub is an interdisciplinary center housed under ICDS and is operated in collaboration with NSI and the Materials Research Institute (MRI). It was created to position the University at the forefront of quantum information science, technology, and education. The hub connects key quantum research domains \u2014 computation, materials, devices, sensing, communication, and simulation \u2014 through integrated programs and initiatives.\u00a0 \u00a0 Through the Hub, successful candidates will have opportunities to connect with faculty across colleges and disciplines, participate in interdisciplinary research and educational activities, develop collaborative proposals and large-scale research initiatives, engage with external academic and industry partners, and help shape Penn State\u2019s growing quantum computing ecosystem. https://quantum.psu.edu/ \u00a0 About the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences ICDS seeks to advance Penn State science, engineering, and humanities through computational and quantum theory, high-performance computing, Artificial Intelligence and data science, driving technological breakthroughs that redefine what is possible. https://icds.psu.edu/ \u00a0 About the National Security Institute NSI seeks to advance national security solutions through interdisciplinary research and strategic partnerships with government and industry. NSI focuses on the translation of academic breakthroughs into mission-ready solutions while developing the next generation of security-focused researchers and leaders. https://nsi.psu.edu/ \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Faculty-Position-in-Biomechanics-and-Biorobotics_REQ_0000083086-1": {"title": "Faculty Position in Biomechanics and Biorobotics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Kinesiology and the Department of Mechanical Engineering, in partnership with the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences, invite applications for a tenure-line faculty position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor in Biomechanics and Biorobotics . The successful candidate will also serve as the Director of the Center for Movement Science and Technology (C-MOST) within the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences. The anticipated start date is Fall 2027. This is a strategic leadership opportunity for an internationally recognized scholar to help shape the future of biomechanics and biorobotics at Penn State. The successful candidate will lead the continued development of C-MOST while establishing a broader interdisciplinary Biorobotics Research Cluster that connects and facilitates world-class research across Penn State's colleges, institutes, and campuses. The Opportunity Penn State has longstanding strengths in biomechanics, movement science, engineering, the life sciences, neuroscience, materials, computation, medicine, and human health. C-MOST provides a foundation for bringing these complementary strengths together around fundamental questions of movement and the development of transformative technologies. We seek an accomplished scientist, engineer, or physician-scientist with an outstanding record of scholarly achievement, external research funding, interdisciplinary collaboration, and scientific leadership. The successful candidate will develop and advance a compelling vision for C-MOST and create new opportunities for collaboration among researchers, engineers, clinicians, and external partners. The Director will be expected to build C-MOST as a platform for interdisciplinary discovery and technology development while advancing a broader vision for Biorobotics at Penn State . This effort will bring together expertise spanning biomechanics and neuromechanics, robotics and control, biological systems, materials, computation, medicine, rehabilitation, and human performance. The position provides an opportunity for a senior scholar to help define a field at the intersection of biology, movement, engineering, and robotics and to build research programs that extend from fundamental discovery to technologies with meaningful applications in health, medicine, performance, and beyond. The Director will also contribute to the strategic activities and administration of C-MOST, including personnel, budgetary resources, research infrastructure, development activities, education and outreach, and engagement with internal and external partners. Importantly, this is a faculty leadership position . The successful candidate will maintain an independent, externally funded research program and will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education and mentorship. Areas of Research We seek candidates whose scholarship contributes to the broad and rapidly evolving field of biomechanics and biorobotics. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: Human and biological movement biomechanics Neuromechanics and sensorimotor control Biorobotics and bio-inspired robotics Human-robot interaction Assistive and rehabilitative robotics Wearable and robotic technologies Computational biomechanics and movement science Robotics for health, medicine, and rehabilitation Musculoskeletal and neuromuscular systems Mechanobiology and biological materials Robotics, sensing, and control of biological movement Translational technologies for human performance, health, and rehabilitation We particularly encourage applications from candidates whose research crosses disciplinary boundaries and who have demonstrated the ability to build collaborative programs involving scientists, engineers, clinicians, and/or external partners. Penn State's Interdisciplinary Research Environment Penn State offers an exceptional environment for interdisciplinary research at the intersection of biomechanics, biorobotics, life sciences, engineering, and human health. C-MOST was established in 2015 to advance interdisciplinary research and training in basic and applied movement sciences. The center includes faculty from across 14 Departments and 6 colleges, bringing together expertise in biomechanics and neuromechanics, physiology, cognition, biorobotics, computational modelling and clinical science. The center is housed within the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences . The Huck Institutes serve as a hub for life sciences research at Penn State, bringing together scientists from across the University to address fundamental questions and societal challenges. The Huck Institutes supports Centers and Institutes, including C-MOST and the Neuroscience Institute; graduate programs, including the Interdisciplinary Graduate Degree Programs in Integrative and Biomedical Physiology and in Neuroscience; and manages shared and core facilities with instrumentation and expertise in genomics, metabolomics, imaging, and other technologies. The Department of Kinesiology is home to over 50 faculty and 900 students. Faculty have funded research in the areas of biomechanics, motor neuroscience, women\u2019s health, cardiovascular physiology, environmental physiology, clinical rehabilitation, and behavior change to increase physical activity. The Department offers separate B.S., M.S., M.A.T., and Ph.D. degrees. There are also options for dual Ph.D. degrees in Clinical and Translational Sciences and in Neuroscience. The Department of Mechanical Engineering is home to more than 65 faculty, 350 graduate students, and 1110 undergraduate students. The Department offers separate B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degree programs in mechanical engineering including online graduate programs in mechanical engineering and in additive manufacturing and design.\u00a0 Together, the faculty across the departments conduct in excess of $60M per year of funded research across a broad spectrum of traditional and emerging areas. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate broadly across Penn State, including with the College of Health and Human Development, College of Engineering, College of Medicine, Materials Research Institute, Department of Computer Science and Engineering , and other interdisciplinary institutes, centers, and programs. The position is designed to capitalize on these complementary strengths and create new intellectual and technological connections across the University. The Director will have an opportunity to help define the next generation of interdisciplinary research in biomechanics and biorobotics and to establish Penn State as a leading destination for researchers working at the interface of movement, biology, engineering, and robotics . Qualifications Candidates must have an earned doctorate or equivalent terminal degree in biomechanics, kinesiology, mechanical engineering, biomedical engineering, robotics, neuroscience, medicine, or a closely related discipline. Successful candidates will have: An outstanding record of research excellence and scholarly productivity appropriate to the rank of Associate or Full Professor; A sustained record of peer-reviewed extramural research funding , including active awards; A record of leadership in interdisciplinary research initiatives and collaborations; National or international recognition for scholarly contributions; Demonstrated ability to develop and sustain productive collaborations across disciplinary and organizational boundaries; Experience developing large-scale research programs or multidisciplinary research initiatives; Experience translating fundamental research, technologies, or discoveries toward clinical, industrial, or other applications; Evidence of effective teaching and mentorship at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels; Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills; Demonstrated ability to bring together individuals and groups with diverse scientific and technical expertise around shared research goals. Candidates for the rank of Full Professor should demonstrate a sustained record of national or international scholarly leadership, significant external funding, and contributions to the development of interdisciplinary research programs. Candidates for Associate Professor should demonstrate a strong record of scholarly achievement, external funding, interdisciplinary collaboration, and leadership appropriate to the rank. About Penn State The Pennsylvania State University is a land-grant institution and one of the top 30 research universities in the United States, ranking among the top 15 public institutions. The University Park Campus is located in State College, a vibrant university town in central Pennsylvania, offering excellent schools and outstanding recreational and cultural activities. The campus is within a 3-4 hour drive to major metropolitan areas, including Washington, DC, Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City, and Pittsburgh. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Our campuses are located on the original homelands of the Erie, Haudenosaunee (Seneca, Cayuga, Onondaga, Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and Wahzhazhe (Osage) Nations. As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and honor the traditional caretakers of these lands and strive to understand and model their responsible stewardship. We also acknowledge the longer history of these lands and our place in that history. \u00a0 Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials through the online application system: Cover letter (1\u20132 pages) describing the candidate's qualifications and interest in the position. Research statement (3\u20134 pages) describing current research, future research directions, and plans for developing an externally funded interdisciplinary research program at Penn State. C-MOST and Biorobotics Vision Statement (2\u20133 pages) describing the candidate's vision for C-MOST and for developing a broader Biorobotics research cluster at Penn State, including opportunities for interdisciplinary research, external partnerships, and growth. Teaching and mentoring statement (1\u20132 pages). Curriculum vitae. Names and contact information for three professional references. Please upload all of your materials at the first upload prompt, including a list of references. There is a maximum of five files. Some materials might need to be combined to be included.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately, and continue until a suitable candidate is identified. For more information, please contact Search Chair Jonas Rubenson (jonas@psu.edu). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Saharan-Dust-Analysis_REQ_0000083171-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Saharan Dust Analysis", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Meteorology and Atmospheric Science at Penn State (University Park, PA) announces a one-year Postdoctoral Scholar position for the analysis of Saharan dust using a regional modeling framework.\u00a0The candidate will undertake sensitivity studies using the WRF/MPAS model to address lower tropospheric heating in the presence of Saharan Dust.\u00a0The successful candidate will have experience in simulating dust aerosols using regional models and comparing them the satellite and surface observations. Responsibilities: Analysis of observations and numerical simulations of Saharan dust using reanalyses as lateral boundary conditions. Lead or support peer-reviewed publications built around these analyses. Requirements: A Ph.D. in atmospheric science or a related field by the time of hire. Experience use of the WRF or MPAS model. Strong computational skills. Good communications and writing skills. Interested Candidates should submit a cover letter describing their interest in the position and career goals, a CV including publication list, and names & contact information of up to three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Teaching-Faculty-Positions-in-Human-Centered-Computing_REQ_0000083027-2": {"title": "Teaching Faculty Positions in Human-Centered Computing", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Human-Centered Computing and Social Informatics (HCCSI) in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for two open-rank, non-tenure-line teaching faculty positions beginning in January or July of 2027 at the University Park campus. These are term appointments with an excellent possibility of renewal as multi-year appointments.\u00a0 Candidates should demonstrate strong technical expertise in designing and developing AI-powered applications and interactive systems, a commitment to teaching undergraduate and graduate students from varied backgrounds, and an interest in curricular innovation and development.\u00a0 The primary responsibility will be teaching residential undergraduate and graduate courses. These are in-person teaching positions based in State College, Pennsylvania, and most courses associated with these positions are taught in person. University service is also expected of teaching faculty.\u00a0 We seek candidates who can teach students how to integrate AI models and capabilities into larger software systems and develop robust, scalable, maintainable, and usable AI-powered applications. Candidates should be prepared to help students develop the technical and critical judgment needed to build AI-powered systems effectively and responsibly. Expertise in developing or training AI or machine-learning models is not required, but experience in these areas is a plus.\u00a0 The successful candidates may teach in the following areas, listed in order of importance for this search: \u00a0 Design and development of AI-powered applications and interactive systems, including integrating AI models and capabilities into larger software systems and building robust, maintainable, and usable applications.\u00a0 AI application architectures and development frameworks, including model integration and orchestration, deployment, monitoring, and evaluation.\u00a0 Agent-based application development, including LLM-powered agents, single-agent and multi-agent systems, agent coordination, and AI-powered interactive systems.\u00a0 Human-centered design and evaluation of AI-powered applications, including prototyping, human-AI interaction, user needs, human values, responsible use, and user experience.\u00a0 Software design, engineering, and application development, including object-oriented design, software validation and verification techniques, testing, debugging, deployment, maintenance, mobile application development, and capstone development.\u00a0 Programming and application development, particularly in Python and/or Java.\u00a0 Applicants must hold a master's degree or higher in a relevant field by the appointment start date. A Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred but not required. Relevant fields include, but are not limited to, Computer Science, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Informatics, Information Science, Human-Computer Interaction, Computer Engineering, and related computing disciplines. Depending on qualifications, appointments may be made at the rank of Lecturer, Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, Teaching Professor,\u00a0or Professor of Practice\u00a0in accordance with Penn State policy AC21.\u00a0 Applicants must include the following materials with their application: (i) a cover letter describing qualifications for the position and relevant expertise in AI-powered application development and related technical areas; (ii) a one-page teaching statement; (iii) curriculum vitae; and (iv) contact information for at least three professional references. The teaching statement should describe the candidate's teaching philosophy, pedagogical approach, and teaching style, including how they engage students and support effective learning in technical courses. Applicants should also indicate which of the teaching areas described above they would be most interested in contributing to, as well as any new courses they would be interested in developing. Please upload one document that combines the above materials into a single PDF.\u00a0 For more information, please visit the HCCSI department website and the College of IST degree programs .\u00a0 Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin November 12, 2026, and will continue until the positions are filled. Candidates are encouraged to apply early. On-site interviews in State College may begin as early as November 2026.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Chemistry-Department_REQ_0000082892-1": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor - Chemistry Department", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratories of Professors\u00a0Amie Boal, J. Martin Bollinger, Jr., and Carsten Krebs in the Department of Chemistry,\u00a0at The Pennsylvania State University, seek to fill an assistant research professor position in the area of mechanistic bioinorganic chemistry. Research will focus on the investigation of the reaction mechanisms of various mono- and dinuclear non-heme-iron enzymes and the elucidation of how their reactivity can be manipulated. The successful candidate should demonstrate extensive experience in a combination of various spectroscopic methods, enzymology, analytical chemistry, and structural biology. Applicant must hold a Ph.D. in Chemistry. The individual should be self-motivated and is expected to lead the projects,\u00a0as well as contribute to collaborative research efforts. Interested and qualified applicants must submit applications electronically to include a cover letter describing\u00a0your research background to include prior training,\u00a0and research interests, as well as a CV. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0Following a screening of\u00a0initial application materials,\u00a0candidates will be contacted by email\u00a0asking for letters of reference\u00a0to be sent. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Electro-Optics-Materials-and-Device-Engineer--FACULTY-_REQ_0000083290-2": {"title": "Electro-Optics Materials and Device Engineer (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Your working location will be fully on-site, located in State College, PA. This position will require periodic travel to remote locations (including the Electro-Optics & Electronics (EOE) Freeport Office near Pittsburgh, PA) in support of collaboration and testing as part of a small team of researchers, engineers, and technologists. We are searching for an Electro-Optics Materials and Device Engineer Faculty to join our EOE Division at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State.\u00a0 EOE develops innovative optical solutions for imaging, high-energy laser (HEL) delivery, and sensing systems, and maintains the design and testing capabilities required to build and fully characterize all aspects of optical performance \u2013 from image quality to HEL coating damage testing. \u00a0This role will lead and conduct basic and applied research of advanced electro-optical designs, including metasurfaces, photonic structures and other emerging material and nano-science applications. You will have the ability to take on challenges where the path the research may take is not clear, and the outcome is not known or guaranteed. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Act as part of team leadership that operates in this ambiguous space and develops the executable plan for the rest of the team Perform physics-based modeling to predict the performance of imaging system concepts and designs Drive system level trade studies to develop architectures and allocate system level requirements across subsystems and engineering disciplines Routinely interface with sponsors, customers, end-users, and collaborators to understand their problems, brainstorm solutions, scope research, communicate the technical aspects of research execution, and convey the significance of results Provide input to the strategic direction of the department\u2019s research pursuits by helping to establish the appropriate core competencies and evaluating where our capabilities best align with a sponsor\u2019s needs Additional responsibilities of the higher-level include: Leverage prior first-hand experience with building and testing advanced, state-of-the-art electro-optic systems Track the latest developments in electro-optic systems and advise on how and when to integrate them into on-going and future research opportunities. Perform project planning, budgeting, and scheduling Manage vendors and suppliers, from purchase orders through statements of work Lead other engineers in day-to-day tasking to satisfy stakeholder\u2019s requirements and expectations Independently manage multiple and/or large electro-optic projects Develop and propose solutions for new applications Perform the role of Trusted Agent to the government to assess and validate state-of-the art electro-optic systems and solutions Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/Experience areas include: Ability to work independently as well as in a team environment and meet project schedule requirements Design, analysis, procurement, assembly and testing of components and complete electro-optic and infrared (EO/IR) systems for military applications Microelectronic systems and detector fabrication processes Past success in a multitude of optical and electrical materials and systems Past success operating as a systems engineer for imaging systems Photonic structures and other optical metamaterial designs approaches Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: Past success within an organization responsible for manufacturing EO/IR systems Visible and infrared imaging system design and characterization Electro-optical metamaterial designs approaches Radiometry (analysis and laboratory measurements), development of link budgets, prediction of sensor response, and image quality metrics Electro-optic designs that extend the electro-optic state-of-the-art Significant experience bringing together distributed teams to achieve multiplied results Active security clearance, at the secret level, with eligibility for TS/SCI ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Intel Community (IC), and other federal government customers. FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our website at www.arl.psu.edu. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor--Department-of-Applied-Linguistics_REQ_0000083283-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Applied Linguistics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The College of the Liberal Arts at The Pennsylvania State University at University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the Department of Applied Linguistics to begin Fall 2027, with flexibility.\u00a0 The Assistant Professor will be expected to perform undergraduate and graduate teaching, pursue an active research program at the intersection of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Applied Linguistics, and secure external research funding.\u00a0 Duties related to the research program will include applying conceptual and computational approaches to advance understanding of how AI is reshaping questions fundamental to applied linguistics and how the field can engage with these developments.\u00a0 The areas of research may include, but are not limited to, theoretically informed applications of AI in language teaching, learning, and assessment; computational and AI-supported approaches to language research, generative AI and language use; human-AI interaction and communication, the linguistic and communicative capacities of AI systems, and the social, ethical, educational, and professional implications of AI.\u00a0 Responsibilities Maintain an active program of research and scholarly publication at the intersection of AI and Applied Linguistics and pursue external funding to support their research program.\u00a0 Contribute to shaping the Department\u2019s evolving engagement with AI in research, teaching, and curriculum development.\u00a0\u00a0 Contribute to the Department\u2019s existing undergraduate and graduate courses and develop new courses related to AI and Applied Linguistics. The standard teaching load is two courses per semester (2-2).\u00a0 Mentor undergraduate and graduate students and supervise doctoral research in areas related to their expertise.\u00a0\u00a0 Contribute service and leadership to the Department, College, University, and relevant professional communities.\u00a0 Required Qualifications\u00a0 Ph.D. in Applied Linguistics, Computational Linguistics, Linguistic Anthropology, Educational Linguistics, Second Language Studies, or a closely related field by the time of appointment.\u00a0\u00a0 An established or emerging research profile at the intersection of AI and Applied Linguistics.\u00a0 Evidence of or potential for excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring.\u00a0 The Department of Applied Linguistics is an intellectually diverse community committed to advancing understanding of language use and language learning across social, cultural, educational, and professional contexts. The Department offers a B.A. and minor in Applied Linguistics, an M.A. in Teaching English as a Second Language, a Ph.D. in Applied Linguistics, and related certificates and programs. Its faculty pursue research across a broad range of theoretical, methodological, and substantive areas. This vibrant intellectual environment is further enriched by programming and research activities undertaken by several centers associated with the Department, including the Center for Language Acquisition (CLA) and the English for Professional Purposes Intercultural Center (EPPIC). Opportunities also exist for interdisciplinary collaboration with scholars, centers, and initiatives across Penn State working on AI and its applications and implications. Please visit https://aplng.la.psu.edu/ for more information about the Department of Applied Linguistics. Inquiries can be sent to the search committee chair, Xiaofei Lu, at xxl13@psu.edu . \u00a0 Interested individuals must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board . Any questions or concerns with the online application can be directed to Kaylee Keller at kec5626@psu.edu . Complete applications will include a detailed letter of application describing the candidate\u2019s research, teaching trajectory, and future plans; a CV; a highly relevant writing sample or publication; evidence of teaching effectiveness; and the names and contact information for three references. The Search Committee will not contact references without informing the candidate. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000083322-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS A temporary research and training position is available working on multiple community-engaged, applied prevention research and evaluation projects led by Dr.\u2019s Sarah Chilenski and Jochebed Gayles. The successful candidate will have experience in executing mixed methods research projects with a variety of populations and in collective community change topics. The primary goal of this role is to foster the scholar\u2019s independent research capabilities, scientific writing, and project management skills. \u00a0 Key Responsibilities & Duties \u00a0 Research Execution (70%): Design, execute, and manage independent and collaborative community-engaged, applied prevention research, implementation practice documentation, and evaluation projects centered around project goals and objectives. Collect, analyze, report, and interpret results of mixed methods data analyses. \u00a0 Scholarly Output (15%): Prepare and co-author manuscripts for publication in high-impact peer-reviewed journals. Present research findings at national conferences. \u00a0 Grant and Proposal Contribution (15%): Contribute to preliminary data generation and drafting sections for grant renewal applications or new funding proposals. \u00a0 Qualifications & Skills \u00a0 Education: Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Psychology, Developmental Psychology, Human Development and Family Studies, Public Health, Social Work, or related field obtained within the last year. \u00a0 Technical Expertise: Demonstrated hands-on experience in both qualitative and quantitative data analysis; designing and executing data collection systems; summarizing qualitative and quantitative data in table and graphical forms. Ability to translate logic models to data collection protocols and communicate with community partners. \u00a0 Communication: Strong written and verbal communication skills as evidenced by a peer-reviewed journal articles or co-authorship of community-engaged project evaluation reports. \u00a0 Work Style: Ability to work both independently with minimal daily supervision and collaboratively within an interdisciplinary team. Interacting with community partners from a place of mutual respect, partnership, and trust is crucial. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-line-Faculty-Positions-in-Artificial-Intelligence-_REQ_0000083172-1": {"title": "Tenure-line Faculty Positions in Artificial Intelligence", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Tenure-line Faculty Positions in Artificial Intelligence\u202f\u202f\u00a0 \u00a0 The Department of Informatics and Intelligent Systems (IIS) in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for multiple tenure-line faculty positions in Artificial Intelligence (AI). The appointments will be at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank and will begin in July of 2027 at the University Park campus in State College, Pennsylvania.\u202fRemote appointments are not permitted for these hires.\u00a0 \u00a0 We seek to build on the strengths of the department in AI, including causal inference, computer vision, human-centered and socially responsible AI, knowledge representation, machine learning, natural language processing, multi-agent systems, AI ethics, and/or transformative AI\u202fapplications that tackle major scientific and/or societal challenges. We seek scholars who complement our existing strengths, and bring expertise in core areas of AI, or who bridge fundamental research in AI with transformative applications in the sciences, healthcare, security, critical infrastructure, public policy, the humanities, and/or social sciences.\u202f\u00a0 \u00a0 The department is home to Penn State\u2019s undergraduate B.S. degree in Artificial Intelligence Methods and Applications (AIMA) and offers the Applied Data Sciences Option of the tri-college B.S. degree in Data Sciences . Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, conduct cutting-edge research, supervise and mentor graduate students, secure external funding to support research activities, engage in service activities at the college and university levels, and collaborate with faculty across the university and industry partners.\u202f\u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates must possess a PhD in Artificial Intelligence, Cognitive Science, Computer Science, Informatics, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. Applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will demonstrate a potential for research excellence (as demonstrated by publications in top venues), strong potential for securing external funding for research, and potential to contribute to teaching in AI and related areas. Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have an established record of research excellence, external funding, teaching and curriculum development, and service.\u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants should include i) a cover letter with information about their interests and qualifications for the position; ii) a research statement summarizing past accomplishments and future plans; iii) a teaching statement summarizing teaching philosophy, teaching experience, and teaching interests; iv) a curriculum vitae; and v) contact information for at least three professional references.\u202f\u202f\u00a0 \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is among the top 25 research universities in the United States. The Department of Informatics and Intelligent Systems and the College of Information Sciences and Technology offer fertile grounds for interdisciplinary collaborative research at the interface of computing, data science, AI and other disciplines. Additional collaborative opportunities and extensive resources are offered by the interdisciplinary research institutes \u2013 Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (which provides excellent high-performance computing facilities and support), Huck Institute of the Life Sciences, Materials Research Institute, Institute for Energy and the Environment, Social Science Research Institute, Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute, and the National Security Institute.\u202f\u00a0 \u00a0 The Penn State University Park campus is located in State College, a vibrant and welcoming college town in central Pennsylvania. The area offers an excellent quality of life, with highly regarded schools, a strong sense of community, and abundant cultural, recreational, dining, and outdoor opportunities. State College combines the amenities and energy of a major research university with the affordability, convenience, and natural beauty of a smaller community. The campus is served by nearby State College Regional Airport, providing convenient air travel and connections to major transportation hubs. State College is also within approximately a 2\u20134 hour drive of several major metropolitan areas, including Pittsburgh, Washington D.C., Baltimore, Philadelphia, and New York City. This combination of accessibility, community, and quality of life makes State College an attractive place to live, work, and build a career.\u00a0 \u00a0 Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu . Review of applications begins on November 1, 2026, and will continue while positions remain open.\u202f\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/William-Elliott-Chaired-Professor-of-Insurance-and-Risk-Management_REQ_0000083296-1": {"title": "William Elliott Chaired Professor of Insurance and Risk Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Risk Management Department in the Smeal College of Business at the Pennsylvania State University (University Park Campus) invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Full Professor in the fields of risk management, insurance, or economics. The position is the William Elliott Chaired Professor of Insurance and Risk Management. The desired start date is Fall 2027. \u00a0 Job Requirements and Duties The William Elliott Chair carries an expectation of sustained research excellence and thought leadership in the discipline, department leadership in Risk Management programs, mentorship, and high ethical standards. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in risk management, insurance, economics or a closely related field, a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research, including publications in premier journals with evidence of impact, and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. \u00a0 Faculty members in the Risk Management department are expected to pursue an active research program, perform undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, engage in professional service, and supervise graduate students when appropriate. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. \u00a0 Application Requirements \u00a0 Applicants should apply directly online on the Penn State site. Supporting materials should include a letter of interest and a CV. If you have questions about the position, please send an email to rm@smeal.psu.edu . \u00a0 Academic Environment \u00a0 The Risk Management Department is home to faculty in Risk Management, Actuarial Science, Business Economics, Business Law, International Business, and Real Estate. The department houses three undergraduate majors: Risk Management, Actuarial Science, and Real Estate as well as undergraduate minors in the Legal Environment of Business and International Business and graduate programs in Real Estate. It also houses the Laboratory for Economics Management and Auctions (LEMA), a dedicated laboratory space for conducting economics-style experiments. Department faculty and students are supported by two external advisory boards, including the Risk Management and Actuarial Science (RMAS) Advisory Board. \u00a0 The internationally ranked Penn State Smeal College of Business prepares students for professional success now and across their careers. Within a vibrant intellectual community, we are a source of expertise, research, and talent that influences the business practices of tomorrow. The college seeks recognition as a top five U.S. public business school through the strategic priorities of enriching the student experience, transforming teaching and learning through innovative curricula, advancing research excellence with investment in faculty and resources, accommodating organizational growth with infrastructure investment, and driving external engagement and philanthropy with new partnerships and brand enhancement. The Pennsylvania State University\u2019s main campus (University Park) is located in the heart of State College, PA.\u00a0Commonly referred to as \u201cHappy Valley,\u201d our community features charms of a small town with the opportunities\u00a0typically only experienced in larger cities. It has award winning public schools that have been ranked among the best in the country. It has also been recognized as one of the safest metropolitan areas and best college towns in the United States. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000083332-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Medina group ( https://sites.psu.edu/medinalabgroup/ ) at The Pennsylvania State University has two open positions for postdoctoral scholars . Projects span a range of programmatic themes, including molecular biophysics, nano-therapeutic and -diagnostic technologies, and bioresponsive materials. Open projects include : 1. Investigating the thermostability of nucleic acid/nucleoprotein complexes using surface-assembled molecular dispersants.\u00a0 2. Exploring the activity, mode of action, and structural plasticity of novel fluorinated chemotherapeutics.\u00a0 3. Exploiting the fluorous effect to create adaptive matter and rationally design bioresponsive materials. \u00a0 The position will be in the Biomedical Engineering (BME) Department and affiliated with the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences ( http://www.huck.psu.edu ) and/or Penn State Cancer Institute ( https://cancer.psu.edu/ ). We offer a rich environment where faculty, postdocs, graduate students and undergraduate researchers regularly interact and collaborate. Scholars will have unrestricted access to our state-of-the-art core facilities to explore their emerging and interdisciplinary research interests. \u00a0 Qualified individuals will hold a Ph.D. by the time of appointment in Chemistry, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Engineering, or a related discipline. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in fluorine chemistry, nanotheranostics, and molecular self-assembly. The appointment duration is for one year, renewal possible depending on availability of funds. Qualified candidates should apply online and include: a one-page cover letter detailing their research expertise, scientific interests and career goals, as well as a complete curriculum vitae with three professional references. For more information, please contact Dr. Scott Medina ( shm126@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Fluids-Machinery-Department-Head--FACULTY-_REQ_0000083257-2": {"title": "Fluids Machinery Department Head (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Your working location will be fully onsite located in State College, PA. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. We are searching for a Department Head to join our Fluids Machinery Department of the Fluid Mechanics Division\u00a0at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. In this role, you will contribute to and direct the work and growth of a team whose focus is the design, analysis and testing of turbomachinery and devices for the motion and control of fluids, ranging in technical maturity from fundamental physics to fabricated devices, and in size from small-scale models to full-scale propulsion systems for UUV\u2019s, surface ships and submarines. Mentorship and business development will be significant components of this position. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. \u00a0 You will: Provide organizational leadership to a growing group of Engineers, to include employee management, recruitment, development, retention, and technical direction Direct technical excellence, cost control and on-time delivery of work Lead the technical execution of research, design, development and testing of turbomachinery systems for a range of U.S. Government and Industry customers Provide subject matter expertise in the areas of turbomachinery, fluid dynamics and cavitation Develop and maintain long-term professional relationships with sponsors and relevant stakeholders Oversee the development of proposals for new programs Embrace ARL\u2019s mission to discover, demonstrate, transition and educate \u00a0 Additional responsibilities for higher-level position includes:\u00a0 Provide technical and managerial leadership for research and development programs, establishing technical vision, priorities, and standards across one or more engineering disciplines Lead and oversee small or moderate size and scope projects, ensuring technical rigor, feasibility, quality, cost effectiveness, and on-time execution Guide concept development, design analyses, and problem resolution by independently evaluating and applying appropriate scientific and engineering methods to meet sponsor and customer needs Manage, mentor, and develop engineering staff, including hiring, performance management, workforce planning, and professional development Serve as a primary technical and managerial point of contact for sponsors and partners; maintain external research relationships and contribute to business development through identification of funding opportunities and proposal development Review and author technical reports, publications, and presentations; represent the organization in technical reviews and collaborations Ensure compliance with applicable DoD, University, safety, security, and export control requirements, while collaborating across teams to advance organizational goals \u00a0 Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. \u00a0 Required Skills/Experience areas include: Fluid mechanics or aerodynamics Taking an idea from concept through design and analyses into test-validated hardware Proposal writing and subsequent securing of funding. Past success in leadership of technical personnel Past success in management of sponsored programs Strong presentation and communication skills, both technical and inter-personal Design and execution of experiments utilizing wind or water facilities Active security clearance, at the Secret level or higher \u00a0 Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: Ph.D. degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering or related field Numerical modeling of fluids and systems using MATLAB or Simulink Solid modeling and CAD systems ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Intel Community (IC), and other federal government customers. FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our website at www.arl.psu.edu. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Embedded-Software-Department-Head--FACULTY-_REQ_0000083255-3": {"title": "Embedded Software Department Head (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS \u00ad\u00ad\u00adYour working location will be fully on-site and located in State College, PA.\u00a0Options exist for hybrid of on-site/work from home based on project-dependent ability. This role may require periodic travel to remote locations. \u00a0 We are searching for a Department Head to join our Embedded Software (ES) department at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State University. ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the U.S. Military. \u00a0 The ES Department\u2019s mission is to design, build, test, and deliver software and firmware for undersea systems.\u00a0 The department is responsible for designing, implementing, and integrating software for Science & Technology demonstrations as well as Engineering Development and In-Service system programs.\u00a0 The ES department serves as the leading resource for our Undersea Systems Office (USO) in real-time embedded software/firmware design, development, integration, and testing. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. \u00a0 ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. \u00a0 You will: Develop and sustain a high-performing workforce through coaching, mentorship, succession planning, talent development, and employee engagement Establish the technical vision and strategic direction for the department, ensuring capabilities, resources, and investments align with office, division, and laboratory objectives Direct and oversee the software engineering function in developing, releasing, and maintaining software and firmware applications to meet program, customer, and business needs Guide the architecture, design, development, integration, and testing of embedded software and firmware solutions for autonomous and undersea systems Foster a culture of technical excellence, innovation, continuous improvement, and adherence to software engineering best practices Establish and maintain policies, processes, and standards that produce high-quality products, including coding principles, engineering tools, and development methodologies Coordinate with office engineering leadership to ensure rigorous execution, sound research and engineering practices, and the highest standards of technical work Collaborate with division and office leadership to prioritize work, allocate resources, manage staffing requirements, and support current and future programs \u00a0 Additional responsibilities for higher-level position includes: Lead major research and development initiatives and shape the department's long-term research and technology portfolio Lead strategic initiatives through customer engagement, business development activities, and proposal development \u00a0 Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/Experience areas include: Management of projects, people, and technical teams, including demonstrated leadership and the ability to establish and achieve organizational goals and objectives Demonstrated experience leading technical teams and providing technical direction in the development and delivery of complex engineering systems Demonstrated experience leading, mentoring, and developing technical personnel Design and development of embedded real-time, multi-threaded software, FPGA/CPLD firmware, or hardware design, including experience with C/C++ and modern embedded development tools and environments Effective verbal and written communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills. Active security clearance at the Secret level or higher, or the ability to obtain and maintain a Secret security clearance Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: Bachelor's degree in software engineering, computer engineering, electrical engineering, computer science, or a related STEM discipline. Advanced degree preferred Demonstrated experience leading engineering teams and mentoring technical staff in a research, development, or a product-focused environment Managing multiple technical projects, balancing workforce priorities, and allocating resources to meet program objectives Developing technical proposals, supporting business development activities, or leading strategic growth initiatives Working within DoD, Navy, defense research, or other government-sponsored programs Past success establishing technical roadmaps, guiding architecture decisions, and aligning departmental capabilities with strategic business and research objectives ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Intel Community (IC), and other federal government customers. FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our website at www.arl.psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Department-Head-of-Architecture_REQ_0000083106-1": {"title": "Department Head of Architecture", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Stuckeman School in the College of Arts and Architecture at Penn State seeks a responsive, visionary, and thoughtful leader to serve as Head of the Department of Architecture. The Department of Architecture is grounded in a longstanding culture of interdisciplinary collaboration. Throughout its history, the department has developed strong connections with units across the University, creating opportunities for integrated teaching, research, and design exploration. This collaborative ecosystem brings together diverse expertise in every dimension of the built environment. The next Department Head will value and strengthen these relationships while advancing architecture\u2019s distinctive disciplinary voice and ambitions. The Department Head will lead the department through significant changes in higher education, the architectural profession, and at Penn State. Working collaboratively with faculty and administrators across the School and College, the Department Head will identify new opportunities and strategic directions in response to complex institutional, financial, academic, and societal challenges. The successful candidate will demonstrate effective communication, sound judgment, fiscal responsibility, and the ability to make timely, decisive decisions. They will embrace change as an opportunity for innovation while upholding the academic excellence, integrity, and values of the Department, the School, the College, and the University. The next Department Head will work to implement the Department\u2019s 2026-2030 strategic plans and support strategic goals and initiatives across the School, College, and University. Candidates must possess an established record of teaching, scholarship, and service, as well as an active research agenda and/or creative practice that contributes to the field of architecture and advances the department\u2019s scholarly and creative impact. \u00a0 The Department The Department of Architecture provides a nationally and internationally recognized education responsive to the social, environmental, technological, and cultural challenges of the twenty-first century. Through excellence in teaching, research, outreach, advising, and service, the Department prepares students to contribute meaningfully to society and the built environment. Administratively housed within the Stuckeman School in Penn State\u2019s College of Arts and Architecture, the Department includes approximately 32 full- and part-time faculty members, 316 undergraduate students, and 62 graduate students. It offers professional B.Arch. and M.Arch degrees, as well as research-based M.S. and Ph.D. programs. Since its inception, the department has expanded its degree programs and strengthened faculty research. Its research, creative practice, and scholarship continue to flourish through national and international exhibitions, symposia, design-build projects, publications, sponsored research, and other recognized contributions to the field. More information is available on the Department of Architecture website: https://arts.psu.edu/academics/department-of-architecture/ In support of this mission, the Department Head will support the following core areas:\u00a0 Educate undergraduate and graduate students in architecture and prepare them for lives of creative engagement and professional excellence in practice, research, and inquiry; Foster exemplary work in architectural design, theory, critical analysis, and research within a studio-centered environment; Support and embrace diversity in all its forms across the student body, faculty, staff, and curriculum; Provide an educational environment that connects architecture with the design disciplines, the arts and sciences, and engineering, while engaging students and faculty in urgent contemporary social, cultural, and environmental issues; Integrate professional and environmental ethics, critical thinking, research inquiry, creative practice, life-long learning, and service to society throughout the curriculum; Cultivate a teaching and learning environment that values collaboration and teamwork alongside individual research and creative activity; and Expand outreach to local, national, and international communities in support of Penn State\u2019s land-grant mission. \u00a0 Responsibilities of the Department Head Lead the day-to-day administration of the department; Recruit faculty to contribute to the department\u2019s initiatives through tenure and non-tenure track roles; Manage the promotion and tenure review processes; Conduct annual assessments of all faculty and 5-year post-tenure reviews; Maintain program accreditation and support and develop curricular initiatives; Support and develop graduate education; Support and promote faculty development, research, creative work and scholarship within an R-1 university setting, including the pursuit of external funding to sustain and strengthen these activities; Demonstrate responsible and sustainable fiscal management of the departmental budget; work collaboratively with the financial staff and officers in the School and College; Serve as a member of the School leadership team; Serve as a member of the College academic leadership team; Engage with the College\u2019s Office of Advancement to develop opportunities for alumni relationships and philanthropic support; Maintain a research agenda or creative practice; Uphold and lead by example the Penn State values of Integrity, Respect, Responsibility, Discovery, Excellence, and Community. Assure faculty within the Department of Architecture are upholding the Penn State values. \u00a0 Qualifications Required Qualifications: Terminal Degree: A terminal degree in architecture, such as a professional Master of Architecture (M. Arch), a Ph.D. in Architecture, or Doctoral of Design (D. Des) in Architecture; Rank Eligibility: A distinguished record of scholarship, peer-reviewed publications, or creative design practice that meets the criteria for a tenured appointment at the rank of Full Professor at Penn State; Administrative Experience: Experience in departmental or college-level leadership, such as serving as a Program Director, Department Chair/Head, or Associate Dean, or having equivalent administrative experiences; demonstrated oversight of strategic planning, budget planning and management, and personnel management; demonstrated familiarity with the promotion and tenure process; Teaching Excellence: A proven track record of architectural education at the undergraduate and graduate levels; Research Excellence: A proven track record of scholarly and/or creative achievement, and/or a record of pursuing and securing external support appropriate to the candidate\u2019s field of expertise; Accreditation Oversight: Proven capacity to manage professional NAAB accreditation processes and coordinate multi-tier degree paths; Leadership and Mentorship: Demonstrated ability to lead collegially, inclusively, respectfully, responsibly, and responsively, with a record of mentoring and supporting the success of a diverse community of students, faculty, and staff; Inclusive Excellence: Demonstrated commitment to advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, access, and belonging for all through leadership, teaching, research, and community engagement. Desired Qualifications: Professional Licensure: Professional architecture licensure in the United States; Research Leadership: Demonstrated international recognition and leadership in interdisciplinary and/or transdisciplinary research, including but not limited to a record of securing significant external funding and advancing research impact; Curricular Innovation: Experience with emerging technologies, AI literacy, experiential and proactive learning, and evolving modes of design and professional practice; Professional Engagement: A strong record of engagement with the architectural profession, industry, professional organizations, community partners, and/or public agencies; Fundraising and External Relations: Demonstrated experience cultivating relationships with alumni, donors, foundations, industry, and other external partners to advance academic, research, and departmental priorities; Global Engagement: Experience developing international academic, research, and professional partnerships that enhance the global visibility and impact of architectural education and scholarship. \u00a0 Terms of Appointment This is a 42-week appointment reporting directly to the School Director. The successful candidate must meet all employment background checks and be able to work in the United States by the time of hire. \u00a0 Application To apply, upload a cover letter addressing how your experiences and leadership practice have prepared you for the department head\u2019s responsibilities and qualifications listed above, and how you envision you will contribute to the mission of the department and the Stuckeman School. In addition, address how the Penn State values relate to your leadership experience. Include a full curriculum vitae, selected samples of scholarly and/or creative work, and the names and contact information of three references.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 For questions, contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Robin Thomas, rlt18@psu.edu \u00a0 . For full consideration, submissions must be received by November 9, 2026. The review of applications will continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 The Stuckeman School The Stuckeman School comprises three departments\u2014Architecture, Graphic Design, and Landscape Architecture\u2014and three research centers: the Center for Ecology + Design, the Hamer Center for Community Design, and the Stuckeman Center for Design Computing. The School also includes the Office for Access, Wellbeing, and Equity; the Office of Career Services; and the Office of Marketing and Communications. The School provides shared administrative support, physical infrastructure, and endowment resources that promote the success and well-being of its students, faculty, and staff while fostering a culture of transdisciplinary collaboration. Its state-of-the-art, LEED Gold\u2013certified building includes wood and metal shops, digital and analog fabrication facilities, an immersive environment learning lab, and extensive technological resources. The department heads of Architecture and Landscape Architecture hold the Stuckeman Chair in Integrative Design. Additional endowments support chairs and professorships for senior faculty, a Career Development Professorship in Design for early-career faculty, and a competitive integrative research grant program open to faculty at all ranks. These resources also provide generous support for departmental initiatives, faculty research and travel, visiting critics, lectures and exhibitions, research assistants, and course enhancement. \u00a0 The College of Arts & Architecture Penn State's College of Arts and Architecture proudly serves as one of the major cultural centers between Philadelphia and Pittsburgh. The college is a comprehensive arts and design community committed to artistic and scholarly creativity, research and the preparation of specialized practitioners in all of the arts and design disciplines; to undergraduate general arts courses for all students; and to community engagement in its programs. The college offers undergraduate and graduate programs in the Department of Art History, the H. Campbell and Eleanor R. Stuckeman School of Architecture and Landscape Architecture, the School of Music, the School of Theatre, and the School of Visual Arts. Please visit the units\u2019 websites to learn more about the degrees they offer to approximately 1,700 students. The college also includes the Center for the Performing Arts, the Palmer Museum of Art, Penn State Centre Stage, which serve as important cultural resources that provide educational outreach programs for Penn State and area communities. In addition, the college is home to research centers and institutes, which help to foster a vibrant culture of inquiry that promotes excellence within the arts and design disciplines, while at the same time leveraging the potential of a comprehensive research university. The college is housed in sixteen buildings that include performance and exhibition spaces as well as specialized studios and labs. \u00a0 The University Founded in 1855, Penn State is a multi-campus, land grant, public research university that educates students from around the world and supports individuals and communities through integrated programs of teaching, research, and service. With over $800 million in annual research expenditures, Penn State ranks among the top 20 U. S. research universities.\u00a0 \u201cAdvancing the Arts and Humanities\u201d and \u201cStewarding our Planet\u2019s Resources\u201d are two of five thematic priorities relevant to our department in the University\u2019s Strategic Plan ( strategicplan.psu.edu ). As a land grant university, Penn State is responsible for providing a wide array of programs in professional and technical disciplines, as well as a balanced offering of undergraduate and graduate programs in the arts and sciences. Recently the provost established funds for multi-disciplinary research institutes offering unique opportunities. The University Park campus is located within State College, PA, which was recently ranked number 5 in a ranking of top college towns by the American Institute for Economic Research, and number 15 in a ranking of the Safest College Towns in America by Safewise. State College has excellent public school system and is a family-friendly town. Located in a valley in the Appalachian Mountains, in Centre County, Pennsylvania, employment at Penn State offers incredible opportunity to enjoy the beauty of the central Pennsylvania outdoors combined with the cultural, athletic, and entertainment opportunities a large university community can bring, and is within drivable distance from New York City, Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, and Washington DC. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Physics--Tenure-Tenure-Track-_REQ_0000082843-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Physics (Tenure/Tenure-Track)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, Pennsylvania, USA) invites applications for a faculty position (tenure-track/tenured). We are conducting a broad search across all ranks ( Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Full Professor ). The department is open to candidates from all subfields of physics, with a particular interest in the subfields of biological physics and particle-astrophysics. Required duties will combine research, teaching and service to the university and broader research community. The biological physics research in the department benefits from partnerships with Penn State\u2019s Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences.\u00a0 The Huck Institutes supports interdisciplinary life science research through 11 core facilities, 6 interdisciplinary graduate training programs, and several Centers and Institutes, including the National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences. The department offers state-of-the-art infrastructure for particle-astrophysics research, including access to Penn State's high-performance computing resources associated with the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences. Additionally, our faculty and students in particle-astrophysics will benefit from the high bay facility to be located in the newly constructed Osmond north wing, which provides specialized space for experimental instrumentation. These resources, plus those of the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos (IGC), offer an exceptional platform for innovative research and development. Competitive applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will hold a Ph.D. in physics or closely related field before beginning employment at Penn State; will demonstrate potential for developing an innovative, externally funded and collaborative\u00a0research program; and will demonstrate the potential to contribute to the department\u2019s and college\u2019s teaching and service missions. Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have the same qualifications as the rank of Assistant Professor, as well as a strong track record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service. Candidates for Full Professor should have the same qualifications as the rank of Associate Professor, as well as a track record of research publications, funding, teaching, and service that distinguishes them internationally. Applications must comprise: A cover letter (maximum of 2 pages) that includes: An overview of the goals/vision of your research program in the context of our department and institution Your most significant scientific accomplishments A summary of experiences and qualifications that position you to achieve your goals Curriculum vitae Detailed statement of research accomplishments and future plans (maximum of 4 pages) Statement of teaching philosophy and interests (1 page) For applicants for Assistant Professor: Four reference letters must be uploaded to Academic Jobs Online . For applicants for Associate or Full Professor: A list of six references must be named in the application. Candidates are encouraged, but not required, to arrange for reference letters to be submitted to Academic Jobs Online . PSU system limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Application Portals: Candidates for Assistant Professor should apply here: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32889 Candidates for Associate/Full Professor should apply here: https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32892 In addition to the Academic Jobs Online application, Penn State requires all applicants to register and complete the application form at the Penn State employment website . Completed applications received by November 22, 2026 are assured of full consideration; later applications may be considered until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Strategic-Systems-Operation-Division-Head--Faculty-_REQ_0000083178-1": {"title": "Strategic Systems Operation Division Head (Faculty)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Your working location will be a hybrid of on-site/work from home, on-site location is State College, PA. We are seeking a Division Head for the Strategic Systems Operations Division (SSO) to join the Information Advantage Office of the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. SSO specializes in delivering systems, products and information to leading edge DoD and IC operations worldwide. SSO consists of 4 departments: Signals Prototyping; Trusted Systems Engineering; Signals Implementation; National Programs Solutions. The Division Head will report directly to the Head of the Information Advantage Office and will be responsible for managing the division\u2019s research engineers, scientists, technicians, and support personnel. This position will be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD Skill Bridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You Will: Provide strategic and technical leadership for the Strategic Systems Division (SSO), guiding its emergence as a new division onto ARL\u2019s, Penn State\u2019s, and the broader national security landscape Build and lead comprehensive, high performing and collaborative teams across engineering, scientific, and support personnel; foster a culture of excellence, cohesion and professional development Lead interdisciplinary R&D programs from concept to delivery, ensuring technical rigor, mission relevance, and effective communication of program goals, outcomes and resource needs Manage division operations including strategic planning, budgeting, staffing, facilities challenges, proposal development, and risk mitigation to ensure growth is both sustainable and aligned Build and maintain strong sponsors, academic, and industry relationships, actively shaping new opportunities and positioning SSO as a central contributor to ARL\u2019s future Represent the division\u2014and as needed, the larger organization\u2014 through polished, executive level engagement with sponsors, ARL leadership, university stakeholders and strategic partners Lead, manage and continuously improve professional development, training and onboarding\u00a0 Faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Minimally requires a Master's degree in an engineering or science discipline and 10 years related experience. Required skills/experience areas include: Active TS/SCI Security Clearance Demonstrated leadership in technical program and personnel management, with experience operating in high- growth, mission-driven, and research-oriented environments Principal Investigator, technical lead, or senior contributor on applied and basic research efforts, with a record of securing and sustaining external funding in technical areas related to electromagnetic propagation modeling and simulation, radio frequency spectrum research, electromagnetic effects, signals processing, and or general electrical engineering skill sets Strong executive presence and polished communication skills- able to articulate needs, requirements and impact clearly to diverse audiences in various formats Demonstrated ability to manage complex organizational dynamics, navigate conflict, lead through challenges and shape forward-looking strategies Demonstrated strength in business and/or program management capabilities, including experience managing budgets, staffing, performance management, and strategic planning Strong professional demeanor and interpersonal agility, with the ability to work effectively across organizational levels and with external sponsors, collaborators and partners, with a proven ability to establish credibility, influence outcomes, and build trust ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Intel Community (IC), and other federal government customers. \u00a0 FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our website at www.arl.psu.edu. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Line-Asst-Professor-of-RPTM_REQ_0000083191-1": {"title": "Tenure-Line Asst. Professor of RPTM", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA Department of Recreation, Park, and Tourism Management Tenure-line Assistant Professor: Visitor Use Management, Outdoor Recreation Management, and/or Nature and Health The Department of Recreation, Park, and Tourism Management (RPTM) at Penn State is seeking to hire a\u00a0faculty member who can contribute to our engaged, productive, and collegial group whose mission is to transform human health and wellbeing through research, teaching and outreach associated with engaging people with recreation, park, and tourism activities ( http://www.hhd.psu.edu/rptm ). Specifically, we are seeking to hire a tenure-line faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in Fall 2027 whose research focuses broadly on outdoor recreation management (public lands policy and governance, outdoor recreation economy, environmental justice and access to\u00a0nature, climate adaptation),\u00a0visitor\u00a0use management (carrying capacity,\u00a0visitor\u00a0monitoring technologies, recreation ecology), and/or the intersection between people,\u00a0nature, and health (nature-based health interventions, restorative environments, environmental psychology). Candidates must have an active line of programmatic research and be prepared to supervise and fund graduate (M.S./Ph.D.) student research. We are particularly interested in researchers whose work is fit for inter- or transdisciplinary collaborations, and researchers who are engaging in cutting-edge research-methods, whether that is innovative quantitative, qualitative, or mixed-method approaches, or emerging computational methods (e.g., machine learning applications, wearable sensors and physiological monitoring, environmental sensors and GPS tracking, agent-based modeling, scenario modeling).\u00a0We are also interested in candidates who can make meaningful contributions and linkages to cross-campus entities (e.g., Institutes for Energies and Environment , Ecology Institute , Social Science Research Institute , Institute of Computational or Data Sciences , Shaver\u2019s Creek Environmental Education Center , Center for Social Data Analytics and associated SODA dual-title doctoral program , and/or the dual-degree graduate program in Transdisciplinary Research on Environment and Society (TREES). Additionally, w e are eager to consider candidates who would be able to engage community organizations and agencies involved in land management, outdoor recreation management, or engagement with individuals in the outdoors. As a department of approximately 350 undergraduate students at the University Park campus and in our World Campus online program, we also value effective teaching and student engagement inside and outside the classroom. We seek candidates who are willing and able to teach into the RPTM undergraduate core as well as specifically within the Outdoor Recreation Management option area or the Sustainability Leadership Minor, as well as the graduate program.\u00a0Candidates should have a c ommitment to engaged and inclusive learning practices in the context of in-person and/or online (synchronous and asynchronous) classrooms. Finally, we seek candidates that recognize the importance of service commitments to the RPTM department, the College of Health and Human Development, the University, and to their profession. About the College The College of Health and Human Development offers a robust program of eight interdisciplinary programs, including RPTM, that share one common goal: enriching the lives of others. We continually examine contemporary issues facing people in today\u2019s changing times, and we develop cutting-edge solutions for addressing them. Our impact extends from our classrooms, across communities and industries, and around the globe. About Penn State University The Pennsylvania State University is a land-grant institution and one of the top 30 research universities in the United States, ranking among the top 15 public institutions. The University Park Campus is located in State College, a vibrant university town in central Pennsylvania, offering excellent schools and outstanding recreational and cultural activities. The campus is within a 3-4 hour drive to major metropolitan areas, including Washington, DC, Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City, and Pittsburgh. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. Our campuses are located on the original homelands of the Erie, Haudenosaunee (Seneca, Cayuga, Onondaga, Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and Wahzhazhe (Osage) Nations. As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and honor the traditional caretakers of these lands and strive to understand and model their responsible stewardship. We also acknowledge the longer history of these lands and our place in that history. Benefits Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. For more detailed information, please visit our Benefits Page. Application Instructions To apply, please upload a resume/curriculum vitae, a cover letter outlining your interest in the position, and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin on November 01, 2026 will continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Questions related to the position can be addressed to Dr. Carter Hunt at cah59@psu.edu . BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES: Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Hire---Redwing-Group---Department-of-Materials-Science-and-Engineering_REQ_0000083293-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Hire - Redwing Group - Department of Materials Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences at Penn State seeks postdoctoral scholar applicants at the University Park campus. Several positions are available that focus on metalorganic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) of two-dimensional transition metal dichalcogenides (TMDs) and related materials. Scholars will use synthesis and characterization capabilities in the 2D Crystal Consortium facility and engage with related activities focused on developing AI tools and workflows to accelerate thin-film materials research. Example research opportunities include developing MOCVD growth, characterization, and doping processes for TMDs in support of p-type device development; investigating new precursor chemistries for TMD growth employing in situ spectroscopic ellipsometry to monitor growth and accelerate process development and related topics. The specific research focus will be shaped by the scholar\u2019s expertise and the needs of the program. Postdoctoral scholars will plan and conduct experiments, analyze relationships among growth conditions, material structure, and properties, and communicate results through publications, group meetings and conference presentations. Working with collaborators, they will help develop data-rich experimental workflows that connect MOCVD synthesis and in situ measurements with AI-assisted planning, analysis, and feedback. The work offers opportunities to collaborate with interdisciplinary teams including researchers focused on materials characterization, computational modeling, device fabrication and machine learning and intelligent system design. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in materials science and engineering, electrical engineering, chemical engineering, chemistry, physics, or a related field. Preferred requirements: Hands-on experience in electronic materials synthesis, characterization and/or device fabrication. Strong experimental, analytical, and communication skills are required. Experience with MOCVD or related vapor-phase deposition, TMDs, materials characterization, or data-driven experimentation is desirable. Applicants need not have experience in every area described above. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000083295-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Dr. Feifei Shi is looking to hire a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar with expertise in electrochemistry and battery technologies to join her research team. The successful candidate will work on cutting-edge projects related to advanced battery systems, electrochemical energy storage, materials development, or interface characterization. \u00a0 Key Responsibilities: \u00b7 Design and conduct experiments in electrochemical energy storage systems (e.g., Li-ion, Li metal batteries, beyond Li-ion batteries) and critical element extraction . \u00b7 Develop and characterize novel electrode materials, electrolytes, or battery architectures. \u00b7 Utilize advanced electrochemical techniques (e.g., CV, EIS, GITT, PITT) and materials characterization tools (XRD, SEM, TEM, XPS, etc.). \u00b7 Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams and industry partners. \u00b7 Publish high-impact research in peer-reviewed journals and present findings at conferences. \u00a0 Qualifications: \u00b7 Ph.D . in Chemistry, Materials Science, Chemical Engineering, or a related field by start date. \u00b7 Strong background in electrochemistry, metallurgy, battery materials, or energy storage technologies . \u00b7 Hands-on experience with battery assembly/testing (coin cells, pouch cells), electrochemical methods, and materials characterization . \u00b7 Proficiency in data analysis and scientific writing (evidenced by publication record). \u00b7 Creative problem-solving skills and ability to work independently. \u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants should submit (1) a current curriculum vitae, (2) a detailed statement of research interests and experiences relevant to the required qualifications, and (3) a list of three professional references. The review of applications will start immediately and continue until the position is filled. This position is funded for one year from the date of hire, with the possibility of renewal based on funding availability and satisfactory performance. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor--Nuclear-Engineering_REQ_0000083012-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor, Nuclear Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pan Research Group at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a highly motivated Assistant Research Professor to join a leading research group in cutting-edge research in electrochemical devices. This position focuses on the development of nanotechnology for biosensing applications and nanobiotechnology research. \u00a0 Led by Prof. Dipanjan Pan, Pan Research Group at Penn State, University Park fosters research excellence, education, and industry collaboration in nanomedicine. The laboratories are located at the world-renowned Huck Institute of Life Sciences and Millennium Sciences Complex within the flagship University Park campus that promotes an inclusive and multidisciplinary environment in life sciences research. The selected candidate will work within a fast-paced multidisciplinary research environment and contribute to the design, fabrication, and optimization of electrochemical devices, and drug delivery applications. Qualifications: A Ph.D. or D.Sc. degree in Chemistry, Materials Science, Chemical Biology, or related fields. A proven track record (ideally multiple first author publications in internationally reputed journals) in one or more of the following technical areas: Electrochemical sensors and devices and deep understanding of electrochemical measurements. Extensive expertise in in vitro and in vivo characterization of nanomaterials. We are looking for highly self-motivated candidates who: Can work independently while collaborating in a multidisciplinary research team comprised of chemists, materials scientists, biologists, engineers and medical students. Can work without daily instructions or supervision and proactively make progress. Demonstrate creativity and adaptability in solving research challenges. Are highly organized, goal-oriented, and can operate within a fast-paced environment collaborating with industry partners. Have experience with novel 2D materials other emerging nanomaterials platform (preferred). Have English proficiency and experience in independently drafting manuscripts. Have strong experimental, analytical, and troubleshooting/problem-solving skills. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Head-of-Library-Experience-and-Services_REQ_0000082710-1": {"title": "Head of Library Experience and Services", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Head of Library Experience and Services\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Responsibilities\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 The Penn State University Libraries seeks a collaborative and engaged Head of Library Experience and Services at Associate or Full Rank to advance a culture of service quality, collaboration, and student success at Penn State University Libraries.\u00a0 This position will lead a newly aligned portfolio and provide strategic leadership and operational responsibility for most of the public service points across University Park Libraries spaces, including service points at Pattee & Paterno Libraries and multiple branch library locations. This newly established portfolio consolidates previously distributed service functions under unified leadership to ensure consistent, high-quality, values-driven service experiences for students, faculty, staff, and community guests across all Libraries facilities.\u00a0 \u00a0 The Head of Library Experience and Services serves as an academic administrator responsible for setting departmental vision and standards and manages and mentors service point supervisors and employees. Additionally, the Head of Library Experience and Services closely collaborates with University Libraries colleagues, stakeholders, and partners to cooperatively develop and advance the Libraries' strategic priorities and values, including equitable access, inclusion, user-centered design, and continuous improvement, through the daily experience students and other patrons have at our service points. The Head of Library Experience and Services will collaborate closely with library partners and units that manage complementary programs and services within Libraries spaces on the University Park campus, managing these relationships and connecting our partners\u2019 programmatic goals with the Libraries\u2019 programmatic goals.\u00a0 \u00a0 This position reports to the Associate Dean for Learning and Engagement and is a member of the Learning and Engagement Leadership Team and the University Libraries\u2019 Leadership Council. This position is located at the University Park campus in State College, PA and the University expects regular onsite presence to fully participate in their university workspace or on-campus intellectual and educational community.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The successful candidate will be responsible for the following\u00a0\u00a0 Set strategic direction for the Library Experience and Services portfolio, establishing its vision, structure, and operational expectations, and leading change management efforts to unify distinct service cultures into a cohesive, values-aligned department;\u00a0\u00a0 Supervise and develop employees, directly managing service point managers, supervisors, and coordinators while fostering accountability, collaboration, and professional growth;\u00a0\u00a0 Oversee service operations, including scheduling, staffing models, cross-training, and coverage planning, to ensure consistent, flexible, and resilient service delivery, including foundational reference services, across all University Park library service points and spaces;\u00a0\u00a0 Drive evidence-based improvement by developing and applying assessment tools, user feedback, and service data to evaluate quality, identify opportunities, and demonstrate impact, championing a user-centered, inclusive approach throughout;\u00a0 Coordinate with campus and library stakeholders, serving as the primary contact for campus units operating within library spaces and collaborating on building operations, renovations, and service integration;\u00a0\u00a0 Manage budget and resources, directing departmental budget, staffing, and resource planning;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Ensure compliance and safety, collaborating on adherence to University policies for safety, security, accessibility, and emergency response in library spaces;\u00a0\u00a0 Represent the Libraries in governance, serving on internal committees, task forces, and working groups, as well as representing the Libraries on external committees and consortia.\u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications\u00a0\u00a0 A Master of Library Science degree from an ALA-accredited institution (or equivalent);\u00a0 Substantial relevant experience with academic library public services including reference services, service integration, space partnerships, accessibility, operational planning, and organizational change;\u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated supervisory and empathetic leadership and communication skills;\u00a0 Commitment to and experience with shared governance and faculty partnership;\u00a0\u00a0 Demonstrated leadership style that promotes accountability, communication and employee engagement and demonstrated supervisory experience, including hiring, performance management, coaching, employee development and facilitating teams to foster a collaborative and supportive work environment;\u00a0\u00a0 Commitment to and demonstrated leadership experience fostering collaboration across diverse communities and supporting the success of individuals with varied backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences through practices that promote accessibility, fairness, engagement, and equal opportunity;\u00a0\u00a0 Strong reputation for distinguished scholarship and professional accomplishments and strong record of service in appropriate professional or disciplinary associations as evidence of ability to meet the requirements of a tenured position at the rank of Associate Librarian or Librarian at the University Libraries, https://libraries.psu.edu/policies/ul-acg07 ;\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred\u00a0\u00a0 Evidence of substantive leadership initiatives that promote equal access to library resources and services, enhance accessibility, deliver exceptional customer service, and foster a welcoming environment where all users and employees are treated fairly and can fully participate, contribute, and succeed based on their needs, qualifications, and engagement;\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with fiscal/budget management;\u00a0 Experience with leading and assessing library programs;\u00a0\u00a0 Experience with strategic planning and demonstrated ability to implement a strategic vision and lead collaborative efforts across library units and with external partners.\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Application Process\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Interested candidates are expected to upload prompt submission and a resume or CV. Application materials should demonstrate the candidate\u2019s professional qualifications, experience, and contributions to librarianship, teaching, research, and/or service. Application materials should reflect a commitment to equal opportunity and respect for all individuals. Candidates are encouraged to highlight how their work promotes inclusive access to information and supports the academic mission of the institution.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 In addition, candidates are required to provide a response to several prompts in lieu of a cover letter. Responses to the prompts (350 word-limit each) are to be uploaded with candidate materials when applying. \u00a0\u00a0 Prompts to be addressed are:\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Share why you are interested in serving in the position of Head of Library Experience and Services at this time.\u00a0\u00a0 Describe a specific initiative in which you led significant organizational change. What was your role, what strategies did you use to engage stakeholders and colleagues, and what was the ultimate impact of the change?\u00a0\u00a0 The Head of Library Experience and Services will manage a team of high-level supervisors. Please describe your approach to building an effective, supportive, and inclusive team culture. In your response, share a specific example from your experience to illustrate how you have established trust and role clarity, supported professional growth, or navigated challenges or disagreements within a team.\u00a0\u00a0 Describe a collaborative initiative involving faculty, librarians, instructional designers, administrators, or students that supported student success or employee success. How did you build partnerships and navigate challenges?\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 References will be contacted later in the search process. While 4 furnished references are to be provided at the candidate\u2019s discretion, references must include a current/previous direct supervisor, a colleague, an employee who was/is a direct report, and one at the candidate's discretion. Candidates must clearly identify the relationship for each reference provided. All references must be submitted at the time of application submission. References will be contacted later in the search process.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Candidates currently assigned to campuses undergoing closure may be eligible for a transition plan, subject to the operational needs of the position and their current campus assignment. Any transition arrangements will be determined at the discretion of Libraries\u2019 leadership.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 All application materials should demonstrate the candidate's impact in advancing access, accessibility, user-centered service, community engagement, and equal opportunity through their librarianship, teaching, research, and/or service.\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Academic Rank \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Candidates for the rank of Associate Librarian should demonstrate excellence in librarianship, show evidence of an established reputation in research, and have a strong record of service to the University and the profession. Candidates for the rank of Librarian should demonstrate sustained excellence in librarianship, give evidence of creativity in his/her field of specialization (including a continuing capacity for significant contributions in research and creative accomplishments), and show evidence of leadership in the profession. More information can be found in the Guideline for Promotion and Tenure Criteria https://libraries.psu.edu/policies/ul-acg07 .\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Department-Head--Autonomy-and-Emerging-Technology--FACULTY-_REQ_0000083071-1": {"title": "Department Head, Autonomy and Emerging Technology (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Your working location will be fully on-site located in State College, PA. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. The Systems and Emerging Capabilities Division in the Undersea Systems Office (USO) at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) is seeking a Department Head for Autonomy and Emerging Technology (AET). This department is an innovation hub for our Systems Engineering Division.\u00a0The AET Department\u2019s primary mission is to develop, test, and evaluate emerging capabilities in the Subsea and Seabed (SSW) mission area.\u00a0It's secondary mission is to rapidly evaluate and field test new and emerging capabilities applicable to SSW \u2013 including testing of systems, payloads, and software. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. Research areas include, but not limited to: Autonomy for Unmanned Vehicles (UxVs), including autonomy architectures, behaviors, mission planning, and autonomy standards that improve reliability, endurance, and mission effectiveness in challenging maritime environments.\u00a0 Payloads/payload delivery of effects Sensor/sensor integration Navigation ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Technical Leadership - Lead innovation in SSW mission area to include autonomy for UxVs, including adaptive mission behaviors, environmental awareness, distributed autonomy, multi-vehicle coordination, and integration of autonomy with UxV sensors and payloads. Drive advancements in UxV simulation, field testing, and fleet-relevant autonomy capabilities Programmatic Leadership - Oversee SSW-focused UxV programs and multidisciplinary teams working across undersea navigation, endurance optimization, acoustic communications, environmental modeling, and autonomy-enabled CONOPS. Collaborate closely with ARL\u2019s SSW Portfolio Manager and sponsors to shape new SSW research directions Resource Management - Align personnel and technical resources\u2014including UxV test assets, autonomy laboratories, software infrastructure, and field test facilities\u2014with program needs and strategic priorities Personnel Management - Mentor engineers and researchers specializing in UxV autonomy, control systems, undersea sensing, navigation, and environmental modeling. Foster growth in mission-focused undersea autonomy competencies Department Management - Ensure effective planning and execution of programs involving system integration, sea testing, autonomy software development, mission simulation and evaluation, and cross-domain unmanned systems collaboration Collaboration - Work across ARL departments to integrate autonomy with undersea vehicles, sensors, communications, and emerging technologies. Partner with oceanography, acoustics, guidance & control, and materials experts to develop next-generation UxV capabilities New Business \u2013 Must be entrepreneurial in nature.\u00a0 You will need to work with the SSW Portfolio manager to create and shape new UxV autonomy research opportunities. Help develop seedling efforts in areas such areas as: long-duration UxV autonomy, autonomous behaviors for complex missions, resilient undersea communications autonomy, and cross-domain unmanned vehicle coordination Customer Interaction \u2013 Engage directly with Navy sponsors, DoD collaborators, and other stakeholders to present UxV autonomy advancements, field-test results, and new capability concepts. Represent ARL at autonomy and undersea systems conferences and technical reviews Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/Experience areas include: Past success managing technical teams and programs Strong decision-making skills in complex technical and operational environments. Autonomy for unmanned systems including: autonomy architectures, behavior frameworks and mission planning for undersea missions, undersea navigation and perception autonomy behaviors, autonomy standards for UxVs (e.g., MOSA, A-GRA, UMAA, PCX), UXV simulation, evaluation, and verification environments DEVSECOPS approaches used for government autonomy and control software Test and evaluation of maritime platforms Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Top Secret level or higher and may be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility, if required Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: UxV systems, including platforms, mission payloads, launch and recovery, acoustic comms, and energy management Oceanography, seabed features, and environmental data used for UxV autonomy Past success supporting Navy missions, operational training, or UxV fleet experimentation Development or use of UxV simulation frameworks (e.g., high-fidelity hydrodynamic or environmental modeling) Principal Investigator or business development experience in UxV or autonomy programs AI/ML methods applied to UxV navigation, perception, environmental characterization, mission planning, or anomaly detection Past success managing technical personnel in undersea systems or autonomy fields\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Intel Community (IC), and other federal government customers. FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our website at\u00a0 www.arl.psu.edu . \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/College-of-IST-Part-time-Academic---ETI-300W_REQ_0000083190": {"title": "College of IST Part-time Academic - ETI 300W", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) invites applications for a part-time academic job to teach in-person at University Park, for the academic term of Spring 2027. \u00a0 Job duties to include teaching ETI 300W: Development and Documentation of Enterprise Web (Cloud Design) \u00a0 (full course description from the undergraduate bulletin ) \u00a0 Applicants must possess a master's degree or equivalent experience and education and be committed to teaching learners at all levels and from all backgrounds; preference given for prior teaching experience and professional experience in a relevant area.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/College-of-IST-Part-time-Academic---SRA-497-Special-Topic--Public-Private-Cybersecurity-Integration_REQ_0000083252": {"title": "College of IST Part-time Academic - SRA 497 Special Topic: Public-Private Cybersecurity Integration", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) invites applications for a part-time academic job to teach in-person at University Park campus, for the academic term of Spring 2027. \u00a0 Job duties to include co-teaching SRA 497 Special Topic: Public-Private Cybersecurity Integration \u00a0 This course examines how cybersecurity is organized and executed across federal civilian government, the military and defense enterprise, national security organizations, and private technology firms. Students will study mission-driven cyber requirements, governance structures, incident response, supply-chain security, and the benefits and tensions of cross-sector cooperation. \u00a0 Applicants must possess a master's degree or equivalent experience and education and be committed to teaching learners at all levels and from all backgrounds; preference given for prior teaching experience and professional experience in a relevant area.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor--Associate-Professor--or-Full-Professor-of-Accounting_REQ_0000083074-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor of Accounting", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Accounting of The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) seeks to fill one or more tenured faculty positions in accounting at the rank of Assistant Professor , Associate Professor , or Full Professor beginning in Fall 2027. Candidates must contribute to the mission of the Smeal College of Business and the Department of Accounting in the areas of research, teaching, and service. \u00a0 JOB QUALIFICATIONS: Those in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointment as an Assistant Professor. To be considered for an Associate Professor appointment, the successful candidate should possess the same qualifications as the Assistant Professor, but must also provide evidence of an established reputation in scholarly or professional achievement. To be considered for Full Professor rank, the candidate should possess the same qualifications as the Associate Professor, but must also provide evidence of a substantial record of advanced research and of leadership in their field of specialization. All successful candidates are expected to hold a Ph.D. in Accounting or a related field by the start of their appointment, possess a publication record commensurate with their rank, pursue an active research program, and demonstrate teaching competence in accounting analytics, auditing, financial accounting, managerial accounting, or taxation. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. \u00a0 APPLICATION PROCEDURE Candidates should apply directly online on the PSU site and submit the following documents as PDF files: vita copies of representative working papers teaching evaluations (when applicable) names of references or letters of reference; the letters themselves will need to be emailed to accounting@smeal.psu.edu \u00a0 Priority will be given to completed applications received by November 10 . However, reviews will continue until the position is filled or the search is closed. \u00a0 ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT Information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at www.smeal.psu.edu/accounting . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Applied-AI-Systems-Tenure-line-Faculty_REQ_0000083026-1": {"title": "Applied AI Systems Tenure-line Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Applied AI Systems Tenure-line Faculty Positions\u00a0 \u00a0 The Department of Human-Centered Computing and Social Informatics in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for multiple tenure-line faculty positions in applied AI systems, located in State College, Pennsylvania. The appointments are at the assistant or associate professor rank and begin in August 2027 at the University Park campus. Remote appointments are not permitted for these hires.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 We seek outstanding scholars in one of the following two areas. Applicants are invited to address the area that fits their work; there is no expectation that a candidate speaks to both.\u00a0 Physical AI: We seek scholars who design, build, and/or deploy physical AI systems, particularly edge AI and cyber-physical systems, which can sense, reason, and act in the physical world. Such systems take many forms, including embedded and autonomous systems, robotics, wearables and health-sensing devices, instrumented environments, and the Internet of Things. Examples of relevant expertise include embedded and on-device machine learning, resource-constrained and real-time computation, sensing and actuation, hardware-software co-design, and/or edge-cloud system architecture, demonstrated through working systems that are prototyped, deployed, and/or evaluated in real environments. We are interested in candidates whose systems reach domains such as healthcare, smart homes and buildings, manufacturing, transportation, and public services, and who treat usability and/or sustainability as engineering requirements. Successful candidates will be prepared to build hands-on, project-based curricula in collaboration with industry partners.\u00a0 Enterprise AI: We seek scholars who study and teach how AI is engineered, integrated, deployed, governed, and/or continuously improved in real organizational contexts. Examples of relevant expertise include generative AI and agentic systems in the enterprise; human-AI collaboration and the redesign of work; AI governance, assurance, and risk; and/or the integration of AI into core business functions such as accounting, finance, human resources, management, marketing, operations, and supply chain. We welcome candidates working at the intersection of information systems and applied AI, including those whose scholarship engages enterprise systems, business processes, digital transformation, and organizational computing. We are especially interested in candidates who build and evaluate AI-enabled systems in partnership with organizations, and who are prepared to develop project-based curricula that prepare students to deploy and govern AI at scale.\u00a0 We particularly welcome applicants whose research demonstrates interdisciplinary collaboration and addresses significant societal, governmental, or industrial challenges.\u00a0 Candidates will demonstrate a record of research accomplishment or strong research potential in the area to which they apply, an ability to publish in high-quality peer-reviewed venues, a record of teaching or strong teaching potential in relevant subjects, and technical competence in contemporary AI technologies and their application.\u00a0\u00a0 Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses; conduct cutting-edge interdisciplinary research; supervise and mentor graduate students; actively pursue external funding to support research activities; engage in service activities at the college and university levels; and collaborate with faculty across the university and with industry partners.\u00a0\u00a0 Candidates will possess a PhD in information sciences, informatics, information systems, computer science, artificial intelligence, human-computer interaction, computer engineering, electrical engineering, business analytics, or a related field before their appointment start date at Penn State. Applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will demonstrate strong potential for developing a collaborative, interdisciplinary research project that is competitive for external funding and potential to contribute to the college\u2019s teaching mission. Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have a strong record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service.\u00a0 Applicants will attach documentation during their application process and should include a cover letter with information about their interests and qualifications for the position, indicating which of the two areas they are applying to. They will also include their i) research statement covering accomplishments and plans (2-3 pages), ii) teaching statement (1-2 pages), iii) curriculum vitae, and iv) contact information for at least three professional references. Candidates may combine these materials into one document prior to uploading, or they may upload separate files.\u00a0 Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu . Review of applications begins on November 1, 2026, and will continue until positions are filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Post-Doctoral-Scholar--Avian-Medicine-and-Pathology-Residency-_REQ_0000083103-1": {"title": "Post-Doctoral Scholar (Avian Medicine and Pathology Residency)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Animal Diagnostic Laboratory in the Department of Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences at The Pennsylvania State University in University Park, PA invites applications for an Avian Medicine and Pathology Residency (Post-Doctoral Scholar) training position.\u00a0 This is a full-time 48-week position annually renewable for up to 2 years and is intended for specialty training to qualify the resident to take the American College of Poultry Veterinarians (ACPV) board examination.\u00a0 The resident will be supervised by full-time faculty members based in an academic diagnostic laboratory setting.\u00a0 Two avian pathologists are on faculty to provide instruction with an emphasis on gross and microscopic avian pathology, including necropsies on animals submitted through the diagnostic service. \u00a0Additional experience may be obtained in other sections of the diagnostic lab including bacteriology, virology, serology, and molecular diagnostics.\u00a0 \u00a0 Duties will include performing gross and histopathologic examinations on avian necropsy cases, writing necropsy reports, consulting with submitting veterinarians and clients, participating in weekly rounds, assisting with undergraduate and veterinary extern instruction, and assisting with collaborative academic research.\u00a0 Other duties include participating in field investigation visits to flocks, hatcheries, and processing plants with poultry veterinarians, poultry extension faculty in the College of Agricultural Sciences, and private practice/industry poultry veterinarians.\u00a0 The candidate is expected to present case reports or applied research findings at scientific meetings and submit clinical or research paper(s) to peer-reviewed journals.\u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants must hold a Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM)/ Veterinariae Medicinae Doctoris (VMD) or equivalent degree from an American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA)-accredited college/university (or have successfully passed the Educational Commission for Foreign Veterinary Graduates [ECFVG] examination) and must have a current license to practice veterinary medicine in 1 or more US state(s).\u00a0 The start date for the residency will be July 1, 2027 .\u00a0 Applications should be submitted to https://hr.psu.edu/careers and include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, veterinary medical school transcript, and the names and contact information for at least three professional references familiar with the candidate (at least one reference should be a member of American Association of Avian Pathologists [AAAP] and/or an American College of Poultry Veterinarians [ACPV] diplomate).\u00a0 Review of applications will begin December 11, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is identified.\u00a0For additional information, contact Dr. Megan Lighty at (814) 863-0837 or mul132@psu.edu.\u00a0 The Animal Diagnostic Laboratory is a member of the Pennsylvania Animal Diagnostic Laboratory System and is a full service, American Association of Veterinary Laboratory Diagnosticians (AAVLD) accredited, National Animal Health Laboratory Network (NAHLN) laboratory with histopathology, necropsy, virology, serology, microbiology, parasitology, and molecular biology sections. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor--Penn-State-Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000082681-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor- Penn State Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The College of Engineering and the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences at the Pennsylvania State University are seeking a qualified and motivated individual to fill an Assistant Research Professor position to lead in vivo studies in dual-switch selection gene drives. This position will play a key role in advancing the in vivo delivery, efficacy, and safety of candidate dual-switch selection drives. Requirements and Qualifications: Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or a related field by the time of appointment and strong hands-on expertise in in vivo mouse handling and tumor models. Candidates with additional expertise in one or more of the following are especially encouraged to apply: cell and gene therapy, synthetic biology, tyrosine kinase-driven drug resistance, in vivo imaging, and agent-based modeling. The successful applicant needs excellent interpersonal and communication skills and must be able to work across multiple labs, including the Hemann Lab at MIT. Interested applicants should apply online and submit a single PDF file including: (1) a cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, and (3) names and addresses of three references. Review of applications will start immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Additional Information: The position will be in the Biomedical Engineering (BME) Department and affiliated with the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences. The Penn State BME Department and Huck Institutes provide a rich environment in which faculty, postdocs, and graduate and undergraduate students regularly interact and conduct collaborative studies, with access to state-of-the-art core facilities. Assistant Research Professors will have the opportunity to write their own grants and develop independent research directions from the security of an established, R01-funded program. Direct questions regarding the position to Justin Pritch, jrp94@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Immunology--Microbiology----Toxicology--Grembi-Lab_REQ_0000080624-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar- Immunology, Microbiology, & Toxicology, Grembi Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Grembi Lab at Penn State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar with expertise in immunology, microbiology, toxicology, or a related field to join our team studying the ecology of the human small intestine. Our work focuses on environmental enteropathy, a subclinical condition characterized by intestinal inflammation and increased permeability that is thought to contribute to childhood undernutrition and stunting. We use an interdisciplinary approach combining microbiology, immunology, biochemistry, computational biology, and epidemiology to understand how microbial communities in the small intestine develop, interact with the host, and respond to environmental conditions, with an increasing focus on environmental contaminants. Our team is based at Penn State's main campus in State College, Pennsylvania (a.k.a. Happy Valley), a welcoming college town with a remarkably low cost of living and easy access to outdoor recreation. Penn State's position as a leading R1 research university means you'll also have access to cutting-edge technology, a vibrant research community within the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences and the One Health Microbiome Center, and numerous opportunities for local and global collaborations. Responsibilities The Postdoctoral Scholar will: Independently initiate, execute, and complete interdisciplinary research involving immunology, toxicology, molecular biology, and biochemistry Communicate research findings via presentations at conferences and peer-reviewed manuscripts Contribute to grant proposals and fellowship applications, gaining experience in research funding and scientific writing Mentor and train graduate and undergraduate students Qualifications Applicants should have a PhD in Immunology, Microbiology, Biology, Toxicology, Biochemistry, or a related field, along with excellent oral and written communication skills and at least one first-author publication. Strong candidates will have experience in at least two of the following areas: multiparameter flow cytometry; single-cell, RNA sequencing, or shotgun metagenomics data generation and analysis; intestinal organoids, primary human cells, or animal models of gut inflammation. Candidates should be highly motivated and creative, with a genuine interest in global health. What We Offer We are committed to building an inclusive and equitable lab environment and strongly encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds. You will benefit from close mentorship from the PI and significant autonomy over your project. This position offers an excellent platform to develop skills in data science and statistics, with flexibility to tailor your training to align with your professional goals. Position Details Start date is flexible between September 2026 and January 2027. This is a limited-term position funded for one year with the potential to extend based on performance and funding. Applicants are required to have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in an appropriate field and be able to provide evidence that all requirements have been met for completion of the Ph.D. prior to the effective date of hire. Application Process Interested candidates should submit an online application at Penn State's Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically:\u202f \u202f \u00a0 CV a recent manuscript they were a primary author on (preprints are fine) a brief statement of their research interests and how they envision pursuing those on the Grembi lab contact information for 2-3 professional references \u00a0 System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Teaching-Professor-of-German_REQ_0000082706-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor of German", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Germanic and Slavic Languages and Literatures at Penn State (University Park) invites applications for a full-time Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor\u00a0position in German (non-tenure-track), to begin in August 2027, with flexibility. Responsibilities include coordinating our residential basic German language program and supervising graduate teaching assistants who teach in the basic language program, as well as teaching introductory, intermediate and advanced German language classes, and any combination of literature and culture (including visual culture), business German, or linguistics courses based on expertise. Teaching load is three courses per semester, with reductions for coordination duties. Applicants must have native or near-native fluency in English and German and have completed a Ph.D. in German or in a related field by the appointment date. Demonstrated excellence in teaching German is required, as well as knowledge of current approaches and theories of foreign-language pedagogy. Rank will be determined based on education and experience. Please submit, electronically, a cover letter, curriculum vitae and the names/contact information of three references. A summary of recent teaching evaluations and teaching philosophy (2 pages maximum) will be requested for candidates invited for an interview. For more information on our program, please consult https://german.la.psu.edu/ . Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Carrie Jackson ( cnj1@psu.edu ). The College of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.\u00a0Information on faculty ranks and progression can be found at https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21 . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Cybersecurity-and-Privacy-Tenure-line-Faculty-Position_REQ_0000081189-1": {"title": "Cybersecurity and Privacy Tenure-line Faculty Position", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Cybersecurity and Privacy Tenure-line Faculty Position The Department of Privacy and Cybersecurity in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for two tenure-line faculty positions in Cybersecurity and Privacy located in State College, Pennsylvania. The appointments are at the assistant or associate professor rank and begin in January of 2027 at the University Park campus. We seek outstanding scholars with expertise in one or more of the following areas:\u00a0the intersection of\u00a0artificial intelligence (AI), security, and privacy; organizational, behavioral, and/or human factors in cybersecurity and privacy; digital forensics and/or cyber investigations; systems and software security; cryptography; quantum computing and post-quantum security; or other emerging areas in cybersecurity, privacy, and/or trustworthy computing. We particularly welcome applicants whose research demonstrates interdisciplinary collaboration and addresses significant societal, governmental, or industrial challenges. Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in residential, online, and/or hybrid modes; conduct cutting-edge interdisciplinary research; supervise and mentor graduate students; actively pursue external funding to support research activities; engage in service activities at the college and university levels; and collaborate with faculty across the university and with industry partners. Candidates will possess a PhD in information science, computer science, cybersecurity, or a related field before their appointment start date at Penn State. Applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will demonstrate strong potential for developing a collaborative, interdisciplinary research project that is competitive for external funding and potential to contribute to the college\u2019s teaching mission. Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have the same as Assistant Professor and a strong record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service. Applicants will attach documentation during their application process and should include a cover letter with information about their interests and qualifications for the position. They will also include a description of their i) research accomplishments and plans (2-3 pages), and ii) approach to teaching (1-2 pages). They provide the iii) applicant\u2019s curriculum vitae and iv) contact information for at least three professional references. Applicants may combine their descriptions into one cover letter and combine all file(s)\u00a0into one document prior to uploading, or they may upload separate files. Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu . Review of applications begins on September 15, 2026, and will continue until positions are filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000082790-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Ultrasound in Imaging and Therapy (UIT) Lab, led by Dr. Mohamed Almekkawy, in the School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, is seeking a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar in Ultrasound Imaging. The successful candidate will contribute to a recently funded five-year multidisciplinary research project focused on developing advanced ultrasound technologies for quantitative brain imaging and tissue characterization. The project centers on the development of a dedicated ultrasound platform that integrates hardware and system development with data acquisition, signal processing, computational imaging, and image reconstruction. The research involves close collaboration with investigators and clinicians at Penn State College of Medicine and Penn State Health Milton S. Hershey Medical Center, providing opportunities for both engineering development and translational imaging studies. As a Postdoctoral Scholar, you will play a central role in the design, development, integration, and validation of the ultrasound platform. The work will involve ultrasound system and hardware development, including PCB design, FPGA-based components, transmit/receive electronics, system synchronization, and high-speed data acquisition. You will also develop signal-processing and image-reconstruction methods for quantitative tissue-property estimation. Additional responsibilities will include processing raw RF/channel data, developing research software, and investigating computational imaging and inverse-problem approaches. Experimental work will include system characterization and validation using tissue-mimicking phantoms, ex vivo specimens, and clinical imaging studies involving human participants under approved research protocols. The Postdoctoral Scholar will work closely with engineering researchers, clinicians, and other members of the multidisciplinary project team in the design, execution, and evaluation of these studies. Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science, Medical Physics, or a closely related field by the appointment start date. Candidates who are in the final stages of their Ph.D. and expect to defend their dissertation soon are also encouraged to apply, provided that the Ph.D. is completed before the postdoctoral appointment begins. Preferred qualifications include experience in biomedical ultrasound, particularly in computational or quantitative ultrasound. Experience with ultrasound computed tomography and deep learning for medical imaging is desirable. Candidates should demonstrate strong problem-solving, scientific programming, scientific writing, communication, and teamwork skills. The successful candidate will join the interdisciplinary research environment of the Almekkawy Lab and will have opportunities for professional development and scholarly output through peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, collaborative research activities, and the development of emerging ultrasound imaging technologies. Compensation and benefits will be provided in accordance with Penn State University\u2019s guidelines for postdoctoral appointments. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, a cover letter describing how their prior experience and future research interests align with the advertised position, two to three representative peer-reviewed journal publications, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor---Electrical-Engineering_REQ_0000082629-1": {"title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor - Electrical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Electrical Engineering (EE) in the School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA invites applications for a faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor . Applicants should have qualifications commensurate with the level of Assistant Professor, including a demonstrated excellent track record in scholarship and education, recognition from the research community, and the promise of continued distinction. Exceptional candidates are sought for this position covering a broad range of research in the areas of microwave and millimeter wave devices, microwave/mmWave integrated circuit design, and systems. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain an outstanding research program and to be effective, inspiring teachers at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will be co-funded by the Materials Research Institute (MRI) at Penn State, which coordinates interdisciplinary research across the university. The successful candidate will have opportunities to interact with and benefit from new devices and systems packaging, with institutional strengths in materials under programs such as the National Science Foundation Materials Innovation Platform 2D Crystal Consortium ( https://www.mri.psu.edu/mip )and a Department of Energy Frontier Research Center focused on three-dimensional integration of ferroelectric materials ( https://3dfem.psu.edu ), among many other opportunities. The EE Department has 38 tenured/tenure-track faculty members, with average annual research expenditures of $15 million. The undergraduate (juniors and seniors) and graduate programs enroll over 500 and 250 students, respectively. The department is also home to the Center for Heterogeneous Integration of Micro Electronic Systems (CHIMES), a JUMP 2.0 center supported by the Semiconductor Research Corporation (SRC) and DARPA ( www.chimes.psu.edu ).\u00a0Information about the Department and School can be found at http://www.eecs.psu.edu . The Materials Research Institute supports a university-wide community of approximately 270 affiliated faculty spanning 30 departments. MRI operates three shared user facilities, the Materials Characterization Lab, a 15,000 sq.ft. Nanofabrication Laboratory including newly expanded facility for device packaging, and the Two-Dimensional Crystal Consortium, providing integrated capabilities in materials synthesis, characterization, nanofabrication, and device development. Information about MRI can be found at http://www.mri.psu.edu . Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering or related discipline by the appointment start date . Applications should be submitted directly on the PSU site and will be accepted for priority until December 31, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted until May 15, 2027 or when the position is filled. \u00a0 Applicants should submit the following materials: Curriculum vita Statement of advancing the Penn State values Statement of research Statement of teaching Names and addresses of four references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5 document limit. If you have any questions regarding the application process, please contact Isaac Knepp ( imk4@psu.edu ) or 814-865-2366. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-in-the-Department-of-Mechanical-Engineering_REQ_0000082914-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mechanical Engineering at the Pennsylvania State University in University Park is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-line position in Mechanical Engineering at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the area of construction robotics. Funding for construction robotics is seeing explosive growth, with global construction-tech markets surging and major startups raising massive rounds. This position would align with efforts across Penn State in the areas of robotics and the built environment. This position is co-funded by the Department of Mechanical Engineering and the Cocoziello Institute of Real Estate Innovation. The Department of Mechanical Engineering is home to more than 65 faculty, 350 graduate students, and 1110 undergraduate students. The faculty conduct in excess of $48M per year of funded research across a broad spectrum of traditional and emerging areas. Penn State actively encourages and provides resources for interdisciplinary research collaboration through university-level institutes primarily focused on materials, health, and energy. The Department offers separate B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degree programs in mechanical engineering including online graduate programs in mechanical engineering and in additive manufacturing and design.\u00a0 The Department has a dedicated faculty and staff forming a strong sense of community and belonging. Further information on the Department can be found at: http://www.me.psu.edu/ . Penn State\u2019s Cocoziello Institute of Real Estate Innovation is a university-wide research institute within the Office of the Senior Vice President for Research focused on advancing innovation across the built environment. The Institute brings together over 150 interdisciplinary experts in engineering, artificial intelligence, construction, energy, materials, health, and public polict to address complex challenges in how buildings and infrastructure are designed, built, operated, and experienced. Institute faculty gain access to interdisciplinary collaborators across Penn State, industry and government partners, grant and proposal-development support, opportunities for industry-sponsored and applied research, Living Laboratory projects and testbeds, and competitive seed funding. Further information on Cocoziello Institute can be found at https://cocoziello.psu.edu/ The Assistant Professor should possess a Ph.D. in engineering or a closely related field by the appointment start date; must have demonstrated ability as a teacher or research worker; and must have shown definite evidence of growth in scholarly or professional achievement. The Associate Professor should possess the same qualifications as the Assistant Professor, but must also provide evidence of an established reputation in scholarly or professional achievement. The successful candidates are expected to teach courses at both undergraduate and graduate levels, to develop an internationally recognized, externally-funded research program, and to contribute to the operation and promotion of the department, college, university, and profession through service. The successful candidate will also assume a key role in interdisciplinary research collaborations, particularly in partnership with the Cocoziello Institute. The successful candidate should be a collaborative leader who will promote and enhance excellence and innovation in interdisciplinary research. Nominations and applications will be considered until the positions are filled. Screening of applicants will begin on November 16, 2026. Applicants should submit the following documents: a cover letter; a curriculum vitae; a statement on research; a statement on teaching; a statement on alignment with and experience related to Penn State\u2019s Values of Respect and Community; copies of 3 key publications; and names and addresses of five professional references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine all materials into a single PDF to meet the 5-document limit . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-in-the-Department-of-Mechanical-Engineering_REQ_0000082877-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mechanical Engineering at the Pennsylvania State University in University Park is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-line position in Mechanical Engineering at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the area of solutions for thermal management in large-scale electronics packaging. Solutions for thermal management can include modeling and/or experiments exploring electro-mechanical-thermal management of a range of electronics applications. Electronics for data centers and other high-capacity computing are a critical growth area for the AI revolution. This growth challenges the world energy supply, climate, reliability of the systems, and the economics of the AI revolution. This position would align with a new center at Penn State focusing on all aspects of semiconductor innovation. This position is co-funded by the Department of Mechanical Engineering and the Materials Research Institute. \u00a0 The Department of Mechanical Engineering is home to more than 65 faculty, 350 graduate students, and 1110 undergraduate students. The faculty conduct in excess of $48M per year of funded research across a broad spectrum of traditional and emerging areas. Penn State actively encourages and provides resources for interdisciplinary research collaboration through university-level institutes primarily focused on materials, health, and energy.\u00a0The Department offers separate B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degree programs in mechanical engineering including online graduate programs in mechanical engineering and in additive manufacturing and design.\u00a0 The Department has a dedicated faculty and staff forming a strong sense of community and belonging.\u00a0Further information on the Department can be found at: http://www.me.psu.edu/ . Penn State\u2019s Materials Research Institute (MRI) is a university-wide research institute that connects and supports interdisciplinary teams of researchers that are solving some of the world\u2019s most difficult materials challenges. Further information on MRI can be found at https://www.mri.psu.edu/ . \u00a0 The Assistant Professor should possess a Ph.D. in engineering or a closely related field by the appointment start date; must have demonstrated ability as a teacher or research worker; and must have shown definite evidence of growth in scholarly or professional achievement. The Associate Professor should possess the same qualifications as the Assistant Professor, but must also provide evidence of an established reputation in scholarly or professional achievement. The successful candidates are expected to teach courses at both undergraduate and graduate levels, to develop an internationally recognized, externally-funded research program, and to contribute to the operation and promotion of the department, college, university, and profession through service. The successful candidate will also assume a key role in interdisciplinary research collaborations and is co-funded through Penn State University\u2019s Materials Research Institute. The successful candidate should be a collaborative leader who will promote and enhance excellence and innovation in interdisciplinary research. \u00a0 Nominations and applications will be considered until the positions are filled. Screening of applicants will begin on November 16, 2026. Applicants should submit the following documents: a cover letter; a curriculum\u00a0vitae; a statement on research; a statement on teaching; a statement on alignment with and experience related to Penn State\u2019s Values of Respect and Community; copies of 3 key publications; and names and addresses of five professional references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine all materials into a single PDF to meet the 5-document limit. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Penn-State-Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000082621-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Penn State Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pritchard Lab in the Department of Biomedical Engineering at the Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position. The scholar will lead in vivo mouse studies at the interface of evolution, synthetic biology, and targeted therapy, supporting an NIH-funded program (5 year grant) that develops \"selection gene drives,\" a regulated gene therapy that partners with standard-of-care targeted therapies to overcome drug resistance. The successful candidate will design and execute efficacy and safety studies across cell line-derived xenograft (CDX), orthotopic, patient-derived xenograft (PDX), and immune-competent syngeneic models, including intravenous vector delivery, in vivo imaging (IVIS, micro-CT), and pharmacokinetic, pharmacodynamic, and toxicology cohorts. Qualified individuals will hold a Ph.D. by the time of appointment in Biomedical Engineering or a related scientific field and will have extensive hands-on experience with mouse tumor models and in vivo techniques including IP, IV and SC injections, oral gavage, as well as modern molecular biology. Interested candidates should apply online and submit a CV that includes a list of education, publications, and work experience.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Direct questions regarding this position to Justin Pritchard at jrp94@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---BMB_REQ_0000082848-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - BMB", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Bisanz Lab in the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at Penn State seeks a motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to investigate how the human gut microbiome shapes health and disease. We combine multi-omics, artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML), synthetic microbial communities, and gnotobiotic animal models to uncover how microbes interact with dietary components including xenobiotics to influence infectious and chronic diseases. Responsibilities: Design and lead research projects investigating interactions among the gut microbiome, dietary components, drugs, and other xenobiotics. Develop and apply experimental and/or computational approaches appropriate to the project. Analyze and interpret data, prepare manuscripts, and present findings at scientific meetings. Collaborate with lab members and investigators across disciplines. Contribute to mentoring trainees and maintaining a rigorous, supportive, and inclusive research environment. Applicants must hold a PhD, MD, or equivalent degree by the start date, with relevant training in microbiology, microbial ecology, immunology, biochemistry, bioinformatics, or a related field. This position is intended for scientists who have recently completed, or are completing, their doctoral training. Please submit the following materials: A curriculum vitae. A cover letter describing your relevant experience, research interests, and how you would contribute to a collaborative and inclusive laboratory culture. Contact information for two to three references, including your PhD advisor. A first-author research manuscript that best represents your recent work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please indicate your anticipated availability in your cover letter. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/RPTM-Post-Doc-Mobility-Data-Analytics_REQ_0000082545-1": {"title": "RPTM Post-Doc Mobility Data Analytics", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University is seeking an outstanding postdoctoral researcher to join the Department of Recreation, Park, and Tourism Management (https://hhd.psu.edu/rptm). The position is available starting in March 2027 and will be involved in leading and assisting in multiple projects working with National Park Service and other federal agencies on utilizing mobility data to study visitor flows, improving visitor counting procedure, and developing dashboard to visualize visitor use on public lands. This position will also be involved with proposal preparation, research execution, and mentoring students on projects related to public lands and big data analytics. In addition to the public land and data analytics projects, the postdoctoral scholar and the faculty mentors may identify and scope other areas of research to pursue. Position requires a Ph.D. preferably in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Statistics, Mathematics, or a related area. Required skills include a strong record of technical excellence and achievement as demonstrated through publications, presentations at national and international meetings, and research in relevant discipline in data mining, machine learning, natural language processing, deep learning, large language models, pattern recognition, computer vision, etc. The applicant must possess strong prior experience in software development and the ability to design and perform experiments to validate research hypothesis. The applicant must demonstrate strong written communication skills. The candidate must be self-directed and have the ability and willingness to mentor Ph.D., M.S., or undergraduate students working on these projects. Prior experience working in an interdisciplinary, team-oriented technical atmosphere is desirable. The position fully focuses on research with no expectation of teaching. However, should the scholar want to teach, arrangements can be made to build teaching experience. The objective of this position is to enhance the researcher\u2019s skills and record for a placement in a leading university or research laboratory at the end of the post-doctoral position. Penn State is a premier Research I university in the northeastern United States situated in a university town, State College, that is within three to four hours by car from New York, Washington, D.C., Philadelphia, Cleveland, Pittsburgh, Baltimore, etc. Situated in a valley surrounded by mountains, State College has a low cost of living and small university town charm. More information about future plans for the project will be provided to interested candidates. Please submit an application that includes a current CV, a cover letter outlining your interest in the position, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Questions about the position can be sent via email to Professor\u00a0Bing Pan\u00a0( bingpan@psu.edu ). Applications will be considered starting immediately and will be accepted on a continuing basis until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Fellow---AI--Computational-Biology----Systems-Biology_REQ_0000083000-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Fellow \u2013 AI, Computational Biology, & Systems Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Fellow in AI, Computational Biology, and Systems Biology, to join an interdisciplinary research program focused on understanding the molecular mechanisms underlying complex biological mechanisms using the integration of large-scale multi-omic datasets. The successful candidate will develop and apply computational and statistical approaches to integrate genomic, transcriptomic, epigenomic, proteomic, and physiological phenotypes to identify molecular mechanisms, regulatory networks, disease-associated pathways, and potential therapeutic targets. The position provides an opportunity to work at the intersection of physiology, AI, computational biology, and systems biology, with access to increasingly large and diverse multi-omic datasets. A major focus of the position will be the development of computational frameworks to decipher organ-cross talk by connecting molecular dataset (multi-omics) to cellular phenotypes, tissue-specific regulatory programs, and physiological responses to exercise. Candidates with expertise in multi-omics integration, single-cell and long-read transcriptomics are particularly encouraged to apply. \u00a0 Research Areas The postdoctoral fellow will have opportunities to contribute to projects involving: Multi-omics data integration across genomics, transcriptomics, proteomics, epigenomics, and metabolomics, long-read RNA sequencing and rRNA isoform discovery using PacBio HiFi and other long-read platforms, single-cell RNA-seq analysis and cell-type-specific molecular profiling, gene regulatory network inference using approaches such as GENIE3, SCENIC, and related network-based methods, develop computational approaches for therapeutic target discovery and prioritization, and integration of heterogeneous datasets to generate and test mechanistic biological hypotheses. \u00a0 Candidate Profile We are seeking candidates with a Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in bioinformatics, computational biology, systems biology, genomics, genetics, biostatistics, biomedical engineering, molecular biology, or a related discipline with documented experience using the appropriate methodology described above including but not limited to long-read RNA-seq analysis (PacBio HiFi sequencing), transcript and isoform discovery, alternative splicing and isoform characterization, genome/transcriptome alignment and annotation, single-cell and gene regulatory network discovery using scRNAseq, and integration of single-cell data with bulk and multi-omic datasets \u00a0 Desired computational skills: Strong programming experience in Python and/or R is expected. Experience with Linux/HPC environments, workflow development, statistical modeling, machine learning, and reproducible computational pipelines is highly desirable. Experience with tools and resources such as Scanpy, Seurat, GENIE3, SCENIC, DESeq2, STAR, minimap2, Salmon, kallisto, Bioconductor, Ensembl, GTEx, and protein-interaction databases would be advantageous. Candidates with experience developing new computational methods rather than exclusively applying existing pipelines are particularly encouraged to apply. \u00a0 Research environment The fellow will work in a highly interdisciplinary environment involving computational biologists, molecular biologists, physiologists, and data scientists. The position provides opportunities to develop independent research directions while contributing to collaborative projects involving large-scale human and experimental datasets. The candidate will lead and co-lead publications, present research at national and international conferences, develop grant proposals and fellowship applications, collaborate with experimental investigators to generate and test computationally derived hypotheses, and develop expertise in emerging multi-omic and AI-enabled approaches to biomedical research \u00a0 Required qualifications Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in a relevant field Demonstrated research experience in computational biology, bioinformatics, genomics, or a related field Strong programming skills in R and/or Python Experience analyzing high-throughput biological datasets Strong quantitative, analytical, and problem-solving skills Excellent written and oral communication skills \u00a0 Preferred qualifications: Experience with long-read transcriptomics/PacBio HiFi, single-cell transcriptomics, gene regulatory network inference, and working with HPC environments and reproducible computational workflows \u00a0 How to Apply Applicants should submit: \u00a0 1. A curriculum vitae 2. A brief statement describing research experience and interests 3. A description of relevant computational and bioinformatics expertise 4. Contact information for three professional references \u00a0 Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director--Academic-Administrator-_REQ_0000082683-2": {"title": "Director, Social Sciences Research Institute", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Director, Social Sciences Research Institute \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 As one of Penn State\u2019s seven, university-wide interdisciplinary institutes in the Office of the Senior Vice President for Research (OSVPR), the Social Sciences Research Institute (SSRI) supports and promotes innovation and excellence in the social and behavioral sciences and contributes to a University-wide culture of interdisciplinary collaborative research. \u00a0The new SSRI Director will build on a strong foundation to promote the social and behavioral sciences at Penn State, including by working with faculty from across the University as well as the other OSVPR Institute Directors, College Deans, Research Associate Deans and Department Heads to advance the Institute\u2019s and University\u2019s strategic priorities. With an annual budget of approximately $11 million, the SSRI\u2019s mission is to foster research that brings the social sciences to bear on critical challenges at the local, national, and international levels. The Institute does so by bringing together researchers from a range of disciplines and by providing consultation, financial support, shared accessible infrastructure, and services to social and behavioral scientists across Penn State\u2019s colleges and campuses.\u00a0 The SSRI\u2019s five strategic foci, Reducing Social Disparities, Smart and Connected Health, The Human System, Innovative Methods, and Dissemination and Implementation Science, are contained within a portfolio of activities within SSRI\u2019s research units https://ssri.psu.edu/about . The SSRI Director reports to the Senior Vice President for Research who oversees Penn State research--currently exceeding $968 million annually. The Director\u2019s responsibilities include: (1) advancing a vision for Penn State\u2019s social and behavioral sciences, university-wide leadership, and catalyzing translational research excellence at the interfaces of the social and \u00a0behavioral science and other science disciplines; (2) building interdisciplinary collaborations across the social and behavioral sciences and beyond including by developing policies and incentives for faculty engagement and creating an atmosphere of inclusion of diverse expertise and perspectives; (3) chairing SSRI\u2019s Executive and Steering Committees, which advise on SSRI investments, policies, and programs; (4) chairing the SSRI Deans, Associate Research Deans, and Department Head Advisory Committees, which provide input and insights on both strategic and operational \u00a0matters; (5) identifying new funding opportunities; (6) promoting interdisciplinary, collaborative, and translational research through seed funding and research infrastructure support; and (7) serving as a liaison between the University\u2019s social and behavioral science research initiatives and state, national, and international organizations.\u00a0 The successful candidate will be an internationally recognized leader in the social, behavioral, or population health sciences, with a strong record of interdisciplinary research and the vision and leadership needed to advance new initiatives, sustain existing research strengths, and translate research into evidence-based programs, policies, and practices. The candidate must have credentials appropriate for appointment as a tenured professor in an appropriate college and demonstrate a commitment to advancing Penn State\u2019s land-grant mission. The candidate should also bring experience maintaining research excellence in the face of change, enthusiasm for fundraising and resource development, along with the ability to create new opportunities for sponsored research, philanthropic support, and industry partnerships, including the translation of research into science- and technology-based solutions, programs, government policies, and practices. The successful candidate must also support maintaining and nurturing an exceptional work environment. Our employees are our greatest asset and our success as an organization in achieving our goals is based on having a team of inspired individuals with unique perspectives, an array of skills, and providing them with an engaging environment with opportunities for growth.\u00a0 The successful candidate will ensure Penn State Values are in the forefront of workforce expansion; they will provide professional development and opportunities for career advancement; and they will provide a work environment that positions individuals to do their best work, ranging from opportunities for individuals to excel, teams to be creative, and units to inspire. The Pennsylvania State University is in central Pennsylvania. Coined Happy Valley for its\u00a0highly\u00a0ranked livability, the area is known for its\u00a0access to nature spanning\u00a0beautiful mountains, streams, and parks, as well as superb sports and recreational opportunities. The area has excellent schools and offers a multitude of cultural and sporting events. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a letter expressing their interest in this position with a detailed vision statement for advancing Penn State social sciences research, managing talented faculty and staff to achieve greater impact. Also include a curriculum vitae and contact information for four references. Interested individuals are invited to visit SSRI\u2019s website for more information about SSRI.\u00a0 Inquiries can be directed to Craig Newschaffer, Raymond E. and Erin Stuart Schultz Dean, College of Health and Human Development ( cjn5389@psu.edu ), chair of the search committee. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Finance-Instructor_REQ_0000083009-1": {"title": "Adjunct Finance Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Finance at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park) seeks to hire adjunct instructors to teach finance courses in the spring 2027 semester. The positions are part-time, limited term, non-tenure track positions with teaching between January and May 2027. The appointments may be renewed based on department need. Teaching responsibilities will be predominantly at the undergraduate level and are onsite. We seek candidates dedicated to delivering excellent teaching of rigorous courses that incorporate the responsible use of AI. We seek individuals who will work effectively with our talented faculty and students and contribute to our vibrant and collegial environment. JOB QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must hold a Ph.D, MBA, or a master\u2019s degree in finance or a closely related field at the time of hiring. \u00a0 APPLICATION PROCEDURE: \u00a0 To apply for this position, candidates are to apply directly online through WorkDay and submit the following documents as PDF files: \u00a0 Cover letter of interest Vita Teaching evaluations (when applicable) Names of at least three (3) references \u00a0 A minimum of three reference letters should be emailed directly from reference providers to this address : finance.recruiting@psu.edu \u00a0 For full consideration, applications should be completed by November 1, 2026, though review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. More information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at www.smeal.psu.edu/finance .\u00a0For questions about the application process and portal, please contact Kayla Horting ( keo131@psu.edu ), 814-863-0486. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-in-Subsurface-Energy-Engineering_REQ_0000082922-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Subsurface Energy Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The John and Willie Leone Family Department of Energy and Mineral Engineering (EME) in the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a tenure-line faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank with a research focus in Subsurface Energy Engineering . The appointment will be made at a rank commensurate with the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. We seek an exceptional scholar who will contribute to and strengthen the department\u2019s leadership in subsurface energy engineering through innovative, interdisciplinary research addressing critical challenges in subsurface energy production and storage and flow in porous media . Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, all traditional petroleum engineering disciplines , including reservoir engineering; drilling and completions engineering; production and operations engineering; formation evaluation and petrophysics , as well as related and emerging areas such as enhanced geothermal systems; nuclear waste disposal; subsurface recovery of critical minerals; microfluidics and lab-on-a-chip technologies; and AI-, data-, and computationally enabled approaches to subsurface engineering . EME is a dynamic, multidisciplinary department that thrives on collaboration and impact-driven research, fostering partnerships across academia, industry, and government. Penn State provides exceptional opportunities for collaboration through its renowned interdisciplinary institutes, offering access to world-class resources and networks. Competitive applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor must possess a Ph.D. in an engineering field directly related to their research area before beginning employment at Penn State. Candidates should demonstrate strong potential to establish an externally funded experimental, computational, or integrated research program that strengthens EME\u2019s Subsurface Energy Engineering research area. Candidates must also demonstrate a commitment to excellence in education and mentoring, including teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across EME programs, advising and mentoring graduate students, and contributing service to the Department, College, University, and profession. Candidates for the rank of Associate Professor must meet the qualifications for Assistant Professor and additionally demonstrate excellence in teaching and mentoring, a strong record of research, publications, and external funding, and an established national or international reputation for scholarly or professional achievement. The successful candidate will play a key role in advancing interdisciplinary research within the department and college and to serve as a collaborative leader who contributes to innovation and excellence across the department. To apply, submit the following materials: A cover letter describing the candidate\u2019s principal research interests and providing the names and contact information of four references; A complete curriculum vitae, including a full list of publications; A research statement of no more than three pages describing the candidate\u2019s research vision and future directions and explaining how their program would strengthen and expand EME\u2019s research leadership; A teaching statement of no more than one page describing the candidate\u2019s approach to teaching and mentoring and identifying courses within the EME undergraduate and graduate curriculum, as well as curricular areas, in which the candidate could make the greatest contributions; and Two published journal articles that the candidate considers their most impactful scholarly contributions. Applications received by November 27, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Please direct inquiries and nominations to Prof. Sanjay Srinivasan, Chair of the Search Committee , at szs27@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Professor-and-Head--Department-of-Agricultural-and-Biological-Engineering_REQ_0000082804-1": {"title": "Professor and Head, Department of Agricultural and Biological Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Professor and Head, Department of Agricultural and Biological Engineering The Pennsylvania State University The Department of Agricultural and Biological Engineering (ABE) at The Pennsylvania State University seeks applications for an accomplished and visionary leader to serve as its next Department Head . The Department Head reports directly to the Dean of the College of Agricultural Sciences and serves on the executive leadership teams in the College of Agricultural Sciences and the College of Engineering. Department Administered by the College of Agricultural Sciences and formally aligned with the College of Engineering, the ABE department is composed of 23 faculty, nine affiliated faculty, eight staff, and 120 graduate and undergraduate students. Its undergraduate and graduate programs consistently rank in the top 10 in the US. The ABE department has two undergraduate degree programs: 1) Biological Engineering and 2) Agricultural and Biorenewable Systems Management, as well as two M.S. and Ph.D. graduate programs: 1) Agricultural and Biological Engineering and 2) Biorenewable Systems. Research and Extension in the department include a broad portfolio focused on food and bioprocessing; bioproducts including those from crops, livestock, and forestry; natural resources engineering; agricultural engineering; business; and ethics. The ABE department is housed in a 93,500 sq. ft. building with state-of-the-art research, teaching, and collaborative spaces. The building is also home to the CSL Behring fermentation facility, one of the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences\u2019 core facilities. More information is available at https://abe.psu.edu/ . College and University Founded in 1855, Penn State University has campuses and facilities across the Commonwealth and is ranked among the top public universities in the nation with linkages around the globe. The College of Agricultural Sciences leads the University\u2019s land grant mission with the integration of teaching, research, and Extension. The College employs over 1,200 full-time employees, including nearly 300 faculty, and is the home of nearly 3,300 graduate and undergraduate students. Its nine academic departments offer 17 undergraduate majors, 13 graduate programs, and 31 other minors and certificates. Research expenditures in the College exceeded $140M in FY25, and through our robust Extension portfolio, research-based educational programs are offered in all 67 counties and online. The College is deeply committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning and a working environment where everyone can succeed. Responsibilities The person filling this position serves as the Departmental program leader and administrative officer. Duties include: Create and maintain an environment that facilitates: 1) a strong sense of community; 2) an effective shared vision; 3) a highly productive, innovative, and entrepreneurial faculty and staff; 4) collaborative opportunities, and 5) a mutually supportive, inclusive and intellectually stimulating environment for students, staff, and faculty. Lead faculty and staff in implementing and enhancing the Department\u2019s undergraduate and graduate education programs, research programs, Cooperative Extension, and outreach initiatives to ensure programs are responsive to the evolving interests and needs of students and society. Create a supportive environment for faculty at all stages of their careers by being a good role model and by developing creative and effective strategies for mentoring and faculty support. Guide and enhance the Department\u2019s research environment to ensure that programs meet the needs of stakeholders and sponsors. Proactively engage in teaching, research and Extension programs, and enhance the Department\u2019s state, national and international reputation. Support development programs to attract external support for educational programs, research initiatives, centers and institutes, and Extension engagement strategies. Administer and manage the Department\u2019s academic affairs, personnel, finances, and physical facilities. Represent, promote and advocate for the Department within the College and University, and with disciplinary groups, alumni and other private and public stakeholders within the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania and beyond. Qualifications Earned doctorate in a field relevant to ABE's mission and a distinguished record of scholarship, including peer-reviewed publications, extramural funding, and mentorship of undergraduate and graduate students, sufficient to qualify for appointment as a tenured professor. Strong commitment to fostering a positive departmental culture grounded in integrity, inclusive excellence, participatory decision-making, and excellence in teaching, research, extension, and service. Significant understanding of the evolving mission of the land-grant university system, and the opportunities and challenges facing public research and education institutions. Demonstrated commitment to mentoring and supporting the professional development of faculty, staff, and students at all career stages. Demonstrated ability to manage budgets strategically and balance diverse priorities and resource needs. Understanding of state and national funding environments and experience developing interdisciplinary and transdisciplinary collaborations. Strong leadership, communication, and advocacy skills, with experience advancing organizational priorities through effective personnel management, stakeholder engagement, and fundraising. Familiarity with accreditation processes and assessment of academic programs. Applications should include: A letter of application that states an applicant\u2019s specific interest in the position, qualifications, previous professional and administrative responsibilities, and achievements; Statement of vision for the future of our profession; Statement of leadership and management philosophy, including examples of effective leadership of teams; Curriculum vitae (C.V.) which includes statement of current position and responsibilities; Contact information for five professional references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Applications will be reviewed beginning December 1, 2026 and will be accepted until a suitable candidate is chosen. Desired start date is July 1, 2027 or as negotiated. Inquiries should be addressed to the search committee chair: Dr. David Abler at dga2@psu.edu . Applications must be submitted on Penn State\u2019s online job website ( hr.psu.edu/careers ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Fellow---Center-for-Theory-of-Emergent-Quantum-Matter--C-TEQ-_REQ_0000082815-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Fellow - Center for Theory of Emergent Quantum Matter (C-TEQ)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Penn State's interdisciplinary Center for Theory of Emergent Quantum Matter (C-TEQ) , part of the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS) Quantum Hub , invites applications for several \"C-TEQ Fellow\u201d Postdoctoral Scholar positions. Start dates are flexible but can be immediate.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The successful candidates will have expertise in one or more areas related to quantum information science, quantum materials, quantum computation, artificial intelligence and computational approaches to emergent quantum matter, quantum geometry, Majorana modes, the fractional quantum anomalous Hall effect, or closely related fields.\u00a0 \u00a0 C-TEQ Fellows will benefit from a highly collaborative and intellectually stimulating research environment, working alongside fellow postdoctoral scholars and faculty affiliates from Physics, Mathematics, Computer Science and Engineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Electrical Engineering, and Information Sciences and Technology. Faculty affiliates include Zhen Bi, Long-Qing Chen, Swaroop Ghosh, Vasant Honavar, Thomas Iadecola, Jainendra Jain, Ribhu Kaul, Xiantao Li, Chaoxing Liu, Vincent Meunier, Lukas Muechler, Marcos Rigol, Sarah Shandera, Abhinav Verma, and Binghai Yan. Fellows will also have access to the advanced computational resources and cyberinfrastructure of the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS).\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates must possess a Ph.D. before their appointment start date at Penn State.\u00a0 \u00a0 In addition to completing a Penn State application, you must submit an application at https://academicjobsonline.org . Applications must be submitted electronically and include 1) cover letter, 2) CV, and 3) a statement of research interests. Please also arrange for at least three reference letters to be uploaded to the http://academicjobsonline.org website.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The salary of the C-TEQ Fellows is $80,000, with an additional one-time award of $5,000 toward research-related expenses, such as conferences.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Applications will be reviewed beginning immediately. Applications received by October 30, 2026 , will receive first-round consideration. We will continue reviewing applications on a rolling basis until the positions are filled.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/PT-Lecturer---CSD-895A-Speech-Language-Clinical-Practicum_REQ_0000083032-1": {"title": "PT Lecturer - CSD 895A Speech/Language Clinical Practicum", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Penn State College of Health and Human Development Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders University Park invites applications for a Part-Time Lecturer position teaching CSD 895A Speech/Language Clinical Practicum for the Fall 2026 Semester. The Part-Time Lecturer will teach a three-credit, graduate-level course that includes supervision of M.S. student clinicians in the Penn State Speech, Language, and Hearing Clinic. Requirements: A master\u2019s degree or equivalent education and experience in a related field is required. Holding an active Certificate of Clinical Competence in Speech-Language Pathology (CCC-SLP) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association (ASHA) is required. Holding\u00a0an active license to practice as a speech-language pathologist in Pennsylvania from the Pennsylvania State Board of Examiners in Speech-Language Pathology and Audiology is required. Holding current CPR certification is required. Meeting requirements for ASHA-certified Clinical Educators, Supervisors, and Clinical Fellowship Mentors is required. A minimum of three years of clinical practice is required. Previous experience in clinical supervision is required. The position is a one semester, non-tenure track appointment with the possibility of reappointment. Part-time lecturers normally teach one section. All applications will be considered until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Researcher-Research-Professor-Center-of-Excellence-in-Directed-Energy_REQ_0000080958-2": {"title": "Researcher/Research Professor Center of Excellence in Directed Energy", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Researcher / Assistant Research Professor/ Associate Research Professor The Center of Excellence in Directed Energy (CEDE) at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a highly qualified individual for a non-tenure-line position at the rank of Researcher or Assistant / Associate Research Professor . The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in coordinating projects and managing lab facilities within CEDE. Key Responsibilities: The primary responsibility of the position will be assisting cutting-edge research programs, including electromagnetic and mechanical simulations, managing and setting up fabrication and measurement equipment, as well as the preparation of reports for relevant sponsored contracts. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to participate in funded projects. Typical duties include, but are not limited to: Coordinate projects and manage the production lab Assist in proposal writing Prepare project reports Oversee and manage projects Develop and implement project timelines, as well as ensure deliverables, deadlines, goals, and objectives of projects are met Requirements and Qualifications: Candidates will be considered for the rank commensurate with their education and experience in accordance with AC21 . A successful candidate at the Assistant Research Professor or Associate Research Professor rank will hold a terminal degree or its equivalent in electrical or mechanical engineering or a related field by the appointment date. Candidates without an MS who are active candidates for a terminal degree will be considered at the Researcher rank. In addition, they must have working knowledge of SolidWorks and be proficient in the creation and critical review of engineering drawings, tolerancing, and tolerance analysis. United States Citizenship is required. Industrial experience is preferred. Additional Information: Applicants should submit a current CV/resume with their online application and be prepared, if requested, to send the names and addresses of at least three references to: Prof. Douglas H. Werner The Pennsylvania State University Department of Electrical Engineering 211A EE East University Park, PA 16802 dhw@psu.edu The working location for this position will be University Park, PA. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Research-Professor---Greenhouse-Gas-Measurements-and-Modeling_REQ_0000082668-2": {"title": "Research Professor - Greenhouse Gas Measurements and Modeling", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Meteorology and Atmospheric Science\u00a0at Penn State (University Park, PA) announces an opening for a Research Professor to contribute to and to lead research on greenhouse gas (GHG) measurements and modeling. The successful candidate will contribute to projects targeted at understanding sources of sink of GHGs in the earth system. The successful candidate will contribute to both measurements and numerical modeling of GHGs from a variety of systems, potentially including but not limited to oil and gas production, agricultural systems, cities and ecosystems. The candidate will co-lead the measurement and analysis programs of a highly collaborative research group. \u00a0 Responsibilities : Leadership of the group responsible for setup, operation and maintenance of ground based GHG observing systems. Evaluation of networks of GHG measurements. Evaluation of surface-atmosphere exchange of GHGs using atmospheric budgets and inversions. Lead and contribute to publications using these measurement systems. Serve as lead investigator, as appropriate, for funded research efforts related to these topics. Advise or co-advise graduate and undergraduate researchers working in these areas. \u00a0 Requirements: \u00a0 A Ph.D. in atmospheric science or a related field and ten or more years of experience testing, deploying and maintaining ground-based GHG observational systems. Nationally-recognized expertise with instrument calibration, field deployment and operation, including established ties with national and international instrument network leaders and a record of publication in this field. Strong communications and writing skills, ability to multi-task, and ability to work with a diverse array of collaborators.\u00a0 Ability to advise project graduate students. Ability to lead a group of instrument scientists. Ability to serve as principal investigator for funded research efforts. \u00a0 Interested Candidates should submit a cover letter describing their interest in the position and career goals, a CV including publication list, and names & contact information of up to three references. \u00a0For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Ken Davis ( kjd10@psu.edu ). \u00a0 This position is funded for one year from the date of hire with the excellent possibility of renewal pending available funding and satisfactory performance. \u00a0 \u00a0 The position will be available as early as 1 November, 2026 and will remain open until filled. Salaries will be commensurate with education and\u00a0experience.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Pure-Math-Faculty_REQ_0000082488-1": {"title": "Pure Math Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The \u00a0Department of Mathematics\u00a0 at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park Campus, State College, PA, USA) invites applications for a\u00a0 tenure-track faculty \u00a0position at the rank of Assistant , Associate or Full Professor in\u00a0 Pure Mathematics , with a preference for Number Theory and related areas. The anticipated starting date for this appointment is Summer or Fall of 2027. The duties include research, teaching, mentorship of students in their research endeavors at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and service to the university and the greater professional community. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate interest in and capacity for developing a strong, independent research program, and teaching and mentorship excellence at both the undergraduate and graduate levels.\u00a0 Applications submitted electronically by November 1, 2026, will receive full consideration. Applicants must complete the Penn State application for REQ_0000082488 at myworkdayjobs.com, and must also submit an application through\u202f mathjobs.org with the following materials:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0Cover letter (maximum of 2 pages) that includes:\u00a0 Summary of the vision and goals of your research program, potential collaborations and alignment with our department and institution.\u00a0 Short summary of your most significant accomplishments.\u00a0 \u2022 Curriculum Vitae (which includes a full publication list).\u00a0 \u2022 Research statement: a detailed statement of your research accomplishments and your future research plans (maximum 5 pages).\u00a0 \u2022 Teaching statement: a statement of your teaching philosophy and interests (maximum 2 pages).\u00a0 \u2022 Four reference letters (one of which must address your teaching experience and effectiveness in detail) uploaded by the letter writers in the mathjobs application .\u00a0 Competitive applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree) in Mathematics or a closely related field before beginning employment at Penn State.\u00a0 Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have the same qualifications as the rank of assistant professor, as well as a strong track record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service.\u00a0 Candidates for Full Professor should have the same qualifications as the rank of associate professor, as well as a track record of research publications, funding, teaching, and service that distinguishes them, nationally or internationally.\u00a0 The Mathematics Department at Penn State has a history of excellence in both pure and applied mathematics with groups in number theory, dynamical systems, geometry, algebra, analysis and partial differential equations, applied mathematics and numerical analysis. The Department seeks to advance its robust agenda of research that fosters interdisciplinary connections across departments. The department also hosts several research centers including the Anatole Katok Center for Dynamical Systems and Geometry, the Center for Computational Mathematics and Applications, and the Center for Mathematical Biology. The University Park campus is located in State College, a vibrant, family friendly university town in central Pennsylvania.\u00a0 Questions about the position and the Department of Mathematics at Penn State may be directed to Professor Paul Milewski, by e-mail at\u00a0 ppm5454@psu.edu , or Professor Kirsten Eisentraeger, by e-mail at\u00a0 kxe8@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000082655-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Computer Science and Engineering Department at Penn State invites applications for a full-time postdoctoral research position in quantum computing, working with Professors Chunhao Wang and Xiantao Li. The successful candidate will conduct research on the development and analysis of quantum algorithms, with particular emphasis on simulating quantum systems and applications to scientific computing. Topics of interest include Hamiltonian simulation, open quantum system dynamics, quantum state preparation, and quantum algorithms for optimization and sampling. Responsibilities include developing algorithmic techniques, establishing theoretical performance guarantees, conducting numerical investigations as appropriate, collaborating with faculty and graduate students, and disseminating research through journal publications and conference presentations. Applicants must possess a doctoral degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, or a related discipline by the appointment start date. Candidates should have strong mathematical and analytical skills, a demonstrated record of research relevant to the position, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: quantum algorithms, quantum information theory, quantum simulation, numerical analysis, or scientific computing. Candidates with complementary expertise and a strong interest in quantum computing are also encouraged to apply. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include: a CV a statement of research interests names of three references who will provide letters of recommendation. Inquiries about the position should be directed to Chunhao Wang or Xiantao Li. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Open-Rank-Professor-in-Business-Analytics-and-Information-Systems_REQ_0000082577-1": {"title": "Open-Rank Professor in Business Analytics and Information Systems", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Supply Chain & Information Systems (SCIS) Department of the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) invites applications for an open-rank tenure-track faculty position in Business Analytics & Information Systems for a Fall 2027 start date. Salary is competitive.\u00a0 Candidates must have a PhD degree in information systems or related field by the appointment start date. Those who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor.\u00a0A strong commitment to research and teaching excellence is expected.\u00a0Candidates at the Associate or Full Professor level should have a demonstrated record of high-quality research and teaching commensurate with rank, as well as a sufficient number of publications in high-quality journals and a demonstrated significant impact of their work on the field. Faculty members are expected to maintain an active research program, perform undergraduate and graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in service activities.\u00a0 \u00a0 The SCIS Department comprises a vibrant, research-active faculty with research and teaching interests in information systems that include artificial intelligence, digital platforms, business analytics and blockchain. The department offers degree programs in supply chain management, business analytics & information systems, and AI and business transformation. We seek outstanding candidates with expertise in information systems, with a desired emphasis on artificial intelligence, that would complement the faculty with high-quality research and teaching in student-centered and collaborative learning environments.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 The Smeal College of Business offers a collegial working environment and excellent campus facilities. The College is home to the Center for Supply Chain Research\u00ae ( www.smeal.psu.edu/cscr ) which advances cutting-edge research and outreach in supply chain management. The SCIS Department ( www.smeal.psu.edu/scis ) also has strong connections with the business community through various research centers that provide opportunities to collaborate with faculty across disciplines within Smeal and across Penn State. For more information, please visit www.smeal.psu.edu/research-centers .\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For further information, please contact Autumn Hanley at adh5253@psu.edu .\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 Applications should be submitted directly on the Penn State site and include a cover letter, a statement of research and teaching, and a CV. Contact information for three references also should be provided.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Grain-Crop-Production_REQ_0000082366-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Grain Crop Production", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar Opportunity Grain Crop Production Laboratory - Department of Plant Science - The Pennsylvania State University https://plantscience.psu.edu/research/labs/grain-production-lab Position Summary The Grain Crop Production Lab in the Department of Plant Science at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a\u00a0 Postdoctoral Scholar \u00a0position focused on investigating best management practices for increasing the sustainability and productivity of grain cropping systems in Pennsylvania. Two main lines of investigation within our research and extension program include improving water and nutrient use efficiency in corn, soybean, and wheat production. This position provides a unique opportunity to lead integrative research combining precision agriculture, plant abiotic stress physiology, data analysis and predictive modelling for the development of decision support tools. This position will also provide ample opportunity for the development of grant and scientific writing skills and leadership skills. Key Responsibilities Lead field experiments aiming to improving water and nutrient use efficiency in corn, soybean, and wheat production. Integrate field experimentation, analysis of large, multidimensional datasets, and modelling to develop decision support tools for site-specific agronomic management. Prepare peer-reviewed manuscripts, contribute to grant proposals, and present findings at conferences. Mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers and collaborate with faculty and interdisciplinary teams. Lead outreach efforts to disseminate research results. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Agronomy, Plant Science, Soil Science, or related discipline. Expertise in field experimentation, grain crop management, plant abiotic stress physiology, and plant-soil interactions. Proven publication record in peer-reviewed journals and strong scientific communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative, cross-disciplinary team. Selected candidate must possess a U.S. driver's license and will be required to complete a motor vehicle record background check. Appointment Details * Position Type: Full-time, 1-year appointment, renewable based on performance and funding. * Start Date: 01/01/2027 (preferred). * Location: University Park, Pennsylvania. * Salary: Competitive, with full Penn State benefits. Application Instructions Submit the following materials as a single PDF file: 1. Curriculum vitae (CV). 2. Contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Contact Information Daniela Carrijo Grain Crop Production Lab Department of Plant Science Pennsylvania State University Email:\u00a0dzc5794 @psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor-in-Supply-Chain-Management_REQ_0000082547-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Supply Chain Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The SC&IS Department of the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) invites applications a tenure-track position in Supply Chain & Information Systems at the assistant professor level for a Fall 202 7 start date . Salary is competitive. \u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates must have a PhD degree in supply chain management or related field by the appointment start date. Those who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered. \u00a0 A strong commitment to research and teaching excellence is expected .\u00a0 Faculty members are expected to maintain an active research program, perform undergraduate and graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in service activities. \u00a0 \u00a0 The SC&IS Department comprises a vibrant, research-active faculty with research and teaching interests that traverse the end-to-end supply chain and includes business logistics , sourcing, manufacturing, and service operations. The department offers degree programs in supply chain management, management information systems, and business analytics. We seek outstanding candidates with expertise in supply chain and operations with an emphasis in analytics that would complement the faculty with high-quality research and teaching in student-centered and collaborative learning environments.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 The Smeal College of Business offers a collegial working environment and excellent campus facilities. It has the Center for Supply Chain Research\u00ae ( www.smeal.psu.edu/cscr ) which advances cutting-edge research and outreach in supply chain management. The SC&IS Department ( www.smeal.psu.edu/scis ) also has strong connections with the business community through various research centers that provide opportunities to interface with faculty across various disciplines within Smeal and across Penn State. For more information, please visit www.smeal.psu.edu/research-centers .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Review of applications will begin approximately October 1 , 202 6 and will continue until the position is filled .\u00a0 For further information, please contact Autumn Knepp at adh5253@psu .edu .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants should apply directly on the Penn State site and upload a letter of intent, a statement of research and teaching, the job market paper, and a CV. Contact information for three references also should be provided .\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Line-Faculty-in-Finance_REQ_0000082662-1": {"title": "Tenure Line Faculty in Finance", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Finance of The Pennsylvania State University (University Park) seeks to fill up to three tenure-line faculty positions, including two Assistant Professors and one Full Professor position, beginning in Fall 2027. A Chaired appointment may be available for an exceptionally qualified candidate. Candidates must contribute to the mission of the Smeal College of Business and the Department of Finance in the areas of research, teaching, and service. In particular, candidates must conduct high-quality research that is published or publishable in top-tier academic journals; effectively teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels; serve as a research advisor and mentor to PhD students; engage in service activities commensurate with their rank; and contribute to the collegial and intellectual atmosphere of the department. JOB QUALIFICATIONS: Those who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor. For consideration for the Full Professor level position, applicants must have a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. Candidates for all ranks must have a PhD in Finance or a closely related field by the appointment start date. APPLICATION PROCEDURE: To apply for this position, candidates are to apply directly on-line at https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Tenure-Line-Faculty-in-Finance_REQ_000008266 2 and submit the following documents as PDF files: vita copies of representative publications and working papers teaching evaluations (for seasoned applicants) names of at least three (3) references A minimum of three reference letters should be emailed directly from reference providers to this address : finance.recruiting@psu.edu For full consideration, applications should be completed by November 1, 2026, though review of applications will continue until the position is filled. More information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at www.smeal.psu.edu/finance .\u00a0For questions about the application process and portal, please contact Kayla Horting ( keo131@psu.edu ), 814-863-0486. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Steven-Fisher-Professorship-in-Creative-Writing_REQ_0000082286-1": {"title": "Steven Fisher Professorship in Creative Writing", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of English at The Pennsylvania State University at University Park, Pennsylvania, USA, invites applications for the Steven Fisher Professorship in Creative Writing. This is a tenure-track position ( Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor ) in Creative Writing (Fiction) to begin August 2027, with flexibility. Secondary expertise in Creative Nonfiction is also desirable. Responsibilities include teaching two courses per semester, to both undergraduates and those enrolled in the bachelor/masters (BA/MA) graduate program. The BA/MA program offers an integrated undergraduate/graduate degree in English with a creative writing concentration in poetry or prose. Students complete the program in two years\u2014their senior undergraduate year and an additional M.A. year. Information on the BA/MA program can be found here: https://english.la.psu.edu/graduate-creative-writing/ . This position will include resident and online instruction and normal university service. Onsite teaching is an essential function of this job. Candidates for the position must have a terminal degree (MFA or PhD) in creative writing or related field in hand by the starting date. They must also have a record of publications in prominent venues and at least one book of fiction in print or under contract. Candidates for Professor should have an outstanding publication record, a commitment to securing external funding, and a track record of excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Candidates for Associate Professor should have a significant publication record, a commitment to securing external funding, and a track record of excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Candidates for Assistant Professor should have a promising publication record, a commitment to securing external funding, and a track record in teaching and mentoring students. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board and upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae (with a list of names and contact information for three references), and a writing sample of approximately 7,500 words. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor-of-Dairy-Production-Systems_REQ_0000082040-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Dairy Production Systems", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Assistant Professor of Dairy Production Systems JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Animal Science at The Pennsylvania State University , University Park, invites applications for a tenure-line faculty position in Dairy Production Systems . Candidates will be considered for appointment at the Assistant Professor level. The successful candidate will have a 50% research, 25% teaching, and 25% extension appointment. This full-time, 36-week appointment will begin on a mutually agreed upon date. We seek an outstanding scientist who will develop an externally funded, nationally recognized research program in dairy production systems with an emphasis on applied research addressing critical challenges and opportunities facing modern dairy operations. The successful candidate will be expected to integrate research, teaching, and extension activities to generate practical solutions for dairy producers and allied industries. Strong preference will be given to candidates whose approaches are multidisciplinary and contribute to collaborative scholarship across the College of Agricultural Sciences and the University. Areas of emphasis may include nutrition, management, reproduction, efficiency, sustainability, precision technologies, or systems approaches. The successful candidate will develop and deliver effective extension programs that translate research findings into practical recommendations for dairy producers, consultants, veterinarians, and allied industry professionals. They will advise M.S. and Ph.D.\u00a0graduate students, mentor undergraduate students, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in dairy science and related disciplines, and engage in appropriate professional and service activities within and outside the Department. Teaching responsibilities will be aligned with the candidate\u2019s expertise and the needs of the department. Priority areas may include dairy cattle production and management, dairy herd or farm financial management, milk secretion, ruminology, and dairy reproduction, genetics, or nutrition. Additional teaching opportunities may include dairy challenge, dairy judging, or careers in animal agriculture. The Department of Animal Science at Penn State includes 32 faculty members and is home to internationally recognized programs in animal nutrition, reproduction, physiology, and genetics. Penn State maintains extensive dairy facilities housing approximately 500 animals, including modern lactating cow, heifer, dry cow, calf, and intensive research facilities that support basic, applied, and translational research. Opportunities exist to conduct studies ranging from whole-farm systems and management to intensive nutritional, physiological, and metabolic investigations. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty across the College of Agricultural Sciences and the University, including Agricultural and Biological Engineering, Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences, Plant Science, Nutritional Sciences, and related disciplines. These collaborations provide opportunities to address sustainability, nutrient management, circular agricultural systems, and emerging technologies relevant to modern dairy production. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Applicants must have a Ph.D.\u00a0in Animal Science, Dairy Science, or a closely related field. Postdoctoral or industry experience is preferred. Candidates must have a strong record of academic outputs, demonstrated ability or potential to obtain external funding, experience or demonstrated interest in teaching and extension, and plans to develop an innovative research program that will address important challenges in dairy production systems. Candidates who approach important questions broadly and whose programs integrate applied research with stakeholder engagement are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. Excellent communication, teamwork, and leadership skills are essential. SALARY & BENEFITS The salary for this position is competitive and commensurate with experience. An attractive benefits package is available. HOW TO APPLY: Candidates should apply online with the following information: (1) Letter of Interest; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) Statement of research interests, including synergies with the department; (4) Statement of teaching philosophy and interest, and proposed extension programing; and (5) Names and contact information for three references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. For questions about this position, please contact Dr. Rebecca Krisher (rlk5688@psu.edu). Apply online to Job REQ_0000082040 at https://hr.psu.edu/careers . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000082403-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The\u00a0Pennsylvania State University\u2019s Department of Plant Pathology and Environmental Microbiology seeks one\u00a0 Postdoctoral Scholar to research innovative biological control strategies for managing the North American beech leaf nematode. The scholar will lead or coordinate studies using naturally occurring bacteria from areas affected by Beech Leaf Disease (BLD) to suppress Litylenchus crenatae (Lc) nematode populations. Additionally, the scholar will test our collection of bacterial pathogens for nematocidal activity against Lc. This position requires a PhD in nematology (preferred), plant pathology, microbiology, microbial ecology, or a related field. Competitive candidates must have significant experience working with plant-parasitic nematodes, sequence analysis, and microbiology, along with excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills (both oral and written). Applicants are asked to submit the following on Penn State's Job Posting Board : 1/ Cover Letter 2/ Contact Information for 3 References 3/ Resume/CV Contact person for questions regarding this position: Dr. Mihail Kantor ( mpk6148@psu.edu) \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Head--Collection-Strategies_REQ_0000082510-1": {"title": "Head, Collection Strategies", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Head, Collection Strategies \u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 Penn State University Libraries (PSUL) seeks applications for Head, Collection Strategies. Reporting to the Associate Dean for Collections and Commonwealth Campus Libra ries, thi s tenure-line position provides strategic guidance for the development , stewardship, assessment, and long-term direction of the Libraries\u2019 \u202fresearch and teaching collections . The Head will focus on\u202fcollaborating with library colleagues across the University Libraries , institutional partners and constituents across the University, and external partners to develop and implement a unified collections strategy that aligns collection development, acquisitions, interlibrary loan, and intentional, forward-looking stewardship with institutional values, budget realities, and user needs. \u00a0 \u00a0 This is a faculty appointment and an academic administrator . This position requires regular onsite presence at the University Park campus. \u202f \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 Duties and Responsibilities \u202f \u202f \u00a0 Provide strategic leadership and direction for collection development: Articulate and implement vision and strategies for sustainable collection building; co-lead the Libraries' Collections Council in developing collection strategies, policies, and practices that prioritize equitable access, diverse and inclusive collecting, and responsiveness to emerging research, curricular, and University priorities. \u00a0 \u00a0 Lead the Collection Strategies Department: Supervise and mentor faculty and staff within the Collection Strategies Department (Collection Analysis, Collection Maintenance, and Annex units). \u00a0 Shape collections budget strategy and investment priorities: In collaboration with the Head of Acquisitions and Resource Sharing, synthesize data, usage trends, and community input to develop the Libraries' collections budget strategy , advise on equitable fund allocation, and provide timely expenditure projections to Libraries\u2019 Administration \u00a0 Lead strategic vendor and publisher negotiations: Develop and maintain relationships with key vendors and publishers in support of major contract negotiations and transformative agreement frameworks . Design and oversee a framework for ongoing assessment of collections investments, including transformative licensing efforts. \u00a0 Advance collection initiatives: Serve as PSUL representative to membership organizations (e.g., BTAA) for group purchasing and collection development decision-making; provide leadership on shared collection projects . \u00a0 Maintain scholarly and professional engagement: Participate in relevant professional committees, leadership roles in professional organizations, and scholarly activity and research. \u00a0 The successful candidate is expected to be hired at the rank of Associate Librarian or Librarian and appoint ed with tenure within the University Libraries . Ca ndidates qualified for appointment at the rank of Assistant Librarian will also be considered. \u00a0 Candidates for the rank of Assistant Librarian should possess a graduate degree in library or information studies or other appropriate degree ; must have demonstrated ability as a librarian; and must have shown growth in research and service.\u00a0 \u00a0 Candidate for the rank of Associate Librarian should possess the same qualifications as the Assistant Librarian, demonstrate excellence in librarianship, show evidence of an established reputation in research, and have a strong record of service to the University and the profession. \u00a0 Candidates for the rank of Librarian should possess the same qualifications as the Associate Librarian; demonstrate sustained excellence in librarianship; have achieved a distinguished reputation in research, scholarship, or librarianship accomplishment; and maintain a substantial record of service and leadership to the University, the profession, and/or the broader community. \u00a0 \u00a0 More information about faculty appointments in the University Libraries can be found in the Guideline UL-ACG07 Promotion and Tenure Criteria ( https://libraries.psu.edu/policies/ul-acg07 ). \u00a0 \u00a0 Required Qualifications \u00a0 Master\u2019s degree in library and information science from an ALA-accredited program, or an equivalent combination of advanced degree and relevant professional experience. \u00a0 Five or more years of professional experience in academic or research library collections, acquisitions, or a closely related area. \u00a0 Demonstrated knowledge of collection development principles, practices, and emerging trends in academic and research libraries, including print and electronic resources in all formats. \u00a0 Experience working in a consortia or networked library environment . \u00a0 Experience using data and assessment methods to inform collection decisions, including the ability to collect, analyze, and communicate findings to support strategic planning. \u00a0 Knowledge of open access models, scholarly communication trends, and the evolving scholarly publishing landscape, including transformative and Read & Publish agreements. \u00a0 Demonstrated leadership experience, such as supervisio n, mentoring, chairing cross-departmental committees, teams, a nd initiatives, and/or project management.\u00a0 \u00a0 Strong analytical, written, and oral communication skills, with the ability to effectively collaborate across departments and with external partners. \u00a0 Evidence of active professional engagement, and a record of research, publication , or other scholarly activity. \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications \u00a0 Experience with budget management and financial planning for library collections, including expenditure tracking, projection, and reporting. \u00a0 Knowledge of copyright, fair use, and rights management as applied to library resources and licensing. \u00a0 Experience with deselection , space planning, or physical collection management projects, including shared print or collaborative retention programs. \u00a0 Awareness of emerging technologies and their responsible application in collections work, including AI-assisted tools for collection assessment or resource discovery. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 About the Collection Strategies Department \u00a0 \u00a0 The Collection Strategies Department is a new department result ing from realignment planning at the Penn State University Libraries. This new position will provide strategic direction for collection development at the PSUL and manage ongoing analysis and maintenance of the PSUL\u2019s print collections and electronic holdings. Three units: Collection Analysis , Collection Maintenance, and the Annex , report to this position. This person will work closely with the Head of Acquisitions and Resource Sharing , who also reports to the Associate Dean for Collections and Commonwealth Campus Libraries. The University Libraries 2025-2030 Strategic Plan has prioritized advancing open scholarsh ip and transforming library collections as part of its goal of Empowering Researchers.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 About Penn State\u2019s Collections \u00a0 \u00a0 The P enn State University Libraries holds over 10 million titles , of which, approximately 3.6 million are electronic books. We have collections at all our locations across the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania (800,000 a t Commonweal th Campus Libraries, with the remaining collections on the Univers ity Park campus in State College). The Annex, located in State College, consists of thre e off-site facilities that hold 5.6 million items, including more than 1.3 million print, 4.1 million microforms, 92,000 maps, and 17,000 audiovisual materials .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 We are in the Top 20 Association of Research Libraries for collection size and expenditures . Penn State University Libraries participate in multiple consortia, including BTAA, PALCI, CRL, and HathiTrust . Penn State is one of four State Library Resource Center s (SLRC) included in the Pennsylvania Code t o receive annual funding to provid e resources for all citizens of Pennsylvania. In 2026-2027 Penn State will be migrating its ILS to Alma. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 For more information about Penn State\u2019s budget and collections, please see Library Statistics and Data .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 APPLICATION PROCESS \u00a0 \u00a0 All candidate materials must be submitted via Workday .\u00a0 Applicants should also upload a cover letter and resume or CV and a list of four references . Furnished references must include a current/previous direct supervisor, a colleague, an employee who was/is a direct report, and one at the candidate's discretion. Candidates must clearly identify the relationship for each reference provided. References will be contacted later in the search process. \u00a0 \u00a0 Application materials should demonstrate the candidate\u2019s professional qualifications , including a record of significant accomplishments and excellence in librarianship, teaching, research, and/or service, as well as evidence of sustained professional engagement and contributions to the profession. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Application materials should reflect a commitment to equal opportunity and respect for all individuals. Candidates are encouraged to highlight how their work promotes inclusive access to information and supports the academic mission of the institution. \u00a0 \u00a0 Individual compensation packages are based on various factors unique to each candidate, including a candidate\u2019s qualifications, education, experience, and rank. In addition to a competitive salary, full-time employees also receive a comprehensive benefits program, generous paid time off, and tuition discount for employees and eligible family members. Total Compensation Calculator provides an estimated summary of the value of compensation and benefits. \u00a0 \u00a0 Information about the University Libraries\u2019 employment opportunities, processes, and culture can be found at https://libraries.psu.edu/about/jobs \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Mechanical-Engineering_REQ_0000082453-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mechanical Engineering \u00a0at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar in Battery Mechanics, Physics-Based AI, and Energy Storage Manufacturing under the direction of Dr. Jun Xu. Job Duties: Research: Develop and lead research integrating AI with battery science and engineering; design computational and/or experimental studies; and collaborate with academic, national laboratory, and industry partners. Publications: Lead the preparation of high-quality journal manuscripts and present findings at conferences. Proposal development: Work closely with the PI to identify funding opportunities, develop research concepts, generate preliminary results, and prepare technical proposals. Laboratory management: Help coordinate daily laboratory activities, equipment use and maintenance, research documentation, data and code management, and safety practices. Mentoring and coordination: Mentor graduate and undergraduate students, support project planning, and track research milestones and deliverables. Qualifications and Requirements: A Ph.D. in mechanical engineering, materials science, chemical engineering, electrical engineering, or a closely related field by the start date. Strong expertise in AI/machine learning, demonstrated through substantive research contributions. Experience preparing research proposals, mentoring students, or coordinating laboratory projects. Experience applying AI to batteries, energy storage, materials, or related physical systems. Experience with battery experiments, electrochemical or multiphysics modeling, scientific data infrastructure, or automated research workflows. A strong publication record appropriate to career stage and excellent scientific writing and communication skills. Interested applicants should send the following materials as a single PDF file : Curriculum vitae Brief research statement describing prior research experience and future research interests Representative publications Contact information for three references \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Open-Rank-Professor-in-Supply-Chain-Management_REQ_0000082573-1": {"title": "Open-Rank Professor in Supply Chain Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The S upply Chain & Information Systems (SCIS) Department of the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) invites applications tenure-track position s at the open rank professor level for a Fall 202 7 start date .\u00a0 Salary is competitive. \u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates must have a PhD degree in supply chain management or related field by the appointment start date . Those who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor. \u00a0 A strong commitment to research and teaching excellence is expected .\u00a0 Candidates at the Associate or Full Professor level should have a demonstrated record of high-quality research and teaching commensurate with rank, as well as a sufficient number of publications in high-quality journals and a demonstrated significant impact of their work on the field. Faculty members are expected to maintain an active research program, perform undergraduate and graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in service activities. \u00a0 \u00a0 The SCIS Department comprises a vibrant, research-active faculty with research and teaching interests that traverse the end-to-end supply chain and includes business logistics , sourcing, manufacturing, and service operations. The department offers degree programs in supply chain management, business analytics & information systems, and AI and Business Transformation . We seek outstanding candidates with expertise in supply chain management with an emphasis o n business logistics that would complement the faculty with high-quality research and teaching in student-centered and collaborative learning environments.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 The Smeal College of Business offers a collegial working environment and excellent campus facilities. It has the Center for Supply Chain Research\u00ae ( www.smeal.psu.edu/cscr ) which advances cutting-edge research and outreach in supply chain management. The SC&IS Department ( www.smeal.psu.edu/scis ) also has strong connections with the business community through various research centers that provide opportunities to interface with faculty across various disciplines within Smeal and across Penn State. For more information, please visit www.smeal.psu.edu/research-centers .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Review of applications will begin approximately October 1 , 202 6 and will continue until the position is filled .\u00a0 For further information, please contact Autumn Knepp at adh5253@psu .edu .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Applications should be submitted directly on the Penn State site and include a letter of intent, a statement of research and teaching, and a CV. Contact information for three references also should be provided . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Position---BMB_REQ_0000076780-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Position - BMB", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS A postdoctoral position is available in the research lab of Dr. Tim Miyashiro within the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at The Pennsylvania State University. The Miyashiro lab investigates mechanisms of bacterial colonization of hosts using the squid- Vibrio model system using a range of techniques including animal studies, genomics, and molecular biology. Responsibilities will include providing intellectual leadership in experimental design, execution, and interpretation of results. This person will also assist with writing publications and assuring scientific rigor, consistency, and record keeping within the labs, and is expected to participate in all aspects of the labs, including squid-colonization assays. Candidates must have a background in mass spectrometry-based proteomics, including protein identification, quantitation, and thermal proteome profiling, and in mass spectrometry-based targeted and untargeted metabolomics. In addition, the candidate should have experience with biochemical assays assessing biomolecular interactions. Experience with bacterial genetics and molecular cloning is expected. Applicants must hold a PhD in\u00a0microbiology or equivalent life-sciences field. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted electronically. Qualified candidates should submit the following: a cover letter describing interest a CV outlining background and experience the contact information for three references. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Agile-Systems-Engineering-Department-Head--FACULTY-_REQ_0000082175-2": {"title": "Agile Systems Engineering Department Head (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Your working location will be fully on-site located in State College, PA. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. We are searching for a Department Head for the Agile Systems Engineering Department (ASE) of the Materials, Manufacturing and Sustainment Office (MMSO) at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. The Agile Systems Engineering Department is dedicated to the application and training of systems engineering to support the advancement of warfighter capability at the speed of relevance. The department focuses on the rapid development of complex engineering systems requiring the integration of cross-disciplinary solutions and expertise, including system architecture design, functional analysis, requirements development, and model-based engineering. Additionally, the department has a lead role in workforce development and systems engineering training. This role will lead and manage all aspects of the Agile Systems Engineering Department, providing strategic direction, technical leadership, and operational oversight of a department of approximately 10 people. This leadership position requires a visionary leader capable of building and directing a multidisciplinary team focused on tailored application of systems engineering, model-based engineering, architecture development, and rapid, tailored systems integration. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Lead and manage all aspects of the Agile Systems Engineering Department, providing strategic direction, technical leadership, and operational oversight, personnel management, workforce planning, talent development, and performance evaluation Build and direct a multidisciplinary team focused on the application of systems engineering to a diverse set of programs, technologies and sponsors Mentor systems engineers in applying systems engineering to a variety of complex engineering problems that span levels of technical maturity ranging from early science and technology to system acquisition Support division leadership in developing and maintaining relationships with sponsors in support of meeting funding objectives Lead individual research projects and portfolios including developing technical concepts, writing winning proposals, staffing projects, conducting research, managing budgets, and delivering high-quality results Foster partnerships with U.S. Military Program Offices, defense contractors, systems integrators, and other government laboratories Lead department personnel in developing and delivering training on systems engineering to ARL staff and external partners Foster a culture of innovation, technical excellence, and mission focus Additional responsibilities for the higher-level position includes: Support development of a comprehensive roadmap for embedded systems and integration methodologies pertinent to systems of interest to the division including but not limited to missiles, hypersonics, and uncrewed aerial systems Establish and maintain partnerships with U.S. Military Program Offices, defense contractors, systems integrators, and other government laboratories Build strategic relationships with Defense Industrial Base stakeholders Collaborate across ARL departments and with external stakeholders as a trusted agent in identifying and applying appropriate systems engineering activities for large U.S. Military development programs Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required skills/experience areas include: Leading individual research projects and portfolios including developing technical concepts, writing winning proposals, staffing the project, conducting the research, managing budgets, and delivering high-quality results Past success applying systems engineering techniques for complex system development, with emphasis on streamlined and/or tailored processes System architecture design, functional analysis, requirements development, system decomposition, and flow down of requirements System and interface architecture development and testing Evaluation of communications, messaging, and data architectures Developing logical and physical representative models of system requirements and architectures Developing time-varying physics-based models Model-based approaches to supplement traditional test & evaluation (T&E) methods for more complete and cost-effective verification & validation of system requirements systems engineering challenges in complex systems (e.g., maritime, aerospace, ground vehicles, unmanned systems) Past success in writing white papers or reports Active security clearance, at the Secret level or higher \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/AAC---Literacy-Research-Translation-and-Community-Engagement-Specialist_REQ_0000082171-2": {"title": "AAC & Literacy Research Translation and Community Engagement Specialist", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS This position will lead research dissemination, translation, and community engagement activities within the AAC research program. As a subject-matter expert, the position will translate research findings into accessible, meaningful, and actionable information for AAC users, families, educators, clinicians, administrators, researchers, and community stakeholders. The position will independently develop and implement dissemination strategies and create research products for websites, social media, presentations, webinars, and other community-facing platforms. The position will also build collaborative relationships with AAC users and families, schools, educators, clinicians, administrators, and other service providers and independently conduct research-related data-collection activities to understand community needs and perspectives and inform research translation efforts. Professional experience working with AAC users and implementing literacy instruction in school and community settings is an essential research competency for this position. This is a limited-term position funded for one year from date of hire with excellent possibility of refunding. PRIMARY DUTIES 1. Research Dissemination & Translation Translate AAC and literacy research into clear, accessible, actionable resources. Develop and implement dissemination strategies for diverse audiences. Adapt research findings for AAC users, families, educators, clinicians, administrators, researchers, and community stakeholders. Apply professional expertise in AAC and literacy to guide research translation. 2. Community Engagement & Outreach Build and maintain relationships with AAC users, families, schools, educators, clinicians, and administrators. Identify stakeholder needs, priorities, barriers, and facilitators. Ensure research products are relevant, accessible, and responsive to the AAC community. Provide practice-based expertise to inform research and implementation. 3. Research & Community-Engaged Data Collection Conduct interviews, focus groups, surveys, observations, and other research data-collection activities. Develop data-collection materials and protocols with research investigators. Recruit and engage research participants and manage collected data. Contribute to analysis and interpretation of stakeholder perspectives and implementation experiences. 4. Digital Dissemination & Professional Outreach Develop and maintain research-informed websites and digital resources. Create materials for families, AAC users, educators, clinicians, and community stakeholders. Conduct presentations, workshops, webinars, and conference activities. Share AAC and literacy research findings and evidence-based practices with professional and community audiences. 5. Research Collaboration & Dissemination Evaluation Collaborate with principal investigators and research teams to identify findings ready for dissemination. Contribute to grant dissemination plans, reports, manuscripts, presentations, and conference materials. Track dissemination activities, products, audiences, and stakeholder engagement. Collect and evaluate data on the reach, use, and impact of dissemination efforts. This position will involve travel to various research sites and on campus work for about 1 week a month. APPLICATION Interested candidates should submit a curriculum vitae, a cover letter describing their interest in the position and qualifications for the role, and contact information for three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, beginning October 9th and will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position or application process may be directed to Dr. Jessica Caron at jgc169@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Department-of-Engineering-Science-and-Mechanics--College-of-Engineering_REQ_0000082013-1": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor - Department of Engineering Science and Mechanics, College of Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Penn State's College of Engineering is seeking candidates for an Assistant Research Professor within the Department of Engineering Science and Mechanics. The Assistant Research Professor will conduct research on two-dimensional materials and next-generation semiconductor devices, with emphasis on scalable 2D FETs and CMOS, interface/contact and high-k gate-stack engineering, and monolithic 3D integration. Responsibilities include materials and process development; cleanroom micro/nanofabrication; dielectric and metal-contact integration; electrical characterization and data analysis; design and evaluation of devices and circuits; documentation and publication of research results; participation in collaborative research and proposal development; and mentoring/training of students in laboratory procedures. \u00a0 Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Engineering Science, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Physics, or a closely related discipline. Candidates should have demonstrated research experience in 2D semiconductor devices and nanoscale fabrication. Preferred experience includes MOCVD/CVD growth or 2D material transfer, photolithography/e-beam lithography, thin-film deposition, ALD, etching, semiconductor device characterization, MATLAB/Python-based data analysis, peer-reviewed scientific publication, and collaborative research. \u00a0 Compensation will be determined based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications and relevant experience. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Distributed-Acoustic-Sensing-and-Machine-Learning_REQ_0000082208-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor \u2013 Distributed Acoustic Sensing and Machine Learning", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Research Assistant Professor \u2013 Distributed Acoustic Sensing and Machine Learning The Department of Geosciences at Penn State seeks a Research Assistant Professor to support a project developing machine-learning methods for seismic source characterization using distributed acoustic sensing (DAS). The successful candidate will conduct physics-based wavefield simulations, generate synthetic DAS datasets, develop deep-learning models for seismic event detection, location, and full moment-tensor estimation, and validate these methods using field observations from earthquakes and controlled-source experiments. The position will also contribute to publications, project reports, student mentoring, and collaborations with university and national-laboratory partners. Requirements Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in geophysics, seismology, applied mathematics, computer science, or a related field by the date of hire. Experience in DAS, seismic modeling, moment-tensor inversion, machine learning, scientific programming, and high-performance computing is highly desirable. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000082026-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Concrete Durability and Sensing", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Post-Doctoral Positions \u2013 Concrete Durability and Sensing \u2013 Rajabipour\u2019s Group Dr. Farshad Rajabipour\u2019s research group in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) at Penn State invites applications for two post-doctoral scholar positions. One position will be focused on developing and deploying a pore solution resistivity/pH sensor for assessing concrete quality and durability. The second position focuses on prediction and mitigation of alkali-silica reaction (ASR) in concrete. Rajabipour\u2019s group leads cutting-edge research in areas of concrete decarbonization, utilization of marginal and nonconventional pozzolans, durability and service life extension of concrete infrastructure, biochar-augmented concrete, and ultra-high-performance concrete. The postdoctoral positions offer exceptional opportunities for leadership and collaboration across these research domains, including partnerships with academic and industrial R&D teams both in the U.S. and internationally. Dr. Rajabipour seeks highly motivated and knowledgeable candidates eager to expand their expertise while contributing to the management and execution of research projects and mentoring of graduate students. The required qualifications are: PhD degree in Civil Engineering, Materials Science, Chemical Engineering, or related field Extensive research experience related to concrete materials and their characterization Strong track record in scientific contributions supported by peer-reviewed publications Strong communication and interpersonal skills To apply, please submit a single PDF file (5MB max) that includes: a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, and the contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Dr. Rajabipour at fxr10@psu.edu or +1-814-863-0601. CEE and Dr. Rajabipour are committed to effective mentorship and growth of postdocs. The selected candidates will join a highly collaborative team of faculty and researchers within CEE\u2019s Materials Innovation Studio, the Civil Infrastructure Testing and Evaluation Lab , the Additive Construction Lab , and the Materials Research Institute . Teaching opportunities may be available depending on the candidate\u2019s interest. Additional resources and career development opportunities are available through the Office of Postdoctoral Affairs . The position is housed within the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and the Larson Transportation Institute at Penn State. CEE\u2019s vision is to achieve the highest quality of life for all, through sustainable and resilient civil infrastructure systems. CEE faculty lead pioneering research in five key areas: Safe and equitable transportation systems; Water, environment, and sustainability; Infrastructure resilience and adaptation; Decarbonization of the built environment; and AI for water security, infrastructure, and innovation. CEE is a vibrant and dynamic unit with 36 faculty members, 16 staff members, more than 470 undergraduate students, and more than 90 graduate students and postdocs. Our programs are highly ranked by the U.S. News and World Report with top 15 and top 20 national rankings at the undergraduate and graduate levels, respectively. CEE is home to outstanding faculty members, including 7 NSF CAREER Award recipients and a member of the National Academy of Engineering. In Fall 2024, CEE moved to the new, LEED certified, Engineering Collaborative Research and Education (ECoRE) building, featuring 9 active-learning classrooms and 51,000 square feet in support of research with state-of-the-art laboratories. Please see https://www.cee.psu.edu/ for additional information about the department. The College of Engineering at Penn State prepares current and future generations for impactful careers as practicing engineers, managers, researchers, educators, and community leaders through highly ranked residential and online programs. We provide innovative educational experiences and supportive programs designed to foster a more welcoming community. In collaboration with industry, non-profit organizations, governmental agencies, and other academic institutions and partners, our faculty lead research initiatives across all areas of engineering that create jobs, fuel economic growth, inform policy, solve global problems, and positively impact humanity. This position is located in State College, Pennsylvania, which has been repeatedly voted as one of the most desirable and safest places to live in the United States. State College fosters a vibrant, diverse, and sustainable community. The region hosts outstanding public schools, reasonable housing costs, a calendar of social and cultural events, and abundant outdoor recreation opportunities. State College is served by a regional airport and is within driving distance to Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, Washington DC, Baltimore, and New York City. Please see https://www.statecollegepa.us/ for more information.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor-of-Philosophy--Philosophy-Department_REQ_0000082425-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy, Philosophy Department", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Philosophy Department at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position, at the rank of Assistant Professor with a specialization in \u00a0 the ethical and philosophical questions raised by artificial intelligence (AI ethics). \u00a0 Candidates must have \u00a0 demonstrated \u00a0 ability as a researcher, scholar, and teacher in AI ethics, and have evidence of growth in scholarly achievement. \u00a0 The Department hopes candidates will be able to develop curriculum related to AI ethics for general education, the major, and other university-wide initiatives. \u00a0 The \u00a0 anticipated \u00a0 start date for this position is Fall 2027 , \u00a0 with flexibility . \u00a0 \u00a0 A Ph.D. in \u00a0 philosophy \u00a0 or related field is required by the appointment date. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. \u00a0 The position will include residential and online instruction and normal university service. \u00a0 In-person \u00a0 teaching is an essential function of this job. \u00a0 \u00a0 Penn State\u2019s Department of Philosophy \u00a0 teaching and research strengths \u00a0 include: \u00a0 continental philosophy , \u00a0 critical philosophy of race , \u00a0 feminist philosophy, \u00a0 the history of philosophy , \u00a0 Latin American philosophy, and critical theory. \u00a0 \u00a0 The successful candidate will hold a 50% appointment \u00a0 in \u00a0 the Rock Ethics Institute ( https://rockethics.psu.edu ). Based in the College of the Liberal Arts, the Institute pursues a university-wide mission of promoting interdisciplinary and engaged ethics research and ethical leadership, with research strengths in the ethical dimensions of agriculture and food, artificial intelligence, citizenship and immigration, climate and sustainability, criminal justice and policing, empathy and moral psychology, engineering, gender and sexuality, health, race, and technology. The Institute seeks candidates who will be effective in working on and leading interdisciplinary teams that embed ethical analysis into research projects and who have experience and interest in integrating ethics into undergraduate and graduate curricula. \u00a0 The standard teaching load during the academic year is four courses per academic year. \u00a0 \u00a0 However, t he successful candidate will receive \u00a0 one \u00a0 course release \u00a0 each year \u00a0 for the first five years for enhancing existing ethics research and curricular initiatives as well as building new initiatives and programs aligned with the Institute\u2019s mission. \u00a0 Interested candidates must \u00a0 submit \u00a0 an online application at \u00a0 Penn State's Job Posting Board , \u00a0 and should upload the following application materials electronically: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information. \u00a0 Review of applications will be gin on October 17, \u00a0 2026 \u00a0 and will continue \u00a0 until \u00a0 filled. \u00a0 Inquiries may be directed to the search chair, \u00a0 Nancy Tuana, DuPont/Class of 1949 Professor of Philosophy and Women \u2019s , Gender, and Sexuality Studies \u00a0 at \u00a0 ntuana@psu.edu. \u00a0 \u00a0 Visit our website at \u00a0 https://philosophy.la.psu.edu/ \u00a0 for more information on our \u00a0 Philosophy Department . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Business-Librarian_REQ_0000081675-1": {"title": "Business Librarian", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University Libraries invite applications and nominations for Business Librarian (Assistant/Associate Librarian) at its University Park Campus. We seek a proactive and creative candidate for a tenure-track faculty position in the Schreyer Business Library https://libraries.psu.edu/business .\u00a0 The candidate will serve as the subject specialist and liaison for the Department of Economics in the College of the Liberal Arts ( https://la.psu.edu/ ) and the Departments of Accounting, Finance, and Risk Management in the Smeal College of Business ( https://www.smeal.psu.edu/ ). In addition, this librarian will assist with the unit\u2019s work with foundational business courses. Successful candidates will benefit from the strong mentoring program developed by the University Libraries to support new faculty in tenure-track appointments in fulfilling expectations in the areas of librarianship, research, and service. The University Libraries welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds and identities who are excited to support business and economics research and learning. \u00a0Early career professionals are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: The Business Librarian serves with a team of other subject specialists in related fields, reports to the Head of the Schreyer Business Library, and is responsible for Economics, Accounting, Finance, Risk Management, and related subject areas in the following categories:\u00a0 Design and deliver a program of library instruction (including the development of online library guides and tutorials) that supports the curriculum of liaison academic units.\u00a0 Provide reference assistance and research consulting (both face-to-face and online) for subject-specific research at all levels.\u00a0 Build, maintain, and assess collections in all media and formats to support research and teaching in assigned academic units.\u00a0 Collaborate and coordinate with librarians in related subject areas and libraries, including Commonwealth Campus Libraries (CCLs) and peers through the Big Ten Academic Alliance (BTAA).\u00a0 Participate in the intellectual life and operations of assigned academic units; engage with faculty and students as a colleague in both disciplinary activities and in library services; and serve as liaison to centers affiliated with assigned academic units.\u00a0 Contribute to the advancement of Penn State Libraries\u2019 programs for scholarly communication, open access (OA) initiatives, and open educational resources (OER). Engage in research, scholarly publication, and professional service\u00a0activities in areas appropriate to academic librarianship and the disciplines served.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Perform other duties as assigned.\u00a0\u00a0 Required Qualifications:\u00a0\u00a0 Masters of Library Science degree from an ALA-accredited institution (or relevant graduate degree)\u00a0 Instruction and/or reference experience in an academic, special, or research library Ability to work independently and collaboratively\u00a0 Commitment to fostering an equitable and inclusive workplace\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Potential to achieve the requirements for tenure and promotion in the areas of librarianship, research, and service\u00a0 Effective oral and written communication and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications:\u00a0\u00a0 Experience in business librarianship Demonstrated experience or education working with business, economics, or related information sources Familiarity with business information sources Experience finding and using economic, financial, and related data to support research Academic Rank: Candidates for the rank of Assistant Librarian should possess a graduate degree in library or information studies or other appropriate degree; must have demonstrated potential ability as a librarian; and must have shown promise of growth in research and service. Candidates for the rank of Associate Librarian should possess the same qualifications as the assistant librarian, demonstrate excellence in librarianship, show evidence of an established reputation in research, and have a strong record of service to the University and the profession. More information can be found in the Guideline for Promotion and Tenure Criteria https://libraries.psu.edu/policies/ul-acg07 .\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Application Process\u00a0 All candidate materials must be submitted via Workday. Interested candidates are expected to upload a resume or CV, cover letter and a list of three professional references. Cover letter and other application materials should demonstrate the candidate\u2019s interest in business librarianship, as well as their professional qualifications, experience, and contributions to librarianship, teaching, research, and/or service. Application materials should reflect a commitment to equal opportunity and respect for all individuals. Candidates are encouraged to highlight how their work promotes inclusive access to information and supports the academic mission of the institution. References will be contacted later in the search process. While furnished references are at the candidate\u2019s discretion, references must include a current/previous direct supervisor, a colleague, and one at the candidate's discretion. Candidates must clearly identify the relationship for each reference provided. All references must be submitted at the time of application submission.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director--McCourtney-Institute-for-Democracy--and-Associate-Professor-Professor-in-the-College-of-the-Liberal-Arts--Penn-State_REQ_0000082100-1": {"title": "Director, McCourtney Institute for Democracy, and Associate Professor/Professor in the College of the Liberal Arts, Penn State", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University, College of the Liberal Arts, in University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for the position of Director of the McCourtney Institute for Democracy , which will be filled at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with tenure within an appropriate academic department within the College. The anticipated start date is Fall 2027, with flexibility. \u00a0 The McCourtney Institute for Democracy promotes scholarship and practical innovations to understand, preserve, and advance democracy. Through research, teaching, and public outreach, the Institute leverages the resources of Penn State and the College of the Liberal Arts to conduct research on democracy and society, defend democratic practices, and foster democratic citizenship and educate for democratic engagement. \u00a0 Some of the regular activities of the Center include awarding the Brown Democracy Medal annually, publishing the Podcast \u201cDemocracy Works,\u201d providing funding to support for faculty and student research, recruiting students in the Nevins Fellows program, and connecting with other institutions studying democracy. The institute supports two research centers, the Center for Democratic Deliberation and the Center for Research on Democratic Resilience. \u00a0 We seek a thoughtful Director who will lead the Center administratively and intellectually by supporting rigorous research on democracy, expanding the connections and research activities of the Center around campus, devising new research and outreach initiatives, engaging alumni to support the Center, growing the community of scholars engaged with the Center, and maintaining current signature activities. \u00a0 The Director manages four Institute staff (the managing director, communications specialist, podcast group manager, and administrative assistant). \u00a0 The Director will be expected to maintain an active research agenda and to be part of their academic unit and disciplinary community. A teaching release and supplement will be provided during the successful candidate\u2019s term as Director. \u00a0 Candidates for the Director of the Institute (Associate Professor rank) must have demonstrated excellence as a researcher, scholar, and teacher in a relevant field and have an established reputation in scholarly achievement. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Candidates for the Director of the Institute (Professor rank) must have demonstrated excellence as a researcher, scholar, and teacher in a relevant field, and evidence of a substantial record of advanced research as well as leadership in their field of specialization. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. \u00a0 Qualified applicants for both ranks will have a Ph.D. in a relevant humanities or social science discipline by date of appointment. \u00a0 For both ranks, an applicant\u2019s research should align with the Institute\u2019s interest in promoting research and knowledge about democracy in the United States or global context, broadly defined. Candidates should have an excellent publication record in their field; a commitment to securing external funding; a commitment to working with alumni and development; and a track record of excellence in teaching, mentoring, and academic service. Successful candidates must demonstrate experience in developing and maintaining institutionally sustainable research centers or other initiatives, and the ability to productively engage and support the research of scholars from other disciplines. \u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants must apply online at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board and should include a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, and a list of three references. In the cover letter, applicants should discuss their experience in managing, creating, or supervising academic programs or research centers, as well as in pursuing external funding. They should also discuss their vision of a research center centered around the mission described above. \u00a0 We will request letters of recommendation and teaching materials from candidates who advance in the search process. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026, and will continue until the position has been filled. \u00a0 Please direct questions about the process via email to one of the committee co-chairs (Scott Bennett, Senior Associate Dean for Research and Graduate Studies, sbennett@psu.edu ; Amy Allen, Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs and Advancement, ara17@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000082301-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Kovac Laboratory in the Department of Food Science at The Pennsylvania State University seeks a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to lead research on the prevention of cereulide contamination in infant formula and fermentation-derived food ingredients. The successful candidate will work on a multidisciplinary project focused on improving detection of cereulide-producing Bacillus cereus , understanding factors driving cereulide formation in industrial fermentation systems, and contributing to the development of quantitative microbial risk assessment models to support industry and regulatory decision-making. The Postdoctoral Scholar will play a central role in experimental design, laboratory research, data analysis, project coordination, publication development, mentoring trainees, and communication with collaborators. Major Responsibilities Research and Laboratory Activities Lead and conduct independent research aligned with project objectives. Perform microbiological analyses involving isolation, cultivation, enumeration, characterization, and preservation of Bacillus cereus group isolates. Develop, validate, and optimize culture-based and molecular detection methods for emetic B. cereus . Conduct experiments evaluating microbial growth, toxin production, and survival under conditions relevant to infant formula and industrial fermentation systems. Conduct whole genome sequencing and sequence data analyses. Design and execute challenge studies and storage studies involving foodborne pathogens and spoilage microorganisms. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety protocols, biosafety procedures, and quality assurance practices. Maintain detailed laboratory records and support data reproducibility and research integrity. Data Analysis and Risk Modeling Manage, organize, and analyze large microbiological and experimental datasets. Perform statistical analyses using R or similar software. Support the development of predictive microbiology and quantitative microbial risk assessment (QMRA) models. Generate figures, tables, and visualizations suitable for scientific publications, reports, and presentations. Contribute to data integration across laboratory, environmental, and risk modeling components of the project. Assist with development of decision-support tools for industry and regulatory stakeholders. Conduct whole genome sequence analyses. Project Management and Coordination Coordinate project activities across collaborating institutions and industry partners. Assist in tracking project milestones, deliverables, and timelines. Organize and document project meetings, prepare agendas, and distribute meeting summaries and action items. Contribute to annual reports, progress reports, and sponsor-required deliverables. Maintain organized project documentation and data management systems. Facilitate communication among project participants and external collaborators. Scientific Writing and Dissemination Lead and co-author peer-reviewed scientific publications. Prepare conference abstracts, posters, oral presentations, and extension materials. Contribute to grant proposals, progress reports, and technical reports. Present research findings at national and international scientific meetings. Communicate scientific findings to academic, industry, and stakeholder audiences. Mentoring and Laboratory Leadership Mentor undergraduate researchers, graduate students, and visiting scholars. Provide training in microbiological techniques, laboratory safety, data analysis, and research best practices. Supervise undergraduate research projects and assist with student professional development. Foster a collaborative and productive laboratory environment. Contribute to onboarding and training of new laboratory personnel. Laboratory Operations Assist with laboratory organization, equipment maintenance, and inventory management. Coordinate purchasing of laboratory supplies and reagents. Monitor laboratory resources and ensure continuity of research activities. Contribute to development and maintenance of laboratory standard operating procedures (SOPs). Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Food Science, Microbiology, Biotechnology, Biological Engineering or a closely related field. Strong research background in food microbiology, microbial ecology, food safety, or related disciplines. Experience working with bacterial pathogens and standard microbiological techniques. Demonstrated ability to design experiments and independently conduct research. Experience analyzing large datasets and applying statistical methods. Record of peer-reviewed publications. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Strong organizational, project management, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently while contributing to multidisciplinary teams. Demonstrated commitment to mentoring and collaborative research. Preferred Qualifications Experience with Bacillus cereus , spore-forming bacteria, foodborne pathogens, or toxin-producing microorganisms. Experience with molecular methods such as PCR, qPCR, genomic analyses, or sequencing-based approaches. Experience with microbial risk assessment, predictive microbiology, or mathematical modeling. Proficiency in R and/or Python for statistical analysis and data visualization. Experience with food manufacturing, fermentation systems, or food processing environments. Familiarity with analytical chemistry techniques used for toxin detection. Prior experience coordinating multi-investigator or industry-partnered research projects. Experience supervising or mentoring undergraduate researchers. Desired Professional Attributes The ideal candidate will be scientifically curious, highly organized, and capable of balancing multiple project components simultaneously. Successful candidates will demonstrate initiative, attention to detail, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to manage complex projects while maintaining high standards of scientific rigor. The ability to collaborate effectively with academic researchers, industry partners, students, and regulatory stakeholders is essential. Expected Outcomes The Postdoctoral Scholar will have the opportunity to lead high-impact research addressing an emerging food safety issue with direct relevance to infant health, contribute to the development of new detection and risk assessment tools, publish in leading food safety journals, build an independent research portfolio, and gain experience managing multidisciplinary collaborative projects. Application Process Candidates should apply online at https://hr.psu.edu/careers and should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for three references . Application material should be addressed to Dr. Jasna Kovac ( jzk303@psu.edu ) . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor-of-Agribusiness-Management_REQ_0000082133-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Agribusiness Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Agricultural Economics, Sociology, and Education (AESE) in the College of Agricultural Sciences at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park campus) invites candidates to apply for an Assistant Professor of Agribusiness Management position. This is a full-time, 36-week, tenure-track appointment with a 60% teaching and 40% Extension appointment. The successful candidate will be expected to teach five 3-credit courses per year in the Agribusiness Management (AGBM) undergraduate program. Most of these courses will be taught online via Penn State\u2019s World Campus program, though some may be taught in person at Penn State\u2019s University Park campus. Potential course topics include agricultural market and price analysis, agribusiness finance, managing the food system, food product marketing, and economic principles applied to agriculture and the food system. The successful candidate will be expected to advise and mentor undergraduate students, including professional development for future employment in industry. The successful candidate will also be expected to develop a nationally and internationally recognized Extension program on agribusiness management that enhances the university\u2019s engagement with the agricultural industry in Pennsylvania. Pertinent Extension topics may include price and income risk management, agricultural products and markets, smart ag technologies, and related areas. The successful candidate will be expected to secure external funding to support their Extension program. Qualifications: Doctorate in agricultural economics, agribusiness, or a related economics or business field. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. Experience in agriculture, agribusiness, or the food industry is preferred. Applicants should demonstrate excellent communication skills and the ability to work in multi-disciplinary teams. The ability to engage professionally with an inclusive population of faculty, staff, students, and Extension audiences is required, and the successful candidate will actively strive to provide an inclusive learning environment for all. Application Requirements: Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026, with a start date of July 1, 2027, or as negotiated. Candidates should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, names and contact information for three references, a writing sample, a statement of teaching/pedagogy related to the position description, and a statement of Extension vision and philosophy related to the position description. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Questions can be directed to the Search Committee chair: Ted Jaenicke ( ecj3@psu.edu ). AESE is a welcoming community with our scholarship focusing on people, society, and economic systems grounded in theory and methods from the social, economic, and behavioral sciences. Faculty and students develop and employ rigorous approaches to discover fundamental and applied principles that advance science in their core disciplines. AESE strives to improve the health, prosperity, and welfare of people in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania and beyond. Our core areas for teaching and research are (1) Agricultural and Food Systems, (2) Community Development and Engagement, (3) Environment and Natural Resources, and (4) Population Processes in Global Perspective. The Department offers three resident and one online graduate programs and oversees four undergraduate majors. For more information visit our site at https://aese.psu.edu/ . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Professor--Tenure-Track--in-Department-of-Sociology---Criminology_REQ_0000082241-1": {"title": "Associate Professor (Tenure-Track) in Department of Sociology & Criminology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Sociology and Criminology at The Pennsylvania State University, in University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position, at the rank of Associate Professor, to start in Fall 2027, with flexibility. A Ph.D. in Sociology or related field is required by the appointment date. Candidates for Associate Professor of Sociology must have demonstrated excellence as a researcher, scholar, and teacher, and have an established reputation of scholarly achievement. Responsibilities and Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. The successful candidate will have expertise in social psychological approaches to studying groups, communities and social networks and will be able to use experimental and survey methodology in their scholarship. The successful candidate will also have experience teaching undergraduate and graduate-level theory and social psychology courses and be able to teach other courses offered by the university. Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information. Inquiries may be directed to sociology@psu.edu . Visit our website at sociology.la.psu.edu for more information on our Department. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor--Tenure-Track---Department-of-Sociology---Criminology_REQ_0000082237": {"title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track), Department of Sociology & Criminology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Sociology and Criminology at The Pennsylvania State University, in University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position, at the rank of Assistant Professor, to start in Fall 2027, with flexibility. A Ph.D. in Sociology, or related field, is required by the appointment date. Candidates for Assistant Professor must have demonstrated ability as a researcher, scholar, and teacher and have evidence of growth in scholarly achievement. Duties and responsibilities for assistant professor candidates include a combination of research, service, and teaching. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. The successful candidate will have expertise in population-based approaches to aging, broadly defined. Their academic portfolio will also fit with the mission of the aging initiative being supported by the College of Liberal Arts and other units on campus,\u00a0including the Social Science Research Institute (SSRI). The initiative includes a focus on federally funded aging research. Thus,\u00a0candidates should be grant-active or show strong evidence of external funding potential. Successful candidates will also strengthen the Department and College, and contribute to SSRI\u2019s mission, which is to foster novel, interdisciplinary collaborative research that addresses critical human and social problems. Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information. Inquiries may be directed to sociology@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 15 and continue until the position is filled. Visit our website at sociology.la.psu.edu for more information about the department. Visit the SSRI website for more information about the Institute. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Colby-Group---Materials-Science-and-Engineering_REQ_0000082176-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Colby Group - Materials Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences is seeking a postdoctoral scholar. The final candidate will run and maintain two Novocontrol dielectric spectrometers. They will train new users and supervise both graduate and undergraduate students in properly loading their sample, running the experiments, and interpreting the data. A particular research emphasis will be zwitterions mixed with polymers. Requirements Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Physics, or a related field. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Law-Group---Materials-Science-and-Engineering_REQ_0000082214-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Law Group - Materials Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences is searching for a postdoctoral scholar. The position will involve machine learning for autonomous thin-film materials synthesis by molecular beam epitaxy (MBE). This work will be performed as part of LATTICE (Layered and Thin Film Technologies with Intelligent Cloud Experimentation), a National Science Foundation Programmable Cloud Laboratory at the Pennsylvania State University\u2019s University Park campus.\u00a0The postdoctoral scholar will help integrate existing III-V and chalcogenide MBE systems into the LATTICE ecosystem, with emphasis on in situ feedback and control, autonomous operation of deposition tools, and AI/ML workflows for synthesis and characterization. The scholar will also support integration of experimental data and model outputs into the Lifetime Sample Tracking database and contribute to cloud-lab interfaces for external users of the LATTICE platform. This position will involve close collaboration with equipment vendors, AI researchers developing agentic workflow frameworks, data scientists, and future users of the LATTICE cloud laboratory. Requirements Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Physics, or a related field. Hands-on experience with molecular beam epitaxy synthesis is required.\u00a0 Preferred\u00a0 Experience with chalcogenide, two-dimensional, and/or III-V semiconductor materials is preferred. Programming experience in Python or experience with machine automation or AI/ML workflows will be an advantage. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Post-Doc-position-in-AI--Knowledge-Graphs---Digital-Twins-for-Engineering-and-Construction_REQ_0000082238": {"title": "Post-Doc position in AI, Knowledge Graphs & Digital Twins for Engineering and Construction", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The DII Lab at Penn State (College of Engineering) is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to conduct research at the intersection of artificial intelligence, digital twins, engineering informatics, and intelligent construction. Potential research topics include: AI agents and large language models for engineering applications Knowledge graphs and graph-based reasoning BIM / IFC and digital twins Engineering requirement formalization and traceability Construction planning, scheduling, and constraint reasoning Automated verification and engineering decision support Dependency and impact analysis Integration of design, manufacturing, construction, and verification information Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in engineering, computer science, or a closely related field, completed by the start date Strong research and programming background Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research Strong scholarly publication record Strong written and oral communication skills Experience in one or more of the following is particularly desirable: AI/ML LLMs/AI Agents Knowledge Graphs BIM/IFC Digital Twins Graph Neural Networks Construction Informatics Semantic Modeling Engineering Data Integration Start Date: As soon as possible Location: Penn State University Park, Pennsylvania Appointment: Full-time Postdoctoral Scholar How to Apply Please submit the following materials: Curriculum Vitae Brief statement of research experience and interests 1\u20132 representative publications Contact information for three references Immediate availability for an on-site appointment is strongly preferred. Applications will be reviewed immediately and on a rolling basis until the position is filled. JOIN US to develop next-generation AI-enabled engineering systems connecting knowledge, digital models, and physical construction. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/XMLNAME-2DCC-Operations-Director_REQ_0000082065-2": {"title": "2DCC Operations Director", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Materials Research Institute at The Pennsylvania State University seeks outstanding applicants for an Operations Director to provide management and operational leadership for the Two-Dimensional Crystal Consortium (2DCC) Materials Innovation Platform, a national user facility supported primarily by the National Science Foundation. This position will be filled at the Research Faculty position ( Researcher, Assistant Research Professor, Associate Research Professor, or Research Professor ). \u00a0 The 2DCC comprises three state-of-the-art user facilities: (1) Thin Films and In Situ Characterization; (2) Bulk Crystal Growth; and (3) Theory, Simulation and Data Science. These integrated facilities are focused on advancing the synthesis science of layered chalcogenide films and bulk crystals and related two-dimensional (2D) materials for next-generation nanoelectronic and quantum technologies. The 2DCC provides researchers from universities, federal laboratories, and industry with specialized equipment, expertise, data resources, and collaborative support to discover and develop advanced materials and help maintain U.S. leadership in electronic materials, devices, and component technologies.\u00a0 The Operations Director will work closely with the Platform Director, Associate Director, and Executive Leadership Team to provide day-to-day management of Platform activities. The position has broad responsibility for budget oversight, user-program administration, personnel supervision, data and reporting systems, communications and marketing, education and outreach, assessment, and facilities coordination. The Operations Director will also help expand the Platform\u2019s research and user communities by coordinating targeted funding opportunities and supporting external-user identification, engagement, and scientific and technical success.\u00a0 Key Responsibilities \u00a0 Leadership and General Management\u00a0 Provide day-to-day operational and administrative leadership across the 2DCC and coordinate activities among its user facilities.\u00a0 Organize regular meetings of the Executive Leadership Team and External Advisory Board; prepare information and follow through on decisions and action items.\u00a0 Provide data, analysis, and recommendations to support strategic planning and decision-making by the Platform Director and leadership team.\u00a0 Serve as a 2DCC representative at appropriate institute, and University-wide meetings.\u00a0 Manage projects and other initiatives assigned by the Platform Director and leadership team.\u00a0 User Programs and Training\u00a0 Coordinate with the Director of User Engagement and Training to provide a high level of customer service and sufficient technical understanding to assist faculty and external users, identify areas for improvement, recommend solutions, and coordinate specialized scientific support as needed.\u00a0 Support effective interactions with an interdisciplinary community of researchers from universities, federal laboratories, and industry.\u00a0 Coordinate user-facility management activities, including review and updating of user fees, analytical costs, and related procedures.\u00a0 Personnel Management \u00a0 Supervise assigned administrative and technical staff and coordinate their work in support of Platform objectives.\u00a0 Assist the Platform Director and leadership team in recruitment, hiring and onboarding of facility staff. \u00a0 Assist the Platform Director in developing staffing plans and recommendations for staff and research-level advancement.\u00a0 Budget, Administration, and Reporting\u00a0 Manage core facility accounts and sponsored research budgets, prepare financial analyses, and coordinate and implement financial strategies that support strategic priorities and cost-effective facility operations.\u00a0 Review and approve 2DCC purchasing in coordination with the 2DCC admin support coordinator.\u00a0 Support government grant and contract administration, including post-award management, compliance, documentation, and coordination with appropriate University offices.\u00a0 Coordinate collection, management, and analysis of operational, user, financial, and assessment data.\u00a0 Lead or assist with agency and internal reporting, including quarterly reporting, annual reports, site visits and reviews, presentations, and other sponsor requirements.\u00a0 Use relevant facilities and administrative systems to generate reports, analyze performance, track space use as appropriate, and make evidence-based recommendations.\u00a0 Communications, Marketing, and Outreach\u00a0 Identify potential external users and partners and maintain organized information to support sustained engagement.\u00a0 Develop a working knowledge of 2DCC capabilities and relevant Penn State faculty expertise to connect external users with the resources needed for successful projects.\u00a0 Communicate Platform opportunities, activities, research successes, and educational programs to current and prospective users and other stakeholders.\u00a0 Assist Director of User Training and Engagement to organize and coordinate relevant conferences, workshops, seminars, user meetings, training events, and other education and outreach activities.\u00a0 Facilities, Infrastructure, and Safety \u00a0 Coordinate with Materials Research Institute leadership and facility directors on building activities, space needs, equipment and infrastructure issues, and operational continuity.\u00a0 Maintain awareness of and help ensure compliance with applicable University, government, sponsor, safety, and regulatory requirements.\u00a0 Represent the 2DCC on the Materials Research Institute safety committee and work with safety personnel to communicate and implement safety policies and initiatives.\u00a0 Coordinate operational decisions and tracking related to hazardous-material and hazardous-waste management, storage, and disposal, and support corrective and preventive actions.\u00a0 Required Qualifications\u00a0 An advanced degree in physics, materials science and engineering, chemical engineering, electrical engineering, chemistry, or a related science or engineering field. A Ph.D. is preferred; highly qualified candidates with an M.S. degree will also be considered.\u00a0 At least five years of relevant experience, including a strong record of project, program, research center, and/or facility management.\u00a0 Demonstrated experience managing personnel and coordinating a project team.\u00a0 Excellent organizational, time-management, written communication, oral communication, and interpersonal skills.\u00a0 Demonstrated ability to work effectively with interdisciplinary technical teams, and institutional leaders. \u00a0 Ability to manage multiple complex priorities with sound judgment, attention to detail, accountability, and a strong service orientation.\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications\u00a0 Hands-on technical experience or strong technical familiarity with thin-film deposition, bulk crystal growth, semiconductor processing, materials characterization, theory and simulation, data science, or a closely related field.\u00a0 Experience with government grant or contract solicitation, proposal development, post-award management, sponsor reporting, and site reviews.\u00a0 Experience managing budgets, user programs, research facilities, safety and regulatory requirements, or scientific data and assessment systems.\u00a0 Experience developing external partnerships, user communities, scientific communications, workshops, conferences, education programs, or outreach activities.\u00a0 Application Information \u00a0 The position is fully in office, and no hybrid option is offered. Candidates should submit a curriculum vitae or r\u00e9sum\u00e9; a cover letter summarizing relevant skills and experience; and contact information for three professional references, including name, position title, mailing address, telephone number, and email address. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This is a fixed-term appointment with an excellent possibility of renewal, contingent upon continued funding.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Time-Domain-and-Multi-Messenger-Astrophysics_REQ_0000082049-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor - Time Domain and Multi-Messenger Astrophysics", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Astronomy and Astrophysics at Penn State invites applications for an Assistant Research Professor position to work with Professor Jimmy DeLaunay and collaborators. The successful applicant will work with the Fermi GBM and Swift-BAT GUANO teams to search for hard X-ray to gamma-ray transients in real-time as well as archivally over the decades of Fermi\u2019s and Swift\u2019s lifetime. Additionally, the successful applicant will perform multi-messenger and transient population studies. Research duties will involve improving transient search pipelines, analysis of large quantities of data, transient classification, detailed studies of newly discovered, interesting transients, and publication of scientific results. Penn State is home to the Swift Mission Operation Center and has a significant community of researchers who study high-energy transients. Penn State is also home to the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos and its Center for Multimessenger Astrophysics , which includes members of several experiments, such as LIGO, the IceCube Neutrino Observatory, and the HAWC TeV gamma-ray detector. Education and Experience Applicants should have a PhD in Physics, Astronomy, or a closely related field and at least three years of experience in postdoctoral research. Experience with HPC systems, machine learning, and GRB monitor data analysis would be an advantage.\u00a0 Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, statement of research interests, a CV, and a list of publications. In addition, please arrange for three professional reference letters to be sent to jjd330@psu.edu . Questions regarding the application process can be directed to Professor Jimmy DeLaunay at jjd330@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenured-Tenure-line-Positions-in-Interdisciplinary-Research--and--AI--ICDS-Co-hire-_REQ_0000082162-1": {"title": "Tenured/Tenure line Positions in Interdisciplinary Research \"and\" AI (ICDS Co-hire)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS) at Penn State University is hiring multiple Tenure-track or Tenured faculty as part of the second year of an ambitious multi-year cluster hire in AI across multiple university campuses. These faculty will complement a strong cohort of over 30 existing AI faculty plus many more whose work leverages AI to advance the sciences and engineering. The focus of this year\u2019s search is on faculty with expertise in AI + Materials, AI + Health, and Foundations of AI . Ideal candidates\u2019 research will focus on AI + X , meaning faculty who advance AI methods to solve scientific problems in different disciplines (X), rather than X + AI, where faculty use existing methods. The successful candidates will join a vibrant, interdisciplinary research community at Penn State and will have collaborative opportunities and access to extensive resources offered by the interdisciplinary research institutes. As a joint appointment, successful candidates will be expected to contribute to both their tenure home units and to ICDS. Faculty members in these positions will be expected to develop nationally recognized research programs, contribute to excellence in education, and engage in collaborative, interdisciplinary scholarship. The tenure home and specific requirements will be based on the specific position(s) applied for and the successful candidate\u2019s expertise. Applicants should submit a single PDF through the application portal containing the following materials in this order: cover letter, teaching statement, research statement, the names and contact information for four references, and their curriculum vitae. The cover letter should explicitly specify the area(s) and department(s) to which the applicant is applying (see below for information about calls for each department). Applicant review will begin in October 2026. For full consideration, please submit applications no later than December 7, 2026. For Questions, contact ICDS director Guido Cervone ( icds@psu.edu ). Penn State Academic Ranks Defined: Assistant professors should show early promise in teaching or research through emerging scholarly or professional contributions. Associate professors should have a record of high-quality publications and demonstrate teaching excellence in their field. Full professors should demonstrate a distinguished record of advanced work and leadership, reflecting established excellence in teaching, mentoring, and/or research. AI + Materials Department of Materials Science and Engineering, College of Earth and Minerals Science, University Park, PA : An Assistant , Associate , or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance interdisciplinary materials science by adopting advanced methods in artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML), and data-driven research to generate new fundamental science and accelerate materials innovation. The research will be accompanied by department service and teaching that reflects both ML/AI approaches and the traditional tenets of Materials Science and Engineering. The successful candidate will develop, manage, and sustain an active extramurally funded research program; participate in service activities within the departmental, college, university, and professional society domains; and excel in teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels. The department seeks to accelerate and streamline the discovery, development, and understanding of novel materials by incorporating machine learning, artificial intelligence, and data-driven research approaches with established experimental and computational methods. Candidates must possess a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Physics, Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. School of Engineering, Penn State Behrend, Erie, PA AI + Polymers : An Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance novel artificial intelligence and machine learning methodologies motivated by challenges in polymer materials, polymer informatics, plastics manufacturing, intelligent manufacturing, digital twins, and AI-enabled characterization. The successful candidate will establish an internationally recognized, externally funded research program that develops novel AI methodologies motivated by engineering materials and manufacturing challenges; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers; collaborate across Penn State through the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS), the Materials Research Institute, and related interdisciplinary initiatives; engage with industry through the Behrend Open Lab and the Center for Manufacturing Competitiveness (CMC); and contribute to service within the school, university, and profession. The anticipated tenure home for this position is the Department of Computer Science and Software Engineering (CSSE), with strong interdisciplinary collaborations with faculty in polymers, materials, and manufacturing across the School of Engineering. This position is one of two complementary faculty hires that together will establish the Penn State Behrend AI + Materials Cluster. The successful candidate will work closely with the companion AI + Metals faculty member to create a collaborative research community focused on AI-enabled engineering materials manufacturing. The department desires to advance research with the philosophy that polymers are not simply an application domain, but a rich scientific and engineering driver for advancing artificial intelligence itself. The successful candidate will leverage Behrend's strengths in manufacturing, industry engagement, and experiential learning to pursue transformative research, build interdisciplinary collaborations, and create exceptional opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students. Candidates must possess a Ph.D. in Polymer Engineering, Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Industrial Engineering, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. School of Engineering, Penn State Behrend, Erie, PA AI + Metals: An Assistant, Associate , or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance novel artificial intelligence and machine learning methodologies motivated by challenges in metallurgy, metal materials, additive manufacturing, computational materials science, intelligent manufacturing, digital engineering, and AI-enabled quality assurance. The successful candidate will establish an internationally recognized, externally funded research program that develops novel AI methodologies motivated by engineering materials and manufacturing challenges; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers; collaborate across Penn State through the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS), the Materials Research Institute, and related interdisciplinary initiatives; engage with industry through the Behrend Open Lab and the Center for Manufacturing Competitiveness (CMC); and contribute to service within the school, university, and profession. The anticipated tenure home for this position is the Department of Computer Science and Software Engineering (CSSE), with strong interdisciplinary collaborations with faculty in metals, materials, and manufacturing across the School of Engineering. This position is one of two complementary faculty hires that together will establish the Penn State Behrend AI + Materials Cluster. The successful candidate will work closely with the companion AI + Polymers faculty member to create a collaborative research community focused on AI-enabled engineering materials manufacturing. The department desires to advance research with the philosophy that metals are not simply an application domain, but a rich scientific and engineering driver for advancing artificial intelligence itself. The successful candidate will leverage Behrend's strengths in manufacturing, industry engagement, and experiential learning to pursue transformative research, build interdisciplinary collaborations, and create exceptional opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students. Candidates must possess a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Metallurgical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. AI + Health School of Science, Engineering and Technology (SSET), Penn State Harrisburg, Middletown, PA : An Assistant or Associate Professor whose research and teaching advance the development and/or implementation of AI and technology to improve health outcomes in isolated and/or vulnerable populations. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the department of appointment plus interdisciplinary courses in artificial intelligence, health technology, biomedical systems, or related program areas of SSET. In research, the successful candidate will address challenges in healthcare access, delivery, diagnosis, or treatment, with particular attention to rural communities, older adults, and other populations with limited access to care. Examples of relevant research may include using AI to enhance remote access to health care professionals and diagnostic services, timely diagnostics, improved environments for living and working, or collecting long-term patient data to enhance whole-patient evaluation. They will be expected to collaborate with one or more Penn State Harrisburg and SSET research initiatives: Smart Homes, Smart Medical Technology prototyping, AI Innovation, and appropriate departments in the College of Medicine. They will be expected to be an active member of ICDS and provide service to the school, college, and profession. The school aims to harness the potential of AI in health care engineering to improve the quality and timeliness of care to isolated and vulnerable populations. Candidates must possess a PhD in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Civil Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. College of Medicine, Hershey, PA : An Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level scholar to apply world-class computing and AI anchored in real-world reality to answer key health questions in basic, translational, and/or clinical sciences. Researchers will be expected to make real-world impacts on health to address important questions in biomedicine, disease prevention, improved medical/behavioral treatments, diagnostics, drug safety, and effective health care delivery. The College seeks to expand leadership in strategic priorities such as rural health, aging, cancer, cardiovascular, neurological, immunological, and maternal and child health, while leveraging Penn State\u2019s strengths in interdisciplinary and translational research, biomedical informatics, basic sciences, and population health sciences. Applicants at the Associate or Full Professor level should have an established externally funded research program. Candidates must possess an MD and/or PhD in Artificial Intelligence, Health Data Science, Computational Biology, Bioengineering, Clinical Informatics, Translational Science, Public Health with a computational focus, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. Department of Statistics, Eberly College of Science, University Park, PA : An Assistant Professor in Statistics with a research emphasis on AI and Machine Learning for health data science, with applications in areas such as neuroscience, environmental health, and the social determinants of health. The successful candidate will contribute to interdisciplinary research in health analytics and develop new statistical and computational methodology at the interface of AI, population health, and societal impact. Applicants will be expected to develop an independent research program and will contribute to the department\u2019s and college\u2019s teaching and service mission. Competitive applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree) in Statistics, Biostatistics, Bioinformatics, Data Science, Machine Learning, or a closely related field before their appointment start date at Penn State. College of Health and Human Development, University Park, PA: An Assistant, Associate , or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance our understanding of how AI can be leveraged in the design, adaptation, and implementation of interventions to improve health outcomes and/or leverage AI to help integrate these interventions into clinical and population health practice. The successful candidate will help expand our understanding of AI and translate that knowledge into evidence-based, sustainable practices that enhance health and well-being. The college seeks to complement existing areas of strength, including but not limited to: physical activity, cognitive health, substance abuse, healthy eating, weight regulation, sleep, stress management, language and communication disorders, and/or the management of chronic diseases associated with these areas. There is the potential to hire multiple candidates under this initiative, and successful hires will be placed in the appropriate department based on their area of research (e.g., Biobehavioral Health, Communication Sciences and Disorders, Human Development and Family Studies, Kinesiology, Nutritional Sciences). Candidates must possess a PhD in an aligned or closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. Department of Informatics and Intelligent Systems, College of Information Sciences and Technology, University Park, PA : An Assistant , Associate , or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance innovative artificial intelligence methods for health and biomedicine. The successful candidate will establish an externally funded research program; develop new AI methods for electronic health records, biomedical images and videos, genomic and multi-omics data, physiological signals, or other multimodal health data; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in artificial intelligence, data science, biomedical informatics, or related areas; mentor students and postdoctoral scholars; collaborate with computational researchers, biomedical scientists, clinicians, and health-system partners; and contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service. The college aims to strengthen Penn State\u2019s leadership in AI + Health by connecting foundational and methodological advances in AI with important problems in diagnosis, prognosis, precision medicine, computational biology, medical informatics, and human health. Candidates must possess a PhD in Information Science, Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Biomedical Informatics, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. Foundations of AI Department of Informatics and Intelligent Systems, College of Information Sciences and Technology, University Park, PA : An Assistant , Associate , or Full Professor whose research and teaching advance the foundations of artificial intelligence. The successful candidate will establish an externally funded research program; develop fundamental methods in one or more areas such as machine learning, generative AI, foundation models, physical or embodied AI, trustworthy and privacy-preserving AI, explainable and human-centered AI, or socially responsible AI; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in artificial intelligence, machine learning, data science, and related areas; mentor students and postdoctoral scholars; collaborate across disciplinary and institutional boundaries; and contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service. The department seeks to strengthen Penn State\u2019s leadership in foundational AI while creating methodological advances that support responsible innovation and scientific discovery across disciplines. Candidates must possess a PhD in Information Science, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Data Science, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Robotics, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. Department of Mathematics, Eberly College of Science, University Park, PA : An Assistant or Associate Professor whose research and teaching advance the mathematical foundations of AI. This includes, but is not limited to, mathematical contributions to learning theory, information geometry and geometric deep learning, uncertainty quantification and probabilistic methods, and integrating any area of mathematics research and AI. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a leading research program, contribute to undergraduate teaching and commit to teaching excellence, collaborate across campus on AI initiatives when appropriate, and contribute to a positive departmental environment, including our departmental strategy for AI. Our current faculty\u2019s research includes AI methods in: Life Sciences and Health, Scientific Machine Learning, Operator Learning, Geometric & Topological Data Analysis, Quantum Computing, Number Theory, and Formal proofs. Applicants will be expected to develop an independent research program and will contribute to the department\u2019s and college\u2019s teaching and service mission. Applicants seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have the same qualifications as the rank of Assistant Professor, as well as a strong track record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service. Competitive applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent terminal degree) in Mathematics or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Instrument-Automation_REQ_0000081177-1": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor \u2013 Instrument Automation", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Materials Research Institute (MRI) at Penn State seeks outstanding applicants for an Assistant Research Professor position focused on instrument automation. The position is supported by multiple efforts at Penn State, including the Department of Energy funded 3DFEM2 Energy Frontier Research Center and the National Science Foundation funded LATTICE Cloud Laboratory national facility. The automation of experimentation and data collection is increasingly critical with the rise of artificial intelligence and machine learning enabled materials synthesis and characterization. The successful candidate will support the development of new automated synthesis and characterization tools along with training and supporting users of these instruments. Candidates for this position must have a Ph.D. in Physics, Materials Science and Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field, a strong record of related research, and experience maintaining and operating thin film deposition equipment. Specific experience with sputter deposition and characterization of ferroelectrics and semiconductors is a plus. This position requires excellent organizational, time management, and communication skills as well as the ability to work in an interdisciplinary team environment in support of the goals of in-house research and external users.\u00a0 Position responsibilities: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop hardware and software solutions to interface with and control measurement equipment to enable unique automated research and sample processing or conditioning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Instruments span the Materials Science and Engineering Department, Materials Characterization Laboratory (MCL), Radiation Science & Engineering Center (RSEC), and Silicon Carbide Innovation Alliance (SCIA). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Integrate new measurement equipment, temperature controllers, and switching hardware to existing synthesis and processing tools. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Train users on automated deposition tools and instruments in the Materials Science and Engineering Department and electrical characterization laboratory of MCL. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Work with users and senior staff to identify and correct existing acquisition deficiencies and software bugs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support automated thin film deposition activities of external users for the LATTICE NSF Cloud Laboratory. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain and enhance the function and stability of current data acquisition software written in the National Instruments CVI development environment. To be considered for this position, applicants should include a curriculum vitae, a cover letter with a summary of relevant skills and experience and contact information for two professional references (name, position title, mailing address, telephone number and e-mail address). Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This is a term appointment with possibility of re-funding.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Teaching-Faculty-in-Mathematics_REQ_0000081847-2": {"title": "Teaching Faculty in Mathematics", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mathematics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a Teaching Professor at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, or Full Teaching Professor depending on qualifications. This is a non-tenure track appointment. Interest and documented expertise in teaching precalculus and calculus are essential. Research or teaching experience in linear programming, game theory, operations research, machine learning, or a related field is preferred. Candidates must be ready to contribute to the development of new or existing courses. A Ph.D. in mathematics is required . Applicants must complete the Penn State application and must submit an application through Mathjobs.org ( https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28842 ).\u00a0 The following materials must be uploaded to the application in order to be fully considered: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae At least three reference letters submitted directly to Mathjobs.org (two of which should address in detail the candidate\u2019s abilities as a teacher) Publication List Teaching Statement Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026\u200b \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Special-Collections-Library-Lead-for-Archival-Processing-and-Collection-Strategies_REQ_0000080914-1": {"title": "Special Collections Library Lead for Archival Processing and Collection Strategies", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS This role advances Penn State's strategic priorities by strengthening research infrastructure, expanding access to distinctive collections, and supporting student-centered learning through engagement with rare and unique materials. Reporting to the Head of the Eberly Family Special Collections, the Lead for Archival Processing and Collection Strategies provides strategic and operational leadership for the full lifecycle stewardship of collections in all formats and mediums in the Eberly Family Special Collections Library (SCL). This tenure-line faculty position leads the planning, coordination, and execution of accessioning, processing, description, digitization coordination, and long-term stewardship to ensure collections are accessible, sustainable, and aligned with institutional priorities.\u00a0 The Lead for Archival Processing and Collection Strategies supervises staff responsible for collections management and establishes clear, efficient workflows that support discovery, teaching, and research use. \u00a0The position serves as the primary liaison between SCL and the Preservation, Conservation, and Digitization (PCD) department, ensuring that stewardship decisions are coordinated across the Libraries and grounded in best practices. \u00a0This position will work closely with the Head of Cataloging and Metadata Services and the Special Collections Cataloging Team to establish policies for descriptive standards and set priorities. Candidates for the rank of Assistant Librarian should possess a graduate degree in library or information studies or other appropriate degree; must have demonstrated potential ability as a librarian; and must have shown promise of growth in research and service. Candidate for the rank of Associate Librarian should possess the same qualifications as the Assistant Librarian, demonstrate excellence in librarianship, show evidence of an established reputation in research, and have a strong record of service to the University and the profession. Candidates for the rank of Librarian should possess the same qualifications as the Associate Librarian; demonstrate sustained excellence in librarianship; have achieved a distinguished reputation in research, scholarship, or librarianship accomplishment; and maintain a substantial record of service and leadership to the University, the profession, and/or the broader community. The University expects regular onsite presence to fully participate in their university workspace or on-campus intellectual and educational community. Occasional hybrid work may be permissible upon approval of the supervisor. Duties and Responsibilities\u00a0 Collections Services Leadership. \u2022 Leads strategy and operations for the full cycle of collections management in SCL, including accessioning, processing, arrangement and description, digitization coordination, rehousing, and collections maintenance \u2022 Supervises and mentors collections services employees, building a stable and collaborative team culture grounded in transparency, accountability, and shared purpose \u2022 Establishes and maintains policies, procedures, and documentation standards to ensure consistency, efficiency, and adherence to professional best practices \u2022 Sets and manages processing priorities in alignment with SCL\u2019s collection development plan, donor commitments, teaching and researcher demand, and institutional goals \u2022 Oversees accessioning workflows, including documentation, donor agreements coordination, and integration of new acquisitions into collection management systems \u2022 Ensures compliance with archival standards (e.g., DACS, EAD, ArchivesSpace practices) and promotes scalable, sustainable processing models \u2022 Tracks and reports on collections access metrics, backlog reduction, and stewardship outcomes Preservation, Conservation, and Digitization Coordination \u2022 Serves as the primary liaison between Special Collections and Preservation, Conservation, and Digitization units \u2022 Collaborates on prioritization of conservation treatments, rehousing initiatives, environmental monitoring, and preservation planning \u2022 Coordinates digitization workflows for archival collections in alignment with access priorities and resource capacity \u2022 Ensures that digitization initiatives are integrated into overall collections strategy rather than functioning as isolated projects \u2022 Partners with Digital Collections colleagues to support responsible digital stewardship and long-term preservation planning \u2022 Contributes to shared infrastructure planning for physical and digital collection care Access and Stewardship Strategy The Lead for Archival Processing and Collection Strategies advances access to collections while safeguarding their long-term preservation: \u2022 Develops processing strategies that balance researcher access, preservation needs, and available staffing resources \u2022 Collaborates with Research Services to align description and processing decisions with teaching and research use \u2022 Supports the integration of newly processed collections into instruction, exhibitions, fellowships, and public programming \u2022 Ensures ethical stewardship practices that reflect commitments to diversity, equity, inclusion, and responsible archival representation Contributions to Special Collections Leadership As a member of the SCL leadership team, this position: \u2022 Advises the Head of Special Collections on collections stewardship strategy, space planning for processing and storage, and staffing needs \u2022 Contributes to long-range planning related to facilities, environmental controls, and collections growth \u2022 Participates in the Special Collections Curation Team and collaborates on prioritizing acquisitions and stewardship commitments \u2022 Supports Penn State\u2019s learning and teaching mission, faculty research, and land-grant commitment through accessible and well-stewarded collections \u2022 Participates in donor stewardship efforts related to processing, preservation, and access outcomes \u2022 Provides reference service to faculty, students, and researchers on a rotating basis. Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, and Accessibility This position integrates inclusive and ethical practices into all aspects of collections stewardship, including accessing, description, prioritization, and access. \u00a0This includes attention to culturally responsive description and expanding access to collections that document historically underrepresented communities. Research, Service, and Professional Development As a tenure-track faculty member, the Lead for Archival Processing and Collection Strategies: \u2022 Maintains an active research agenda appropriate to rank and tenure status (if applicable) \u2022 Represents the Special Collections Library on relevant library and university committees and task forces \u2022 Participates in the governance structure of the Libraries and advances the mission and values of the University \u2022 Engages in service to the profession through scholarship, presentations, and professional organizations \u2022 Pursues continuing education and professional development in archival stewardship, preservation strategy, and leadership Required Qualifications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Master\u2019s degree in library and information science from an ALA-accredited program or an equivalent combination of advanced degree and relevant experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrated experience leading archival processing, arrangement and description, accessioning, collections management, or related archival stewardship functions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrated leadership experience, such as supervision, mentoring, fostering a collaborative work environment, and/or project management. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge of archival standards, practices, and technologies, including DACS, EAD, ArchivesSpace, and contemporary archival processing methodologies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Effective written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Evidence of the potential to meet the University Libraries\u2019 expectations for research and reservice, and scholarship as a tenure-line faculty member. Preferred Qualifications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience coordinating with preservation, conservation, and/or digitization initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience working with born-digital archival materials and digital stewardship. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience with Aeon. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience using data and assessment to inform collections priorities and operational decision-making. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience supporting archival instruction, exhibitions, or public engagement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience working with community archives or culturally responsive stewardship practices. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Record of scholarly publication, grant activity, or professional leadership. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience leading organizational change or implementing new workflows. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with AI-enabled tools and emerging technologies that support archival processing, description, and discovery. About the Eberly Family Special Collections Library The Eberly Family Special Collections Library (SCL) preserves and provides access to Penn State University's rare book, manuscripts, archives, oral histories, photographs, and other distinctive collections in support of research, teaching, and public engagement. \u00a0As part of one of the nation's leading research libraries, SCL is building a future-focused program that combines exceptional stewardship with innovative approaches to teaching, scholarship, and access. \u00a0Through collaborative partnerships across the University and beyond, Special Collections is expanding opportunities for students, faculty, researchers, and communities to engage with rare and unique collections in meaningful and transformative ways. \u00a0The library is committed to responsible stewardship, inclusive description, emerging technologies, and creating new pathways for discovery that ensure distinctive collections remain vital to the University's land-grant mission. APPLICATION PROCESS All candidate materials must be submitted via Workday. Interested candidates are expected to upload a cover letter, resume or CV, and a list of four references. Furnished references must include a current/previous direct supervisor, a colleague, an employee who was/is a direct report, and one at the candidate's discretion. Candidates must clearly identify the relationship for each reference provided. References will be contacted later in the search process. \u00a0 Application materials should demonstrate the candidate\u2019s professional qualifications, experience, and contributions to librarianship, teaching, research, and/or service.\u00a0 \u00a0 Application materials should reflect a commitment to equal opportunity and respect for all individuals. Candidates are encouraged to highlight how their work promotes inclusive access to information and supports the academic mission of the institution. \u00a0 Individual compensation packages are based on various factors unique to each candidate, including a candidate\u2019s qualifications, education, experience, and rank. In addition to a competitive salary, full-time employees also receive a comprehensive benefits program, generous paid time off, and tuition discount for employees and eligible family members. Total Compensation Calculator provides an estimated summary of the value of compensation and benefits. \u00a0 Information about the University Libraries\u2019 employment opportunities, processes, and culture can be found at https://libraries.psu.edu/about/jobs \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Faculty-Position-in-Eukaryotic-Gene-Regulation_REQ_0000081702-1": {"title": "Faculty Position in Eukaryotic Gene Regulation", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at Penn State , University Park campus, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor .\u00a0The successful applicant will join the highly collaborative Penn State Center for Eukaryotic Gene Regulation . \u00a0 The search is open to any area of eukaryotic gene regulation.\u00a0Of particular interest for this year\u2019s search is the use of biochemical methods to investigate eukaryotic gene regulation. \u00a0 The anticipated starting date for this appointment is summer or fall of 2027 or spring of 2028. The duties include research, teaching, supervision of student research at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and service to the university and the greater professional community. Candidates are expected to demonstrate interest in and capacity for developing a strong, independent research program, and teaching and mentorship excellence at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. \u00a0 Applications submitted electronically by October 15, 2026 will receive full consideration, and should include the following: A brief cover letter (maximum of 2 pages) that highlights the applicant\u2019s most relevant qualifications for a faculty position at Penn State. Overview of goals/vision of your research program in context of our department and institution Your most significant scientific accomplishments A summary of experiences and qualifications that position you to achieve your goals Curriculum vitae including a list of publications. Two statements addressing: Research accomplishments, plans, and vision (up to 4 pages, including figures and references), Teaching experience, philosophy, and/or interests (1 page) Application materials may comprise no more than 5 documents, each with a size limit of 5MB. Applicants may need to combine materials to meet the 5-document limit and should ensure all documents are uploaded and correct prior to final submission. \u00a0 In addition to the above materials, applicants should arrange for at least three (or more) letters of recommendation to be sent directly to\u00a0 gene_regulation_search@psu.edu \u00a0by the same deadline. \u00a0 Competitive applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will possess a Ph.D. in biochemistry, cell biology, molecular biology, systems biology or a related field before beginning employment at Penn State; will demonstrate potential for developing an externally funded and collaborative\u00a0research program; and will demonstrate the potential to contribute to the department\u2019s and college\u2019s teaching and service missions. \u00a0 Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have the same qualifications as the assistant professor, as well as a strong track record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service. \u00a0 Questions about the position and the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at Penn State may be directed at the Chair of the Faculty Search Committee, Professor Song Tan by e-mail at\u00a0 gene_regulation_search@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Dept-of-Engineering-Science---Mechanics--Ozbolat-Lab_REQ_0000081380-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar, Dept of Engineering Science & Mechanics, Ozbolat Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Ozbolat Laboratory \u00a0in Penn State's College of Engineering has multiple openings for Postdoctoral Scholars in the field of bioprinting, tissue engineering, and regenerative medicine. The successful candidates will work on multiple projects funded through National Institutes of Health (NIH) and private foundations. The Postdoctoral Scholars will join a multidisciplinary research laboratory at the Millenium Science Complex, which is part of Huck Institute of Life Sciences. There are excellent opportunities to interact and collaborate with other researchers in the Institute, as well as others established at Penn State who specialize in biomaterials, tissue engineering, stem cells, regenerative therapies, and clinical translation. A Ph.D. degree in the field of biomedical engineering, molecular/cellular/developmental\u00a0biology, chemistry, or a closely related field is required by the start date.\u00a0The successful candidates will have a strong background in a range of molecular biology techniques, 2D and 3D cell culture models (hydrogels), imaging techniques (TEM, SEM, confocal), protein analysis (immunohistochemistry/immunofluorescence), and handling of rodents. Specific skills in bioprinting and lab-on-a-chip device development, as well as high throughput tissue bio-fabrication, will be advantageous. Interested applicants should submit an online application including a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three referees. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Biotechnology-Teaching-Faculty_REQ_0000081580-2": {"title": "Biotechnology Teaching Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology (BMB) at Penn State invites applications for a Lecturer, Assistant Teaching Professor, or Associate Teaching Professor appointment with expertise in Biotechnology, Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Microbiology, and/or related fields. We are seeking a dynamic, collaborative, and self-motivated educator who is passionate about teaching and committed to mentoring the next generation of biotechnology scientists and entrepreneurs. The department is particularly interested in candidates with experience in the biotechnology industry who will work to strengthen and grow our Biotechnology B.S. program. \u00a0 The ideal candidate will demonstrate the ability to work effectively across disciplines, fostering partnerships with industry, academia, and the community to enhance our undergraduate biotechnology offerings. A proactive collaborator who takes the lead in developing innovative curricula, cultivating industry connections, and creating opportunities for student engagement will thrive in this role. Expectations include teaching biotechnology and related courses, and overseeing biotechnology internships; other duties may include mentoring graduate teaching assistants, teaching introductory or advanced undergraduate lecture and laboratory courses, undergraduate student advising, and service to the department or college. Work expectations for the position include fall, spring, and summer duties, with time for curriculum development and improvement over the summer. Professional development opportunities are also supported and encouraged.\u00a0This appointment will be filled at the rank of Lecturer, Assistant Teaching Professor, or Associate Teaching Professor. Rank and length of term will be commensurate with the candidate's education, experience, and leadership qualities.\u00a0 Competitive applicants will have: Master's degree (Lecturer) or Ph.D. (Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor) in Biotechnology, Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Microbiology, or a related field Experience teaching at least one course as either the lead or assisting instructor Demonstrated ability to achieve teaching excellence at both introductory and advanced undergraduate levels Proven commitment to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive community in the practice and teaching of science Professional experience in the biotechnology or biopharmaceutical industry (preferred) Experience or interest in curriculum development and innovative, evidence-based pedagogy, such as active learning or course-based undergraduate research experiences (preferred) Applications must be submitted electronically and should include: Cover letter with names and contact information for three references who may be contacted for letters of recommendation Curriculum vitae A teaching dossier ( all compiled into one document ) including a statement of teaching philosophy and interests, evidence that demonstrates a commitment to excellence in teaching and improving pedagogical practices, and how you plan to contribute to or advance the Penn State Values .\u00a0 As part of the teaching dossier, applicants are asked to submit materials that demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence. These materials could include any of the following: a recorded lesson with a personal reflection on the lesson, results and reflection from a teaching practices inventory, syllabi authored by you for a class that you have taught or a class that you would like to teach, student or peer evaluations from previous teaching experiences, example teaching materials that you have developed, peer-reviewed articles authored on teaching-related topics, other materials that demonstrate your understanding of and commitment to research-based teaching practices, awards and recognition for teaching and teaching-related scholarly activities (a brief explanation for why you were recognized should be provided). \u00a0 Review of applications will begin as received and continue until the position is filled. Expected start date would be January 1, 2027 or July 1, 2027 but off cycle start dates would be considered. We seek a dedicated professional who is passionate about education, collaborative in approach, and driven to make a meaningful impact on our students and community. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director-of-Intensive-English-Communication-Program--IECP-_REQ_0000081504-2": {"title": "Director of Intensive English Communication Program (IECP)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Applied Linguistics in the College of the Liberal Arts \u00a0 seeks a visionary administrator to direct its Intensive English Communication Program (IECP).\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 The Director will provide daily oversight of program operations; model and facilitate excellence in program communications; cultivate a transformative academic environment; develop and oversee recruitment efforts; hire, train, review and foster professional development of faculty and staff; and represent the IECP on campus and within the profession. The Director of the IECP reports directly to the Head of the Department of Applied Linguistics. As a member of the graduate faculty, the Director is eligible to teach a 1-0 course load in Applied Linguistics and to serve on graduate committees. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 Minimum Required Qualifications: A PhD or EdD in Teaching English as a Second Language (T.E.S.L.), Applied Linguistics or related field \u00a0 is required by appointment date. \u00a0 Experience in IEP program administration. Teaching experience in an intensive English or academic English preparation program in a college or university setting. Record of on-going professional development. Demonstrated successful program assessment and development. Outstanding professional, cross-cultural communication and interpersonal skills. \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 This is a full-time twelve-month academic professional position. \u00a0 A start date of January 2027 is preferred; however, this start date may be negotiated with the successful candidate. \u00a0 Salary is commensurate with experience, qualifications, and the personal characteristics required of a demanding and significant role in administrative leadership. \u00a0 This position is \u00a0 Open Rank \u00a0 and will be filled at \u00a0 the \u00a0 rank of \u00a0 Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, or Teaching Professor . \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please provide (combine into seven uploads of any combination of documents) a cover letter; CV; transcripts of graduate program(s); documentation of administrative/supervisory/teaching excellence; supporting materials such as observation reports, peer reviews, and student evaluations; and copies of any published materials relevant to this position. Applicants should identify three references who may be contacted to provide letters or recommendation. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Inquiries may be directed to \u00a0 Stephen Looney ( sdl16@psu.edu) , chair of the search committee. \u00a0 The College of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.\u202fInformation on faculty ranks and progression can be found at \u00a0 https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Visit our website at \u00a0 IECP.la.psu.edu \u00a0 for more information on our \u00a0 IECP Program . \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Instrument-Scientist-for-Neutron-Beam-Techniques-within-the-Radiation-Science-and-Engineering-Center-at-the-Pennsylvania-State-University_REQ_0000081308-2": {"title": "Instrument Scientist for Neutron Beam Techniques within the Radiation Science and Engineering Center at the Pennsylvania State University", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Radiation Science and Engineering Center (RSEC) within the College of Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University has an opening for an Instrument/Data Scientist position for Neutron Beam Techniques.\u00a0 A V16 -VSANS facility was donated by HZB-Germany to Penn State. The VSANS facility was relocated and installed at newly expanded neutron beam hall at Penn State, making it the only university research reactor facility in the United States with SANS capability. Main activities for the selected candidate involve primarily maintenance, and utilization of PSU-SANS facility. The successful candidate must have a PhD in a physical science, or engineering, excellent experimental skills, and good communication skills.\u00a0Experiences in scattering techniques and/or computer simulation are highly desirable. The candidate will be expected to carry out studies or involved others research for soft condensed matter systems using SANS. \u00a0The successful candidate will also be responsible for developing stimulating and supporting research utilizing other RSEC facilities and will be given appropriate academic work title corresponding the education and academic experiences. The RSEC facilities include the Penn State Breazeale Reactor (PSBR), gamma irradiation facilities (In-pool Irradiator and Dry Irradiator), Neutron Beam Laboratory and Hot Cells, Radionuclear Applications Laboratory with NAA and Compton Suppression system, Radiochemistry Teaching Laboratory, Nuclear Security Education Laboratory, Subcritical Graphite Reactor Facility, and various Radiation Detection and Measurement Laboratories. The RSEC facilities are expanded with installation of new core moderator assembly and new beam ports, a cold neutron source, new expanded neutron beam hall and office and laboratory spaces.\u00a0 The RSEC facilities are a regulated drug-free work place and applicants must pass drug screening and are subject to random and for-cause testing. \u00a0Selected applicant must pass additional federal background investigation and Environmental Health and Safety Radiation Worker qualification orientation.\u00a0 Vehicles and personal property may randomly be subject to search upon entering and exiting the facility. P ossible faculty titles may include Assistant Research Professor or Associate Research Professor ; which is dependent on candidate's experience. This is a non-tenure-line professional track position, and title/rank will be dependent upon experience and qualifications. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---Nursing---Adjunct-Clinical-Professor_REQ_0000074635": {"title": "Part Time - Nursing - Adjunct Clinical Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for Adjunct Clinical Instructor openings. Adjunct Instructors will (visit clinical sites) graduate nurse practitioner clinical sections in the nurse practitioner program for students located throughout Pennsylvania. Requirements and Qualifications A Master\u2019s degree in Nursing (doctorate preferred)\u00a0is required. A c urrent National Certification as a Nurse Practitioner, Pennsylvania RN and CRNP license is required. To be considered for this opening, applications must be submitted electronically and include a letter of application detailing relevant qualifications for this job and a curriculum vitae. Employment with the University for this job will require successful completion of the Pennsylvania (PA) Publicly Available Clearances: PA Child Abuse History Clearance, PA State Police Criminal Record Check, and the FBI Criminal History Background Check. These are one semester, non-tenure track appointments with the possibility of reappointment. All applications will be considered until vacancies are filled. For a more detailed description of the College, please visit our website at http://nursing.psu.edu/ .\u00a0 Candidates should be prepared to provide the names, titles, and contact information (telephone, email, and mailing address) of three (3) professional references, if requested.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor_REQ_0000081356-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Materials Research Institute (MRI) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a non-tenure-line Assistant Research Professor . The position will involve machine learning for autonomous thin-film materials synthesis, including representation learning for scientific data, multimodal data fusion, and real-time predictive modeling. This work will be performed as part of LATTICE (Layered and Thin Film Technologies with Intelligent Cloud Experimentation), a National Science Foundation Programmable Cloud Laboratory at The Pennsylvania State University's University Park campus.\u00a0 The successful candidate will lead the development of specialized machine learning models that enable AI systems to interpret scientific data from instruments including atomic force microscopy, reflection high-energy electron diffraction, spectroscopic ellipsometry, X-ray diffraction, and similar characterization methods. These models serve as the perceptual layer for a multi-agent AI framework that will guide autonomous materials synthesis and interact with robotic systems. The models will be trained, calibrated, and validated against the specific data modalities produced by LATTICE instrumentation. The candidate will deploy these models on edge-computing infrastructure for real-time feedback during deposition and integrate them with the Lifetime Sample Tracking data platform. The position requires close collaboration with LATTICE domain scientists in thin-film growth and characterization, AI researchers developing the agentic workflow framework, and future users of the LATTICE framework. The candidate will also contribute to the scientific direction of the LATTICE ML/AI effort and mentor graduate students and postdoctoral scholars as appropriate.\u00a0 Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field, and should have postdoctoral or equivalent research experience demonstrating an independent record of publication in applied machine learning, computer vision, and/or scientific data analysis. Experience with one or more of the following is strongly preferred: deep learning for image analysis, multimodal or multi-task learning, or deployment of ML models in real-time or edge-computing environments. Domain knowledge of materials science, chemistry, or physics will be an advantage. Extensive programming experience in Python is required, and familiarity with PyTorch or JAX is preferred.\u00a0 This is a non-tenure-line, limited-term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with excellent possibility of renewal. To apply, applicants should upload a cover letter detailing their qualifications for and interest in the position, a copy of their CV, and names and contact details (e-mail addresses and telephone numbers) for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Cocoziello-Digital-Twin_REQ_0000080944-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor - Cocoziello Digital Twin", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Cocoziello Institute of Real Estate Innovation at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a three-year Assistant Research Professor position with expertise in digital twins for the built environment (buildings and infrastructure), building information modeling, and data analytics for buildings. The position will be located on the University Park campus of Penn State. This position has a possible extension contingent on performance review and continued funding. The position has 60% research, 30% project management, and 10% research advising responsibilities. The successful candidate will manage the development of a robust digital twin effort, focusing on creating and implementing a digital twin strategy for the Penn State University Park campus. The candidate will collaborate with Institute faculty and industry partners, and guide graduate/undergraduate students on digital twin research and development activities. The successful candidate is expected to secure external funding for their research and disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed journals, conferences, and other effective channels. The individual should be highly motivated and knowledgeable of relevant literature, be able to lead their own individual projects, write grant proposals, and contribute to collaborative research efforts. Candidates should have: (1) an ability to manage and lead collaborative teams on research projects with significant industry engagement, (2) experience designing and/or adapting new technologies and techniques with a particular focus on digital twins and BIM related to the built environment, (3) strong written, visual, and oral communication skills, and (4) knowledge of human subject ethics and research procedures. Experience with industrialized construction, construction robotics, Virtual/Augmented Reality, and Artificial Intelligence is a plus. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Architectural Engineering, Civil Engineering, Architecture, or a related field is required. Applicants should provide evidence of strong potential for conducting and publishing research, competitiveness for external research funding, and excellence in communication across a range of audiences. Experience in industry-supported research activities is preferred. Selection Criteria Candidates will be evaluated on their potential to manage collaborative industry research projects, experience in research involving digital twins and Building Information Modeling, ability to secure external research funding, and ability to publish high-impact work. Applicants must submit the following: (1) a cover letter; (2) a complete CV; (3) a statement summarizing the applicant's philosophy and plan for pursuing successful research; and (4) contact information for three references. Applicants should address in their materials how they would contribute to creating/maintaining an inclusive and respectful work environment. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. For more information about the position, please contact John Messner ( jim101@psu.edu ), Chair of the Search Committee. This is a term appointment, funded for three years from the date of hire, with an excellent possibility of renewal. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Organization-Development-and-Change-_REQ_0000079398-2": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor (Organization Development and Change)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Learning & Performance Systems (LPS) invites applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor position to support its fully online master\u2019s degree in Organization Development and Change (ODC) and other LPS programs, as needed. students to design and implement organization development and continuous improvement initiatives. Faculty in this role contribute to a collaborative instructional team and engage students in applied, globally informed coursework aligned with professional standards.\u00a0 This non-tenure-line position is a 48-week faculty appointment, with the possibility of renewal and has primary responsibilities in teaching and graduate advising, as well as in supporting program administration. Faculty in LPS are part of a collegial, student-centered department that prioritizes strong teaching, thoughtful collaboration, and a positive, supportive work environment. Key Responsibilities Teach online, asynchronous courses in the fall, spring, and summer terms, with synchronous engagement for advising, webinars, and meetings; occasional in person teaching may be assigned. Coordinate with Penn State World Campus instructional designers and media specialists to ensure high\u2011quality online course development and delivery, accessibility/UDL, media integration, and continuous improvement; Advise master\u2019s students including the master's in professional studies in Organization Development and Change, throughout the program, including capstone completion Advise online D.Ed. doctoral students, supporting progress through qualifying, comprehensive, and final examinations; course planning; and the development, implementation, and writing of the culminating capstone project. Includes annual participation in the 2\u20133 day Summer Summit residency held at the University Park campus; Support program administration activities including assisting with the course scheduling, program assessment and accreditation work, admissions review, orientation and community\u2011building for master\u2019s students, onboarding of part\u2011time or new faculty, and student success initiatives; Collaborate and communicate effectively with the LPS department head, professor\u2011in\u2011charge of the WFED program, faculty colleagues, and department staff to support cohesive and responsive program operations; Participate in department and program meetings and events. Minimum Qualifications (Required) Earned doctorate (PhD or DEd) in education; workforce education and development; organization development and change; or a closely related field Evidence of excellence, or potential excellence, in online graduate teaching (asynchronous) and inclusive pedagogy Strong communication and collaboration skills Demonstrated strengths in time management, ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities, and organization Desired Qualifications Experience as an organization development and change or talent and development professional Familiarity with Canvas, online quality standards, and program assessment Experience designing or revising online courses in collaboration with instructional designers Understanding of the ethics surrounding the uses and integration of AI in higher education courses Evidence of student\u2011centered responsiveness including the ability to provide timely feedback and grading, respond promptly to working professionals, and manage multiple course deadlines in fast\u2011paced online environments Representative Teaching Portfolio ODC (examples): Appraising Organization Change and Development and Consulting; Implementing Training as an Organization Development Intervention; Marketing Organization Development; Project Management for Professionals; Lean\u2011Sigma for Professionals; Technologies for Work Effectiveness; Facilitating Organization Development and Change Through Technology; Leadership Competencies for Professionals Application Instructions Apply online at hr.psu.edu/careers and upload one PDF containing: a) Cover letter that clearly identifies the candidate\u2019s qualifications related to the position; b) Curriculum vitae; c) Names and contact information for three professional references ; d) Teaching philosophy statement ( maximum two single\u2011spaced pages ) describing prior teaching and course design experience, ODC program alignment, relevant course expertise, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Campus/Unit: College of Education \u2014 Department of Learning & Performance Systems (LPS), University Park, PA Appointment: Assistant Teaching Professor (non\u2011tenure-line), 48\u2011week; one year term with the possibility of renewal based on need, performance, and/or availability of funding. Full University benefits apply. Work Arrangement: In person preferred. The Department of Learning & Performance Systems\u00a0is supportive of flexible (hybrid) work arrangements when aligned with the ability to meet the needs of the unit and the essential duties of the position. Questions related to flexible work should be directed to the department head during the interview process. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-RF-Neuromorphic-Systems--Das-Lab_REQ_0000081197-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in RF Neuromorphic Systems, Das Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Engineering Science and Mechanics is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to work on the development of radio-frequency neuromorphic hardware for next-generation sensing, communication, and signal-processing applications. The project will focus on the design, fabrication, and experimental demonstration of neuromorphic circuits and devices capable of processing RF and analog signals directly in the hardware domain. The successful candidate will contribute to the design and implementation of RF circuits, including oscillators, amplifiers, mixers, filters, detectors, and nonlinear or adaptive circuit architectures. The researcher will also participate in device and circuit fabrication, integration, packaging, and high-frequency electrical characterization. Experience connecting emerging electronic devices with RF circuit concepts, analog computing, in-memory computing, or neuromorphic signal processing is particularly desirable. Applicants should have a Ph.D. in electrical engineering, electronics engineering, applied physics, materials science, or a closely related field. Strong experience in RF or microwave circuit design, electromagnetic and circuit simulation, device or circuit fabrication, and RF measurement techniques is required. Familiarity with tools such as Cadence, ADS, HFSS, COMSOL, or equivalent platforms, as well as experience with vector network analyzers, spectrum analyzers, signal generators, and probe-station measurements, will be advantageous. Candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas are especially encouraged to apply: RF and microwave integrated-circuit design Analog and mixed-signal circuit design Neuromorphic or bio-inspired hardware Emerging electronic devices and heterogeneous integration Semiconductor microfabrication and cleanroom processing RF device modeling, packaging, and high-frequency characterization Adaptive RF systems, edge sensing, or signal classification The postdoctoral researcher will work in a multidisciplinary environment involving device physicists, circuit designers, materials researchers, and system engineers. The position will provide opportunities to lead high-impact research, mentor graduate students, collaborate with academic and industrial partners, and publish in leading journals and conferences. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, a brief statement of research experience and interests, representative publications, and contact information for references. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor-in-Cryo-EM-Studies-of-Amyloids--Virus-Host-Interactions--and-Protein-Complexes_REQ_0000081532-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor in Cryo-EM Studies of Amyloids, Virus/Host Interactions, and Protein Complexes", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-27\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS This position is in the Jiang lab at The Pennsylvania State University in the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology and the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences. The lab is located in the Millennium Complex of Sciences with state-of-the-art instruments for cryo-EM, including Titan Krios and Talos Arctica TEMs with energy filters and direct electron detectors for single-particle cryoEM and cryo-ET, and a Hydra FIB-SEM for in situ structural studies of cellular and tissue sections. The lab has multiple GPU workstations and access to the university computing center. \u00a0 In this Assistant Research Professor position, you will join an interdisciplinary team and work on cryo-EM structural studies of amyloids in neurodegenerative diseases, virus/host interactions, and protein complexes relevant to cancers using single-particle cryoEM and cryo-ET. The daily work involves cryo-EM sample preparation/screening, data collection, image processing, 3D reconstruction, and structural modeling/analyses. Please check our publications to learn about our research interests. \u00a0 The ideal candidate should have: A Ph.D. degree or its equivalent Highly self-motivated and passionate for cryo-EM structural studies Prior experience in cryo-EM sample preparation/screening, data collection, and image processing/3D reconstruction Prior experiences in protein biochemistry and molecular biology Ability to work independently and as part of a team Assisting the PI in mentoring junior members in the lab Excellent communication and writing skills Applications must be submitted electronically and include a curriculum vitae and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Lecturer-in-Landscape-Architecture_REQ_0000064550": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Lecturer in Landscape Architecture", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Landscape Architecture Department within the Stuckeman School of Architecture and Landscape Architecture in the College of Arts and Architecture seeks to hire various part-time faculty appointments throughout the academic year. These appointments will be semester-by-semester or year-long, non-tenure track academic appointments without benefits and no guarantee of renewal.\u00a0 Positions require:\u00a0 Bachelor`s degree, Master`s degree or Ph.D. and teaching experience at the University level.\u00a0 Education requirements vary depending on the specific position and usually are required in the related field or discipline of Landscape Architecture.\u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants should apply by submitting a short letter of interest with their qualifications and current Curriculum Vita (CV).\u00a0 Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as the need arises. Degree will be verified at the time of the offer. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor--Child-Clinical-Psychology--Department-of-Psychology_REQ_0000081645-1": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Child Clinical Psychology, Department of Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Psychology at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position, at the rank of Assistant Professor of Child Clinical Psychology . Responsibilities of the Assistant Professor of Child Clinical Psychology include maintaining a strong record of publications in top outlets. This position will include resident instruction at the undergraduate and graduate level and normal university service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. A Ph.D. in clinical Psychology and clinical internship are required with license eligibility in Pennsylvania by the appointment date. Areas of specialization within child clinical psychology are open, but not limited to, candidates whose research would synergize with our current expertise in community and school-based prevention, childhood adversity and maltreatment, cognitive-neuropsychological bases of attention and behavior, stress and coping, emotion regulation, and developmental psychopathology. \u00a0Two priority areas are: (1) mental health needs of and interventions for children, adolescents, including, but not limited to, families of color and other marginalized populations, and (2) mechanism-driven research in developmental psychopathology to elucidate pathways to risk and resilience. Candidates with other related research programs will also be considered and are encouraged to apply. The Penn State clinical psychology doctoral program is a clinical science program, accredited by both PCSAS and APA. The Psychology Department is strongly connected with the Social Sciences Research Institute (SSRI; http://www.ssri.psu.edu/ ) and the Child Study Center (CSC; https://csc.la.psu.edu/ ), which function as university-wide translational research centers, supporting advances in developmental science aimed at promoting positive educational, health, and mental health outcomes for children, adolescents, and families. Strong collaborative links exist with the other centers, as well as with the PSU Psychological Clinic and satellite centers in urban areas throughout the state. A record of collaboration is desirable for both ranks. Substantial collaboration opportunities exist within the department that align with the department\u2019s cross-cutting research themes and across campus. Candidates for the tenure-track Assistant Professor of Child Clinical Psychology position must have demonstrated ability as a researcher, scholar, and teacher in a relevant field and have evidence of growth in scholarly achievement. Duties will involve a combination of teaching (both undergraduate and graduate), research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. The ideal candidate will have a strong record of publications in top outlets and have either history of or potential for external funding. Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s\u00a0 Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically: a letter of interest, CV or resume, concise statements of research and teaching interests and three selected (re)prints. \u00a0Inquiries may be directed to the search chair, Martha Wadsworth, Professor of Psychology at ChildClinicalsearch@psu.edu. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. In addition, please arrange to have three letters of recommendation sent electronically to PsychApplications@psu.edu with the subject line: \u201cChild Clinical Psychology.\u201d\u00a0 Questions regarding the application process can be emailed to PsychApplications@psu.edu and questions regarding the position can be sent to the search chair: ChildClinicalsearch@psu.edu Visit our website at https://psych.la.psu.edu/ for more information on our Department. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-line-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Psychology--Industrial-Organizational-Psychology_REQ_0000081629-1": {"title": "Tenure-line Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology, Industrial-Organizational Psychology", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Psychology at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA, USA, welcomes applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology search for a full-time tenure-track faculty member to join the Industrial-Organizational (I-O) Psychology program ( https://psych.la.psu.edu/graduate/program-areas/industrial-organizational ) .\u00a0 A Ph.D. in I-O Psychology or a related field is required by the appointment date for all ranks. All levels are welcome to apply, with preference for candidates who have completed their PhD and have at least a few years of experience in an academic position. Candidates with advanced quantitative skills are preferred; content of research focus is open, but ideally complements existing expertise (e.g., leadership, selection, individual and group differences, organizational/national culture). Candidates for Assistant Professor of Psychology must have demonstrated ability as a researcher, scholar, and teacher in a relevant field and evidence of growth in scholarly achievement that is commensurate with years of experience. The ideal candidate is publishing in top I-O psychology journals, has record of or clear potential for external funding, and has clear potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Candidates for Associate Professor of Psychology must have demonstrated excellence as a researcher, scholar, teacher and mentor in a relevant field. The ideal candidate has strong record of publication in top I-O journals, has a history of external funding, and strong record of teaching and mentoring of students and early career scholars. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. Responsibilities for both Assistant Professor and Associate Professor include maintaining a strong record of publications in top outlets, resident instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and normal university service.\u00a0Onsite teaching is an essential function of this job. Rich opportunities exist for collaboration within the department and across campus, and a record of collaboration is desirable. Substantial collaboration opportunities exist if the candidate has interests that align with any of the department\u2019s cross-cutting research themes. More information on these cross-cutting research themes can be found at https://psych.la.psu.edu/about-us/research/. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates should submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically:\u00a0\u00a0 a cover letter of application,\u00a02) concise statements of research and teaching interests, 3) a CV, and 4) three selected (re)prints System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. In addition, please arrange to have three letters of recommendation sent electronically to PsychApplications@psu.edu with the subject line: \u201cI-O Psych.\u201d Inquiries may be directed to the search chair, Alicia Grandey, Liberal Arts Professor of Psychology at IOsearch@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Professor--Political-Science_REQ_0000081601-2": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Political Science", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-26\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Political Science at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA, USA, invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position, at the rank of Assistant Professor . The Department invites applications from scholars in any political science subfield whose research and teaching examine the intersection of artificial intelligence and politics and who can offer undergraduate and graduate courses in political methodology, including causal inference. Relevant areas of research and teaching include, but are not limited to, the uses of AI by governments, politicians, or candidates; the effects of AI on political institutions, disinformation, public discourse, or political behavior; the regulation of AI technologies; the political economy or geopolitics of AI; the role of AI in political violence and its effects on democracy; or the development of social science methodologies related to artificial intelligence. The Assistant Professor will have demonstrated ability as a researcher and a promising research agenda with a focus on artificial intelligence and political science. The candidate should show potential for excellence in instruction and mentoring at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Promise for securing external research funding is also desirable. This position will include resident and online teaching and normal university service. The teaching load during the academic year is four courses. Onsite teaching is an essential function of this job. Duties will involve a combination of teaching, research, and service, based on the candidate\u2019s qualifications. A Ph.D. in Political Science or related field is required by the appointment date. Review of applications will begin\u00a0immediately\u00a0and will continue until an applicant is selected. Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically: a letter of interest, CV or resume, a writing sample, and a list of three references with contact information. Inquiries may be directed to Paige McCarthy, Assistant to the Head of Political Science ( pem5220@psu.edu ). Visit our website at https://polisci.la.psu.edu/ for more information on our department. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor-in-Advanced-Manufacturing_REQ_0000081248-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor in Advanced Manufacturing", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Harold and Inge Marcus Department of Industrial and Manufacturing Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park invites applications for a full-time Assistant Research Professor to lead and support research in advanced manufacturing. The position may involve manufacturing process development, joining and separation, repair and remanufacturing, mechanical design, materials and process characterization, sensing, and data-driven analysis for engineered products and systems. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Design and evaluate manufacturing processes, components, structures, fixtures, tooling, and/or experimental systems. Characterize process behavior, material response, defects, interfaces, and performance using appropriate experimental, sensing, or machine learning methods. Prepare peer-reviewed publications, technical reports, presentations, invention disclosures, sponsor deliverables, and research proposals. Collaborate with faculty, students, technical staff, industry partners, and government sponsors in multidisciplinary research projects. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. by the appointment start date in mechanical, industrial, manufacturing, materials, welding, product design, or a closely related engineering field. Demonstrated research experience in manufacturing-process development, joining or materials processing, repair/remanufacturing, mechanical or structural design, or closely related areas. Relevant capability in one or more areas such as CAD, materials characterization, process monitoring, machine learning. Strong written and oral communication skills and the ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team. Application Materials Full curriculum vitae. Names and contact information for three professional references. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Lecturer-or-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-in-Astronomy-and-Astrophysics_REQ_0000081157-2": {"title": "Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Astronomy and Astrophysics", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Astronomy and Astrophysics at Penn State invites applications for a full-time Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor position (non-tenure track) to begin by January 2027. The successful candidate will join a team that runs very large online interdomain classes in astronomy and art. They will be responsible for working on the day-to-day operations of the classes, including availability on Zoom office hours, answering student emails, grading assignments, and making course announcements. They will also be partners in efforts to improve and update the course materials, which include the University of Mars video game (written in Unity 3D), astronomy art projects, creative writing assignments, and telescope observation quests with the Slooh network. They can also participate in new video game development for other astronomy courses at Penn State, in instructional design, programming, or art design. Education and Experience The successful candidate should have a master\u2019s degree (Lecturer) or a Ph.D. (Assistant Teaching Professor) in Astronomy, Physics, Art, or in a related field. The successful candidate should have teaching experience, a strong interest in teaching in an online format, and a student-centered, experiential teaching philosophy. They should also have experience and interest in a combination of astronomical art, video game design, video game programming, and astronomy education research. Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include the following: Cover letter detailing qualifications for the position including relevant educational background as well as any related teaching experience. Curriculum vitae or resume. Statement of teaching interests. In addition, please arrange for at least three reference letters to be sent to astro-jobs@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by September 30, 2026, will receive full consideration. Salary and benefits will be competitive and commensurate with the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. This position has the potential to be performed as a hybrid of remote and on-site work. For more information about our department or undergraduate program, visit https://science.psu.edu/astro . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Clinical-Professor--Penn-State-Psychological-Clinic_REQ_0000081026-2": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor, Penn State Psychological Clinic", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Psychology at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a full-time adult-track, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor position for the Penn State Psychological Clinic .\u00a0 The Psychological Clinic is a fully licensed comprehensive outpatient community mental health center for the region, as well as the primary training and research site for the Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychology. The clinic is among the largest associated with a doctoral training program in the United States, providing psychological and neuropsychological assessment for adults, adolescents, and children; psychological outpatient treatment for adults, \u00a0adolescents, children, and families, and psychiatric outpatient treatment for adults, including those with serious mental illness and personality pathology; and school- and hospital-based intervention programs. Faculty supervisors and clinical staff are licensed and paneled with major insurance companies to bill for services.\u00a0 Penn State is an APA and PCSAS accredited clinical science doctoral program. The Psychological Clinic facilitates the seamless integration of research and practice in clinical training with a fully developed practice-research network for conducting clinical investigations.\u00a0 This clinical faculty appointment is a non-tenure-line position. We wish to fill this position\u00a0immediately;\u00a0start\u00a0date is negotiable.\u00a0\u00a0 The College of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.\u00a0 Information on faculty ranks and progression can be found at\u00a0 https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21 Responsibilities include\u00a0direct clinical care (i.e., individual and group psychotherapy, assessment, consultation) in the Psychological Clinic and/or in community agencies contracted with the Clinic, as well as a combination of undergraduate/classroom teaching, graduate practicum teaching, and supervision of Clinical Psychology PhD students. This position will include resident and online instruction and normal university service.\u00a0 MINIMUM EDUCATION, WORK EXPERIENCE & REQUIRED CERTIFICATIONS A Doctorate in Clinical or Counseling Psychology or related field is required by the appointment date, and the candidate must be licensed or license eligible within 90 days of hire.\u00a0Rank and length of term are determined by qualifications. Experience with conducting assessments and providing evidence-based treatment is required; experience with one or more of the following is also strongly preferred: Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT), Psychodynamic Therapy/ies (e.g., Transference-Focused Therapy/TFP) and Dialectical Behavioral Therapy (DBT)). Other preferred qualifications include knowledge of HIPPA regulations and mental health law, an exceptional interest in the integration of science and practice, and a commitment to inclusion in the applicant\u2019s clinical practice, teaching, and/or supervision. Interested candidates must submit an online application at\u00a0 Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board, and should upload the following application materials: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information.\u00a0 For\u00a0information or questions regarding the position, please contact\u00a0Dr. Sandra Testa Michelson at smt3@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Deployables-and-Undersea-Connectivity---Department-Head--FACULTY-_REQ_0000081115-2": {"title": "Deployables and Undersea Connectivity \u2013 Department Head (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are searching for a highly motivated and experienced Department Head to join our Engineering Systems Research and Development Division of the Undersea Systems Office (USO) at the Applied Research Laboratory at Penn State. This position will provide strategic and operational leadership for the Deployables and Undersea Connectivity Department (DUC). The mission of the DUC is to develop and mature technical methods and devices to connect platforms in the undersea domain, as well as bridge to above the sea-air boundary, support tethered and untethered communication techniques between stationary or moving undersea platforms, and employ these capabilities to solve the most challenging undersea communications problems. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Technical Leadership - Provide technical leadership by advancing the Department's research and engineering capabilities while ensuring personnel maintain the highest standards of technical excellence Programmatic Leadership - Lead programs and multidisciplinary teams while collaborating with laboratory leadership and external stakeholders to identify, develop, and pursue new research and business opportunities Resource Management - Manage departmental resources by partnering with USO leadership, Project Managers, and Principal Investigators to align staffing and resources with program priorities Personnel Management - Lead personnel development by establishing performance expectations, conducting performance evaluations, identifying professional development opportunities, and recruiting, retaining, and mentoring high-performing engineering, research, faculty, and student staff Lead experiment driven applied research and development to deliver innovative technical solutions that support sponsors and national security missions Plan, staff, and execute programs to ensure departmental personnel are effectively utilized and aligned with organizational goals and customer needs Foster a culture of innovation by encouraging collaboration, technical growth, and the exploration of emerging technologies and research opportunities Additional responsibilities for higher-level positions includes: Leading small to medium sized teams from concept development through prototype capability demonstration in relevant environments Developing and maintaining relationships with external organizations and sponsors Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/Experience areas include: Managing programs, people, and a demonstrated capability to set and meet goals and objective Development of system test and verification plans Underwater acoustics and communication methods Mechanical and optical properties of fiber optic cabling, its deployment, and the fundamentals of data transmission Electronic design and RF communication devices and techniques Ability to express ideas successfully to drive understanding Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Secret level or higher and may be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility, if required Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: Proven history of identifying sponsor needs and developing proposals to address those needs Experience collaborating in multi-disciplinary, team-oriented cultures Experience in the design and testing of tethered and untethered undersea deployable devices (buoys, sensors, tow bodies, etc.) Master\u2019s Degree or PhD in a relevant field Your working location will be fully on-site located in State College, PA. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/School-of-Music-Part-Time-Adjunct-Lecturer_REQ_0000021434-1": {"title": "School of Music Part-Time Adjunct Lecturer", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The School of Music is looking to hire a part-time adjunct lecturer. This position may teach courses and assist with various tasks related to teaching, such as, grading and setting up technology. These positions are typically only for one semester. You will need to submit your Curriculum Vitae in order to apply. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Bharti-Lab_REQ_0000081344-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Bharti Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The\u00a0 Bharti lab \u00a0at\u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University , in the\u00a0 Department of Biology \u00a0and the\u00a0 Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics , is recruiting multiple highly motivated\u00a0 Postdoctoral Scholars\u00a0 to conduct research for an NIH-NSF funded project on human health, movement, and infectious diseases. The project focuses on the transmission dynamics and spatial trajectory of measles and Ebola outbreaks in the Democratic Republic of the Congo as well as the environmental factors that contribute to spillover of Ebola. Successful applicants will have experience in\u00a0 one of the following : Spatial analysis using GIS\u00a0 Quantitative disease modeling in R and/or Python And some command of\u00a0 at least two \u00a0of the following: Statistics Data analysis Public health or global health Strong scientific communication in English (Written and verbal), French fluency is a plus but not required Creative, interdisciplinary thinkers interested in human health and infectious diseases research are encouraged to apply. Applicants with combined backgrounds of natural science and social science or quantitative training will be considered favorably. These positions are 100% research, no teaching with potential for growth into postdoctoral leadership positions within Penn State\u2019s CIDD. Relocation to Penn State is required, remote work is not permitted. Salary follows published NIH postdoctoral pay scale.\u00a0 We are a small, productive, fun lab with a history of placing postdocs into successful careers in academia, government, industry, and humanitarian organizations. Education and Experience Completed Ph.D. degree in Biology, Epidemiology, Ecology, or a related field required. Application Requirements All application materials must be submitted electronically. Please provide: A current CV A personal statement describing why you are a qualified candidate for this position, including your short and long-term professional goals (1-2 pages) A research statement describing your research interests (1-3 pages) Contact information for three references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Ability to start soon is preferred. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Please send questions to\u00a0 nita@psu.edu \u00a0and explore our lab at\u00a0 www.humidlab.com . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director--Silicon-Carbide-Innovation-Alliance_REQ_0000078420-2": {"title": "Director, Silicon Carbide Innovation Alliance", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Director, Silicon Carbide Innovation Alliance (SCIA) \u00a0 Office of the \u00a0 Senior \u00a0 Vice President for Research (OSVPR) and the Materials Research Institute (MRI) \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University \u00a0 Position Overview \u00a0 The Silicon Carbide Innovation Alliance (SCIA) at Penn State Materials Research Institute \u00a0 seeks \u00a0 a dynamic and entrepreneurial leader to serve as its next Director. SCIA is a n \u00a0 industry-engaged research alliance focused on advancing silicon carbide ( SiC ) materials, crystal growth, wafer processing, and device-relevant technologies critical to next-generation power electronics, energy systems, and national security applications. \u00a0 The Director will lead a rapidly growing, externally funded research enterprise that integrates university research strengths with industry needs. This role requires a strategic builder who can expand industrial membership, secure government funding, and translate technical capabilities into impactful collaborations. \u00a0 SCIA operates at the intersection of academia, industry, and government, and is closely aligned with Penn State\u2019s broader leadership in semiconductors, materials science, and workforce development. \u00a0 \u00a0 Key Responsibilities \u00a0 Strategic Leadership & Growth \u00a0 Develop and execute a multi-year strategic vision to grow SCIA\u2019s technical capabilities, membership, and national visibility\u00a0 \u00a0 Expand SCIA\u2019s industrial consortium model, including recruitment and retention of member companies\u00a0 \u00a0 Identify \u00a0 emerging opportunities in \u00a0 SiC \u00a0 and wide bandgap semiconductors and position SCIA for leadership\u00a0 \u00a0 Research Development & Funding \u00a0 Lead proposal development for federal agencies (e.g., DoD, DOE, NSF) and large-scale initiatives\u00a0 \u00a0 Build and manage a diversified funding portfolio spanning industry, federal, and state sources\u00a0 \u00a0 Translate industry needs into funded research programs and collaborative projects\u00a0 \u00a0 Industry Engagement & Partnerships \u00a0 Serve as the primary liaison between SCIA and industry partners \u00a0 while working closely with the MRI Industrial \u00a0 Liaison \u00a0 and \u00a0 Penn State Corporate Engagement Center \u00a0 for member recruitment \u00a0 Develop long-term strategic partnerships with semiconductor manufacturers, suppliers, and end users\u00a0 \u00a0 Operations & Financial Management \u00a0 Oversee budgets across multiple projects and funding streams, ensuring financial sustainability and transparency\u00a0 \u00a0 Manage center operations, including staffing, facilities \u00a0 utilization , and reporting requirements\u00a0 \u00a0 Implement performance metrics and reporting structures aligned with stakeholder expectations\u00a0 \u00a0 Team Leadership & Workforce Development \u00a0 Lead and mentor interdisciplinary teams of faculty, staff, postdoctoral scholars, and students\u00a0 \u00a0 Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performance culture\u00a0 \u00a0 Support workforce development initiatives aligned with semiconductor manufacturing and materials innovation\u00a0 \u00a0 Research Translation & \u00a0 Impact \u00a0 Accelerate the transition of research outcomes into industry-relevant solutions\u00a0 \u00a0 Support intellectual property development, technology transfer, and commercialization pathways\u00a0 \u00a0 Promote SCIA capabilities nationally through workshops, consortia, and technical forums\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications \u00a0 Required \u00a0 Demonstrated \u00a0 expertise \u00a0 in silicon carbide ( SiC ) materials, crystal growth, wafer processing, or closely related semiconductor technologies\u00a0 \u00a0 Proven \u00a0 track record \u00a0 of securing and managing externally funded research /manufacturing \u00a0 programs\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience working with or within industry, including collaborative R&D or product development\u00a0 \u00a0 Strong leadership and organizational skills, with experience managing teams and complex projects\u00a0 \u00a0 Excellent communication skills and ability to engage stakeholders across academia, industry, and government\u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred \u00a0 Significant industrial experience (10+ years) in semiconductor manufacturing, materials processing, or related fields\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience leading or \u00a0 participating \u00a0 in industry consortia or research alliances\u00a0 \u00a0 Demonstrated success in building partnerships and growing membership-based organizations\u00a0 \u00a0 Experience managing shared research infrastructure or core facilities\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Professor of Practice Opportunity \u00a0 Penn State welcomes candidates from industry who bring deep practical experience and leadership in semiconductor technologies. Candidates may be considered for appointment as \u00a0 Professor of Practice , a non-tenure-track faculty title designed for individuals with extensive industry leadership experience. \u00a0 Per Penn State guidelines, Professor of Practice candidates typically: \u00a0 Possess 10+ years of high-level experience in industry or government\u00a0 \u00a0 Are nationally or internationally recognized for their contributions\u00a0 \u00a0 Bring a unique ability to bridge academic research and real-world application\u00a0 \u00a0 A terminal academic degree is not \u00a0 required \u00a0 for this appointment. \u00a0 \u00a0 Reporting Structure and Environment \u00a0 The Director will report to the leadership of the Materials Research Institute and work closely with the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences \u00a0 and Office of the VP for Research . The position interfaces broadly with Penn State colleges, core facilities, and external partners. \u00a0 SCIA benefits from proximity to world-class infrastructure, including materials synthesis, characterization, and semiconductor processing facilities, enabling end-to-end innovation from crystal growth to device-relevant testing. \u00a0 \u00a0 P lease \u00a0 submit \u00a0 a cover letter and resume for consideration. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Pennsylvania-Legislative-Science---Technology-Policy-Fellow--Joint-State-Government-Commission-_REQ_0000080912-2": {"title": "Pennsylvania Legislative Science & Technology Policy Fellow (Joint State Government Commission)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Science and Technology Policy (COPA-STEP) Program COPA-STEP, part of the Law, Policy and Engineering (LPE) Initiative in the College of Engineering, serves as the applied practice branch of LPE\u2019s interdisciplinary mission. While LPE drives interdisciplinary education in law, policy, and engineering, COPA-STEP specializes in real-world policy engagement and professional development, reinforcing LPE's mission to produce actionable knowledge that supports public, environmental, and scientific welfare. COPA-STEP aims to strengthen ties between the scientific community and the General Assembly in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, while encouraging and equipping more scientists and engineers with the skills for effective careers in government and public service. 2026-2027 Pennsylvania Legislative Science and Technology Policy Fellowship The Pennsylvania General Assembly is the largest full-time legislature in the nation and regularly deals with science or technology-related issues. Yet, legislators and staff, as well as advisory bodies could utilize science, technology, engineering and math (STEM) expertise to keep up with increasing science and technology issues facing the Commonwealth. Pennsylvania Science and Technology Policy Fellows help bridge this gap to provide science and technical expertise to lawmakers. Thus, COPA-STEP is recruiting for a one-year Legislative Science & Technology Policy Fellow embedded in the Joint State Government Commission. The Joint State Government Commission (JSGC) serves as a bipartisan and bicameral research agency of the PA General Assembly. The JSGC provides the legislature with a readily available mechanism for conducting interdisciplinary studies. The nonpartisan Fellow will embed with the staff of JSGC in Harrisburg, PA, for twelve months starting Fall 2026. The Fellow will equip JSGC with the expert knowledge and advanced research, analysis, and writing skills needed to meaningfully contribute to policy work within JSGC and enable the Pennsylvania General Assembly to make sound, data-driven policy and decisions. To ensure a successful fellowship year, the Fellow will receive training from LPE/COPA-STEP in Pennsylvania state government, the Pennsylvania policy process, policy writing instruction, communicating science and technology to non-scientific audiences, and on how to be an \u201chonest broker\u201d, i.e., providing evidence-based, objective, and nonpartisan advice that helps expand or clarify the choices for decision-making in an unbiased way. JSGC staff will manage the day-to-day work of the fellow. The primary job functions and responsibilities of the Fellow are: Conduct and synthesize research, write and edit reports, and create policy recommendations on AI or related topics as assigned by the JSGC. Meet both in-person and virtually with experts and stakeholders who have experience in the topic areas being studied. Assist in preparing meeting materials, including presentations, and attend meetings, seminars, conferences, and other events at the direction of the JSGC. Manage schedule and workflow to ensure reports are completed in a timely manner. Work in team settings. Perform other office and administrative functions as needed.\u00a0 Attend trainings and weekly or bi-weekly check-ins with LPE/COPA-STEP and provide feedback, as requested. Support occasional LPE/COPA-STEP programming. Eligible candidates must have a Ph.D. or terminal degree in a relevant field (e.g., M.D., D.V.M., M.P.H., M.Eng., or equivalent). Preferred candidates will have strong quantitative empirical research and data visualization skills. In addition, preferred candidates will have exceptional writing skills, the ability to communicate with nontechnical audiences and translate complex ideas into easily digestible information, take initiative and manage their time well. This position is based in Harrisburg, PA and will work in-office at JSGC for the first six months of employment before being allowed to participate in a hybrid in-office/telework schedule. To apply, candidates should provide 1) a cover letter summarizing their background, relevant skills, interests, and goals, interest in the position, and their contact information; 2) a current resume; and 3) names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Pennsylvania-Legislative-Science---Technology-Policy-Fellow--Local-Government-Commission-_REQ_0000080911-2": {"title": "Pennsylvania Legislative Science & Technology Policy Fellow (Local Government Commission)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Science and Technology Policy (COPA-STEP) Program COPA-STEP, part of the Law, Policy and Engineering (LPE) Initiative in the College of Engineering, serves as the applied practice branch of LPE\u2019s interdisciplinary mission. While LPE drives interdisciplinary education in law, policy, and engineering, COPA-STEP specializes in real-world policy engagement and professional development, reinforcing LPE's mission to produce actionable knowledge that supports public, environmental, and scientific welfare. COPA-STEP aims to strengthen ties between the scientific community and the General Assembly in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, while encouraging and equipping more scientists and engineers with the skills for effective careers in government and public service. 2026-2027 Pennsylvania Legislative Science and Technology Policy Fellowship The Pennsylvania General Assembly is the largest full-time legislature in the nation and regularly deals with science or technology-related issues. Yet, legislators and staff, as well as advisory bodies could utilize science, technology, engineering and math (STEM) expertise to keep up with increasing science and technology issues facing the commonwealth. Pennsylvania Science and Technology Policy Fellows help bridge this gap to provide science and technical expertise to lawmakers. Thus, COPA-STEP is recruiting for a one-year Legislative Science & Technology Policy Fellow embedded in the Local Government Commission. The Local Government Commission (LGC) serves as a bipartisan and bicameral service agency of the PA General Assembly. The LGC provides the legislature with research and resources for more effective and efficient local government. The nonpartisan Fellow will embed with the staff of LGC in Harrisburg, PA, for twelve months starting Fall 2026. The Fellow will equip LGC with the expert knowledge and advanced research, analysis, and writing skills needed to meaningfully contribute to policy work within LGC and enable the Pennsylvania General Assembly to make sound, data-driven policy and decisions affecting local government in the commonwealth. To ensure a successful fellowship year, the Fellow will receive training from LPE/COPA-STEP in Pennsylvania state government, the Pennsylvania policy process, policy writing instruction, communicating science and technology to non-scientific audiences, and on how to be an \u201chonest broker\u201d, i.e., providing evidence-based, objective, and nonpartisan advice that helps expand or clarify the choices for decision-making in an unbiased way. LGC staff will manage the day-to-day work of the fellow. The primary job functions and responsibilities of the Fellow are: Collaborate with the Pennsylvania State Geospatial Coordinating Board, the Pennsylvania Civic Boundary Working Group, LGC staff, and other stakeholders in the analysis and improvement of the methodology for the ascertainment of legal Pennsylvania civic boundary information and accurate representation in geospatial civic boundary data. Conduct and synthesize research, write and edit a civic boundary report including recommendations for legislative or regulatory changes at the state, county, and local level. Assist with the preparation of other reports, and create policy recommendations as assigned by LGC. Meet both in-person and virtually with experts and stakeholders who have experience in the topic areas being studied. Assist in preparing meeting materials, including presentations, and attend meetings, seminars, conferences, and other events at the direction of the LGC. Manage schedule and workflow to ensure reports are completed in a timely manner. Work in team settings. Perform other office and administrative functions, including constituent work and the development of legislative proposals with a heavy emphasis on municipal law, as needed.\u00a0 Attend trainings and weekly or bi-weekly check-ins with LPE/COPA-STEP and provide feedback, as requested. Support occasional LPE/COPA-STEP programming. Eligible candidates must have a Ph.D. or terminal degree in a relevant field (e.g., M.D., D.V.M., M.P.H., M.Eng., or equivalent). Preferred candidates will have strong quantitative empirical research and data visualization skills. In addition, preferred candidates will have exceptional writing skills, the ability to communicate with nontechnical audiences and translate complex ideas into easily digestible information, take initiative and manage their time well. Strong candidates will demonstrate an interest in surveying, geography, geographic information systems, history, and archival and comparative state law research. This position is based in Harrisburg, PA and will work in-office at LGC for the first two months of employment before being allowed to participate in a hybrid in-office/telework schedule. To apply, candidates should provide 1) a cover letter summarizing their background, relevant skills, interests, and goals, interest in the position, and their contact information; 2) a current resume; and 3) names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Pennsylvania-Legislative-Science---Technology-Policy-Fellow--Center-for-Rural-Pennsylvania-_REQ_0000080907-2": {"title": "Pennsylvania Legislative Science & Technology Policy Fellow (Center for Rural Pennsylvania)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Science and Technology Policy (COPA-STEP) Program COPA-STEP, part of the Law, Policy and Engineering (LPE) Initiative in the College of Engineering, serves as the applied practice branch of LPE\u2019s interdisciplinary mission. While LPE drives interdisciplinary education in law, policy, and engineering, COPA-STEP specializes in real-world policy engagement and professional development, reinforcing LPE's mission to produce actionable knowledge that supports public, environmental, and scientific welfare. COPA-STEP aims to strengthen ties between the scientific community and the General Assembly in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, while encouraging and equipping more scientists and engineers with the skills for effective careers in government and public service. 2026-2027 Pennsylvania Legislative Science and Technology Policy Fellowship The Pennsylvania General Assembly is the largest full-time legislature in the nation and regularly deals with science or technology-related issues. Yet, legislators and staff, as well as advisory bodies could utilize science, technology, engineering and math (STEM) expertise to keep up with increasing science and technology issues facing the Commonwealth. Pennsylvania Science and Technology Policy Fellows help bridge this gap to provide science and technical expertise to lawmakers. Thus, COPA-STEP is recruiting for a one-year Legislative Science & Technology Policy Fellow embedded in the Center for Rural Pennsylvania. The Center for Rural Pennsylvania (CRP) is a bipartisan, bicameral legislative agency that serves as a resource for rural policy within the Pennsylvania General Assembly. CRP\u2019s work affects approximately 3.4 million residents who live in Pennsylvania\u2019s rural communities. The nonpartisan Fellow will embed with the staff of CRP in Harrisburg, PA, for twelve months starting Fall 2026. The Fellow will equip CRP with the expert knowledge and advanced research, analysis, and writing skills needed to meaningfully contribute to research-grounded policy work within the center and enable the Pennsylvania General Assembly to make sound, data-driven policy and decisions. The agency has set three research themes for the 2026-2027 year including health and wellness, economic and workforce development, and agriculture and the environment. It is anticipated that the Fellow would contribute to one or more of these areas. To ensure a successful fellowship year, the Fellow will receive training from LPE/COPA-STEP in Pennsylvania state government, the Pennsylvania policy process, applied research and policy writing instruction, communicating science and technology to non-scientific audiences, and on how to be an \u201chonest broker\u201d, i.e., providing evidence-based, objective, and nonpartisan research that helps expand or clarify the choices for decision-making in an unbiased way. CRP staff will manage the day-to-day work of the fellow.\u00a0 The primary job functions and responsibilities of the Fellow are: Conduct and synthesize research, write and edit reports or fact sheets, and create policy recommendations as assigned by the host office. Meet both in-person and virtually with experts and stakeholders who have experience in the topic areas being studied. Support the review and administration of the CRP grant program, which includes a number of external research projects on a variety of topics. Assist in preparing meeting materials, including presentations. Attend legislative committee meetings, Board of Directors meetings, seminars, conferences, and other events at the direction of the host office. Manage schedule and workflow to ensure reports are completed in a timely manner. Work in team settings. Perform other office and administrative functions as needed.\u00a0 Attend trainings and weekly or bi-weekly check-ins with LPE/COPA-STEP and provide feedback, as requested. Support occasional LPE/COPA-STEP programming. Eligible candidates must have a Ph.D. or terminal degree in a relevant field (e.g., M.D., D.V.M., M.P.H., M.Eng., or equivalent). Preferred candidates will have strong quantitative empirical research and experience with inferential statistics with proficiency in statistical software such as SPSS, Stata, and R. In addition, preferred candidates will have exceptional data visualization and writing skills, the ability to communicate with nontechnical audiences, and translate complex ideas into easily digestible information particularly around the research themes that have been adopted by the agency. The Fellow is expected to take initiative and manage their time well. This position is based in Harrisburg, PA and participates in CRP\u2019s hybrid work schedule with 3 core days in the office and the flexibility to telework the remaining 2 days. To apply, candidates should provide 1) a cover letter summarizing their background, relevant skills, interests, and goals, interest in the position, and their contact information; 2) a current resume; and 3) names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director--The-Penn-State-Critical-Materials-Alliance_REQ_0000081293-1": {"title": "Director, The Penn State Critical Materials Alliance", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University invites applications and nominations for the inaugural Director of the Penn State Critical Materials Alliance ( Penn State CMA) , a strategic university-wide initiative focused on advancing research, workforce development, industry engagement, and innovation across the critical minerals and materials value chain. Penn State possesses the breadth required to address the entire critical minerals and materials lifecycle - the new Director will be instrumental in aggregating and focusing expertise across campus . \u00a0 The Penn State CMA is a university-wide initiative managed by the Materials Research Institute (MRI) on behalf of Penn State's Office of the Senior Vice President for Research. The Alliance brings together faculty and research infrastructure from across the University, including the Colleges of Earth and Mineral Sciences, Engineering, Eberly College of Science, Smeal College of Business, and Information Sciences and Technology, together with Penn State's Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) and major interdisciplinary institutes including the Institute of Energy and the Environment (IEE), National Security Institute (NSI), and Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS). \u00a0 The Director will provide visionary leadership for a growing interdisciplinary effort spanning resource discovery and characterization, extraction and separation, advanced materials processing and manufacturing, circular economy approaches, artificial intelligence and supply-chain analytics, and the societal dimensions of critical minerals and materials development. The successful candidate will hold a tenured faculty appointment at the Professor rank in an academic department aligned with their expertise and will work closely with colleges, interdisciplinary institutes, and research centers across the University. Exceptionally accomplished candidates currently at the Associate Professor rank may be considered when their record supports appointment at the Professor rank. \u00a0 The Director will be responsible for building and leading a nationally recognized interdisciplinary program that positions Penn State as a leader in securing domestic supply chains for critical minerals and materials essential to energy technologies, advanced manufacturing, national security, and economic competitiveness. \u00a0 Responsibilities \u00a0 The Director will be expected to : \u00a0 \u2022 Develop and execute a strategic vision for the Penn State CMA . \u00a0 \u2022 Build and lead interdisciplinary teams spanning multiple colleges, institutes, and campuses. \u00a0 \u2022 Foster a collaborative culture that integrates expertise across exploration, extraction, processing, manufacturing, recycling, AI-enabled systems, economics, policy, and workforce development. \u00a0 \u2022 Expand partnerships with industry, federal agencies, national laboratories, state agencies, and international collaborators. \u00a0 \u2022 Develop and lead large-scale research initiatives and center-scale proposals to federal sponsors including DOE, DoD, USGS, NSF, NIST, and related agencies. \u00a0 \u2022 Establish and grow industry partnerships, consortia, and collaborative research programs with Federal Labs ( e.g. DOE Labs) that accelerate technology translation and workforce development. \u00a0 \u2022 Coordinate strategic investments in shared research infrastructure, pilot-scale testbeds, and workforce programs that support critical minerals and materials innovation. \u00a0 \u2022 Advance educational and workforce initiatives that prepare students, postdoctoral scholars, and technical professionals for careers in the critical minerals and materials ecosystem. \u00a0 \u2022 Serve as an advocate and spokesperson for Penn State's critical minerals and materials activities at the regional, national, and international levels. \u00a0 \u2022 Maintain an internationally recognized program of scholarship consistent with appointment at the rank of Professor. \u00a0 Director Resources \u00a0 The successful candidate will receive a competitive salary and startup package commensurate with their experience and consistent with Penn State policies. In addition, Penn State is committed to providing the resources necessary to establish the Penn State Critical Materials Alliance as a nationally recognized center of excellence that convenes academia, industry, and government . This support will include the operational and programmatic infrastructure needed to foster interdisciplinary collaboration, develop strategic partnerships, and accelerate the growth of large-scale research and workforce initiatives. Resources will be provided through a collaborative investment involving the University, participating colleges, and interdisciplinary institutes, with the goal of establishing a sustainable, nationally recognized Alliance. \u00a0 Required Qualifications \u00a0 Candidates must possess : \u00a0 \u2022 An earned doctorate in engineering, materials science, geosciences, chemistry, physics, or a closely related field. \u00a0 \u2022 Qualifications commensurate with appointment as a tenured Professor at Penn State ; exceptionally accomplished Associate Professors may be considered when their record supports appointment at the Professor rank. \u00a0 \u2022 An internationally recognized record of scholarship and research accomplishments relevant to critical minerals, materials, energy technologies, advanced manufacturing, resource systems, recycling, supply chains, or related fields. \u00a0 \u2022 A demonstrated record of leading large interdisciplinary research programs, centers, institutes, consortia, or comparable collaborative efforts, with the stature and credibility to lead senior faculty across multiple academic units. \u00a0 \u2022 Strong communication and relationship-building skills with academic, industry, government, and community stakeholders. \u00a0 \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to fostering collaborative and inclusive research environments. \u00a0 \u2022 US Citizen or Green Card Holder \u00a0 \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications \u00a0 Preference will be given to candidates with: \u00a0 \u2022 Experience leading multi-institutional or center-scale research initiatives. \u00a0 \u2022 Experience working with federal agencies and national laboratories. \u00a0 \u2022 Experience developing industry partnerships and translational research programs. \u00a0 \u2022 Knowledge of one or more areas relevant to the critical minerals and materials value chain, including exploration, extraction and separation, advanced manufacturing, circular economy and recycling, supply-chain resilience, artificial intelligence and digital systems. \u00a0 \u2022 Experience building workforce development, educational, or training programs. \u00a0 \u00a0 Applications should include a curriculum vitae, Research & Leadership Statement, and professional references . \u00a0 \u00a0 About the Penn State Critical Materials Alliance ( Penn State CMA ) \u00a0 The Penn State CMA i s Penn State's university-wide organization for coordinating research, education, workforce development, industry engagement, and strategic partnerships in critical minerals and materials. Managed by the Materials Research Institute on behalf of the Office of the Senior Vice President for Research, the Alliance brings together faculty, facilities, and programs from across the University to address the entire critical minerals and materials value chain\u2014from resource discovery and extraction to processing, advanced manufacturing, recycling, and supply-chain resilience. \u00a0 The Penn State CMA serves as Penn State's focal point for interdisciplinary collaboration and external engagement, accelerating large-scale research initiatives, technology translation, workforce development, and partnerships with industry, federal agencies, national laboratories, and state organizations. By integrating expertise across the Colleges of Earth and Mineral Sciences, Engineering, Eberly College of Science, Information Sciences and Technology, Smeal College of Business, the Applied Research Laboratory, and major interdisciplinary institutes\u2014including the Materials Research Institute (MRI), Institute of Energy and the Environment (IEE), National Security Institute (NSI), and Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS)\u2014the Alliance positions Penn State as a national leader in advancing secure, sustainable, and resilient critical minerals and materials supply chains. \u00a0 \u00a0 About Penn State \u00a0 Penn State is a top-ranked public research university and one of the largest and most comprehensive universities in the United States. With more than $1. 4 billion in annual research expenditures and a longstanding commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration, Penn State provides an exceptional environment for research, innovation, education, and public impact. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Position-in-Functional-Ceramic-Materials_REQ_0000080791-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Position in Functional Ceramic Materials", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar position in the area of functional ceramic materials in the Randall group. The successful candidate will join an internationally recognized research group conducting cutting-edge research on the processing, characterization, and performance of advanced ceramic materials for energy, electronic, and electromechanical applications within the Materials Research Institute (MRI), The research program focuses on a broad range of functional ceramics, including:\u00a0 Piezoelectric and ferroelectric materials\u00a0 Capacitor dielectric materials\u00a0 Cathode materials for next-generation batteries\u00a0 Advanced ceramic processing and microstructural engineering\u00a0 The successful candidate should have demonstrated expertise in the processing, structure, property, and performance relationships of ceramic materials. Experience in one or more of the following areas is highly desirable:\u00a0 Ceramic powder synthesis and processing\u00a0 Structural and microstructural characterization\u00a0 Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM)\u00a0 Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM)\u00a0 Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM)\u00a0 X-ray diffraction (XRD) and related X-ray characterization techniques\u00a0 Electrical and electromechanical characterization of functional ceramics\u00a0 Impedance spectroscopy\u00a0 Electrochemical characterization\u00a0 Thermally Stimulated Depolarization Current (TSDC) analysis\u00a0 Ferroelectric, dielectric, piezoelectric, or electrochemical measurements\u00a0 Other advanced characterization techniques relevant to functional materials\u00a0 The Postdoctoral Scholar will be expected to:\u00a0 Conduct independent, high-quality research leading to publications in leading international journals.\u00a0 Develop and execute innovative research projects aligned with the group's research objectives.\u00a0 Work collaboratively with graduate students, undergraduate researchers, visiting scientists, and faculty collaborators.\u00a0 Provide technical guidance and mentorship to students and visiting researchers.\u00a0 Assist with the operation and development of advanced experimental capabilities within the laboratory.\u00a0 Contribute to the preparation of research proposals, technical reports, and presentations.\u00a0 Present research findings at national and international conferences.\u00a0 Publish\u00a0research in high-level journals.\u00a0 Required Qualifications:\u00a0 Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Ceramic Engineering, Physics, Chemistry, or a closely related discipline.\u00a0 Strong experimental background in functional ceramic materials.\u00a0 Excellent written and oral communication skills.\u00a0 Demonstrated publication record in peer-reviewed journals.\u00a0 Ability to work both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary research team.\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications and Experience in one or more of the following areas will be considered an advantage:\u00a0 Functional oxide ceramics\u00a0 Ferroelectric and piezoelectric materials\u00a0 Multilayer ceramic capacitors (MLCCs)\u00a0 Solid-state electrochemistry\u00a0 Battery materials\u00a0 Advanced microscopy and spectroscopy\u00a0 Reliability and degradation of electronic materials\u00a0 Data analysis and modeling of structure\u2013property relationships\u00a0 This position offers the opportunity to work within a highly collaborative and internationally recognized research environment with access to state-of-the-art characterization and processing facilities. The successful candidate will be encouraged to develop independent research directions while contributing to a broad portfolio of sponsored research programs.\u00a0 Applications should include a cover letter describing research interests and relevant experience, a curriculum vitae, a list of publications, and the names and contact information of three professional references.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Teaching-Professor--of-Companion-Animal-Biology-and-Management_REQ_0000080654-2": {"title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor  of Companion Animal Biology and Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-11\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Companion Animal Biology and Management JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Animal Science at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, invites applications for an Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Companion Animal Biology and Management. This is a 48-week, non-tenure line faculty position with 75% Teaching and 25% Extension responsibilities. The successful candidate will provide leadership in companion animal teaching and youth outreach programs and will play a central role in undergraduate education within the Animal Science major. Undergraduate teaching responsibilities may include ANSC 150S (ANSC Freshman Seminar), ANSC 215 (Pets in Society), ANSC 305 (Companion Animal Nutrition), ANSC 315 (Small Animal Health and Disease), ANSC 415 (Companion Animal Behavior), ANSC 419W (Applied Animal Welfare), and/or development of additional courses aligned with departmental needs and candidate expertise. Penn State values the incorporation of experiential learning into formal coursework. The faculty member will mentor undergraduate students and advise the Small and Exotic Animal Club. The successful candidate will develop and deliver Extension and outreach programs focused on companion animal science through activities such as 4-H/youth programs, workshops, camps, and educational events. They will collaborate with Penn State Extension personnel to deliver educational materials through in person and virtual formats and will engage with stakeholders, alumni, and companion animal organizations to support educational initiatives. The successful candidate will contribute to collaborative scholarship across the Department and College of Agricultural Sciences. They will engage in appropriate professional and service activities within and outside the Department. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Applicants must have a Ph.D. and/or D.V.M/V.M.D. degree in Animal Science, Veterinary Medicine, or a closely related field. A D.V.M/V.M.D is preferred. Areas of expertise may include nutrition, physiology, reproduction, genetics, disease, behavior, or related disciplines. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching and effective outreach to formal and non-formal audiences. Experience with experiential learning, youth programs, or student organizations is desirable. Strong communication, teamwork, and leadership skills to work effectively with a diverse population of faculty, staff, students, youth audiences, and stakeholders are essential. APPLICATION Candidates should apply online with the following information: (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) names and contact information for three references, and (4) a statement of teaching philosophy and interests.\u00a0 The Department of Animal Science at Penn State includes 32 faculty members and is home to internationally recognized programs in animal nutrition, reproduction, physiology, and genetics. The companion animal curriculum is a rapidly growing program in the Department and provides extensive opportunities for student engagement, experiential learning, and outreach. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty committed to excellence in teaching, advising, and student success. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Teaching-Positions--SEDI-_REQ_0000066851-3": {"title": "Part-Time Teaching Positions (SEDI)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The School of Engineering Design and Innovation (SEDI) within the College of Engineering is seeking individuals for part-time teaching positions. A Master\u2019s Degree, in engineering or a closely related field, or similar education and experience required . Applicants should be interested in teaching as part of programs that are offered by the School. These include: 1. Engineering Design (EDSGN) Program Courses within the program, particularly the cornerstone engineering design course, assists students in learning design processes, methods, and decision-making tools while engaged in team-based design projects. Effective use of communication skills and computer-aided analysis tools are an integral part of the cornerstone engineering design course. 2. Entrepreneurship and Innovation (ENTI) Minor Courses are taught in support of the Technology-Based Entrepreneurship or the Social Entrepreneurship cluster within the Entrepreneurship and Innovation (ENTI) Minor that assist students in obtaining skills attributed to entrepreneurial behavior and innovative thinking. 3. Engineering Leadership Development (ELD) Program Courses in engineering leadership provide students with the understanding of individual, team, and organizational leadership; business acumen, global competencies and multicultural awareness; and innovation and management. 4. Law, Policy, and Engineering (LPE) Program Courses in Law, Policy, and Engineering aim to provide new cross-disciplinary perspectives and tools required to solve complex multidisciplinary problems and address societal changes. Students will be versed in science and technology policy, legal and regulatory policy, complex systems design, and anticipating technology trends. 5. Doctor of Engineering in Engineering (D.Eng.) Program T his online program provides a deep understanding of advanced engineering and high-level leadership principles, helping you prepare to direct high-performing research divisions or companies. This D.Eng. incorporates the rigor of a Ph.D. but shifts the focus of career progression from academic research to leadership in an industrial or commercial setting. 6. Other courses as part of SEDI \u2019s growing portfolio. Experience teaching online/remotely is a plus. More information of the School\u2019s programs may be found at www.sedi.psu.edu Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-Lecturer-in-EPPIC_REQ_0000080765-2": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor/Lecturer in EPPIC", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Applied Linguistics at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a full-time\u202f Lecturer or \u00a0 Assistant Teaching Professor \u00a0 position \u00a0 in the department\u2019s English for Professional Purposes Intercultural Center (EPPIC) , starting \u00a0 as soon as possible .\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 EPPIC is an established university center \u00a0 in Penn State\u2019s \u00a0 highly-ranked \u00a0 Department of Applied Linguistics \u00a0 that \u00a0 provides advanced English \u00a0 language communication \u00a0 support services to multilingual students, scholars, faculty, and staff across Penn State\u2019s global community \u00a0 and \u00a0 conducts \u00a0 research on language-in-use across academic and professional units of the university .\u00a0 \u00a0 EPPIC \u00a0 draws on \u00a0 in \u00a0 research in \u00a0 applied linguistics , \u00a0 language for specific purposes (LSP), Vygotskyan sociocultural theory , \u00a0 and move-step analysis of academic discourse. \u00a0 \u00a0 The Lecturer /Assistant Teaching Professor \u00a0 role \u00a0 is central to the delivery of EPPIC\u2019s language support services \u00a0 and includes : \u00a0 Leading workshop series for multilingual \u00a0 undergraduate students, graduate students, \u00a0 and scholars from diverse disciplines on advanced \u00a0 writing and speaking \u00a0 in \u00a0 academic and professional English; \u00a0 Leading weekly speaking-group sessions focused on both formal and informal oral communication in a university setting; \u00a0 Designing and implementing customized workshops \u00a0 by \u00a0 request \u00a0 from \u00a0 departments and programs across Penn State ; \u00a0 Offering individual consultations \u00a0 on spoken and written academic English communication \u00a0 to \u00a0 multilingual students, scholars, faculty, and staff at Penn State ; \u00a0 Providing training and mentorship to \u00a0 graduate teaching \u00a0 assistants \u00a0 assigned to \u00a0 EPPIC ; \u00a0 Initiating and contributing to \u00a0 research projects \u00a0 related to disciplinary \u00a0 genre \u00a0 analysis, \u00a0 the design and content of new language support programming, assessment of the impacts of EPPIC\u2019s language-related services on student and scholar development, and related topics. \u00a0 \u00a0 Minimum Qualifications: \u00a0 An M.A. in Applied Linguistics, TESOL, Linguistics, or a related field emphasizing the teaching of English as a n \u00a0 additional \u00a0 language and/or English for specific purposes At least three years of experience working with matriculated graduate students on discipline-specific research \u00a0 reading, \u00a0 writing, presentations, and informal academic and professional communication Specific training, \u00a0 expertise , and experience in teaching speaking \u2014 including pronunciation and specific-purpose oral genres such as research presentations, discussions, conversations with one\u2019s advisor, networking interactions, and oral examinations Superior command of written and spoken English Outstanding professional, interpersonal, and intercultural communication skills \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: \u00a0 A Ph.D. in Second Language Studies, Applied Linguistics, TESOL, or a related field is preferred. \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.\u202f Information on faculty ranks and progression can be found at \u00a0 https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Interested candidates \u00a0 must \u00a0 submit \u00a0 an online application at \u00a0 Penn State's Job Posting Board , \u00a0 and should upload the following application material s:\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 A cover letter \u00a0 that addresses the candidate\u2019s fit with EPPIC\u2019s mission and the responsibilities described above, including the candidate\u2019s approach to teaching advanced academic and professional speaking and writing and how that approach is informed by relevant theory and research; \u00a0 A current curriculum vitae; \u00a0 A statement of teaching and consultation philosophy \u00a0 that articulates how the candidate supports multilingual graduate students and scholars across disciplines, with particular attention to the teaching of speaking (pronunciation and specific-purpose oral genres); \u00a0 Representative instructional materials \u00a0 that \u00a0 demonstrate \u00a0 experience and \u00a0 expertise \u00a0 relevant to \u00a0 the role \u2014 for example, workshop or speaking-group plans, sample syllabi or session outlines, and materials developed for individual consultations; \u00a0 Evidence of teaching effectiveness, \u00a0 such as student or participant evaluations and peer or supervisor observation reports; and \u00a0 The names and contact information of three references \u00a0 who may be asked to provide letters of recommendation. \u00a0 System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit.\u00a0 For more information on the position, contact \u00a0 Meredith Doran ( mcd15@psu.edu ), chair of the search committee . \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Open-Rank-Clinical-Professor-in-Supply-Chain-Management_REQ_0000080685-2": {"title": "Open-Rank Clinical Professor in Supply Chain Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The SCIS Department of the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) invites applications for a clinical professor position in Supply Chain and Information Systems for a Spring 2027 start date.\u00a0 Salary is competitive. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. Candidates must have a terminal degree in supply chain management, information systems, business analytics or related field prior to their start date.\u00a0 A strong commitment to teaching excellence at the undergraduate and graduate programs is required. Evidence of prior teaching experience is desirable.\u00a0 The SCIS Department comprises a vibrant, research-active faculty with research and teaching interests that traverse the end-to-end supply chain and includes information systems, data analytics, business logistics, sourcing, and operations. The department offers degree programs in supply chain management, management information systems, and business analytics. We seek outstanding candidates with expertise in supply chain management and/or business analytics that would complement the faculty with high-quality teaching in student-centered and collaborative learning environments. Candidates should be able to teach undergraduate and master level courses in supply chain management, business analytics, and information systems.\u00a0 The Smeal College of Business offers a collegial working environment and excellent campus facilities. It has the Center for Supply Chain Research\u00ae ( www.smeal.psu.edu/cscr ) which advances cutting-edge research and outreach in supply chain management. The SC&IS Department ( www.smeal.psu.edu/scis ) also has strong connections with the business community through various research centers that provide opportunities to interface with faculty across various disciplines within Smeal and across Penn State. For more information, please visit www.smeal.psu.edu/research-centers . Review of applications will begin approximately August 27, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 For further information, please contact Autumn Knepp at adh5253@psu.edu . Applicants should upload a letter of intent, a statement of teaching philosophy, and a CV. Contact information for three references also should be provided. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Lecturer--Part-Time_REQ_0000080160-2": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Part-Time", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-06\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Biomedical Engineering invites applications for a part-time adjunct lecturer position for the fall 2026 semester. This appointment will be part-time, non-tenure track without benefits and no guarantee of renewal. Duties will include teaching lecture-based and/or laboratory classes, advising students and helping to assess course learning outcomes. A Ph.D. or master\u2019s degree in biomedical engineering or a closely related field is required. Previous teaching experience is preferred. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until all positions are filled. Interested applicants should upload a cover letter and resume. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Research-Technology-Officer_REQ_0000080229-1": {"title": "Research Technology Officer", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Penn State National Security Institute (NSI) invites applications for a non-tenure-line research faculty position to serve in a senior technical leadership role with the working title Research Technology Officer (RTO) . Appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Research Professor, Associate Research Professor, or Research Professor , depending on the successful candidate\u2019s experience and qualifications. NSI advances interdisciplinary research, strategic partnerships, and mission-relevant innovation to address critical national security challenges. The Institute connects Penn State\u2019s broad research capabilities with government, defense, homeland security, and industry needs, with an emphasis on technically excellent, translational, and deployable solutions. Position Overview The RTO will help shape NSI\u2019s technical strategy and research growth by identifying emerging opportunities, building interdisciplinary teams, leading large-proposal development, and strengthening external partnerships. This is a highly collaborative role for a candidate who can operate effectively at the intersection of research strategy, technical credibility, sponsor engagement, and institutional coordination. Key Responsibilities Identify and develop strategic technical opportunities aligned with NSI priorities and sponsor needs. Lead or co-lead development of large, complex, multi-investigator and multi-institution proposals. Convene Penn State faculty and external collaborators around high-value national security challenges. Help define technical road maps for major initiatives, centers, consortia, and partnerships. Build and maintain relationships with government agencies, industry partners, laboratories, and other external stakeholders. Advise institute leadership on technical positioning, investment priorities, and capability development. Support translation of research into mission-ready, dual-use, or operationally relevant applications. Contribute to institute programs that stimulate collaboration, seed new initiatives, and strengthen proposal competitiveness. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree or equivalent terminal degree in engineering, science, technology, or a closely related field. Significant experience in technical leadership, research development, innovation strategy, or complex program development, including teams that involve federal agencies, academia, and industry. Demonstrated success working across disciplines and organizations to build strategic initiatives or externally funded efforts. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to engage effectively with academic researchers, institute leadership, and external sponsors or partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with DoD, DHS, DOE, NSF, intelligence-community-adjacent organizations, national laboratories, or related federal sponsors. Experience with large-scale proposal development, center formation, or research consortium building. Familiarity with technology transition, translational R&D, dual-use innovation, or mission-driven technical programs. Experience in university-based or university-connected research environments. Additional Compliance and Information-Access Requirements This position may involve access to Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), export-controlled information, or other sensitive information in support of institute activities. The successful candidate must be able to satisfy and maintain all Penn State, federal, and sponsor requirements related to accessing, handling, and protecting such information. Depending on project, sponsor, or regulatory requirements, this position may be restricted to U.S. persons (U.S. Citizens, Lawful Permanent Residents, and/or other protected individuals) as defined under applicable U.S. Export Control Regulations. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of all required background checks and any additional role-specific verifications required by Penn State, applicable law, or sponsor/contracting partner agreements. Application Materials a cover letter describing relevant experience and interest in the role; a curriculum vitae; and any additional materials requested through the final Penn State hiring process. Review of applications will begin on a rolling basis and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Visiting-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-in-the-Archaeology-and-History-of-the-Eastern-Mediterranean_REQ_0000080510-2": {"title": "Visiting Assistant or Associate Professor in the Archaeology and History of the Eastern Mediterranean", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Classics and Ancient Mediterranean Studies (CAMS) and the Department of Anthropology at The Pennsylvania State University invite applications for a Visiting Assistant or Associate Professor in the area of A rchaeology and H istory of the e astern Mediterranean .\u00a0 The appointment will start in January 2027 , with room for some flexibility. \u00a0 This position will be filled at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor or Associate Teaching Professor . Rank will be decided based on education and experience. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Responsibilities include teaching four courses per year (two per semester), research, and some service duties. Onsite teaching is an essential function of this job.\u202f\u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 We seek candidates who are able to teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in the material culture and histo ry of the easte rn Mediterranean . The candidate\u2019 s scholarly expert ise may concern areas such as the Levant, Anatolia, and/or the Aegean , from ca. 3,000 BCE to ca. 300 CE . The candidate \u2019 s research focus may pertain to any of these regions and periods , but they should also be able to integrate material culture with textual sources . C ourses to be taught include both upper- and lower- level classes in A ncient Near Eastern and Classical Archaeology , as well as other courses on history and archaeology in the applicant\u2019s field ; e.g., current CAMS courses, such as Lands of the Bible or Sacrifice in the Ancien t World. \u00a0 \u00a0 The CAMS Department encompasses the entire Mediterranean and Near Eastern world in A ntiquity, and the successful candidate is expected to contribute to the dialogue across the se fields and disciplines . The ability to assist in developing the Department\u2019s graduate program , including an M.A. in A rchaeology, and to contribute to the Department\u2019s study abroad programs are desirable.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates for the Assistant Teaching Professor rank must have a Ph.D. in Ancient Near Eastern Studies, Mediterranean or Near Eastern Archaeology, Ancient History, Anthropology with specialization in the eastern Mediterranean or Levant, Classics, or a closely related field , i n hand by the start date. Candidates should also provide a record of scholarly p ublication and productivity, as well as evidence of undergraduate-level teaching experience.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Candidates for the Associate Teaching Professor rank must have all aforementioned requirements along with substantial undergraduate - and/or graduate-level teaching experience.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 The\u202fCollege of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.\u202f Information on faculty ranks and progression can be found at\u202f https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21\u202f\u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 To be considered for this position, applications must be submitted online at Penn State's Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials: a letter of interest, CV or resume, a sample of scholarly writing, and evidence of teaching excellence. Candidates should also arrange to have three letters of recommendation submitted to Lynn Carey, Administrative Assistant, at lmc5897@psu.edu . \u00a0 \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to the Head of the Department of Classics and Ancient Mediterranean Studies, Prof. Tawny Holm, at tholm@psu.edu . \u00a0 \u00a0 Visit our website at https://cams.la.psu.edu/ for more details on our Department. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Law---Penn-State-Dickinson-Law--University-Park-_REQ_0000080655-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Law - Penn State Dickinson Law (University Park)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-31\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Penn State Dickinson Law invites applications from both entry-level and junior lateral candidates for a tenure-track faculty position (Assistant or Associate Professor of Law), with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027, at our University Park, Pennsylvania location. We are seeking candidates to annually teach Contracts and Sales alongside two courses of their scholarly interest and our institutional need .\u00a0 Candidates may bring a wide range of qualifications, including relevant teaching or practice experience, judicial clerkships at any level, interdisciplinary scholarly work, or post-J.D. studies, degrees, or certificates. The successful candidate will be expected to: Produce high-quality scholarly research in the field of law, Teach law courses and demonstrate excellence in the classroom, Supervise and mentor student research assistants, and Provide service to the law school, university, and broader professional community. A demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence, impactful scholarship, and student mentorship is essential. About Dickinson Law: Founded in 1834, Penn State Dickinson Law is the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania\u2019s first law school and one of the oldest in the nation. Fully accredited by the ABA and a member of the AALS since 1912, Dickinson Law\u2019s mission is to educate and train lawyers equipped to excel in an evolving legal profession. The Law School is guided by core values of teaching, scholarship, service, and community, which define our mission and culture. As part of The Pennsylvania State University, Penn State Dickinson Law values belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. Penn State\u2019s Values may be found here . The position is based in University Park, PA. The University prioritizes regular on-site presence to support full engagement in the campus community. Full-time, tenured or tenure-track faculty are expected to teach in-person and work on-site. Questions about work arrangements should be directed to the hiring manager during the interview process. \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 All candidate materials must be submitted via the Penn State Career website. Interested candidates should upload a cover letter and a resume or CV. A candidate\u2019s application materials are expected to provide clear evidence supporting Penn State values and accessibility throughout their teaching, research, and/or service.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Candidates should provide the names, titles, and contact information (telephone, email, and mailing address) of three (3) professional references. Candidates who advance in the search will be notified to confirm that their references may be contacted. Questions may be sent to the Appointments Committee Chair through Melissa Walters at mbw5955@psu.edu. Applications received by September 18, 2026, will receive full consideration; however, the search will continue until the positions are filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Multiple-Open-Rank-Professor-Tenure-Track-Positions-in-Organizational-Behavior--Organizational-Theory--or-Strategy_REQ_0000080154-1": {"title": "Multiple Open-Rank Professor Tenure-Track Positions in Organizational Behavior, Organizational Theory, or Strategy", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Management and Organization (M&O) Department in the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) has two full-time tenure-track professor positions in the areas of Organizational Behavior (OB), Organizational Theory (OT), or Strategy. We seek to fill these positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor . The desired start date for the position is Fall 2027. Those who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor. For consideration for Associate or Full Professor level positions, applicants must have a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. Candidates for all ranks must have a PhD in Management or a related field by the appointment start date. Candidates at the Associate or Full Professor rank must also have demonstrated both a sufficient number of publications in high-quality journals and sufficient impact of that work on the field. Job Requirement : The preferred candidate will have publications in premier journals, a research program with high-impact or such potential underway and is able to connect with a wide array of doctoral students and faculty in our department. Faculty members in the M&O department are expected to pursue an active research program, perform undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in professional service. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. Candidates for the position can apply by uploading a letter of interest, CV, and three research papers. Candidates should also have three reference letters sent directly to mandosmeal@psu.edu . System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5 document limitations. Any questions about the position can be sent to Amanda Brown, M&O Support Coordinator, at the same email. Review of applications for the position will begin on September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The Department of Management and Organization is consistently ranked in the top-20 management departments for its research productivity and values high-level theoretical and empirical ability, collegiality and collaboration among its members, and the ability to teach management and organizational concepts effectively to multiple audiences. Our department offers two undergraduate majors (Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship; Management), two online masters programs (Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship; Strategic Management and Executive Leadership), a PhD program, courses in Smeal\u2019s full-time rMBA and DBA programs, courses in Smeal\u2019s part-time hMBA and OBMA, and operates the Farrell Center for Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship (which includes the Garber Venture Capital Fund). Our tenure-line faculty are Heejung Byun, Carolyn Dang, Raghu Garud, Don Hambrick, Stephen Humphrey, Trevor Israelsen, Jon Jachimowicz, Margaret Luciano, Vilmos Misangyi, Semin Park, Tessa Recendes, Kira Schabram, Paul Shrivastava, Linda Trevi\u00f1o, Wenpin Tsai, Dani Yin, and Rui Zhong. Our nontenure-line clinical faculty are Shawn Clark, Sean Doherty, Jeanette Miller, Lisa O\u2019Hara, \u00d6zge Pala, Federica Pinelli, and Angela Schwartz. Our nontenure-line full-time teaching faculty are Cameron Conaway, Neil Fogarty, Ron Johnson, James Jones, Dave Lenze, Travis Lesser, and Brad Leve. For more information on our department please visit https://www.smeal.psu.edu/management . The M&O Department is part of the Smeal College of Business, which depends on more than 360 faculty and staff to enact and support its strategic priorities of integrity, diversity, and sustainability and to serve the needs of more than 9,000 students. Media outlets and independent observers regularly rank Smeal among the best business schools in the world. Please visit http://www.smeal.psu.edu/ for additional information. The Smeal College of Business is located at the Pennsylvania State University\u2019s main campus (University Park) in the heart of State College, Pennsylvania. Our community features the charms of a small town with the opportunities typically only found in larger cities, with State College routinely ranked among the top 10 best college towns in the United States ( https://www.collegetransitions.com/blog/best-college-towns-in-america/ ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Smeal-Marketing-Dept-open-rank-tenure-track-position_REQ_0000080142": {"title": "Smeal Marketing Dept. open rank tenure track position", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Marketing Department in the Smeal College of Business, Penn State University (University Park, PA) seeks to fill multiple tenure-track faculty positions (open rank). We seek to fill these positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor . The desired start date for the positions is Fall 2027. T hose who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor. For consideration for Associate or Full Professor level positions, applicants must have a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. Experienced applicants who wish to be considered at the Associate or Full level should have the same qualifications as the Assistant Professor, but should also have demonstrated both a sufficient number of publications in high-quality journals and sufficient impact of that work on the field. Candidates for all ranks must have a PhD in Marketing or a related field by the appointment start date. Although research focus is open, preference will be given to those in Quantitative Modeling and/or Marketing Management and Strategy . Penn State faculty members are expected to pursue an active research program, perform undergraduate and graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in service activities. Salary and benefits will be competitive and commensurate with the background and experience of the chosen candidate. Applications should be submitted online via the PSU site. Applicants should upload a CV and cover letter, and may also provide optional supporting documents (e.g., letters of recommendation, working or published research papers, research and teaching statements, course evaluations). System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. If you have any questions regarding the positions, please contact Meg Meloy, Department Chair ( mgm16@psu.edu ). For questions about the application process and Workday portal, please contact Hollie Meyer ( hlm5317@psu.edu ). Please include \u201cMarketing Tenure Track Position 2027\u201d in the subject line of any email correspondence. More information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at https://www.smeal.psu.edu/marketing . \u00a0 Review of applications will begin late August and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Professor-in-Neurobiology-of-Insect-Chemical-Ecology_REQ_0000080427-1": {"title": "Professor in Neurobiology of Insect Chemical Ecology", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a Full Professor \u00a0in the Neurobiology of Insect Chemical Ecology in the Department of Entomology.\u00a0 This position is supported by the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences, and will contribute to the missions of the Penn State Neuroscience Institute, Center for Chemical Ecology, Center for Pollinator Research and Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics.\u00a0\u00a0 This position is part of an ongoing, cross-University cluster hire in neuroscience. We specifically seek candidates who have multidisciplinary projects that investigate the neurobiological mechanisms underlying insect chemical ecology related to visual and olfactory-mediated behaviors, including plant-insect interactions, insect-host interactions, and impacts of environmental conditions on insect behavior.\u00a0 Successful candidates are expected to have an established track record of extramural funding, published results from multidisciplinary research projects, and evidence of leadership of multidisciplinary scientific teams. \u00a0Candidates are expected to have a strong track record of student and postdoctoral scholar education and training.\u00a0 In addition to establishing a rigorous externally funded research program duties also include: Promote a culture of excellence in chemical ecology and neuroscience research, teaching, and outreach across the Penn State system Foster interdisciplinary collaborations that connect the Department of Entomology with the Huck Institute of the Life Sciences\u2019 Neuroscience Institute, Center for Chemical Ecology, Center for Pollinator Research, and Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics Contribute actively to the intellectual life and strategic growth of these Centers and Institutes through collaborative research initiatives, training activities, workshops, and seminars Join the faculty of one of the Huck Institute's six Interdisciplinary Graduate Degree Programs Engage faculty, postdoctoral scholars, and students across these interdisciplinary communities to build innovative research directions at the interface of chemical ecology and neuroscience Support the training of the next generation of scientists through classroom and experiential learning opportunities Provide mentorship for early-career faculty, postdoctoral scholars, and students Strengthen community development and engagement at the student, staff, postdoctoral, and faculty levels A PhD in life science-related field is required. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. The applicant should have an academic track record commensurate with the level of Full Professor with tenure. The successful applicant will join faculty members with complementary, interdisciplinary research interests, and have access to excellent core facilities: \u00a0 https://www.huck.psu.edu/core-facilities . Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board and should upload the following application materials electronically: a cover letter, CV, Research Statement, Teaching Statement, and the names and contact information for three references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. For more information about the position, please contact Gary Felton, Professor and Head of Entomology or Christina Grozinger, Director of the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Teaching-Faculty-Position-in-Cybersecurity_REQ_0000080140-2": {"title": "Teaching Faculty Position in Cybersecurity", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Teaching Faculty Positions\u00a0in Cybersecurity\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Department of Privacy and Cybersecurity Informatics \u00a0(PCI) in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for multiple open-rank teaching faculty positions in our cybersecurity degree program, beginning in January of 2027 at the University Park campus located in State College, Pennsylvania. These are non-tenure-line term appointments with an excellent possibility of renewal as multi-year appointments. Fully remote appointments are not permitted for these hires.\u00a0 Teaching emphases include, but are not limited to network security, fundamentals of information security, digital forensics, cyber defense tools and technologies, malware analysis, incident handling and response, data-driven cybersecurity including AI-powered cybersecurity, information security management, cybersecurity risk management, hardware security, cryptography including post-quantum cryptography, and /or organizational and human factors in cybersecurity and privacy. Applicants should provide evidence of excellence in teaching at the university level and a desire to collaborate with the PCI department faculty and the IST faculty on curricular innovation and development efforts. A commitment to teaching learners at all levels and from all backgrounds is essential. Primary responsibilities will include teaching undergraduate courses in residential, online, and/or hybrid modes. Qualified faculty may also teach graduate courses. University service is expected by all teaching faculty. \u00a0 Applicants must hold a master\u2019s degree or doctoral degree (Ph.D. or other terminal degree) in information science, cybersecurity, computer science, or a related discipline by the appointment start date with Penn State. Candidates will be considered for a teaching faculty rank commensurate with their education, experience, and qualifications in accordance with Penn State policy\u00a0 AC21 . Teaching faculty ranks within IST include Lecturer, Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, Teaching Professor, and, when appropriate, Professor of Practice. Professor of Practice candidates will be evaluated on their degree and extensive professional experience which must meet the requirements in AC21 . Applicants will include the following materials with their application: i) cover letter detailing your qualifications for the position; ii) teaching statement; iii) curriculum vitae; and iv) contact information for at least three professional references. Please limit your teaching statement to two pages and provide a description of your teaching philosophy, experience, and the pedagogical techniques you use to engage students. Additionally, indicate specific courses from our programs that you would be excited to teach, as well as any new courses you are interested in developing. Please upload one document that combines the above materials into a single PDF. Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu .\u00a0 Review of applications begins September 1, 2026, and will continue until positions are filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Integrated-Power-Systems---Energy-Conversion-Department-Head--FACULTY-_REQ_0000080318-2": {"title": "Integrated Power Systems - Energy Conversion Department Head (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are searching for a decisive, forward\u2011thinking Department Head to lead the Integrated Power Systems \u2013 Energy Conversion (IPS\u2011EC) Department within the Energy Science and Power Systems (ESPS) Division of the Undersea Systems Office (USO) at the Applied Research Laboratory at Penn State. The Department Head serves as the primary leadership interface between Division strategy and departmental execution. The role integrates people management, technical excellence, and mission execution into a coherent unit aligned to USO and ARL goals. This is a key leadership role in a mission\u2011focused organization that develops next\u2011generation energy conversion technologies for critical national defense applications. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. The IPS\u2011EC Department Head is responsible for the strategic direction, technical excellence, personnel development, and execution performance of multidisciplinary engineering programs. This position requires a leader capable of shaping advanced power and energy technologies while ensuring the highest standards of scientific rigor, safety, and programmatic success. \u00a0 Mission and Department Scope The IPS\u2011EC Department delivers cutting\u2011edge research, design, analysis, and technology transition for energy conversion systems supporting thermal power plants for naval undersea platforms and other defense applications. The department\u2019s core competencies include turbomachinery, heat exchangers, fluid systems, pressure vessels, structural components, heat\u2011engine subsystems, and compact integration of complete thermal engine systems. IPS\u2011EC operates in close collaboration with other ESPS departments and across USO, providing capabilities that enable fully integrated power solutions for current and future mission needs. \u00a0 ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. \u00a0 Responsibilities Include: \u00a0 Department and Division Leadership and Strategy Define and communicate the department\u2019s long\u2011term technical vision, capability roadmap, and strategic priorities Ensure alignment of IPS\u2011EC work with ESPS, USO, and ARL mission needs Shape departmental investments, workforce development priorities, and future capability areas \u00a0 Talent Development and Organizational Management Recruit, develop, and retain exceptional engineering, research faculty, and student talent Build a high\u2011performing, collaborative, and innovative technical culture Establish clear expectations, conduct performance evaluations, and identify professional development pathways Ensure the department maintains the highest standards of technical excellence and safety \u00a0 Program Execution and Technical Leadership Lead and manage large or multi\u2011phase technical projects, including planning, scheduling, coordinating, and overseeing major portions of project execution Evaluate and shape project goals and feasibility; convert technical concepts into actionable programs and identify opportunities for new research directions and applications Advance organizational technical capabilities by developing new methods, extending technologies into new domains, and driving innovation through creative problem\u2011solving and collaboration across a broad peer network \u00a0 Collaboration and External Engagement Work closely with USO leadership, PMs, and PIs across ARL to coordinate resources and leverage capabilities Identify and pursue new research and business opportunities that advance ARL\u2019s mission and sponsor relationships (government and non-government) Nurture and maintain relationships with major customers of external research and develop technical proposals for future work \u00a0 Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/ Experience Areas include: Bachelor\u2019s degree or higher in engineering or a related scientific discipline Management of people, projects, and technical teams with a record of setting and meeting objectives Demonstrated expertise in one or more of the following: Thermodynamics, heat transfer, fluid mechanics; machine design and engineering mechanics; materials and materials selection; system-level test planning and execution; geometric dimensioning and tolerancing; program and project management Demonstrated success in writing white papers and reports \u00a0 Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: Master's Degree or PhD in a relevant field \u00a0 Your working location will be fully on site located in State College, PA. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Spatial-Data-Science_REQ_0000080070-2": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Spatial Data Science", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-21\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Geography at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, invites applications for a new full-time, non-tenure line faculty position focused on spatial data science at the Assistant Teaching Professor rank to teach and advise students for Penn State's online geospatial education programs: https://geospatial.psu.edu . This is a 36-week non-tenure line academic appointment, funded for three years from the date of hire with the strong expectation of continuation for subsequent years, pending satisfactory performance. The University provides a clear pathway for professional advancement for its teaching faculty through its non-tenure line promotion process. We seek candidates with professional and/or academic experience (preferably both) in spatial data science, with an emphasis on one or more key focus areas, including: geospatial intelligence, spatial statistics, geographic visualization, GeoAI, cartography, and web mapping. University teaching experience, in particular with online learning, is strongly preferred. The candidate will contribute to graduate teaching and advising in spatial data science topics. In addition, the candidate may contribute to the administration and leadership of Penn State's online geospatial education programs. Teaching responsibilities will be with Penn State's online geospatial education programs, with opportunities to teach in other Penn State resident education programs and to engage in externally-funded research based on candidate expertise and program needs. A total of six courses will be taught each year, although a combination of course development and preparation, course teaching, and program administration tasks may be assigned depending on program needs and candidate qualifications. This position is located at the University Park campus and the professor will be appointed in the Department of Geography. This position may have the possibility for a hybrid schedule working some days in the office and others remotely. Questions related to flexible work should be directed to the hiring manager during the interview process. To apply, please upload a letter (no longer than 3 pages) describing your teaching philosophy, teaching experience, and explaining how your experience will complement our online geospatial education programs; a curriculum vitae; and the names and contact information of three potential referees. Applicants must have earned a Master\u2019s degree or higher (a PhD is strongly preferred) in Geography, Spatial Data Science, Geoinformatics, or a related discipline by July 1, 2027. This is a non-tenure line position. Appointment could begin as early as January 1, 2027. Application review will begin on September 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Chemistry_REQ_0000079874-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-20\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratory of Professor Yi Liu in the Department of Chemistry at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to work in the areas of biocatalysis and synthetic chemistry. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in chemistry. Candidates with expertise in organic synthesis, enzyme studies, or related areas are especially encouraged to apply. Interested candidates should submit their application electronically, including a CV and research summary. After an initial review, selected candidates will be contacted by email and asked to arrange for letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Embedded-Systems-Department-Head--FACULTY-_REQ_0000080129-2": {"title": "Embedded Systems Department Head (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are searching for a department head for the Embedded Systems Department (ESD) of the Materials, Manufacturing and Sustainment Office (MMSO) at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. The Embedded Systems Department is dedicated to developing embedded hardware and software solutions in addition to driving integration of complex systems. The department focuses on real-time control and data acquisition, edge computing architectures, modular system architecture definition, integration methodologies, and test set development to include hardware in the loop and software in the loop. In this role, you will lead and manage all aspects of the Embedded Systems Department, providing strategic direction, technical leadership, and operational oversight. You will also establish partnerships with customer program offices, defense contractors, systems integrators, and other government laboratories to transition cutting-edge embedded capabilities to operational platforms for the warfighter. This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Lead and manage all aspects of the Embedded Systems Department, providing strategic direction, technical leadership, and operational oversight Support division leadership in developing and maintaining relationships with sponsors in support of meeting funding objectives Build and direct a multidisciplinary team focused on embedded systems architectures, complex systems integration, hardware-software integration, edge analytics, and mission-critical control systems Lead individual research projects and portfolios including developing technical concepts, writing winning proposals, staffing projects, conducting research, managing budgets, and delivering high-quality results Provide technical oversight of embedded hardware and software development, ensuring quality and rigor of technical deliverables and research outputs Transition cutting-edge embedded systems capabilities to operational platforms for the warfighter Recruit, mentor, and develop staff with expertise in embedded systems, edge computing, and real-time control Foster a culture of innovation, technical excellence, and mission focus Lead individual research projects and portfolios including developing technical concepts, writing winning proposals, staffing the project, conducting the research, managing budgets, and delivering high-quality results Additional responsibilities for the higher-level position includes: Support development of a comprehensive roadmap for embedded systems and integration methodologies pertinent to systems of interest to the division including but not limited to missiles, hypersonics, and uncrewed aerial systems Establish and maintain partnerships with customer program offices, defense contractors, systems integrators, and other government laboratories Build strategic relationships with Defense Industrial Base stakeholders Collaborate across ARL departments and with external stakeholders to integrate embedded solutions into larger system architectures Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required skills/experience areas include: Embedded hardware architectures (microcontrollers, SoCs, FPGAs) Real-time operating systems (RTOS) and bare-metal programming Hardware-software co-design and integration Edge computing and edge analytics frameworks Data acquisition systems and sensor integration Automated control systems and algorithms Cyber-resilient embedded system design Testing methodologies (Hardware in the loop, software in the loop, etc.) System integration methodologies Embedded systems challenges in complex DoD systems (e.g., maritime, aerospace, ground vehicles, unmanned systems) Past success using edge device deployment for operational environments including size, weight, and power (SWaP) constrained designs, environmental hardening and ruggedization, real-time performance optimization, and system security and anti-tamper techniques Past success in writing white papers or reports Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Secret level or higher and may be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility, if required Your working location will be fully on-site located in State College, PA. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000079870-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Penn State School of Labor and Employment Relations invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar to join a dynamic, interdisciplinary team working at the frontier of artificial intelligence and human-based leadership. As organizations increasingly blend algorithmic and human decision-making, fundamental questions arise about how leadership operates, adapts, and creates value in this new landscape. Our team is dedicated to answering them\u2014and to translating that research into insights that shape the future of work. This is a unique opportunity for an early-career scholar to contribute to high-impact, publishable research while developing the research skills, collaborations, and visibility to launch a thriving academic or research career. As a Postdoctoral Scholar, you will design and conduct original research at the intersection of AI and organizational leadership, collaborate closely with faculty and fellow researchers across disciplines, and contribute to manuscripts for leading peer-reviewed journals. You'll have the freedom to help shape the direction of emerging projects and the support to grow as an independent scholar. We are looking for someone who brings a strong technical foundation, genuine curiosity about leadership and organizations, and a collaborative spirit. Specifically, the ideal candidate has: A strong background in artificial intelligence, machine learning, computational science, data science, computer science, robotics, natural language processing, computer vision, optimization, or a related field A keen interest in, or background studying, the role of leadership in organizations, which could be rooted in human\u2013AI collaboration, agent-driven interaction, human-robot interaction, intelligent interfaces, autonomous systems, and the design and evaluation of AI systems that augment human capabilities and leadership A desire to collaborate with an interdisciplinary team of scholars Ambition to engage in cutting-edge research with the potential to transform organizations and society Requirements: A Ph.D. in a relevant field is required by the date of appointment. Why Penn State: You'll join one of the nation's premier institutions for the study of work, employment, and organizations, with access to world-class resources, a vibrant intellectual community, and an opportunity to work with leading scholars in organizational leadership. How to Apply\u2026 Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Visit our website at https://ler.la.psu.edu/ for more information on our School of labor and Employment Relations \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Researcher-Positions-in-Physicochemical-Water-Treatment-and-Environmental-Chemistry_REQ_0000080130-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Researcher Positions in Physicochemical Water Treatment and Environmental Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The research group of Dr. Onur Apul in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for two (2) Postdoctoral Scholar positions in the areas of physicochemical water treatment, environmental chemistry, and emerging contaminants. Dr. Apul leads the Drinking Water Treatment Innovations Laboratory, which develops fundamental and applied solutions for emerging water quality challenges through advanced treatment technologies, environmental nanotechnology, and adsorption science. \u00a0 The successful candidates will contribute to externally funded research projects focused on one or more of the following areas: PFAS fate, transport, treatment, and destruction Activated carbon adsorption and regeneration Thermal treatment of PFAS-laden treatment residuals Nanobubble-based water treatment technologies Microplastics and nanoplastics in environmental systems Environmental surface chemistry and interfacial phenomena Current projects include NSF-supported research on PFAS-contaminated treatment systems, environmental impacts of PFAS releases, nanobubble technologies, and emerging contaminants in water systems. \u00a0 Responsibilities The postdoctoral scholar will: Lead independent and collaborative research projects, and assist with proposal development and research management Design and conduct laboratory experiments, and mentor graduate and undergraduate students Publish research findings in high-impact peer-reviewed journals, and present research at national and international conferences Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams across Penn State and partner institutions Maintain instruments, and laboratory\u2019s environmental health and safety procedures Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Environmental Engineering, Civil Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Environmental Chemistry, Materials Science, or a closely related field Strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals Demonstrated expertise in experimental research Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively Preferred Qualifications Experience in one or more of the following: PFAS analysis, treatment, or destruction Adsorption and activated carbon systems GC-MS, ICP-MS, TOC, or related analytical techniques Environmental nanotechnology Water and wastewater treatment processes Colloid and interface science Environmental fate and transport modeling Data analysis using AI tools, Python, MATLAB, R, or similar tools Position Details Expected start date: Summer/Fall 2026 (flexible) Competitive salary and benefits Location: University Park, Pennsylvania Penn State offers a highly collaborative research environment with access to world-class facilities, including advanced analytical instrumentation, materials characterization facilities, and interdisciplinary research centers. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop an independent research portfolio while contributing to cutting-edge solutions for critical environmental challenges. \u00a0 Application Instructions Interested applicants should submit the following: 1. Cover letter describing research interests and qualifications 2. Curriculum vitae 3. One-page statement of research interests and future goals 4. Contact information for three professional references Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. For questions regarding the position, please contact: Dr. Onur G. Apul Associate Professor Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering The Pennsylvania State University Email: onur@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Professor_REQ_0000080159-1": {"title": "Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Smeal Chaired Professor (Tenure-Track Position) in Organizational Behavior, Organizational Theory, or Strategy Management & Organization Department Smeal College of Business The Pennsylvania State University The Management and Organization (M&O) Department in the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) has a full-time tenure-track position in the areas of Organizational Behavior (OB), Organizational Theory (OT), or Strategy. We seek to fill this position at the rank of Full Professor . The position is to fill the Smeal Chaired Professor of Management. The desired start date for the position is Fall 2027. Candidates must have a PhD, a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research with sufficient impact of that work on the field, and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. Job Requirement : The preferred candidate will have publications in premier journals, a research program with high-impact, and is able to connect with a wide array of doctoral students and faculty in our department. Faculty members in the M&O department are expected to pursue an active research program, perform undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in professional service. O nsite teaching is an essential function of the job For the Smeal Chaired Professor specifically, there is an expectation of sustained research excellence and thought leadership, an established history of mentorship, high ethical standards for their own professional work, and a strategic vision for growing and sustaining the research culture within the M&O department. Candidates for the position can apply by uploading a letter of interest and CV. Any questions about the position can be sent to Amanda Brown, M&O Support Coordinator, at mandosmeal@psu.edu. Review of applications for the position will begin on October 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The Department of Management and Organization is consistently ranked in the top-20 management departments for its research productivity and values high-level theoretical and empirical ability, collegiality and collaboration among its members, and the ability to teach management and organizational concepts effectively to multiple audiences. Our department offers two undergraduate majors (Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship; Management), two online masters programs (Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship; Strategic Management and Executive Leadership), a PhD program, courses in Smeal\u2019s full-time rMBA and DBA programs, courses in Smeal\u2019s part-time hMBA and OMBA, and operates the Farrell Center for Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship (which includes the Garber Venture Capital Fund). Our tenure-line faculty are Heejung Byun, Carolyn Dang, Raghu Garud, Don Hambrick, Stephen Humphrey, Trevor Israelsen, Jon Jachimowicz, Margaret Luciano, Vilmos Misangyi, Semin Park, Tessa Recendes, Kira Schabram, Paul Shrivastava, Linda Trevi\u00f1o, Wenpin Tsai, Dani Yin, and Rui Zhong. Our nontenure-line clinical faculty are Shawn Clark, Sean Doherty, Jeanette Miller, Lisa O\u2019Hara, \u00d6zge Pala, Federica Pinelli, and Angela Schwartz. Our nontenure-line full-time teaching faculty are Cameron Conaway, Neil Fogarty, Ron Johnson, James Jones, Dave Lenze, Travis Lesser, and Brad Leve. For more information on our department please visit https://www.smeal.psu.edu/management . The M&O Department is part of the Smeal College of Business, which depends on more than 360 faculty and staff to enact and support its strategic priorities of integrity, inclusivity, and sustainability and to serve the needs of more than 9,000 students. Media outlets and independent observers regularly rank Smeal among the best business schools in the world. Please visit http://www.smeal.psu.edu/ for additional information. The Smeal College of Business is located at the Pennsylvania State University\u2019s main campus (University Park) in the heart of State College, Pennsylvania. Our community features the charms of a small town with the opportunities typically only found in larger cities, with State College routinely ranked among the top 10 best college towns in the United States ( https://www.collegetransitions.com/blog/best-college-towns-in-america/ ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Division-Head---Computational-Fluid-Dynamics--FACULTY-_REQ_0000079714-2": {"title": "Division Head - Computational Fluid Dynamics (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are searching for a\u00a0Division Head for the Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) Division in the Fluid Dynamics and Acoustics Office (FDAO) at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. The CFD Division Head will lead a premier group of approximately fifteen of engineers and research faculty in meeting the mission of bringing state-of-the-technology tools, talent and leading-edge computational fluid dynamics to our DoD and industrial sponsors. The Division Head, along with immediate reports, will develop and mature business relationships and programs with other ARL offices, industry, and government sponsors. This critical role requires a blend of technical mastery in fluid dynamics, technical management, and personnel management in a mission-focused environment.\u00a0This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Lead and perform design and performance support analyses, using in-house and commercial CFD tools, for a broad range of applications, including undersea vehicles and propulsion, coupled hydrodynamics/hydroacoustics, low-speed and high-speed aerodynamics, and complex multi-physics systems Lead technical developments and improvements in field of Computational Fluid Dynamics including but limited to code development, V&V, and applications in new and evolving tools and methodologies to solve complex flows. Projects may include but not limited to cavitation and multiphase flows, vehicle maneuvering, turbomachinery, fluid-structure/fluid-acoustic interactions, drag reduction, signatures, and code optimization for modern HPC systems Provide technical oversight of complex simulations and interface across the organization to ensure high quality research output Perform organizational leadership to the CFD Division, to include personnel management, recruitment, development, and retention of employees Additional responsibilities for higher-level position includes: Work with FDAO management team and other ARL offices to build the research portfolio, improve technical capabilities, and enhance cross discipline cooperation and collaboration Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/Experience areas include: Master's degree or higher in an Engineering or Science discipline or higher plus ten years of related experience Past success as a Principal Investigator in this field Strong research track record of computational fluid dynamics with a focus in hydromechanics, hydroacoustics, maneuvering and controls, propulsion systems or related discipline Previous success managing people with supervisory experience Excellent verbal and written communication skills with past success in writing white papers or reports \u00a0 Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Top Secret level or higher and may be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility Preferred Skills/Experience areas include: Successful history of proposed and awarded research projects evidenced through securing external research funding Demonstrated leadership of multi-discipline research projects Expert-level knowledge of high-performance computing architectures and information systems Experience with STAR-CCM+ Fully on-site located in State College, PA but, options exist for hybrid of on-site/work from home based on project-dependent ability. Questions related to flexible work should be directed to the hiring manager during the interview process. This role requires periodic travel to remote locations. ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Department of Defense (DoD), and the Intel Community (IC).\u00a0 FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our website at\u00a0 www.arl.psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 Notice regarding employment at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL):&#xa;Employees must be eligible to obtain a government security clearance, participate in the ARL drug testing program, and comply with electronic and physical monitoring requirements applicable to federal contractors. ARL operates in a secure information environment involving Unclassified, Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), and Classified information. Personal electronic devices brought onsite must be registered and may be restricted from certain areas. You must be a U.S. citizen to apply. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Research-Professor-in-Astronomy-and-Astrophysics_REQ_0000079758-2": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Research Professor in Astronomy and Astrophysics", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Astronomy and Astrophysics at Penn State invites applications for a full-time Assistant or Associate Research Professor position (non-tenure track) to begin immediately. Salary and benefits will be competitive and commensurate with the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will be responsible for undertaking research involving nanofabrication of diffraction gratings and application to future missions. The research involves creating reflection gratings for UV and X-ray applications on a variety of substrates with a variety of groove directions and shapes. The successful candidate will be responsible for performing the various nanofabrication techniques required to fabricate such gratings including, but not limited to, electron-beam lithography, grayscale lithography, ion etching, wet chemistry, deposition, and surface metrology such as ellipsometry, electron microscopy, and atomic force microscopy. It is expected that the candidate will disseminate their research through refereed publications and conference talks. It is also expected that the candidate will contribute to studies specific to future missions such as the Habitable Worlds Observatory and help write proposals for related funding support. Education and Experience A Ph.D. in Astronomy or Physics is preferred, a Ph.D. in a related field with strong research experience in astronomical instrumentation or nanofabrication will be considered. Experience with nanofabrication is desired. Applicants must have demonstrated ability as a researcher and should have a record of successful grant funding. Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV, statement of research interests, and a list of publications. In addition, please arrange for three professional reference letters to be sent to dps7@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000079924-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Artificial Heart and Cardiovascular Fluid Dynamics Lab at The Pennsylvania State University has a Postdoctoral Scholar position open in the field of cardiovascular mechanics. Candidates who have a strong background in Biochemistry, Mathematics, and/or Mechanics (experimental and computational methods (use of OpenFOAM and/or COMSOL)) are welcome to apply. Experience in blood and animal experimentation is a plus. The individual will be expected to help guide graduate and undergraduate students in their research, participate in the preparation and submission of manuscripts and proposals, present results at scientific conferences, and prepare reports for funded projects. The position is focused mostly on experimental studies including animal studies. The research activities will include experiments related to stroke, thrombosis, adhesion, and cardiovascular fluid dynamics with some computational modeling. The position requires a doctoral (Ph.D.) degree in a scientific discipline by time of appointment. Interested applicants should apply online with a resume that includes a list of education, publications, work experience, and a list of references. For more information, please contact Dr. Keefe Manning ( kbm10@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Position_REQ_0000079720-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Position", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Armache laboratory at the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology within The Pennsylvania State University is a member of the Huck Center for Structural Biology and the Center for Eukaryotic Gene Regulation.\u00a0 The laboratory is seeking a driven and enthusiastic postdoctoral scholar to study the structure and function of dynamic multi-subunit ATP-dependent chromatin remodeling complexes using cryo-Electron Microscopy, and biophysical and biochemical methods. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. and have expertise in molecular biology, biochemical or biophysical characterization of macromolecular complexes. Experience in the following is preferred: human cell culture, insect cell expression system and/or cryo-EM structural analysis. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a curriculum vitae, a brief statement of interest and the names and contact information of two-three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---BBH-Social-Determinants-of-Health-Lab_REQ_0000079610-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - BBH Social Determinants of Health Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-30\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Dr. Xue Zhang is recruiting a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar to use an intersectional and interdisciplinary approach to study the individual, interpersonal, community, and structural factors that shape health disparities, with a particular focus on rural communities. The Postdoctoral Scholar should have expertise in and conduct research on health disparities in at least one of the following areas: substance use and mental health, healthcare access and utilization, aging, or mortality. The ideal candidate will be highly motivated, able to work independently and collaboratively, and have strong quantitative and analytical skills. Experience working with large publicly available datasets\u2014such as, but not limited to, the Health and Retirement Study (HRS), All of Us Research Program, Adolescent Brain Cognitive Development Study (ABCD), Youth Risk Behavior Survey (YRBS), and Behavioral Risk Factor Surve \u2014is strongly preferred. The candidate should also have experience conducting sophisticated quantitative analyses, including, but not limited to, structural equation modeling, multilevel modeling, longitudinal analysis, and other advanced statistical approaches relevant to population health and health disparities research. Responsibilities: Work collaboratively with Dr. Zhang to conduct research on multilevel social and structural determinants of health disparities. Conduct independent data management, statistical analyses, and interpretation of findings using large-scale secondary datasets. Develop research manuscripts for publication in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals. Assist in the preparation of research proposals to generate extramural funding support (e.g., R21, R01, foundation grants). Contribute to the development of interdisciplinary research projects related to rural health disparities, healthy aging, substance use, and community health. Required Job Qualifications: Ph.D. required, preferably in public health, biostatistics, social science or a related field. Evidence of strong writing skills required. A strong quantitative background in statistics and/or spatial analysis. Experience with large publicly available datasets To apply, please submit the following materials: CV Cover letter (1 page max). Please emphasize your experience with secondary data analysis, advanced statistical and quantitative modeling skills, and research related to health disparities. Research statement (1 page max). Please describe your research interests and how they align with research on social and structural determinants of health, health disparities, and population health. And a brief research plan during postdoc period. Contact info for three references. 2-3 writing samples. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Please email Xue Zhang ( xuezhang@psu.edu ) with informal inquiries. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Food-Gut-Brain-Lab-_REQ_0000079661-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (Food-Gut-Brain Lab)", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-30\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Food-Gut-Brain lab, headed by Dr. Anna Hayes, seeks a Postdoctoral Scholar to join our research team in the Department of Food Science at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park). The successful candidate will lead and assist with projects tied to the lab\u2019s focus on 1) elucidating how the chemical structures of carbohydrate-containing foods and climate-smart crops influence eating behavior, metabolism, and cognition; 2) valorizing dietary fibers and bioactive compounds such as polyphenols from food byproduct streams and underutilized food components by examining their influences on gut-brain interactions; and 3) exploring the health impacts of process-induced compounds and food-based strategies to alter their consequences. Building on a strong foundation in food chemistry and food science, this work aims to advance understanding of how food physicochemical properties extend beyond their roles within foods to influence human health. Interested applicants must have a Ph.D. in food science, nutrition science, or a related field by the appointment date. Desired qualifications include previous experience conducting research with animal models as well as investigating the chemistry of dietary carbohydrates (e.g., starch, fiber), polyphenols, and/or Maillard reaction products. Experience with LC\u2011MS and/or gut microbiome characterization is preferred. Applicants should have a strong publication record, demonstrate creativity in research and scholarly communication, and work effectively in collaborative environments. The Postdoctoral Scholar will have opportunities to develop independent research directions and contribute to grant writing and mentoring students. The position should be filled by December 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants must upload a CV, names of three professional references, and cover letter describing research interests and career goals to the Penn State Job Posting Board . Application materials should be addressed to Dr. Anna Hayes (amh9504@psu.edu). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000077936-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-29\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Dr. Mathias Martins is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar to join his research program in the Department of Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences at Penn State. The laboratory focuses on poultry viruses, with an emphasis on viral pathogenesis, diagnostic assay development, and vaccine development. Responsibilities for this position include developing and implementing assays for viral detection, vaccine safety and immunogenicity, and the characterization of immune responses in chickens. The postdoctoral scholar will lead and support studies in poultry, including experimental infections and vaccine trials. Additional responsibilities include maintaining laboratory equipment, managing supplies, ensuring accurate recordkeeping, preparing scientific manuscripts, and mentoring students and junior laboratory personnel. The postdoctoral scholar is expected to adhere to all biosafety, laboratory safety, and animal care protocols required by Penn State and relevant regulatory agencies. Required Qualifications: Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree, and/or PhD in a related field, completed by the start date. Preferred Experience and Skills: Strong organizational and time-management skills Ability to maintain detailed and accurate records Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously Strong problem-solving skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment Experience in virology, including molecular and serological assays Experience conducting animal experiments Experience working in BSL-2/ABSL-2 and BSL-3/ABSL-3 facilities Candidates should submit the following materials: 1. A cover letter outlining their background and research interests 2. Curriculum vitae (CV) 3. Names and contact information for 2-3 references \u00a0 Applications are accepted online at https://hr.psu.edu/careers -\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0This appointment is initially for one year, with good opportunities for renewal depending on performance and funding availability. -\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review of applications will begin as they are received and will continue until the position is filled. -\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0For more information or questions, please contact Dr. Mathias Martins at m.martins@psu.edu \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Quantum-Frontiers-Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000079628-1": {"title": "Quantum Frontiers Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST), https://ist.psu.edu/ , at Penn State invites applications for the position of its inaugural Quantum Frontiers Postdoctoral Scholar . This year, two such positions are available, one in Quantum + security and the other in Quantum + AI. There are two separate job postings. This ad is for the Quantum + security position and\u00a0is intended to advance high-impact research at the intersection of quantum computing, cybersecurity, secure systems, and trustworthy AI. Quantum computing is poised to transform computation, communication, cryptography, and national security. At the same time, the emerging quantum era introduces urgent cybersecurity challenges, including the need for post-quantum cryptographic systems, secure quantum protocols, resilient cyber infrastructure, and new methods for protecting quantum-enabled technologies. This position will help IST build research capacity and national leadership in secure and trustworthy systems for the quantum era. The successful candidate will conduct interdisciplinary research on topics including: Security of quantum algorithms, quantum software, and quantum networks Quantum-safe cybersecurity for critical infrastructure AI-enabled cyber defense in quantum and post-quantum contexts Trustworthy, resilient, and policy-aware security systems for emerging quantum technologies The postdoctoral scholar will be based in the IST and will have opportunities to collaborate across Penn State, including with the Penn State Quantum Hub ( https://quantum.psu.edu/ ), Institute for Computational and Data Sciences ( https://icds.psu.edu/ ), and National Security Institute ( https://nsi.psu.edu/ ). The position is designed to catalyze interdisciplinary research, support proposal development, mentor students, and contribute to Penn State\u2019s growing leadership at the quantum\u2013security nexus. Responsibilities The postdoctoral scholar will be expected to: Conduct original research in quantum security, post-quantum cybersecurity, or closely related areas Collaborate with faculty across cybersecurity, quantum computing, AI, systems, and policy Contribute to external funding proposals to agencies such as NSF, DOE, DARPA, and other sponsors Develop a quantum + security course Help develop IST\u2019s visibility and research portfolio in quantum-era cybersecurity Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in computer science, cybersecurity, electrical and computer engineering, mathematics, physics, or a closely related field by the start date. Because this position is centered on quantum-era cybersecurity, we are particularly interested in candidates with a strong Computing-oriented research profile , including expertise in cybersecurity, cryptography, secure systems, quantum software, quantum networking security, or post-quantum security. Candidates from physics or quantum science backgrounds are encouraged to apply when their work has clear security relevance. Strong candidates will have expertise in one or more of the following areas: Cybersecurity Cryptography or post-quantum cryptography Quantum computing, quantum information, or quantum networking Secure systems and software AI for cybersecurity Critical infrastructure security Security policy, risk, and governance related to emerging technologies Candidates with interdisciplinary experience and an interest in building collaborative research programs are encouraged to apply. Appointment Details The position is a full-time postdoctoral appointment, with an anticipated start date in early Fall 2026, though an earlier start date may be possible. Medical insurance and other standard university benefits are also provided. The scholar will be initially supervised by the Head of Department of Privacy and Cybersecurity Informatics (PCI) in the IST to support their integration into the department and the broader Penn State research community. Based on research alignment, the scholar will further have opportunities to collaborate with and be co-mentored by faculty across Penn State. Application Materials Applicants should submit: Cover letter describing research interests and fit for the \u201cQuantum + Security\u201d position Curriculum vitae Research statement (up to two pages) Up to three representative publications Names and contact information for three professional references System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. About Penn State Penn State is a leading public research university with significant strengths in cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, quantum science, computational and data sciences, national security, and interdisciplinary research. This position will contribute to Penn State\u2019s strategic efforts to build research leadership in secure, trustworthy, and intelligent systems for the quantum era. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Quantum-Frontiers-Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-Quantum---AI_REQ_0000079630-1": {"title": "Quantum Frontiers Postdoctoral Scholar in Quantum + AI", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at Penn State invites applications for the position of inaugural Quantum Frontiers Postdoctoral Scholar. Two positions are available this year: one focused on Quantum + Security and the other on Quantum + AI. These are separate searches. This advertisement is for the Quantum + AI position and is intended for applicants whose research advances the development and application of AI methods for quantum computing, as well as the use of quantum-inspired approaches to enhance AI systems. Artificial intelligence and quantum computing are converging to define the next frontier of scientific discovery, national competitiveness, and economic transformation. Penn State is uniquely positioned\u2014through its breadth of expertise, interdisciplinary institutes, and land-grant mission\u2014to lead at this intersection. To accelerate progress in this emerging area, the Quantum Frontiers Postdoctoral Scholar will serve as a catalyst for high-impact research, cross-disciplinary collaboration, and growth in external funding at the intersection of quantum computing and AI. We seek candidates who will conduct innovative research at the intersection of quantum computing and artificial intelligence. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, the following: Quantum Machine Learning and AI: Develop novel quantum algorithms and computational frameworks for machine learning, generative AI, data analytics, and intelligent decision-making, while advancing the theoretical foundations of quantum-enhanced learning systems. Quantum Algorithms for Optimization and Scientific Computing: Design and analyze quantum algorithms for optimization, combinatorial search, differential equations, scientific simulation, and other computational challenges arising in engineering, mathematics, and the physical sciences. AI for Quantum Systems: Apply machine learning and artificial intelligence techniques to improve the characterization, control, calibration, error mitigation, and overall performance of quantum computing systems and quantum devices. AI-Driven Quantum Algorithm and Circuit Design: Develop AI-powered methods for the automated discovery, design, compilation, verification, and optimization of quantum algorithms and quantum circuits, enabling more efficient and scalable quantum software development. Hybrid Quantum-Classical Computing for Scientific Discovery: Create hybrid quantum-classical approaches that combine advances in quantum computing and AI to accelerate scientific discovery and address complex challenges in areas such as materials science, chemistry, biology, healthcare, and other data-intensive scientific domains. This position aligns strongly with Penn State\u2019s growing strengths in AI foundations, AI-enabled scientific discovery, and emerging initiatives in quantum computing. The successful candidate will contribute to the university\u2019s efforts to advance AI-powered science and quantum innovation while helping to build new interdisciplinary research collaborations. The scholar will be based in the College of IST and will have opportunities to collaborate broadly across Penn State, including with the Penn State Quantum Hub ( https://quantum.psu.edu/ ), Penn State AI Hub( https://ai.psu.edu/ ), Institute for Computational and Data Sciences ( https://icds.psu.edu/ ), and other Penn State interdisciplinary research institutes ( https://www.psu.edu/research/interdisciplinary-institutes ).These affiliations will provide access to advanced computational infrastructure, world-class interdisciplinary collaborators, and pathways to large-scale external funding opportunities. Responsibilities The postdoctoral scholar will be expected to: Conduct original research in quantum machine learning and AI, quantum algorithms for optimization and scientific computing, hybrid quantum-classical computing for scientific discovery, AI for quantum systems, or closely related areas. Collaborate with faculty and researchers across AI, quantum computing, cybersecurity, computer systems, mathematics, engineering, and policy to advance interdisciplinary research initiatives. Contribute to the development of externally funded research programs by participating in proposal preparation and collaborative research efforts for agencies such as the NSF, DOE, DARPA, and other federal and industry sponsors. Develop and help deliver a Quantum + AI course that introduces students to the foundations, methods, applications, and emerging opportunities at the intersection of quantum computing and artificial intelligence. Help enhance the College of IST\u2019s visibility, reputation, and research portfolio in Quantum + AI, and engage with Penn State's interdisciplinary research ecosystem , including the Quantum Hub, AI Hub, Institute for Computational and Data Sciences, and other university-wide initiatives focused on AI-powered science and emerging technologies. Disseminate research results through publications in leading conferences and journals, open-source software and tools when appropriate, and presentations to academic, government, and industry audiences. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students and contribute to the development of a vibrant and collaborative research community in quantum computing and AI. Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in computer science, information science, artificial intelligence, electrical and computer engineering, mathematics, physics, or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. Candidates should have demonstrated research experience in one or more of the research areas described above. Experience with quantum computing software frameworks, programming environments, and quantum hardware platforms is desirable. Applicants should have a strong publication record and demonstrated potential to conduct independent, high-impact research in interdisciplinary and collaborative environments. Appointment Details The position is a full-time postdoctoral appointment with an anticipated start date in Fall 2026, although an earlier start date may be possible. Medical insurance and other standard university benefits are provided. The scholar will initially be supervised by the Head of the Department of Informatics and Intelligent Systems (IIS) in the College of IST to support their integration into the department and the broader Penn State research community. Based on research interests and alignment, the scholar will have opportunities to collaborate with and be co-mentored by faculty across Penn State. Application Materials Applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter describing their research interests, qualifications, and fit for the Quantum + AI position. A current curriculum vitae. A research statement (up to two pages) outlining past research accomplishments, current research interests, and future research directions. Up to three representative publications or preprints. Names and contact information for three professional references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. About Penn State Penn State is a leading public research university with internationally recognized strengths in information sciences and technology, computer science, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, human-centered computing, and interdisciplinary research. This position will play a key role in advancing Penn State\u2019s strategic investment in quantum computing and artificial intelligence, contributing to the University's efforts to establish national leadership in Quantum and AI research, education, and innovation. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Instructor-or-Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Learning--Design--and-Technology-UP-36-weeks-_REQ_0000079396-2": {"title": "Instructor or Assistant Teaching Professor (Learning, Design, and Technology UP 36 weeks)", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Learning and Performance Systems (LPS invites applications for an Instructor or Assistant Teaching Professor position to support its undergraduate programming in Learning, Design, and Technology ( LDT ) at the University Park campus, and other LPS programs, as needed. Join a collaborative program focused on undergraduate learning design, where you will guide students in connecting learning theory to the creation of effective, technology-enhanced learning environments. Faculty in this role play a central part in mentoring students through applied coursework, as well as support a culminating design capstone that emphasizes the development of job-ready learning design skills. This non-tenure-line position is a 36-week faculty appointment, with the possibility of renewal. It has primary responsibilities in undergraduate teaching. Faculty in LPS are part of a collegial, student-centered department that prioritizes strong teaching, thoughtful collaboration, and a positive, supportive work environment. Key Responsibilities Teach face-to-face and hybrid undergraduate courses in the fall and spring Coordinate with LDT faculty, instructional designers, and media specialists to ensure high-quality course development and delivery, accessibility/UDL, media integration, and continuous improvement; Led LDT undergraduate minor efforts including supervising undergraduate students; Collaborate and communicate effectively with the LPS department head, professor\u2011in\u2011charge of the LDT program, faculty colleagues, and department staff to support cohesive and responsive program operations; Participate in department and program meetings and events; At Assistant Teaching Professor level only: teach online master\u2019s classes and advise master\u2019s or DEd students throughout the program, including capstone completion. Minimum Qualifications (Required) At Instructor level: Earned master\u2019s degree in education; learning sciences; educational technologies; learning, design, and technology; or a closely related field At Assistant Teaching Professor level: Earned doctorate (PhD or DEd) in education; learning sciences; educational technologies; learning, design, and technology; or a closely related field Evidence of excellence, or potential excellence, in undergraduate teaching and inclusive pedagogy Strong communication and collaboration skills Demonstrated strengths in time management, ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities, and organization Desired Qualifications Experience with and expertise in learning technologies and / or education design work Familiarity with Canvas, teaching quality standards, and program assessment Experience designing or revising courses in collaboration with instructional designers and other faculty members Understanding of the ethics surrounding the uses and integration of AI in higher education courses Evidence of student-centered responsiveness including the ability to provide timely feedback and grading, respond promptly to students, and manage multiple course deadlines in fast paced environments At Assistant Teaching Professor level: Supporting teaching assistants and graduate students as instructors Representative Teaching Portfolio LDT (examples): Primary: World Technologies and Learning and Making with Art and Learning Technologies. Secondary: Effective Communication and Teaching Strategies for Corporate and Community Educators; Creating Designs for Learning; Advanced Learning Experience Design Lab (minor capstone); Systematic Instructional Development; Gaming to Learn; Educational Technology Integration; Emerging Web Technologies and Learning Application Instructions Apply online at hr.psu.edu/careers and upload one PDF containing: a) Cover letter that clearly identifies the candidate\u2019s qualifications related to the position; b) Curriculum vitae; c) Names and contact information for three professional references ; d) Teaching philosophy statement ( maximum two single-spaced pages ) describing prior teaching and course design experience, LDT program alignment, relevant course expertise, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Campus/Unit: College of Education \u2014 Department of Learning & Performance Systems (LPS), University Park, PA Appointment: Instructor or Assistant Teaching Professor (non\u2011tenure-line), 36\u2011week; one\u2011year term with the possibility of renewal based on need, performance, and/or availability of funding. Full University benefits apply. Work Arrangement: In person. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Instructor-of-Integrative-Arts---Game-Design_REQ_0000079596-1": {"title": "Part Time Instructor of Integrative Arts - Game Design", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-22\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The College of Arts & Architecture's Integrative Arts program seeks to fill part-time instructional positions responsible for teaching web-based courses in Video Game Design. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as needed. The College of Arts and Architecture's Integrative Arts program is seeking part-time instructors to teach online courses in video game design. This role is ideal for an educator with a passion for game design who is eager to help guide students on their journey to become game creators and excited to help students think critically about foundational elements of design. The successful candidate will be capable of creating an engaging online learning environment that encourages curiosity, creativity, collaboration, critique and critical inquiry. Successful candidates will help students build strong design foundations through hands-on creation, play analysis, discussion, iteration, and reflection. They should be excited to teach students how games function as systems, stories, cultural artifacts, and forms of creative expression. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as needed. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Researcher_REQ_0000079236-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Researcher", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Rasgon lab at The Pennsylvania State University is hiring multiple Postdoctoral Scholars to join our lab to work on a variety of projects related to the molecular biology of arthropods. Successful candidates will contribute to projects developing novel methods for transgenic manipulation of arthropods, developing novel gene transduction technologies for basic and applied goals, and developing model systems to study the evolutions and mechanisms of arthropod symbiosis. Candidates must have experience in one or more of the following areas, including but not limited to cloning, construct design, CRISPR/Cas9 gene editing, PCR/qPCR, protein expression and purification using bacterial or yeast systems, protein techniques, receptor-ligand interactions, bioinformatics, virology, work with BSL2 and BSL3-level pathogens, and artificial vector infections with pathogens. Experience working with mosquitoes is preferred but not required. Candidates will also be responsible for designing experiments, laboratory research, writing proposals and publications, training graduate students, undergraduate students, and technical staff. Candidates must be able to work independently and in a collaborative team environment. Applicants are required to have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in an appropriate field and be able to provide evidence that all requirements have been met for completion of the Ph.D. prior to the effective date of hire. Interested candidates must\u00a0submit\u00a0an online application at\u00a0 Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board ,\u00a0and should upload the following application materials electronically: CV and a list of three references with contact information. This position will be located at Penn State in University Park, Pennsylvania. It is full-time in person (no remote work). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Huck-Institutes-of-the-Life-Sciences-NSF-NCEMS-Postdoctoral-Scholar---Biophysics_REQ_0000079407-1": {"title": "Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences NSF NCEMS Postdoctoral Scholar - Biophysics", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar (Biophysics) The National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences (NCEMS) at The Pennsylvania State University ( ncems.psu.edu ) seeks an outstanding scientist to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in Biophysics housed within the Huck Institutes of Life Sciences at Penn State. NCEMS is an NSF-funded interdisciplinary research center positioned at the interface of data science, molecular and cellular biology, and quantitative physical sciences. The Center provides leadership in the integration of diverse, publicly available datasets to gain insights into emergent phenomena in molecular and cellular biology. About the Position The successful candidate, in collaboration with faculty and research staff at NCEMS, will conduct original biophysics research involving quantitative, computational, theoretical, or data-driven approaches in molecular and cellular biology. Research may involve protein structure and function, molecular interactions, molecular assemblies, intrinsically disordered proteins, biomolecular condensates, cellular organization, biological networks, molecular evolution, or systems-level biophysical phenomena. The scholar\u2019s independent work may use, extend, or contribute to NCEMS Working Group data products, analytical tools, computational models, and methodological innovations. The scholar will also collaborate with NCEMS Working Groups where their expertise can help advance shared research goals and produce high-impact scientific outputs. This position is full time, on-site at the Penn State University Park campus. This position does not permit remote work. This is a term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with an excellent chance for multiple years of renewal based upon mutual agreement. Requirements A PhD in Biophysics, Physics, Biological Physics, or Quantitative Biology or a closely related field is required. The successful candidate will have a strong foundation in biophysics, statistical mechanics, molecular modeling, computational modeling, quantitative biology, dynamical systems, stochastic processes, complex systems, or related quantitative approaches. Candidates should have experience developing, implementing, or applying analytical or computational models to molecular and cellular systems. Expertise in Python, R, MATLAB, or related scientific computing tools is desirable. The successful candidate should have a demonstrated ability to conduct research and produce scholarly outputs, as evidenced by publications in peer-reviewed journals. Experience working with biological datasets or biophysical systems is desirable, including protein interaction data, structural data, imaging data, molecular dynamics outputs, omics data, cellular organization data, or biological network data. Candidates must be independent self-starters, have a strong work ethic, strong interpersonal and written communication skills, and the ability to work well in a collaborative team environment. Application Process Applications must be submitted electronically in a single PDF and should include: A cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Huck-Institutes-of-the-Life-Sciences-NSF-NCEMS-Postdoctoral-Scholar-Computational-Proteomics-Mass-Spectrometry_REQ_0000079409-1": {"title": "Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences NSF NCEMS Postdoctoral Scholar-Computational Proteomics/Mass Spectrometry", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar (Computational Proteomics/Mass Spectrometry) The National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences (NCEMS) at The Pennsylvania State University ( ncems.psu.edu ) seeks an outstanding scientist to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in Computational Proteomics and Mass Spectrometry housed within the Huck Institutes of Life Sciences at The Pennsylvania State University. NCEMS is an NSF-funded interdisciplinary research center positioned at the interface of data science, molecular and cellular biology, and quantitative physical sciences. The Center provides leadership in the integration of diverse, publicly available datasets to gain insights into emergent phenomena in molecular and cellular biology. About the Position The successful candidate, in collaboration with faculty and research staff at NCEMS, will conduct original research involving proteomics, mass spectrometry data analysis, protein interactions, protein complexes, post-translational modifications, structural proteomics, or systems-level analysis of molecular and cellular biology. Research may involve large-scale public proteomics datasets, data harmonization, cross-study integration, quantitative proteomics, crosslinking mass spectrometry, interactomics, protein structure and function, molecular assemblies, or biological networks. The scholar\u2019s independent work may use, extend, or contribute to NCEMS Working Group data products, analytical tools, computational workflows, and methodological innovations. The scholar will also collaborate with NCEMS Working Groups where their expertise can help advance shared research goals, strengthen proteomics-based discovery, and produce high-impact scientific outputs. This position is full time, on-site at the Penn State University Park campus. This position does not permit remote work. This is a term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with an excellent chance for multiple years of renewal based upon mutual agreement. Requirements A PhD in a proteomics\u2019 relevant field is required. The successful candidate will have a strong foundation in proteomics, mass spectrometry, protein biochemistry, quantitative biology, bioinformatics, or related analytical and computational approaches. An ability to conduct research and produce scholarly outputs as demonstrated through publications in peer-reviewed journals. Candidates should have experience analyzing, interpreting, or integrating mass spectrometry-based proteomics data. Experience with mass spectrometry-based workflows is expected, such as bottom-up proteomics, quantitative proteomics, targeted or untargeted proteomics, post-translational modification analysis, crosslinking mass spectrometry, structural proteomics, protein-protein interaction analysis, or related approaches. Expertise in computational analysis of proteomics data is highly desirable. Experience with Python, R, or related scientific computing tools; proteomics software platforms; biological databases; data repositories; reproducible workflows; or large-scale public proteomics datasets is desirable. Familiarity with public proteomics repositories and resources, such as PRIDE, ProteomeXchange, MassIVE, PeptideAtlas, UniProt, or related resources, is also desirable. Candidates must be independent self-starters, have a strong work ethic, strong interpersonal and written communication skills, and the ability to work well in a collaborative team environment. Application Process Applications must be submitted electronically in a single PDF and should include: A cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoc-Position-in-Hydraulic-Modeling_REQ_0000079302-1": {"title": "Postdoc Position in Hydraulic Modeling", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University has a Postdoctoral Scholar opening starting in July 2026 (starting date negotiable, but preference will be given to candidates who can start at this time). This position is funded through a project to research on roadway hydraulic structure perform, such as culvert, through computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations and flume experiments. The product of this project will be used as a guidance for practitioners. Job responsibility: Under the guidance of the PI and collaborators from other university and industry, the major responsibility of the research associate is to carry out the research tasks in the project, which include literature survey, data collection, flume experiments, computational modeling, result analysis and synthesis, and report writing. Requirements and qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in civil engineering or related fields with a focus on hydraulics, environmental fluid mechanics, or water resources in general. The applicant must have prior experience with computational modeling and flume experiments. Experience with CFD software such as OpenFOAM is preferred, but not required. To be considered for this position or if you need more information, please contact Dr. Xiaofeng Liu ( xzl123@psu.edu) . Dr. Liu\u2019s research group webpage: http://water.engr.psu.edu/liu/ . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Undergraduate-Adjunct-Instructor---Smeal-Management---Organization-Department_REQ_0000079383-1": {"title": "Part-Time Undergraduate Adjunct Instructor - Smeal Management & Organization Department", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-15\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Management and Organization Department within The Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for adjunct instructor positions to teach one or more undergraduate courses during one or more of the fall 2026, spring 2027, and summer 2027 semesters. Each non-tenure track appointment has the possibility of reappointment. A Master's degree or equivalent education and experience is required. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Huck-Institutes-of-the-Life-Sciences-NSF-NCEMS_REQ_0000079386-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences/NSF NCEMS", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-12\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar (Physics / Statistical Mechanics in Molecular Biology) The National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences (NCEMS) at The Pennsylvania State University ( ncems.psu.edu ) seeks an outstanding scientist to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in Physics, Statistical Mechanics, and Quantitative Modeling housed within the Huck Institutes of Life Sciences at Penn State University. NCEMS is an NSF-funded interdisciplinary research center positioned at the interface of data science, molecular and cellular biology, and quantitative physical sciences. The Center provides leadership in the integration of diverse, publicly available datasets, to gain insights into emergent phenomena in molecular and cellular biology. About the Position The successful candidate, in collaboration with faculty at NCEMS, will conduct research in molecular biology by applying methods from physics, statistical mechanics, quantitative modeling, or related areas that synergize with the scientific goals, data products, and methodological innovations of NCEMS. This position is designed to support the scholar\u2019s development as an independent researcher while embedding them in a highly collaborative synthesis science environment. This position is full time, on-site at the Penn State University Park campus. This position does not permit remote work. This is a term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with an excellent chance for multiple years of renewal based upon mutual agreement. Requirements A PhD in Physics or Biological Physics is required. The successful candidate will have a strong foundation in statistical mechanics, stochastic processes, dynamical systems, complex systems, or related quantitative approaches; Experience in developing and implementing analytical or computational models and simulations. An ability to conduct research and produce scholarly outputs as demonstrated through publications in peer-reviewed journals. Familiarity is expected with molecular and cellular biology concepts, such as protein interactions, molecular assemblies, gene regulation, cellular organization, or biological networks. Candidates must be independent self-starters, have a strong work ethic, strong interpersonal and written communication skills, and the ability to work well in a collaborative team environment. Application Process Applications must be submitted electronically in a single PDF and should include: A cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Huck-Institutes-of-the-Life-Sciences-NSF-NCEMS-Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000079401-1": {"title": "Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences NSF NCEMS Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-12\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar (Machine Learning or Artificial Intelligence in Molecular and Cellular Biology) The National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences (NCEMS) at Penn State University ( ncems.psu.edu ) seeks an outstanding scientist to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in Machine Learning or Artificial Intelligence housed within the Huck Institutes of Life Sciences at Penn State University. NCEMS is an NSF-funded interdisciplinary research center positioned at the interface of data science, molecular and cellular biology, and quantitative physical sciences. The Center provides leadership in the integration of diverse, publicly available datasets to gain insights into emergent phenomena in molecular and cellular biology. About the Position The successful candidate, in collaboration with faculty and research staff at NCEMS, will conduct original research applying machine learning, artificial intelligence, computer science, statistical learning, or related computational approaches to problems in molecular and cellular biology. Research may involve large-scale public datasets, biological data harmonization, representation learning, predictive modeling, foundation models, network analysis, graph-based learning, uncertainty quantification, scientific machine learning, or interpretable AI. This position is full time, on-site at the Penn State University Park campus. This position does not permit remote work. This is a term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire, with an excellent chance for renewal based upon mutual agreement. Requirements A PhD in Computer Science, Data Science or a closely related field is required. The successful candidate will have a strong foundation in machine learning, artificial intelligence, statistical learning, scientific computing, data science, or related computational approaches. Candidates must have experience developing or implementing machine learning methods for large-scale data analysis, predictive modeling, or biological discovery. Expertise in Python is expected. A demonstrated ability to conduct research and produce scholarly outputs, as evidenced by publications in peer-reviewed journals. Familiarity with molecular and cellular biology concepts is also desirable. Candidates must be independent self-starters, have a strong work ethic, strong interpersonal and written communication skills, and the ability to work well in a collaborative team environment. Application Process Applications must be submitted electronically in a single PDF and should include: A cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Huck-Institutes-of-the-Life-Sciences-NSF-NCEMS-Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000079387-1": {"title": "Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences NSF NCEMS Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-12\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar (Computational Biology) The National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences (NCEMS) at Penn State University ( ncems.psu.edu ) seeks an outstanding scientist to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in Computational Biology housed within the Huck Institutes of Life Sciences at Penn State University. NCEMS is an NSF-funded interdisciplinary research center positioned at the interface of data science, molecular and cellular biology, and quantitative physical sciences. The Center provides leadership in the integration of diverse, publicly available datasets, to gain insights into emergent phenomena in molecular and cellular biology. About the Position The successful candidate, in collaboration with faculty at NCEMS, will conduct original computational biology research involving large-scale public datasets, multi-omics integration, biological data harmonization, systems-level analysis, or related areas\u00a0 that synergize with the scientific goals, data products, and methodological innovations of NCEMS. This position is designed to support the scholar\u2019s development as an independent researcher while embedding them in a highly collaborative synthesis science environment. This position is full time, on-site at the Penn State University Park campus. This position does not permit remote work. This is a term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with an excellent chance for multiple years of renewal based upon mutual agreement. Requirements A PhD in Computational Biology or Systems Biology is required. The successful candidate will have a strong foundation in computational analysis of molecular and cellular biology data. Expertise in Python and/or R. A demonstrated ability to conduct independent research as demonstrated through a strong track-record of peer-reviewed publications. Experience working with large-scale biological datasets, including genomic, transcriptomic, proteomic, metabolomic, lipidomic, epigenomic, interactomic, structural, glycomic, or single-cell multi-omics data a plus. Familiarity with biological databases and public data repositories, such as NCBI, GEO, SRA, ENA, UniProt, etc. Candidates must be independent self-starters, have a strong work ethic, strong interpersonal and written communication skills, and the ability to work well in a collaborative team environment. Application Process Applications must be submitted electronically in a single PDF and should include: A cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV) \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Line-Assistant-Professor--College-of-Engineering--Department-of-Aerospace-Engineering_REQ_0000079195-2": {"title": "Tenure-Line Assistant Professor, College of Engineering, Department of Aerospace Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Aerospace Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park campus, invites applications for full-time, tenure-track faculty position to start in Fall 2026 or Spring 2027. The position is intended for the rank of Assistant Professor . The College of Engineering and the Department seek to grow their capability for research and education in aircraft designed simultaneously in their physical design and in the algorithms controlling them to create new capabilities for Unmanned Aerial Systems.\u00a0Particular focus is on the design, prototyping and flight testing of aircraft systems via rigorous aeronautical analysis simultaneous with the creation and implementation of novel autonomous capabilities tailored to the needs of flight.\u00a0Candidates are expected to demonstrate expertise in intelligent systems as applied to aeronautics suitable for research topics such as creating and implementing UAS capable of targeted observation and online decision making.\u00a0Experience teaching undergraduate and graduate courses such as AERSP 306 Aeronautics, AERSP 402A/B Aircraft Design, AERSP 462/562 Autonomy and specialized graduate courses in a range of associated topics is also expected.\u00a0 Other practical experience with flying that supports flight test and demonstration is preferred. The job duties include establishing an impactful research program, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, developing new courses at undergraduate and graduate levels, advising students and service to the institute and the profession, and contributing to an inclusive community of faculty, staff and students. Applicants must have an earned doctorate in aerospace engineering or a related field by the start date.\u00a0 Applicants should apply online and submit electronically a single PDF file that contains: a cover letter; a CV; a single (5 pages max) summary of their activities and interests in research and in teaching and advising; and the names and contact information for at least three references. Within their summary, applicants should articulate: their plans to establish a research program attracting outside research sponsorship, contributing to the aerospace industry, and resulting in published research findings; their vision for collaborating with the disciplinary strengths already in place within the Department and around Penn State in support of cross-disciplinary research and teaching;\u00a0 reflecting Penn State\u2019s commitment to our educational mission, candidates should articulate their interests and experience in supporting undergraduate and graduate programs through teaching and advising. The search committee will review applications as they are received; responses received before 7/9/2026 are assured full consideration. Inquiries can be sent to Amy Pritchett (apritchett@psu.edu), Professor and Head of Aerospace Engineering. About the Department: The mission of the Penn State Department of Aerospace Engineering is to nurture and grow aerospace engineers capable of addressing the emerging needs of the aerospace industry. Our vision is to use our collective technical ability and our collective passion for flight to grow thought leaders and technical innovators in our field and to create an environment in which: our faculty are the top scholars and creative leaders in our field, and our students are steeped in an inclusive culture valuing a rigorous approach to tough problems faced by the Aerospace Industry. We have crafted this mission and vision to reflect both our passion for the field of aerospace engineering, and our chosen strategy of contributing to the field by nurturing and supporting people in all their career stages - undergraduate students, graduate students, and faculty - and the community within which we operate. We believe that we have a unique competitive advantage in our emphasis on supporting people and community: we attract faculty who want to work together in a collegial environment with all the benefits this brings to faculty productivity and inter-disciplinary efforts; our instruction is based on a vision of supporting the whole person; and inclusivity is vital to our community. Our community includes 6 teaching faculty, 20 tenure-line faculty, and numerous active emeritus faculty, research faculty, and collaborators in other engineering departments and in the Applied Research Lab. Excitement for our undergraduate and graduate programs are strong and we are growing steadily. We moved to the new Engineering Collaborative Research & Education (ECoRE) building in summer 2024 which provides extensive research labs (including an indoor flight facility), dedicated fourth-year student capstone design space, and innovative classrooms. The department also maintains the Penn State UAS Research Lab (PURL) at the University Park airport, with extensive infrastructure for flight testing at nearby test sites and airfields. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-the-Center-for-Critical-Minerals-at-the-EMS-Energy-Institute_REQ_0000079243-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in the Center for Critical Minerals at the EMS Energy Institute", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Center for Critical Minerals ( http://C2M.psu.edu ) at EMS Energy Institute/Penn State invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar position to conduct cutting-edge research in extracting critical minerals, including rare earth elements, from primary and secondary sources. This position will work on scaling up a three-stage process developed by Penn State to process 10,000 gallons per day of acid mine drainage to extract critical minerals. Successful candidates report to and work with the Center for Critical Minerals director. Responsibilities include: Conduct both applied and fundamental research involving mineral processing and hydro/pyrometallurgical processes; working with pilot-scale research operations is desirable. Assist in research proposals. Document research findings in reports and referred journals. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in engineering or a related discipline by the start date. They should also have excellent written and verbal communication skills and be able to work in teams. Interested candidates should submit the following: An application cover letter highlighting the relevant experience for the position. A curriculum vitae including educational background, employment history, and a list of publications, research projects worked, and the role played in those projects. Contact information for three professional references. Inquiries about the position can be sent to Sarma Pisupati ( sxp17@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Instructor---Undergraduate-General-Education-Course-in-Workforce-Financial-Skills_REQ_0000079287": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor \u2013 Undergraduate General Education Course in Workforce Financial Skills", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-09\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS Position Summary The Workforce Education and Development (WFED) program seeks qualified adjunct instructors to teach undergraduate general education courses related to personal financial planning, financial literacy, and money management for the workforce. These courses serve students across all academic backgrounds and are designed to build foundational financial knowledge and quantitative reasoning skills relevant to career entry and long-term financial well-being. Courses may focus on topics such as personal financial planning, financial decision-making for working adults, financial well-being for the workforce, and related subject areas. Courses are expected to be delivered in-person at University Park , with hybrid delivery possible depending on departmental needs. Primary Responsibilities- Deliver weekly in-person and/or hybrid instruction following approved course syllabus and objectives. Support student learning of core financial concepts, quantitative reasoning, and practical financial skills. Develop and facilitate applied learning activities including calculations, analysis, and scenario-based work. Evaluate student progress through assignments, quizzes, exams, and projects. Maintain timely student grading and records through Canvas. Hold weekly office hours, in person or via Zoom. Submit final grades according to university policies. Example Topic Areas- Budgeting fundamentals and cash flow planning Income, taxation, and cost-of-living comparisons Banking, saving, and financial services Credit, borrowing, and debt strategy Insurance and risk management Retirement accounts and planning options Investment fundamentals Financial decision-making for education and careers Required Qualifications- Master\u2019s degree in: \u2022 Personal finance \u2022 Finance \u2022 Accounting \u2022 Business \u2022 Workforce development / workforce education \u2022 or closely related field Experience teaching or training young adults or adults. Preferred Qualifications- Certified Financial Planner (CFP) designation preferred. Professional experience in financial advising, financial coaching, accounting, HR benefits, retirement planning, or related areas. Experience teaching undergraduate or general education courses. Experience teaching quantitative subjects. Familiarity with Canvas. Appointment Terms- This is a part-time wage appointment , assigned for a single academic semester and contingent upon student enrollment and available funding. Reappointment may be possible based on enrollment needs, performance, and departmental priorities. Delivery is expected to be in-person or hybrid . For questions, please contact: Hyung Joon Yoon, Ph.D., Professor-in-Charge, Workforce Education and Development Program (huy114@psu.edu). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Professor-of-Chemistry_REQ_0000079185-1": {"title": "Professor of Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Chemistry at Penn State, University Park campus, invites applications for a tenure-line faculty position at the rank of Professor . This search is specific to the areas of analytical and physical chemistry of materials. The successful candidate will have an established and widely recognized research program focused on understanding structure-property relationships of nanoscale materials. Research programs that focus on single-entity analysis, including electrochemical characterization, are preferred. Research that complements existing departmental strengths in structurally-precise nanochemistry are of specific interest.\u00a0 Applicants should have a Ph.D. in Chemistry or related field, a record of creative research accomplishments, a research plan clearly articulating future contributions to the field, and a strong desire to achieve teaching excellence at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The position features outstanding research space and a competitive start-up package. The anticipated starting date for this appointment is Fall 2026. The duties include research, teaching, supervision of student research at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and service to the university and the greater professional community. Candidates are expected to demonstrate interest in and capacity for developing a strong, independent research program, and teaching and mentorship excellence at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Applications submitted electronically by July 15, 2026 will receive full consideration. In addition to submitting the Penn State application, an application must be submitted at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/32145 that consists of a cover letter, current CV, one-page teaching statement and a statement of research interests that includes a ~1 page summary and a ~10-page narrative of research plans. For more information on the Penn State Chemistry Department and the application process, visit\u00a0 https://science.psu.edu/chem . Applicants will also need to arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to Academic Jobs Online. The Department of Chemistry at Penn State offers a stimulating environment that supports cutting-edge research in both traditional and interdisciplinary areas, including a 177,000 square foot chemistry research building on the University Park campus, excellent shared instrumentation facilities, and close interactions with the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences ( https://www.huck.psu.edu ), the Materials Research Institute ( https://www.mri.psu.edu ), the Institutes of Energy and the Environment ( https://iee.psu.edu/home ), and the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences ( https://www.icds.psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000078733-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University Department of Plant Pathology and Environmental Microbiology is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to conduct research on plant viruses, mycoviruses, and virome dynamics in agricultural and forest ecosystems. The successful candidate will develop and apply molecular, genomic, and computational approaches to investigate virus epidemiology, emergence, and host\u2013pathogen ecological interactions using high-throughput sequencing and Nanopore-based diagnostic technologies. Research activities will include virus detection, indexing, characterization, and ecological analyses across plant and fungal systems. Applicants are required to have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in plant pathology, microbiology, microbial ecology, plant sciences, or a related field, and be able to provide evidence that all requirements have been met for completion of the Ph.D. prior to the effective date of hire. Applicants should have virology and bioinformatics experience with the terminal and R; experience with other languages is a plus. Applicants should possess excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication (both oral and written) skills. A desire to participate in Penn State Virology and One Health Microbiome Center activities, as well as to provide outreach to groups underrepresented in STEM fields and other stakeholders, will be viewed positively. The Postdoctoral Scholar will work within collaborative, transdisciplinary research teams and contribute to integrating molecular biology, bioinformatics, and ecological approaches to address emerging challenges in plant and fungal health. Additional responsibilities include mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, contributing to manuscript preparation, and supporting the development of competitive grant proposals. This position is ideal for candidates interested in developing expertise at the intersection of viral genomics, bioinformatics, and disease ecology within a highly collaborative research environment. Interested candidates should upload the following application materials: a cover letter describing research interests and experience, a curriculum vitae, a list of relevant publications, and three professional references with contact information. For questions regarding the position, please contact Assistant Professor Ricardo I. Alcal\u00e1 Brise\u00f1o at ria5282@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Chemistry_REQ_0000078886-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratory of Professor Kenneth Knappenberger in the Department of Chemistry, at The Pennsylvania State University, seeks to fill a postdoctoral research position in the area of metal nanoparticle synthesis and spectroscopy. Research will focus on the investigation of structural influences on the spin and magneto-optical properties of nanoclusters and nanoparticles. The successful candidate should have extensive experience in nanocluster synthesis, composition and structure characterization, circular dichroism and magnetic field spectroscopy, and photophysics for atomically precise nanoclusters. Applicants must have recently received, or be scheduled to receive, a Ph.D. in Chemistry by the time employment starts. The individual should be self-motivated and is expected to lead the projects, as well as contribute to collaborative research efforts. Interested and qualified applicants must submit applications electronically to include a cover letter describing your research background to include prior training, and research interests, as well as a CV. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Following a screening of initial application materials, candidates will be contacted by email asking for letters of reference to be sent. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Sengupta-Group_REQ_0000062624-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Sengupta Group", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-21\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Electrical Engineering at Penn State is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar. The successful candidate will work on using machine learning tools for electronic design automation problems. The work will involve research on machine learning, digital twins, electronic design automation efforts working in collaboration with other research groups. Necessary experience and background - Requirements include a Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Computer Science or other relevant fields by the start date. Prior background in machine learning, digital twins and electronic design automation is highly desired. The postdoc will have the opportunity to mentor graduate and undergraduate students. Guidance will be provided toward writing research grants and publications. To apply, please submit an online application, a CV, and contact information of three references. For more details regarding the research group, please visit \u00a0 https://sites.psu.edu/sengupta/ . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Materials-Science-and-Engineering_REQ_0000078554-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar, Materials Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-19\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Materials Science and Engineering Department, within the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences at Penn State is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar to perform research under the direction of Professor Douglas Wolfe (Materials Science & Engineering). Job Duties: Design, develop, and conduct manufacturing experiments for a wide range of materials comprised of CsPbB3, nanocomosite structures, polymer matrix ceramic composites, ceramic matrix composites, and advanced coating systems for a variety of applications in the aerospace, defense, nuclear, and microelectronic industries. Develop standard operating procedures to conduct consistent processing and characterization of materials for extreme environments. Work collaboratively on a multidisciplinary team. Synthesize and manufacture unique design architectures comprised of coatings and bulk materials using a variety of manufacturing methods. Materials synthesis may include perovskite systems, composites, oxides, and mixed components for a variety of applications. Assist in performing a variety of testing and analytical materials characterization using the materials characterization laboratory facilities. Assist in perform modeling and/or experimental analysis (microscopy, spectroscopy) to investigate the fundamentals of radiation effects in electronics and shielding. Analyze data. Disseminate findings in journals and conferences and monthly presentations. Qualifications and Requirements: Applicants should have a Ph.D. or equivalent as of the hire date in Materials/Mechanical/Electrical/Nuclear Engineering or related discipline. Excellent foundation in materials processing. Hands-on experience with device and system characterization. Experience in radiation effects (single event, total ionizing dose, displacement damage) is very helpful. Excellent written/oral communication skills. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter describing their interest in the position, a CV including a publication list, and names and contact information of up to three references. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Digital-Arts-and-Media-Design_REQ_0000077428-2": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Digital Arts and Media Design", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Position Specifics: The Digital Arts Program and School of Visual Arts in the College of Arts and Architecture at the Pennsylvania State University invite candidates to apply for an Assistant Teaching Professor position of Digital Arts and Media Design focusing on 3D Animation. This is a full-time, 36-week, nine-month, non-tenure track appointment. The anticipated start date is August 2026. Full university benefits apply. We are seeking qualified candidates whose creative practice and teaching interests are focused on 3D animation and related technologies. The ideal candidate is a 3D animator/generalist with considerable experience in 3D animation workflows that can instruct and mentor 3d animation students and who stays abreast of 3D professional practices, industry standard software, and emerging technologies and production pipelines. The successful candidate will teach courses in 3D modeling and animation as well as additional courses related to their experience and practice that may include, animation fundamentals, foundational design, experimental animation, emerging practices and technologies, or other related digital arts and design studio courses in the program. We invite applications from qualified candidates with exceptional interpersonal skills and a strong commitment to collegiality and teamwork, who are prepared to contribute through teaching and creative activity at all levels of the Digital Arts Curriculum and majors. Responsibilities: The position will include teaching up to three courses in the Digital Arts and Media Design Program each semester, participation in program activities, and service to the school, college, and university committees as assigned. Teach 3D courses covering animation previsualize, animation, motion capture, lighting, rendering, and compositing. Teach production skills necessary to design, rig, animate, light, and render 3D assets for animated films and digital games. Teach additional digital arts courses in the curriculum based on areas of expertise. Be well-versed in teaching the principles of animation and effective visual storytelling. Join with digital art faculty to cultivate a lively animation studio culture and help set production standards that enhance student creative outcomes. Participate in the guidance and assessment of students, portfolio development, independent studies, internships, and capstone thesis projects. Encourage and support our students in developing animated creative works as part of a socially and culturally engaged research university. Required Qualifications: Terminal degree in Animation, Digital Arts, New Media, Cinematic Arts, Film/Cinema Production, or a comparable terminal degree (such as a Master of Fine Arts - MFA, or a PhD) at the time of appointment. Evidence of a commitment to a successful 3D animation digital arts practice, commensurate with experience. Evidence of equitable considerations for all, awareness, and practice regarding curricula development, along with evidence of working collectively to cultivate a culture that encourages success and enables all members of a college community to thrive. Preferred qualifications: College-level teaching experience (one semester, minimum, including teaching assistantships or equivalent technical training/teaching). Professional experience working in 3d animation for films, games, TV or creative industries. Considerable experience working with Autodesk Maya and Motion Builder Experience with related animation, visual effects, and compositing tools: Blender, Houdini, Substance 3D Painter, ZBrush, Nuke. To Apply To be assured of full consideration, all materials should be submitted via Penn State\u2019s online application system and include the following: a letter of application stating teaching and creative interests, and qualifications for the position a curriculum vitae an artist or designer statement (or statement of practice and creative activity) a statement of teaching philosophy, addressing how they create an inclusive learning environment for all a representative portfolio of creative work in animation and demo reel a representative portfolio of student work and teaching portfolio (in 3D modeling and animation, if available) Name and contact information for three professional references All documents above must be submitted in pdf file format, with external links (to portfolio materials and reels) included as needed/relevant. NOTE: Only five files (5 mb per document) can be uploaded. Please combine smaller files to accommodate this restriction. Screening of applications will begin on May 1 and will continue to be received until the position is filled. Inquiries should be addressed to: Woohun Joo, Chair, Assistant Professor of Art and Digital Arts & Media Design, Digital Arts Faculty Search Committee wxj5122@psu.edu About the Digital Arts Program The Digital Arts Program (DART) at Penn State approaches design through the lens of visual arts as a critical, creative, and experimental studio-based practice. The program prepares students to become leaders in digital media fields, where a commanding knowledge of emerging technologies allows them to contribute and innovate in a range of creative media design careers. Students choose from BDes, BFA, and BA degrees and progress alongside their cohort in an intense, collaborative environment developing research, design, and computational skills to enhance their capacity for critical and creative thinking while honing digital media design and production skills in a range of digital arts, studio art, digital design, and coding courses. Students are encouraged to engage and collaborate across the Penn State community with schools and colleges such as the School of Music, School of Architecture and Landscape Architecture in the College of Arts and Architecture, the Eberly College of Science, the College of Engineering, and the Department of Psychology in the College of Liberal Arts. In the final year of study, students work rigorously on senior thesis projects guided by faculty mentors in one of three emphasis areas: digital art and digital design, animation and time-based media, and interactive media and games. For more information, please visit: Digital Arts and Media Design at Penn State About the School of Visual Arts The School of Visual Arts (SoVA) at Penn State offer undergraduate degrees in Art Education (B.S.), Digital Arts (B.A., B.Des., B.F.A.), Studio Art (BA, BFA) and Photography (B.A., B.Des., B.F.A.) at our residential campus, and a fully online degree in Digital Multimedia Design (B.Des.) and Digital Arts certificate at World Campus. At the graduate level, we offer an M.F.A. in Art (Ceramics, Drawing and Painting, Graphic Design, Digital Arts and New Media, Photography, and Sculpture), and dual M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Art Education with African American and Diaspora Studies, or Women\u2019s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies. SoVA\u2019s mission aim: To contribute to the expansion of knowledge and scholarship in the visual arts, design, arts pedagogy, and related fields of study and practice. To facilitate the highest level of creative and intellection pursuit for students through teaching and learning experiences and opportunities. To provide expertise to the service and benefit of communities across campus, the commonwealth, the nation, and beyond. SoVA will be a safe space for creatively engaged minds and bodies. This community will operate in a cohesive and supportive manner to engender transformative experiences. For more information, please visit Penn State School of Visual Arts About the College of Arts and Architecture The College of Arts and Architecture at Penn State, located on the University Park campus in beautiful central Pennsylvania, is the hub for arts and design education, outreach, and engagement, where new ways of thinking are encouraged and interdisciplinary collaboration is the norm. With academic programs spanning music, theatre, visual arts, graphic design, digital design, art history, architecture, and landscape architecture, we are a complete arts and design community committed to artistic and scholarly creativity, research, and the preparation of creators and educators whose innovation and industriousness make a positive impact around the world. We offer a broad array of\u00a0 undergraduate \u00a0and\u00a0 graduate \u00a0programs, as well as numerous ensembles and clubs open to all students regardless of major. The\u00a0 Center for the Performing Arts ,\u00a0 Palmer Museum of Art ,\u00a0 Penn State Centre Stage , and\u00a0 Penn\u2019s Woods Music Festival \u00a0\u2013 also part of the college \u2013 are key organizations in the area\u2019s thriving cultural landscape, offering performances, exhibitions, and educational outreach programs that are enjoyed by thousands each year. In addition, the college\u2019s research centers and institutes help to foster a vibrant culture of inquiry that promotes excellence within the arts and design disciplines, while at the same time leveraging the potential of a comprehensive research university. College of Arts and Architecture faculty are dedicated to providing high-quality professional instruction to graduate and undergraduate students enrolled in the college. They also are responsible for providing undergraduate literature, history, and studio courses in the arts for all students at Penn State. The college is housed in sixteen buildings in the \u201cArts District\u201d on the University Park campus. Learn more about\u00a0 our extensive facilities . Penn State\u2019s College of Arts and Architecture proudly serves as one of the major cultural centers between Philadelphia and Pittsburgh. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Chemistry_REQ_0000077845-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratory of Professor\u00a0Rongchao Jin in the Department of Chemistry ,\u00a0 at The Pennsylvania State University, seeks to fill a postdoctoral research position in the area of femtosecond transient absorption and fluorescence upconversion spectroscopies. Research will focus on the investigation of ultrafast electron dynamics and mechanism of near-infrared fluorescence of atomically precise nanoclusters of gold and alloys. The successful candidate should demonstrate extensive experience in femtosecond spectroscopy and photophysics for atomically precise nanocluster. Applicants must have recently received, or be scheduled to receive, a Ph.D. in Chemistry by the time employment starts. The individual should be self-motivated and is expected to lead the projects,\u00a0as well as contribute to collaborative research efforts. Interested and qualified applicants must submit applications electronically to include a cover letter describing\u00a0your research background to include prior training,\u00a0and research interests, as well as a CV. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0Following a screening of\u00a0initial application materials,\u00a0candidates will be contacted by email\u00a0asking for letters of reference\u00a0to be sent. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Instructor---School-of-Visual-Arts---2026-27-Academic-Year_REQ_0000078445-1": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Instructor - School of Visual Arts - 2026-27 Academic Year", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-11\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The School of Visual Arts (SoVA) is looking to hire a part-time adjunct instructors. Successful applicants may teach courses and assist with various tasks related to teaching, such as, grading and setting up technology. These positions are typically only for one semester. Requirements: A terminal degree: MFA, Ph.D., or equivalent professional experience College-level teaching experience with a strong interest in undergraduate instruction Hybrid and online teaching experience is highly desirable. Submit: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae For more information on SoVA, please visit https://arts.psu.edu/academics/school-of-visual-arts/ \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Teaching-Faculty---Sociology---Criminology_REQ_0000078233-1": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Teaching Faculty - Sociology & Criminology", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-08\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Sociology and Criminology at the Pennsylvania State University, University Park campus, \u00a0invites\u00a0applications for\u00a0part-time\u00a0lecturer positions. The position will involve teaching courses in Sociology and/or Criminology at the undergraduate level. The ideal candidates will have a minimum of a master\u2019s degree (Doctoral Degree preferred) in Criminology, Sociology, or a closely related field.\u00a0 Teaching experience is required. \u00a0 Adjunct Teaching Professors are expected to teach one to two courses per semester based on College of Liberal Arts guidelines. \u00a0\u00a0Summer teaching opportunities may be available. The start date for the position is August 2026. To be considered for this position, submit a letter of application detailing relevant qualifications for the job, including a description of teaching experience and interests. Additionally, candidates should submit a curriculum vitae, sample syllabi from courses taught, and the names and contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 For a more detailed description of the department, please visit our website at https://sociology.la.psu.edu/ .\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor_REQ_0000077915-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-08\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Assistant Research Professor Mycobacterial & Zoonotic Disease Research Kapur Laboratory\u00a0 \u00b7\u00a0 Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences\u00a0 \u00b7\u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University Position Assistant Research Professor (non-tenure track, full-time) Department Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences Location University Park, PA, with periodic international travel Funding Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation and NIH (multi-year) Duration Annual appointment, renewable based on performance and funding availability About the Position The Kapur Laboratory works on bovine tuberculosis and related zoonotic diseases in low- and middle-income countries, where conventional test-and-slaughter control is not viable. The program develops and validates diagnostics, vaccines, and surveillance tools intended for national deployment, working in close partnership with government, academic, and commercial institutions in India, Ethiopia, and several high-income countries. We seek an experienced research scientist to provide scientific and operational leadership across the program. This is a critical non-tenure-track, 48 week research faculty position with substantial scientific independence and direct engagement with international policy and regulatory processes. This position will be hired at the rank of Assistant Research Professor . Responsibilities Provide scientific oversight across the program portfolio, spanning diagnostics, vaccines, surveillance, and antimicrobial work. Lead experimental design, analysis, and interpretation across multi-site studies. Coordinate consortium activities, support funder reporting, and contribute to subaward and regulatory management. Develop and submit competitive grant applications to NIH, the Gates Foundation, and other agencies. Lead manuscript preparation and contribute to international guideline and regulatory engagement (WOAH and equivalents). Mentor postdocs and trainees, and develop training and capacity-building activities at partner institutions. Travel internationally as required. Qualifications Required PhD in veterinary science, microbiology, immunology, infectious diseases, epidemiology, or a related field. Three to five or more years of post-PhD research experience. Independent research record with first- or senior-author publications in peer-reviewed journals. Demonstrated experience managing multi-partner, multi-site research programs, ideally with international scope. Deep expertise in at least one of: mycobacterial diagnostics, vaccine immunology and field trials, antimicrobial resistance, or molecular epidemiology of zoonotic disease. Strong communication skills across institutional and cultural settings; experience with regulatory documents, grant reports, and scientific manuscripts. Willingness to travel internationally, including to India and Ethiopia. Preferred Experience with large foundation-funded programs and their reporting frameworks. BSL-3 experience with Mycobacterium tuberculosis complex. Familiarity with WOAH, USDA-APHIS, or equivalent diagnostic or vaccine regulatory frameworks. Track record of mentoring postdocs or graduate students. About the Laboratory The Kapur Laboratory at Penn State works on the genomics, pathogenesis, diagnostics, and control of mycobacterial and other zoonotic diseases, with a long-standing focus on low- and middle-income country settings. The lab leads an international consortium with partners across India, Ethiopia, the UK, Canada, and the US, and its work has been published in Science, The Lancet Microbe, The Lancet Infectious Diseases, and other leading journals. The Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences provide interdisciplinary research infrastructure across genomics, proteomics, imaging, and bioinformatics. How to Apply Submit a single PDF containing: Cover letter (maximum 3 pages) describing your research accomplishments, program management experience, and vision for the role. CV with full publication list, funded grants, and mentoring activities. Research statement (1 to 2 pages) outlining scientific priorities and approach to translating research into policy-relevant impact. Names and contact information for three professional references. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Open-Rank-Tenure-Line-Position-in-Computer-Science--College-of-Engineering---Huck-Institute-of-Life-Sciences_REQ_0000074193-1": {"title": "Open Rank Tenure Line Position in Computer Science (College of Engineering) /Huck Institute of Life Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Penn State University is seeking to hire multiple tenure-track or tenured faculty as part of a multi-year cluster hire focused on the intersection of \u00a0 computer science and the life sciences . This effort aims to strengthen the University\u2019s leadership in computational and data-driven approaches to biological, biomedical, and health-related challenges, and to advance the integration of computation into research and education across disciplines. The Department of Computer Science \u00a0 within the \u00a0 College of Engineering, University Park, PA \u00a0 seeks \u00a0 Assistant , \u00a0 Associate , or \u00a0 Full Professors \u00a0 whose research and teaching advance core AI and ML theory, foundation models and generative AI, reinforcement learning and autonomous agents, hardware and systems for AI, edge and federated learning, AI security and privacy, quantum machine learning (QML), robotics, and/or AI-driven discovery in science and engineering (e.g., genomics, bioinformatics, drug discovery, infectious disease modeling, materials, and biomanufacturing).\u202f Candidates will \u00a0 possess \u00a0 a PhD in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Data Science, Mathematics, Statistics, or a closely related discipline before their appointment start date at Penn State. \u00a0 \u00a0 These faculty will complement a strong and growing cohort of researchers working at the interface of computing, biology, and medicine, including those developing novel computational methods, systems, and tools, as well as those applying data-driven techniques\u2014such as machine learning and AI\u2014to advance discovery in the life sciences. The University has recently expanded its educational offerings in data science, computing, and engineering, providing new opportunities to integrate computational thinking and machine learning \u00a0 into \u00a0 life science curricula. \u00a0 The focus of this search is on candidates with expertise in areas such as computational biology, bioinformatics, biomedical data science, health informatics, computational genomics, systems biology, or related fields that bridge computer science and the life sciences. While experience with modern data-driven or AI-based methods is welcome, it is not required; candidates with strengths in foundational computing, modeling, simulation, systems, or data analysis approaches applied to biological or health domains are strongly encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will join a vibrant, interdisciplinary research community at Penn State and will benefit from extensive collaborative opportunities and resources provided by institutes such as the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (including advanced computing infrastructure), the Materials Research Institute, and the Clinical and Translational Sciences Institute. \u00a0 Faculty hired through this initiative will be affiliated with the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences, which serves as a central hub for life sciences research at Penn State. The Huck brings together researchers from diverse fields to address fundamental biological questions and pressing societal challenges. It supports a range of centers and programs, including the Genome Sciences Institute, the Center for Bioinformatics and Computational Biology, and interdisciplinary graduate programs in bioinformatics and genomics, as well as shared core facilities in genomics, proteomics, metabolomics, and related technologies. \u00a0 Successful candidates will be expected to develop internationally recognized research programs, contribute to high-quality graduate and undergraduate education, teach graduate and undergraduate courses, mentor students, and engage in interdisciplinary collaborations across campus and with external partners. They will also contribute to curriculum development that strengthens the integration of computing and life sciences. Academic Ranks Defined: Assistant professors should show early promise in teaching or research through emerging scholarly or professional contributions.\u00a0 Associate professors should have a record of high-quality publications and demonstrate teaching excellence in their field.\u00a0 Full professors should demonstrate a distinguished record of advanced work and leadership, reflecting established excellence in teaching, mentoring, and/or research. Application Instructions: \u00a0 Applications should be submitted online at \u00a0 https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/REQ_0000074193 Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statements outlining plans for teaching, research, and contributing to Penn State values ( https://universityethics.psu.edu/penn-state-values ), and the names and contact information for four references. Please combine these materials into a single PDF file and submit your application. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Research-Professor_REQ_0000077577-2": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Introduction The Department of Health Policy and Administration (HPA) in the College of Health and Human Development, at the Pennsylvania State University is seeking candidates for Director of the Pennsylvania Office of Rural Health (PORH).\u00a0This role also comes with a faculty position as Assistant or Associate Research Professor. The Director provides leadership and administrative oversight for all PORH activities to ensure fulfillment of federal and state mandates and to advance the mission of improving health and access to care for rural Pennsylvanians. This position reports to the Department Head in the Department of Health Policy and Administration and collaborates with external agencies; additional university units; and other local, state, and national partners. About the College The College\u00a0of\u00a0Health\u00a0and\u00a0Human\u00a0Development\u00a0offers\u00a0a\u00a0robust\u00a0program of eight interdisciplinary programs that share one common goal: enriching the lives of others. We continually examine contemporary issues facing people in today\u2019s changing times, and we develop cutting-edge solutions for addressing them. Our impact extends from our classrooms, across communities and industries, and around the globe. About\u00a0the\u00a0Pennsylvania Office of Rural Health \u00a0 The Pennsylvania Office of Rural Health (PORH) is one of the leading state offices of rural health in the\u00a0US\u00a0and is recognized in the state and nation for rural health leadership and innovation. PORH was formed in 1991 as a partnership between the federal government, the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, and The Pennsylvania State University. The office is one of 50 state offices of rural health\u00a0(SORH).\u00a0Funded through the Federal Office of Rural Health Policy under the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services and the Pennsylvania Department of Health, the office\u00a0is one of 10\u00a0SORHs\u00a0that is university-based. The\u00a0SORHs\u00a0are charged with being a source of coordination, technical\u00a0assistance, networking,\u00a0partnership development,\u00a0and\u00a0assisting\u00a0in the recruitment and retention of health care providers. PORH\u2019s mission is to enhance the health status of rural Pennsylvanians and ensure that rural residents have access to high-quality, affordable health care. PORH\u2019s vision is to be recognized as the premier rural leadership and information organization in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania and to be one of the most effective state offices of rural health in the nation. PORH provides\u00a0expertise\u00a0in\u00a0rural\u00a0health, health policy, agricultural health and safety, oral health, and community and economic development. At Penn\u00a0State, PORH is administratively\u00a0located\u00a0in the Department of Health Policy and Administration in the College of Health and Human Development.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Primary Job Responsibilities \u00a0 Primary\u00a0job\u00a0responsibilities\u00a0of\u00a0this\u00a0position\u00a0include:\u00a0\u00a0 Direct and coordinate statewide rural health initiatives, including technical\u00a0assistance, community needs assessments, information dissemination, and applied research.\u00a0 Serve as the Principal Investigator/Director of national,\u00a0state,\u00a0local, and other grants and contracts.\u00a0\u00a0 Identify\u00a0and pursue external funding opportunities; prepare grant proposals to support program operations and\u00a0special initiatives.\u00a0 Provide supervision and leadership for PORH staff, including project management oversight and support for staff development.\u00a0 Manage the PORH budget, including contract negotiation, project approval, expenditure oversight, and long-term financial planning to ensure program viability.\u00a0 Represent PORH on university, state, and federal committees, boards, task forces, commissions, and work groups related to rural health.\u00a0 Collaborate with university departments, other institutions of higher education, state and federal agencies, and state and national partners to support rural health priorities.\u00a0 Mentor students\u00a0and\u00a0interns interested in public health\u00a0and\u00a0health care\u00a0administration;\u00a0serve as\u00a0a guest lecturer\u00a0on topics related to rural health.\u00a0 Serve as lead on designated projects and ensure compliance with program\u00a0objectives\u00a0and reporting requirements.\u00a0 Support statewide efforts related to primary care practitioner recruitment and retention, rural health partnerships, and information clearinghouse functions.\u00a0 Qualifications \u00a0 Qualifications\u00a0for this position include:\u00a0 \u2022 A minimum of a master\u2019s degree or doctoral degree in a health\u00a0or\u00a0business-related\u00a0field.\u00a0 \u2022 Minimum of five years of progressive management experience.\u00a0 \u2022 Demonstrated\u00a0knowledge of health policy issues, legislative and congressional processes, rural health systems, health care delivery, and reimbursement structures.\u00a0 \u2022 Experience in developing and\u00a0submitting\u00a0national, state, and other grant applications and\u00a0fulfilling\u00a0grant requirements.\u00a0 \u2022 Experience in budget development and management.\u00a0 \u2022 Strong written and oral communication skills, including public speaking.\u00a0 \u2022 Proven organizational, leadership, and consensus building abilities.\u00a0 \u2022 Ability to\u00a0facilitate\u00a0group processes and work effectively with diverse stakeholders.\u00a0 \u2022 Willingness and ability to travel within Pennsylvania and nationally Supervisory Responsibilities \u00a0 This position assumes overall responsibility for the supervision of all full-time PORH staff\u00a0positions,\u00a0and, by extension, all part-time staff, including select undergraduate and graduate students.\u00a0 Application\u00a0Instructions \u00a0 To apply, please upload a resume/curriculum vitae, a cover letter outlining your interest in the position, and contact information for three professional references.\u00a0Review\u00a0of\u00a0applications\u00a0will begin\u00a0on\u00a0May 1, 2026 and will continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Questions related to the position can be addressed to Ronald McConnell at rjm824@psu.edu . Our\u00a0campuses\u00a0are\u00a0located\u00a0on\u00a0the\u00a0original\u00a0homelands\u00a0of\u00a0the\u00a0Erie,\u00a0Haudenosaunee\u00a0(Seneca,\u00a0Cayuga,\u00a0Onondaga,\u00a0Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and\u00a0Wahzhazhe\u00a0(Osage) Nations.\u00a0As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and\u00a0honor the traditional\u00a0caretakers\u00a0of\u00a0these\u00a0lands and\u00a0strive to\u00a0understand\u00a0and\u00a0model\u00a0their responsible stewardship.\u00a0We also acknowledge the longer history of these lands and our place in that history.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Lecturer_REQ_0000077992-2": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Lecturer", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-30\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see Notice to Out of State Applicants . POSITION SPECIFICS The School of Global Languages, Literatures, and Cultures\u00a0at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for part-time lecturer openings for the 2026 \u2013 2027 Academic Year, including Summer 2026. Job Duties Part-time lecturers will teach undergraduate resident and/or online courses in Spanish, Italian, and Portuguese, German and Slavic Languages and Literatures, French and Francophone Studies, Comparative Literature, or Asian Studies. Requirements and Qualifications A Master\u2019s degree in a related field is required. In addition, successful candidates must either have demonstrated a commitment to building an inclusive, equitable, and diverse campus community, or describe one or more ways they would envision doing so, given the opportunity. These are one semester or summer session, non-tenure track appointments. Summer lecturers normally teach one to two courses. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until all of the vacancies are filled. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director--Psychological-Clinic--College-of-the-Liberal-Arts_REQ_0000077493-2": {"title": "Director, Psychological Clinic, College of the Liberal Arts", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-27\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Psychology \u00a0at Penn State seeks a full-time\u00a0 Director\u00a0for the Penn State Psychological Clinic . We wish to fill this position immediately; start date is negotiable.\u00a0 The Psychological Clinic is a fully licensed comprehensive outpatient community mental health center for the region, as well as the training and research site for the Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychology. The clinic is among the largest associated with a doctoral training program in the United States, providing psychological and neuropsychological assessment for adults, adolescents, and children;\u00a0psychological and psychiatric outpatient treatment for adults,\u00a0including those with serious mental illness and personality pathology; psychological outpatient treatment for families, adolescents, and children,\u00a0and school-based intervention programs.\u00a0Faculty supervisors and clinical staff are licensed and paneled with major insurance companies to bill for services. The Psychological Clinic employs two full-time assistant\u00a0directors, a medical\u00a0director, psychiatric staff, and a diverse team of full- and part-time clinical and administrative staff. Penn State \u00a0is an APA- and PCSAS-accredited clinical science doctoral program. The Psychological Clinic facilitates the seamless integration of research and practice in clinical training in two parallel tracks (adult and child) for conducting clinical investigations, which also includes a fully developed adult-track practice-research network. This position is a full-time Academic Administrator which is a non-tenure-track clinical faculty position. This position will be filled at the academic rank of Clinical Professor or Associate Clinical Professor; rank and length of term will be commensurate with experience.\u00a0 Responsibilities for the Director \u00a0are mainly administrative and\u00a0include coordination of clinical services;\u00a0oversight of compliance, licensing and state and federal regulations; staff supervision; consultation with community agencies;\u00a0and\u00a0budget administration. Additional duties include\u00a0supervising graduate students in evidence-based therapy and assessment practices, program development, and facilitation of clinical research. There is no expectation that the Director be on call after business hours or outside of working hours although consultation may be requested during business hours.\u00a0 The\u00a0 Director \u00a0will be a fully participating member of the clinical doctoral program and university community. Candidates must have a doctorate from an APA- or PCSAS-approved program, completed an accredited internship, and be eligible for licensure in PA by the appointment date. It is preferred for candidates to have at least 5 years of clinical administrative experience, knowledge of HIPPA regulations and mental health law, an exemplary interest in the integration of science and practice, and a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in their clinical practice\u00a0and supervision. Interested candidates must\u00a0submit\u00a0an online application at\u00a0 Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board ,\u00a0and should upload the following application materials: a letter of application, a CV, and statements describing i) experience with clinic administration/leadership, ii) clinical training and expertise,\u00a0and iii) approach to clinical supervision. \u00a0Selected (re)prints are also welcome but not required. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5 document limit. \u00a0 For information on the position, please contact Kristin Buss, Head of Psychology, at kab37@psu.edu.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-in-Data-Journalism_REQ_0000077315-2": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Data Journalism", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Donald P. Bellisario College of Communications seeks an outstanding faculty member for an Assistant Teaching Professor in Data Journalism position in the journalism department starting in August 2026. We seek candidates with deep professional expertise in data journalism and a demonstrated record of data-driven reporting in professional newsroom settings. The ideal candidate brings hands-on experience exploring, cleaning, analyzing and documenting data \u2014 and translating that work into stories that inform and engage a public audience. Areas of teaching interest may include (but are not limited to): computational methods for investigative reporting; data analysis, statistical literacy and visualization for storytelling; working with large datasets, APIs and public records; data journalism workflows and systems in professional newsrooms; algorithmic accountability and transparency reporting; or related areas that advance the ethical and effective use of data in journalism. Strong candidates will be fluent in tools common to data journalism practice \u2014 such as Python, R, or SQL for data analysis; and structured, well-documented code workflows. They will model a critical and constructive relationship with data, approaching datasets with skepticism rather than cynicism, and integrating data analysis with traditional people-reporting across diverse communities. We are especially interested in candidates who bring a track record of teaching data skills across skill levels \u2014 from introductory data literacy to advanced computational methods \u2014 and who have experience helping colleagues and students develop their own practice. Candidates should have a Master's degree or higher in a relevant field by August 2026 and demonstrate significant professional experience as a data journalist, including reporting, editing, or leading data teams in a newsroom environment. Our department's award-winning programs in sports journalism and news create an ideal environment for research and teaching at the intersection of data and journalism practice. In addition to teaching and research responsibilities, there are opportunities to collaborate with faculty and programs in the department and across the Bellisario Media Center, including the Curley Center for Sports Journalism, the News Lab and Centre County Report. We are especially interested in candidates who can contribute to building and strengthening the data journalism infrastructure of our student-run newsrooms and help shape how the next generation of journalists works with data responsibly and innovatively. Applicants should submit a cover letter, CV and the names and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a qualified candidate is identified. Please direct any questions to committee chair Professor Maggie Messitt at mpm7177@psu.edu . For information on the college and its programs, see http://bellisario.psu.edu/ . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000074690-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Join a Dynamic Team Focused on Foundation AI modeling and Physics-Informed Machine Learning as a Postdoctoral Researcher at The Pennsylvania State University. The Pennsylvania State University is seeking applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position in the field of computational land surface hydrology, with a focus on Foundation AI model pretraining and finetuning, geospatial data processing and physics-informed machine learning. Prior experiences with these topics are highly desired. Pending approval of the grant, the successful candidate will work on innovative research in hydrology, collaborating with Dr. Shen and other faculty members, while also participating in the development of research projects and providing support to graduate students. The postdoctoral scholar will combine foundation AI modeling and differentiable modeling (a genre of physics-informed machine learning) for hydrologic modeling to improve large-scale hydrologic forecast. The scholar will work with a large, interdisciplinary team on the next-generation land surface model. Especially, the scholar will integrate state-of-the-art AI and physics-informed AI techniques into an operational system. The contribution could bring benefits to society and reduce the damage of floods. Duties include, but are not limited to: Develop and implement novel modeling techniques. Stay current with the latest developments and be willing to learn and adopt frontier methods. Collaborate with research team members to design, execute, and interpret research findings. Contribute to the development of high-quality research publications and presentations. Provide support to graduate students within the department. Requirements: The Postdoctoral Researcher should possess a Ph.D. in hydrology, civil engineering, environmental science, or a closely related field by the appointment start date. The successful candidate will also have: A strong background in numerical modeling and the application of computational methods to land surface hydrological problems. Research experience with a track record of published work in relevant scientific journals. Excellent communication, teamwork, and problem-solving skills. Proficiency in programming languages, such as Python or Fortran. Experiences with machine learning is a plus to the application. Solid understanding of the physical hydrologic cycle and large-scale geographic datasets. The Pennsylvania State University offers a dynamic research environment, providing access to world-class facilities and resources. We encourage highly motivated candidates with a passion for advancing the field of computational hydrology to apply for this exciting position. To apply, please submit your CV, a cover letter detailing your research interests and experience, and contact information for three references with your online application. \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Ferrari-lab_REQ_0000076477-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Ferrari lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The \u00a0 Ferr a ri \u00a0 lab \u00a0 at \u00a0 Penn State \u00a0 is seeking \u00a0 up to two \u00a0 Postdoctoral\u202fScholar s \u00a0 to work on \u00a0 computational and mathematical models of surveillance to guide vaccination programs to achieve and maintain disease elimination. \u00a0 This work will primarily focus on \u00a0 Gates Foundation funded projects to support vaccination and control programs for measles and rubella (in humans) and /or \u00a0 foot-and-mouth disease (in livestock) . \u00a0 We will be developing both general methods for spatial targeting of surveillance and reactive vaccination that are agnostic to system and working with in-country partners in DRC and India \u00a0 (and others) \u00a0 to tailor methods to specific human and veterinary public health applications. Scholars will also be members of the diverse community of infectious disease researchers at the \u202f Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics ( cidd.psu.edu ) \u00a0 and be expected to participate in Center activities.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Education and Experience \u00a0: The ideal candidate will have a Ph.D. in a relevant field (such as \u00a0 Ecology, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Epidemiology (human or veterinary), Public Health, Physics, Computer Science ), and a history of productivity. Experience with \u00a0 stochastic simulation and model fitting to temporal and spatial infectious disease data is preferred . \u00a0 Familiarity with R is preferred, though the successful candidate will have freedom to develop analyses and models in the language in which they are most proficient. Experience in communicating quantitative analyses to a non-technical audience and experience working with large collaborative groups is an advantage. \u202f It is likely that this position will involve international travel for extended periods (weeks).\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Additional Information: Applicants should submit a \u00a0 current CV; \u00a0 a \u00a0 personal statement describing why you are a qualified candidate for this position, including your short and long-term professional goals (1-2 pages) ; \u00a0 a research statement describing your research interests (1-2 pages); \u00a0 and contact information for three references. For more information, please email \u00a0 mferrari@psu.edu . \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000076160-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Biomolecular and Biomimetic Materials Laboratory in the Biomedical Engineering Department is seeking to hire two Postdoctoral Scholars to conduct independent research under the direction of Dr. Yong Wang. The lab recently achieved a breakthrough in hydrogel coating technology and is enthusiastic about applying this platform across a broad range of biomedical areas including diabetes treatment, cancer immunotherapy, single-cell analysis, and regenerative medicine. The lab invites applications for Postdoctoral Scholars with strong background in cell biology, diabetes treatment, immunology, single-cell analysis, and/or soft bioelectronics. Candidates with additional expertise in hydrogels and animal surgery are particularly encouraged to apply. This position offers an excellent opportunity to pursue impactful research in a collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. \u00a0 Education and Experience: The position requires a doctoral (Ph.D.) degree in Biomedical Engineering or related discipline by the time of appointment. Preference will be given to candidates with: Expertise cell biology, diabetes, immunology and/or animal surgery Strong ability to conduct independent research An outstanding academic record, demonstrated by at least two first-author publications in high-quality peer-reviewed journals over the past three years Candidate responsibilities include: Lead independent research projects Mentor and help guide graduate students in their research activities Contribute to technical manuscripts, grant proposals, and collaborative publications Application Requirements: Qualified candidates should apply online and include the following two documents: One-page research statement describing your research background and your interests/rationale for pursuing postdoctoral training in our group Complete curriculum vitae that includes a list of education, publications, work experience, and a list of three references For additional information contact Dr. Yong Wang, yxw30@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Neutrino-Physics_REQ_0000073465-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar- Neutrino Physics", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Eberly College of Science, Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill one \u00a0 Postdoctoral Researcher \u00a0 position in the area of \u00a0 Neutrino Physics . The successful candidate will have the opportunity to work on the \u00a0 Project 8 Neutrino Mass Experiment \u00a0 and on detector R&D.\u00a0 The Project 8 experiment seeks to determine the neutrino mass via the precise measurement of the electron energy in beta decays.\u00a0 We have developed and demonstrated the viability of a novel technique called Cyclotron Radiation Emission Spectroscopy (CRES), which allows single electron detection and characterization through the measurement of cyclotron radiation emitted by magnetically-trapped electrons produced by a gaseous radioactive source. We are currently working on the design of a large scale detector aimed at measuring the neutrino mass. In this position you will report to Dr. de Viveiros, and your responsibilities will include leading detector R&D at the Penn State laboratory; work in the design and construction of the next phase of the Project 8 experiment, with a focus on signal acquisition systems using resonant cavities for a large tritium detector; simulations and analysis of Project 8 detector signals; analysis of existing and future science data of the Project 8 experiment. Requirements include a Ph.D. in Physics, and the ideal candidate should have experience with experimental particle astrophysics, nuclear physics, particle physics or a related field. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to \u00a0 physicsapply@psu.edu \u00a0 indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. This is a term appointment funded for one year from date of hire, with possibility of renewal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Informal inquiries about this post may be made to: \u00a0 ldeviveiros@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Particle-Astrophysics---Wissel-Lab_REQ_0000075344-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Particle Astrophysics - Wissel Lab", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Particle Astrophysics group at Penn State is seeking a postdoctoral researcher to work with Prof. \u00a0 Stephanie \u00a0 Wissel on experimental searches for the highest energy neutrinos, multi-messenger, and particle astrophysics. If selected, you will explore the radio detection of ultra-high-energy neutrinos with the Hybrid Elevated Radio Observatory for Neutrinos (HERON). The candidate will play a leading role in building the phased array system for HERON and use it to search for tau neutrinos from a high-elevation mountain. The postdoctoral scholar will be expected to conduct research through instrument development, while also contributing to analysis, simulations, and/or monitoring. There will be opportunities for field campaigns to the site in Argentina. Previous experience in radio instrumentation and/or particle astrophysics is advantageous, but not required. \u00a0 In this position, you will report to Dr. \u00a0 Stephanie \u00a0 Wissel and your responsibilities will include: Contributing to UHE radio neutrino experiments Developing novel instrumentation and expanding the capabilities of the experiments of HERON Developing analysis techniques that calibrate the instruments and enhance their sensitivity to astrophysical and cosmogenic neutrinos, both\u00a0 Mentoring of junior scholars, including graduate and undergraduate students, and outreach to the public The candidate will be embedded in the Wissel Lab which includes researchers who also work on several experiments deployed around the world including in Antarctica and Greenland. Experiments such as the Askaryan Radio Array (ARA) and the future radio component of IceCube-Gen2 at the South Pole and the Radio Neutrino Observatory in Greenland (RNO-G) search for EeV-scale neutrinos with antennas deployed in polar ice. Balloon-borne experiments like the Payload for Ultra-high-Energy Observations (PUEO) and PBR search for neutrino interactions in the ice and upgoing tau neutrinos from a high altitude.\u00a0 Penn State is a vibrant and stimulating environment for particle and multi-messenger astrophysics with ample opportunities for collaboration and career development. The postdoctoral scholar will be embedded within the Particle Astrophysics group and the\u00a0 Center for Multi-Messenger Astrophysics (CMA) at the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos (IGC). Penn State is a leading institution in multi-messenger astrophysics. PSU hosts strong experimental groups UHE neutrinos as well as in LIGO, HELIX, Tigress, LZ, Project8, IceCube, GRAND, and Swift. Penn State also has leading theoretical groups in particle astrophysics, gravitation, and cosmology. \u00a0 A PhD in Physics, Astrophysics, or a related field is\u00a0required. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a CV, cover letter, and brief statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for two reference letters to be submitted through Academic Jobs Online . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Division-Head--Guidance-and-Control-Technology--FACULTY-_REQ_0000077051-2": {"title": "Division Head, Guidance and Control Technology (FACULTY)", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-08\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are seeking a Division Head for the Guidance and Control Technologies (GCT) Division of the Undersea Systems Office (USO) at the Penn State University Applied Research Laboratory (ARL). The GCT Division serves as a research center of excellence in autonomous guidance systems for undersea weapons and uncrewed underwater vehicles (UUVs), with a focus on advancements in sensing and tactical decision-making technologies as well as efficiently integrating and implementing these technologies in real-time systems. The GCT Division consists of four departments: Signal Processing, Tactical and Autonomous Processing, Applications Software, and Embedded Software. The Division Head will report directly to the Head of the Undersea Systems Office. The Division Head position may be filled as either a non-tenure Research Faculty or as a Research and Development Engineer commensurate with the candidate\u2019s education and experience.\u00a0 ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 You will: Lead a team of fifty scientists and engineers across four departments that are engaged in the research, development, implementation, integration and testing of complex undersea guidance systems, including: acoustic signal processing, tracking, classification, and data fusion; vehicle autonomy and tactics design, and embedded, real-time software implementation and testing Develop and maintain division-wide technical expertise in core disciplines, from early development through transition to sponsors Work closely with the Office leadership team to build and maintain trusted relationships with key sponsors and stakeholders, ensure the delivery of superior research products to our sponsors and develop and execute strategic initiatives Lead the development of proposals and projects that further our knowledge and expertise in autonomous guidance systems Provide project updates to sponsors and stakeholders, and lead the development of new business for potential sponsors Collaborate with engineers in technical areas across USO and ARL Oversee the planning, staffing, and execution of programs to ensure all divisional staff and faculty are appropriately and sufficiently tasked at all times Provide a mix of high-level project management, engineering oversight, and technical expertise related to acoustic signal processing, vehicle autonomy/tactics, and embedded real-time software Coordinate research and development activities between disciplines involving exploration, definition of scope, and identification of problems for investigation Recruit, develop, and retain extraordinary R&D engineering staff and faculty Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required Skills/Experience include: Principal Investigator, technical lead, or senior contributor on applied research efforts, with a record of securing and sustaining external funding in one or more of the following technical areas: underwater acoustics, signal processing, autonomous decision-making, and software development Leading individual and multi-disciplinary portfolios of research projects including developing technical concepts, writing winning proposals, staffing, conducting the research, managing budgets, and delivering high-quality results Leading a research organization, including planning and managing labor across projects, managing research budgets, and hiring, coaching, and mentoring employees Coordination across units to ensure rigorous execution, sound research and engineering practices, and the highest standards of technical work are maintained Superior written and oral communication skills DoD, Navy, and industrial research funding activities Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Secret level or higher; candidates may also be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility, if required Your work location will be fully on-site, located in State College, PA. Questions related to flexible work should be directed to the hiring manager during the interview process This position will require periodic travel to remote locations in support of testing as part of a small team of researchers, engineers, and technologists. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 All positions at ARL require candidates to\u00a0possess the ability to obtain a government security clearance; you will be notified during the interview process if this position is subject to a government background investigation.\u00a0 You must be a U.S. citizen to apply.\u00a0 Employment with the ARL will require successful completion of a pre-employment drug screen. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Professional-Track-Teaching-Faculty-Positions-in-Architectural-Engineering_REQ_0000076663-2": {"title": "Professional Track Teaching Faculty Positions in Architectural Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-06\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Architectural Engineering (AE) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for one or more full-time, professional-track (non-tenure-line) teaching faculty or Professor of Practice positions in architectural engineering. Priority will be given to faculty candidate(s) in the building construction, mechanical, and/or structural disciplines, with preference for integrative experience. Successful candidate(s) will teach undergraduate courses and, if qualified, graduate courses, advise students, and contribute to the department through service and committee work. Preference will be given to applicants with significant construction industry- and/or design-related U.S. experience, and to those who hold, or are expected to hold by the time of the appointment, a doctoral degree in architectural engineering, civil engineering, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field. Engineers with a master\u2019s degree and significant relevant industry experience are also invited to apply and will be considered for a Professor of Practice position. Candidates should be, or intend to be, licensed as a professional engineer (P.E.) or a certified construction manager (CCM), or similar qualification, and have demonstrated teaching experience through academic courses, professional conference presentations, or related activities. Please see https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21 for the definitions of academic ranks and promotion opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty at Penn State. Title and rank will be determined by education, experience, and other qualifications. To apply, please submit a single PDF file (5 MB max) that includes: a one-page cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a two-page statement of teaching, highlighting teaching philosophy, experience, and courses or topics they are interested in teaching, an executive summary of industry work performed, highlighting their roles, responsibilities, and contributions to the projects, or one technical publication, and contact information for three references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Application reviews will begin on April 30th, 2026, and continue until filled, with a preferred start date before fall 2026 classes. The position is housed within the Department of Architectural Engineering at Penn State. Widely acknowledged as one of the top architectural engineering programs in the world, the department's primary mission is to advance the built environment through the development of world-class architectural engineers and research. The vision of the Department of Architectural Engineering at Penn State is to lead the world in innovative education and research to achieve high-performing built environments. Our program emphasizes the scientific and engineering aspects of planning, designing, and constructing buildings, providing our architectural engineering graduates with outstanding education and research opportunities. The AE Department has a tradition of excellence in teaching and education for the built environment, integrating scholarly work with leading industry practice and a distinctive emphasis on systems integration. The AE Department has 19 full-time faculty, including three current professional-track faculty and three with joint appointments with other departments. The faculty span four major instructional areas: construction, lighting/electrical, mechanical, and structures, while emphasizing the systems-engineering integration of these technologies to achieve optimal building performance. The department is active in research and confers a full range of degrees, including the Ph.D. and M.S./M.Eng./M.A.E. at the graduate level and the 5-year ABET-accredited degree at the undergraduate level. We currently enroll 66 graduate students, 408 B.A.E. undergraduate students, including 109 integrated B.A.E./M.A.E. students (all included in the B.A.E. count). The Architectural Engineering Department has recently moved to a new facility, the Engineering Collaborative Research and Education Building (ECoRE), which opened in the fall of 2024. The building features cutting-edge teaching facilities and unique research laboratories, offering revolutionary opportunities for the AE Department, including laboratories focused on building materials science and the synthesis of novel, high-performance, and carbon-negative building components; indoor air quality and aerobiology; full-scale facade component testing under simulated thermal and solar conditions; construction robotics, automation, and virtual workforce training; immersive 3D building visualization and BIM and virtual twin innovation; multi-modal (HVAC, IAQ lighting/daylighting, acoustic) occupant-built environment interaction human factors research; building controls and simulation optimization; and lighting and illumination perception research and photometric testing, along with innovative teaching demonstrations and student studios and instructional venues. These are complemented by the shared resources offered in the adjacent Engineering Design and Innovation Building, opened in the summer of 2023, including a world-class strong wall/strong floor large-scale structural testing laboratory and first-rate student maker spaces. Penn State also benefits from a shared 40,000-core supercomputing cluster, a sophisticated and comprehensive instrumentation suite in the Materials Characterization Laboratory, and other university-wide institutes and laboratories. This position is for resident teaching, located in State College, Pennsylvania, which has been repeatedly voted as one of the most desirable and safest places to live in the United States. State College fosters a vibrant, diverse, and sustainable community. The region offers outstanding public schools, reasonable housing costs, a calendar of social and cultural events, and abundant outdoor recreation opportunities. State College is served by a regional airport and is within driving distance to Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, Washington DC, Baltimore, and New York City. Please see https://happyvalley.com and https://www.statecollegepa.u s for more information about State College and its surroundings. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Dickinson-Law-Carlisle/Part-Time---Penn-State-Dickinson-Law---Adjunct-Instructors_REQ_0000076937-3": {"title": "Part Time - Penn State Dickinson Law - Adjunct Instructors", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-02\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS PENN STATE DICKINSON LAW in Carlisle and University Park, PA invites exceptional candidates to apply for short-term, part-time\u202fadjunct \u202ffaculty appointments for the\u202f Fall \u00a0 2026 \u00a0 and Spring 2027 \u00a0 Semester s , in the areas of: \u00a0\u00a0 Advanced Torts \u00a0 Artificial Intelligence in Legal Practice (experiential course proposals on the use of AI \u00a0 welcome) \u00a0 Bankruptcy \u00a0 Business Entities I : Unincorporated Business Entities \u00a0 Business Entities II: Corporations \u00a0 Client Counseling (criminal and/or civil client focuses welcome) \u00a0 Conflict of Laws \u00a0 Construction Law \u00a0 Corporate Finance \u00a0 Elder Law \u00a0 Electronic Evidence \u00a0 Environmental Law \u00a0 Externship Sections \u00a0 Federal Courts \u00a0 First Amendment \u00a0 General Counsel & In-House Legal Department Experience \u00a0 Health Law & Policy \u00a0 Intellectual Property Licensing \u00a0 Legal Research \u00a0 Moot Court and Mock Trial Team Coaches \u00a0 Negotiation/Mediation \u00a0 Payment Systems \u00a0 Race, Racism & the Law \u00a0 Real Estate Transactions \u00a0 Real Estate Negotiation & Drafting \u00a0 Restorative Justice \u00a0 Sales \u00a0 State \u00a0 and Local Government Law \u00a0 Transactional Drafting \u00a0 Trauma Informed Lawyering \u00a0 Wills, Trusts & Estates \u00a0 Other areas as needs arise \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 In addition, \u00a0 Penn State \u00a0 Dickinson Law is always interested in increasing attorney or judge taught experiential learning courses .\u202fEmail the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Jeffrey A. Dodge, at\u202f jad6742@psu.edu \u202fshould you have a course idea that focuses on applied lawyering skills through simulations, writing, and/or research. \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 Requirements and Qualifications \u00a0 Applicants should have: \u00a0 A distinguished record of law practice in the subject matter or experience teaching the \u00a0 course \u00a0 subjects. \u00a0 Scholarly or professional publications \u00a0 to \u00a0 the relevant field of law. \u00a0 Participation and leadership in bar \u00a0 association \u00a0 or other professional organizations related to the subject matter. \u00a0 A J.D. degree from an ABA accredited law school. \u00a0 Superior academic credentials. \u00a0 \u202f \u00a0 While\u202f adjunct \u202ffaculty able to teach live in Carlisle or University Park are preferred, \u00a0 flexible work arrangements, such as remote or hybrid work opportunities, may be considered. To apply, submit a letter of interest and curriculum vitae or resume through the\u202f Penn State Careers Site .\u202f R eview of applicants will begin \u00a0 immediately \u00a0 and continue until all vacancies are filled. \u202f To learn more about Dickinson Law visit \u00a0 our \u202f website . \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Researcher---High-Energy-Transient-Astronomy_REQ_0000068039-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Researchers - Time Domain and Multi-Messenger Astrophysics", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-01\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Astronomy and Astrophysics at Penn State invites applicants for two Postdoctoral Researcher positions to work with Professor Jimmy DeLaunay and collaborators. The successful applicants will work with the Fermi GBM and Swift-BAT GUANO teams to search for hard X-ray to gamma-ray transients in real-time as well as archivally over the decades of Fermi\u2019s and Swift\u2019s lifetime. Additionally, the successful applicants will perform multi-messenger and transient population studies. Research duties will involve improving transient search pipelines, analysis of large quantities of data, transient classification, detailed studies of newly discovered, interesting transients, and publication of scientific results.\u00a0 Penn State is home to the Swift Mission Operation Center and has a significant community of researchers who study high-energy transients. Penn State is also home to the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos and its Center for Multimessenger Astrophysics , which includes members of several experiments, such as LIGO, the IceCube Neutrino Observatory, and the HAWC TeV gamma-ray detector. Education and Experience A Ph.D. in Astronomy, Physics, or a related field is required. Experience with HPC systems, machine learning, and GRB monitor data analysis would be an advantage.\u00a0 Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, statement of research interests, a CV, and a list of publications. In addition, please arrange for three professional reference letters to be sent to jjd330@psu.edu . Questions regarding the application process can be directed to Professor Jimmy DeLaunay at jjd330@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin May 8, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by May 7th will receive full consideration. The expected start date is August 2026, but is negotiable. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---Nursing---Adjunct-Clinical-Instructor_REQ_0000076936-1": {"title": "Part Time - Nursing - Adjunct Clinical Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-27\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for Adjunct Clinical Instructor openings in the Bachelor of Science in Nursing program at our University Park, PA campus for the 2026 to 2027 Academic Year .\u00a0 Job Duties Adjunct instructors normally teach one to two clinical sections per semester as needed. Requirements and Qualifications A Master\u2019s degree in Nursing, or higher. A current Pennsylvania RN license. \u00a0 Recent clinical experience preferred. To be considered for this opening, applications must be submitted electronically and include: A letter of application detailing relevant qualifications for this job; and A curriculum vitae. Candidates should\u00a0be prepared to provide the names, titles, and contact information (telephone, email, and mailing address) of three (3) professional references, if requested. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as the need arises . This is a one semester, non-tenure track appointment with the possibility of reappointment. For more details about the college, please visit the Nese College of Nursing website . For questions about the job requirements please email Dr. Maria Yoder at mdy5032@psu.edu .\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000075266-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-19\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mathematics in Penn State's Eberly College of Science invites applications for Postdoctoral Scholars through the Center for Computational Mathematics and Applications (CCMA). Successful candidates will engage in research in all or any of the areas of scientific computing, data science, and quantum information science. Appointed candidates will collaborate closely with CCMA faculty on cutting-edge research projects involving design, analysis and implementation of advanced numerical methods and algorithms in interdisciplinary applications. The position includes the possibility of an annual 1-1 teaching load. Education and Experience: Applicants must have completed a Ph.D. in mathematics, applied mathematics, or a closely related field such as statistics, computer science, physics, or\u00a0engineering by the start date of employment. Strong expertise in one or more of the fields of scientific computing, data science, and quantum computing\u00a0accompanied by strong programming skills are essential. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---Adjunct-Lecturer---Journalism_REQ_0000076469-2": {"title": "Part Time - Adjunct Lecturer - Journalism", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-11\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Donald P. Bellisario College of Communications seeks to hire adjunct instructors in Journalism for Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters. These appointments will be part-time, non-tenure track appointments without benefits and no guarantee of renewal. Courses include but are not limited to skills-based courses in print/digital, broadcast, and photojournalism. The selected candidates should have professional experience. Positions can require a Bachelor's degree, Master's degree or Ph.D. Applicants should apply by submitting a short letter of interest with their qualifications, current Curriculum Vita (CV) and contact information with at least three references. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as needed. For information on the Donald P. Bellisario College of Communications and the academic programs, please visit http://bellisario.psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Emerging-Disparities-in-Population-Health_REQ_0000074762-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Emerging Disparities in Population Health", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Collaborative on Population Aging Disparities and the Population Research Institute at The Pennsylvania State University anticipates an opening for a Postdoctoral Scholar in Emerging Disparities in Population He alth , starting on or around July 1, 2026 , contingent on funding availability. The Postdoctoral Scholar will devote time to independent research, collaborations with faculty mentors, and mentored training and professionalization. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in a social science field such as sociology, demography, gerontology, human development and family studies, anthropology, economics, public policy, criminology, biobehavioral health, geography, or related fields using social science approaches (e.g., epidemiology) by the start date, and have training and research experience in substantive demographic topics or demographic methods, especially as they are relevant to aging and population health disparities. Additionally, applicants must demonstrate interest and capacity for independent research, evidence or clear plans for an emerging publication record, have outstanding writing and communication skills, and be able to work effectively on a team. Screening of applications will begin on February 17, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Application Materials: Applicants are requested to submit the following: A letter of application A research statement describing: research interests and career plan planned research during the postdoctoral period proposed postdoctoral faculty mentor(s) at Penn State selected from the following list: https://demography.psu.edu/faculty-by-discipline/ A Curriculum Vitae. Two examples of written work (examples include publications, articles in review, or dissertation chapters). List of 3 references (name, current position title, e-mail address).\u00a0 System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Candidates should direct questions to Dr. Ashton Verdery ( amv5430@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-Sentencing-Research-and-Policy_REQ_0000074514-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Sentencing Research and Policy", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Criminal Justice Research Center (CJRC) and Department of Sociology and Criminology at The Pennsylvania State University invite applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar position to begin July 1, 2026, with flexibility. The successful applicant will collaborate with the Pennsylvania Commission on Sentencing (PCS) \u00a0on research related to sentencing guidelines, risk and needs assessment (development and validation of tools), pre-trial release, parole, and related topics. A Ph.D. in criminal justice, criminology, sociology, economics, public policy, or a related field is required at time of appointment. Preference will be given to candidates with advanced training in statistics, experience working with large administrative datasets, and/or an exemplary interest in applied research, and to those with research interests in courts or sentencing and with a knowledge of, or practical experience with, program evaluation. Key responsibilities of the Postdoctoral Scholar will include collaborating with the Pennsylvania Commission on Sentencing (Commission) staff to address legislative mandates; empirically assessing sentencing policy and/or conducting program evaluations (e.g., examining the effectiveness of state and county sentencing programs); working closely with criminal justice stakeholders; assisting in data collection and data management; preparing grant proposals, manuscripts, and conference presentations; and participating in graduate student mentoring. In addition to Commission-specific projects, the scholar will have flexibility to conduct independent research related to sentencing, access to sentencing commission data and data from other criminal justice partners (e.g., Department of Corrections; Administrative Office of the Pennsylvania Courts; local probation offices), and opportunities for research collaboration with Penn State faculty. The Postdoctoral Scholar position is fully funded by the Pennsylvania Commission on Sentencing ( https://pcs.la.psu.edu ). The Commission on Sentencing is a legislative agency responsible for advancing effective, humane, and rational policies that promote fairer and more uniform decisions at sentencing, resentencing, and parole. The Commission maintains a research and data analysis unit that undertakes research and evaluations of the effectiveness of various criminal justice programs and policies, conducts impact analyses, and serves as a clearinghouse and information center for the collection, preparation, and dissemination of information on Commonwealth sentencing, resentencing, and parole practices. The Commission is affiliated with the Department of Sociology and Criminology at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park Campus) and maintains an active research partnership with the CJRC. The CJRC ( https://justicecenter.la.psu.edu ) has an outstanding portfolio of faculty affiliates, seed funding opportunities, and externally funded ongoing research projects. The Department of Sociology and Criminology is ranked among the top in the nation and provides graduate and undergraduate programs focused specifically on crime and the criminal justice system. Interested candidates must submit an online application and should include a letter of interest and CV. If selected as a finalist for the position, recommendation letters will be requested. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Full-or-Associate-Professor-in-Infectious-Disease-Modeling_REQ_0000070169-1": {"title": "Full or Associate Professor in Infectious Disease Modeling", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a Full or Associate Professor in Infectious Disease Modeling to support the mission of the Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics ( http://cidd.psu.edu/ ) of the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences.\u00a0This is a cross-University search, and the position will be appointed in a department and College that is appropriate for the research and teaching program of the candidate. \u00a0 The Penn State Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics (CIDD) is one of the largest and most active infectious disease research centers in the U.S. The center was established in 2003 to foster transformative, cross-college interdisciplinary research in the ecology and evolution of infectious disease in human, animal, and plant hosts.\u00a0The center includes more than 70 faculty from across nine colleges.\u00a0The center is part of the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences, which exists to strengthen interdisciplinary life science research and graduate education across the University. Penn State consistently ranks among the nation\u2019s top 25 public research universities, with fiscal year 2024 research expenditures exceeding $1.3 billion. Dynamic models of pathogen/parasite transmission, interactions with hosts, and evolution have been central to the CIDD mission and provide a critical link between faculty expertise from the bench-top to applications in health, agriculture, and conservation. The scope of data and systems to measure, interpret, forecast, and intervene in infectious disease systems has grown dramatically. CIDD is committed to leading cutting-edge modeling and computational approaches to leverage the breadth and depth of these novel data sources. We are seeking new faculty with a focus and established scholarship in infectious disease modeling to align with CIDD\u2019s goals to maintain its international leadership in the ecology and evolution of infectious disease.\u00a0We specifically seek candidates who have led multidisciplinary projects to combine modeling and computational tools with large time series, epidemiological, or genomic data sets to address fundamental questions in pathogen or parasite persistence, evolution, and control. Successful candidates are expected to have an established track record of successful extramural funding, published results from multidisciplinary research projects, and evidence of leadership of multidisciplinary scientific teams. They will be expected to contribute to the Center leadership through participation on the Executive Committee and development of research, training, and/or outreach initiatives. The Department and College tenure home is open for negotiation based on research interests and could be in one or more of the following colleges: College of Agricultural Sciences, College of Engineering, College of Health and Human Development, College of Liberal Arts, College of Medicine, and the Eberly College of Science. There is an expectation that the candidate will join the faculty of one of the Huck Institute\u2019s six Interdisciplinary Graduate Degree Programs.\u00a0 In addition to establishing a rigorous externally funded research program in any aspect of infectious disease at Penn State, duties also include: Promote a culture of excellence in infectious disease research, teaching, and outreach across the Penn State system; Promote Penn State as a global leader in interdisciplinary infectious disease research through novel collaborations that integrate existing CIDD strengths; Lead the growth of the CIDD through strategic initiatives and development of collaborative, interdisciplinary research teams; Support the training of next generation of infectious disease researchers via classroom and experiential learning opportunities; Participate in strategic planning to ensure financial sustainability of the Penn State CIDD; Participate in the CIDD Executive Committee to develop and execute a strategic vision and approaches for the center; Engage current Penn State faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and student members of the CIDD to shape its future; Actively engage in mentorship of early career faculty hired in association with the Center; and Support community development and engagement at the student, staff, postdoctoral and faculty levels. A PhD in any infectious disease-related field is required. The applicant should have an academic track record commensurate with the level of Full Professor with tenure, although exceptional applications at the Associate level will be considered. The successful applicant will join faculty members with complementary, interdisciplinary research interests, and have access to excellent core facilities https://www.huck.psu.edu/core-facilities . Please submit a cover letter, CV, Research Statement, Teaching Statement, and the names and contact information for three references. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. For more information about the position, please contact Christina Grozinger, Director of the Huck Institutes or Matthew Ferrari, Director of the Penn State Center for Infectious Disease Dynamics. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Clinical-Professor-of-Business-Communication_REQ_0000075955-2": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Clinical Professor of Business Communication", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor position beginning in Fall 2026. QUALIFICATIONS The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching courses in business communication. \u00a0In addition to instruction, the individual will support the teaching mission of the Department through regular office hours, student counseling and advising, involvement in student extra-curricular activities, and academic administration. Typical qualifications include a Ph.D. in communication or related areas. The preferred candidate will have relevant industry and communication experience. The contract structure, including term, salary, and benefits, will be competitive and commensurate with the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS Candidates should apply directly online through the Penn State site and submit the following documents as PDF files: Curriculum vitae (CV) Cover letter Teaching statement and evaluations (if applicable) Names and contact information of at least three references ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT AND SMEAL Information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at www.smeal.psu.edu/accounting . ABOUT PENN STATE The Pennsylvania State University is a land-grant institution and one of the top 30 research universities in the United States, ranking among the top 15 public institutions. The University Park Campus is located in State College, a vibrant university town in central Pennsylvania, offering excellent schools and outstanding recreational and cultural activities. The campus is within a 3-4 hour drive to major metropolitan areas, including Washington, DC, Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City, and Pittsburgh. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Full-Research-Professor_REQ_0000075871-2": {"title": "Associate/Full Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mathematics invites applications for a research professor with strong research potential in number theory. This is a non tenure-track, 36-week appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Research Professor. A demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching is expected, and teaching responsibilities may be part of the appointment. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in mathematics or closely related field. Candidates from all areas of math will be considered. Applicants are required to complete the Penn State application and also submit materials through Mathjobs ( https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28190 ). A complete application includes the following: Curriculum Vitae Publication List Research Statement Teaching Statement At least three letters of reference submitted with your Mathjobs.org application, one of which should address the candidate's teaching abilities in detail. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Mechanical-Engineer---FACULTY_REQ_0000075788-2": {"title": "Mechanical Engineer - FACULTY", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-24\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are searching for talented and motivated Mechanical Engineers to join the High Performance Materials and Processing Department (HPMP) of the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. We are seeking individuals with knowledge across a range of competencies including Design and Analysis, Model and Simulation, Process Development and Optimization, and Characterization and Testing. The successful candidate will support research and development of new materials, innovative material system designs, and novel fabrication and testing methods covering a wide range of material systems including ceramics, metallics, and ceramic/metal matrix composites. ARL-Penn State has a decades long reputation of excellence and demonstrated history of developing systems and technologies currently used by the US Navy and industry. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Use accepted methods and techniques to assist with the design, development, implementation, and analysis of technical engineering products, systems, and subsystems Contribute data/findings for use in technical reports, documents, or oral/written presentations Interact in a collaborative manner with other team members, engineers, and scientists to accomplish organizational goals; may provide ideas to improve efficiency at group. Program management of multi-year research programs, tracking deliverables, milestones, and resource allocation Present research, designs, and findings internally to engineers and scientists as well as externally to sponsors and research partners Aid in the design, fabrication, and testing of advanced material systems across ceramics, metals, and ceramic/metal matrix composites; work spans design and analysis, process development and optimization, and characterization and testing, with opportunities to contribute from concept through prototype and validation Additional responsibilities for higher level position include: Ability to manage a laboratory space Direct work of lower-level staff and undergraduate students Investigate and evaluate applicability of scientific theories and engineering principles in the development and improvement of engineering systems Initiate or contribute data/analysis/design for technical reports, documents, proposals, or oral/written presentations Author/co-author papers, proposals, presentations, and reports Non-tenure faculty rank will be commensurate with education level and experience. Required skills/experience areas include: 5+ years of understanding basic engineering principles and applying them to real-world problems Ability to facilitate the overall design process including conception, analysis, building, and testing of mechanical systems Ability to work independently and in an interdisciplinary team environment Have excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills\u00a0 Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Secret level or higher and may be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility, if required Preferred skills/experience areas include: Prior work in hypersonics, aerospace, and propulsion technologies Ceramic and metallurgical engineering for high temperature environments Defense manufacturing technology development Prototyping, hardware manufacturing, and rapid design iteration NX and Solidworks Abaqus, COMSOL, Ansys, and Matlab Mechanical/Electrical design and troubleshooting Past success presenting work to sponsors and technical audiences Materials characterization using techniques including optical microscopy (OM), scanning electron microscopy (SEM), energy dispersive spectroscopy (EDS), X-ray diffraction (XRD), and optical profilometry Working knowledge of vacuum system pumps, controls, electrical requirements, design, and integration of components Preferred degrees could include: Mechanical Engineer, Aerospace engineering, Process Engineering, and Material Science Engineering Your working location will be fully on-site, located in State College, PA. Questions related to flexible work should be directed to the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will require periodic travel to remote locations in support of testing as part of a small team of researchers, engineers, and technologists. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 All positions at ARL require candidates to\u00a0possess the ability to obtain a government security clearance; you will be notified during the interview process if this position is subject to a government background investigation.\u00a0 You must be a U.S. citizen to apply.\u00a0 Employment with the ARL will require successful completion of a pre-employment drug screen. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Experimental-Condensed-Matter-and-Materials-Physics_REQ_0000075617-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Experimental Condensed Matter and Materials Physics", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill a postdoc position in the areas of superconducting hybrid devices involving superconductors with graphene and topological thin film materials. The successful candidate will lead in thin film synthesis, device fabrication, and transport measurement of devices involving superconductors interfaced with graphene, topological materials and other 2D systems. The project requires fabrication of superconducting thin films using a HPCVD process, nanofabrication, and low temperature and high magnetic field measurements. The ideal candidate should have very good knowledge and experience in the areas of topological superconductivity, quantum materials, and superconducting devices. Technical experience in the areas of epitaxial growth of thin films using CVD and related technique is preferred. Other knowledge of pulsed-laser deposition, sputtering deposition, photo- and electron beam lithography, and transport and superconductivity measurements at low temperatures are also appreciated. Requirements include a Ph.D. in Physics, materials or device physics. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV, and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to physicsapply@psu.edu indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Post-Doctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000075558-1": {"title": "Post-Doctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University's Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering seeks a Postdoctoral Scholar to participate in a multi-disciplinary, multi-investigator NSF-funded research project. The overarching aim of this project is in the development of new knowledge and a new framework to facilitate the optimal design and life-long adaptation of civil infrastructure systems that rigorously accounts for diverse uncertainties in the life-cycle demands, system's state, and decision criteria. This project thus aims to offer an engineering response to infrastructure adaptation, mitigating the impact of evolving hazards on the built environment and society, and fundamentally transforming the basis for which infrastructure is designed, maintained, and adapted, to ensure a prosperous and sustainable future. We seek a highly motivated and knowledgeable individual eager to expand their expertise while contributing to the management and execution of research as well as mentoring of graduate students. The required qualifications are: PhD degree in mathematics, science, engineering, or a related field by the start date. Extensive experience in one or more of the following areas: probabilistic methods, risk and reliability, stochastic control processes, dynamic programing, deep reinforcement learning. Strong track record in scientific contributions supported by peer-reviewed publications. Strong programming skills including proficiency with Python and Matlab. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Knowledge of hydraulics and stochastics in hydraulics, though not required, will be beneficial and considered favorably. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. To apply, please submit a single PDF file (5MB max) that includes: a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, and the contact information for two professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Dr. Gordon Warn at gpw1@psu.edu \u00a0or\u00a0+1-814-863-2786. The College of Engineering at Penn State prepares current and future generations for impactful careers as practicing engineers, managers, researchers, educators, and community leaders through highly ranked residential and online programs. We provide innovative educational experiences and supportive programs designed to foster a more welcoming community. In collaboration with industry, non-profit organizations, governmental agencies, and other academic institutions and partners, our faculty lead research initiatives across all areas of engineering that create jobs, fuel economic growth, inform policy, solve global problems, and positively impact humanity. This position is located in State College, Pennsylvania, which has been repeatedly voted as one of the most desirable and safest places to live in the United States. State College fosters a vibrant, diverse, and sustainable community. The region hosts outstanding public schools, reasonable housing costs, a calendar of social and cultural events, and abundant outdoor recreation opportunities. State College is served by a regional airport and is within driving distance to Philadelphia, Pittsburgh, Washington DC, Baltimore, and New York City. Please see\u00a0 https://www.statecollegepa.us/ \u00a0for more information.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Instructor-in-Supply-Chain-Management-and-Information-Systems_REQ_0000075267-2": {"title": "Instructor in Supply Chain Management and Information Systems", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-13\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The SCIS Department of the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) invites applications for two instructor positions in Supply Chain and Information Systems SCIS) for a Fall 2026 start date. Salary is competitive. Candidates must have a master\u2019s degree in data analytics, information systems, supply chain management, or related field. A strong commitment to teaching excellence is expected. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. The SCIS Department comprises a vibrant, research-active faculty with research and teaching interests that traverse the end-to-end supply chain and includes information systems, data analytics, and business statistics. The department offers degree programs in supply chain management, management information systems, and business analytics. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate expertise and teach courses in business analytics, statistics, and Excel that would complement the faculty with high-quality teaching in student-centered and collaborative learning environments. Candidates will be expected to primarily teach undergraduate level courses and engage in service to support curriculum, programs and student experiences. The Smeal College of Business offers a collegial working environment and excellent campus facilities. It has the Center for Supply Chain Research\u00ae ( www.smeal.psu.edu/cscr ) which advances cutting-edge research and outreach in supply chain management. The SCIS Department ( www.smeal.psu.edu/scis ) also has strong connections with the business community through various research centers that provide opportunities to interface with faculty across various disciplines within Smeal and across Penn State. For more information, please visit www.smeal.psu.edu/research-centers . Review of applications will begin approximately February 27, 2026, and will continue until the position(s) are filled. For further information, please contact Autumn Knepp at adh5253@psu.edu . Applicants should upload a letter of intent, a statement of teaching philosophy, and a CV or resume. Contact information for three references should be provided. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000072094-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-03\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The \u00a0Department of Mathematics \u00a0in Penn State's\u00a0 Eberly College of Science \u00a0is seeking a\u00a0 Postdoctoral Scholar \u00a0beginning August 2026. The successful candidate will work with Professor John Harlim and his collaborators, Yan Li in the Electrical Engineering department, and Daning Huang in the Aerospace Engineering department in the area of Scientific Machine Learning. The project is to develop computationally\u00a0efficient reduced-order dynamical systems on\u00a0graph with modern power grid systems as an application.\u00a0\u00a0 Education and Experience: Applicants must have recently completed a Ph.D. and have exceptional research potential. Teaching may be required. \u00a0 Qualified candidates are expected to have a background in scientific machine learning,\u00a0numerical analysis, and dynamical systems. Preference will be given to candidates that are proficient with graph neural networks and other scientific machine learning tools.\u00a0 Additional Information: Applicants must complete the Penn State application and must also submit an application through Mathjobs.org ( https://www.mathjobs.org/ ) with the following materials for the application to be complete:\u00a0 Cover letter\u00a0 Curriculum Vitae\u202f\u00a0 Teaching Statement\u00a0 Research Statement\u00a0 Publications List\u00a0 At least three reference letters uploaded to Mathjobs.org with your application (one letter must address in detail the candidate\u2019s abilities as a teacher.) Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/CGNE-Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000075271-1": {"title": "CGNE Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-29\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS CGNE Postdoctoral Scholar: Penn State\u2019s Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing seeks applicants for the Tressa Nese and Helen Diskevich Center of Geriatric Nursing Excellence\u2019s (CGNE) Postdoctoral Fellowship. Preference will be given to applicants with research interests related to topics of aging and geriatrics including age-friendly care, care of persons living with dementia, well-being and efficacy of care partners, cognitive and physical functioning, delirium, stigma related to aging and dementia, workforce preparation and support, technological innovations, and person-centered care, as well as other gerontological \u00a0topics aligned with the CGNE mission and research portfolios of faculty in the Center. Successful fellowship candidates will be paired with faculty mentors based on a shared area of focus and interest. Fellows will work directly on research projects of CGNE-affiliated faculty, pursue independent research activities in line with their developing program of research, and engage in professional development opportunities across Penn State. All fellows are funded for one year with the possibility of renewal for a second-year contingent on progress in achieving first-year goals and funding availability. For more information about CGNE, please visit https://www.nursing.psu.edu/cgne/.\u00a0 At this website, you will find information about our vision, mission, and faculty, as well as links to our annual report.\u00a0 Penn State\u2019s Nese College of Nursing is one of the largest educators of pre-licensure students in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, with over 2000 undergraduate and graduate students on 13 campuses. Our College is positioned to lead the next generation of nurses and nurse scientists while enhancing the health of all people through quality care and education . Application Open Date: January 27, 2026 Applications will be reviewed and interviews completed on a rolling basis until the April deadline. Application End Date: April 15, 2026 Expected Hire/Start Date: July I, 2026 preferred but negotiable. Eligibility: PhD prepared Nurses (or related field) within two years of degree completion preferred. Demonstrated commitment to scholarship in aging, geriatrics and/or gerontology. Applicant's area of interest must be aligned with at least one faculty mentor in the Center. ( https://www.nursing.psu.edu/cgne/areas-of-expertise/ ) Evidence of scholarly productivity including research-based publications and excellent dissemination skills (oral and written).\u00a0 Candidates for this position should demonstrate strong motivation to develop an independent research career/ portfolio. Fellowships open to eligible U.S. citizens and international applicants. Applicants who are not United States citizens/residents must be eligible for either H-1B or J-1 Visa and need to pursue this on their own behalf, in association with university resources if needed. Sponsorship is contingent upon federal requirements and associated costs. Applicants from groups underrepresented in the nursing profession are encouraged to apply. Benefits Salary commensurate with background and experience. Health Insurance benefits: Will follow Penn State Policy. Provision of mentorship to develop independent scholarship and promote robust research career trajectory. Funding for conference registration and travel support and/or professional development opportunities. Opportunity to collaborate with nationally and internationally recognized faculty in aging. Working with funded researchers with access to data sets involving older adults across the care continuum. Ability to apply for CGNE project funding support. Responsibilities: The postdoctoral fellow will: Co-create an Individual Development Plan (IDP) with their primary mentor to identify goals, needed training/course work, timeline, outcomes, and planned engagement with other centers/researchers. Refine career goals and grant development skills. Extend their research agenda through the writing and submission of early-stage career grant applications, manuscripts, and presentations. Participate in the primary mentor\u2019s current research initiatives consistent with the IDP. Further develop teaching and mentoring skills. Expand research skills, including methodologic expertise. Contribute to the Nese College of Nursing and the CGNE within their area of expertise. Application Requirements : Phase I: Applicants must begin process via Penn State recruitment site and include the following: Online application Cover Letter which includes prior research experience, area of focus, Penn State Nese CON faculty member to serve as potential primary mentor including alignment with their program of research; goals for postdoctoral training and career, highlights of current and interest in expanding or learning new research skills, potential contributions to research team, and how interests/work would align with CGNE and CON. Current CV with contact information Phase II: After the interview with CGNE search committee, submit the following to Janice Whitaker @ jmw5969@psu.edu 1-2 page/s research statement including goals for program of research over the next 5 years. Copy of 1-2 published articles 3 Letters of recommendation. One of these letters must be from the identified primary mentor at Penn State and include justification for the proposed fellowship. At least one letter should be from a member of the applicant\u2019s dissertation committee. Letters should be sent via email directly from the and should describe the applicant\u2019s scholarly abilities, areas for growth and future potential. Questions related to the postdoctoral fellowship opportunity should be directed to: Donna Marie Fick, PhD, RN, GCNS-BC, FGSA, FAAN Elouise Ross Eberly Endowed Professor \u00a0 Director, Tressa Nese and Helen Diskevich Center of Geriatric Nursing Excellence Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing, Penn State University dmf21@psu.edu Phase I application materials must be submitted to Penn State recruitment site. Candidates will be notified if they are selected for an interview with the search committee. \u00a0 After the interview, Phase II application requirements should be emailed to the CGNE Administrator (as below). Janice Whitaker,\u00a0M.Ed., B.S.N., RN, CDP CGNE Administrator, Education Program Manager, and Community Liaison Tressa Nese and Helen Diskevich Center of Geriatric Nursing Excellence Penn State Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing The Pennsylvania State University jmw5969@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-position-in-Computational-Biology-and-Neuroscience_REQ_0000074651-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Genetics and Neuroscience", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-27\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS A postdoctoral position is available immediately in the Laboratory of Dr. Santhosh Girirajan in the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at Penn State to study the genetic and neural mechanisms underlying neurodevelopmental disorders using mouse models. The research program in the Girirajan laboratory focuses on integrating family-based genetic studies with quantitative functional methodologies to understand how genes and genetic interactions contribute to phenotypes in neurodevelopmental disorders. The postdoctoral scholar will design and implement behavioral and neurodevelopmental assays, linking functional outcomes to genetic perturbations in mouse models. The position provides the opportunity to work at the interface of genetics, mouse behavior, and molecular neuroscience, with additional training in genomics and computational approaches. Education and Experience Applicants should hold a PhD in neuroscience, genetics, psychology, biology, or a related field, with demonstrated expertise in functional studies in mouse models and research relevant to neurodevelopmental or neuropsychiatric disorders. Required qualifications include strong training in genetics, neuroscience, and quantitative data analysis. Programming experience (e.g., R, Python, or related languages) is preferred but not required. Applicants should also be willing to mentor undergraduate and graduate students, as the research program emphasizes collaborative, team-based science. Application Materials Interested applicants should submit a cover letter detailing their research interests, CV, and a list of referees. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor--Experimental-Condensed-Matter---Materials-Physics_REQ_0000074490-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor -Experimental Condensed Matter & Materials Physics", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill a research assistant professor position in the areas of superconducting hybrid devices involving superconductors with graphene and other 2D materials. The successful candidate will lead in thin film growth, device fabrication, and transport measurements of devices involving superconductors interfaced with graphene, topological materials and other 2D materials. The project involves fabrication of superconducting thin films using a HPCVD process, nanofabrication, and low temperature and high magnetic field measurement.\u00a0 The ideal candidate should have very good knowledge and experience in the areas in superconductivity, quantum materials, and superconducting devices. Technical experience in the areas of epitaxial growth of thin films using CVD and related technique is preferred. Knowledge and experience on pulsed-laser deposition, sputtering, photo- and electron beam lithography, and measurements at low temperature and high magnetic fields are desired.\u00a0 Requirements include a Ph.D. in Physics, materials or device physics. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to qil1@psu.edu \u00a0indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Department-of-Physics---Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000065711-2": {"title": "Department of Physics - Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a postdoctoral scholar position in Condensed Matter Physics. The successful candidate will work with Prof. Zhiqiang Mao on a quantum materials research program focused on the discovery and synthesis of novel quantum materials, including magnetic topological materials and multiferroics. The project involves bulk single-crystal growth, characterization, and measurements of magnetic, dielectric, ferroelectric, and transport properties. Candidates should have a Ph.D. in physics or a related field, with experience in single-crystal growth and characterization preferred. Applicants must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a statement of research interests electronically. Additionally, three reference letters should be sent to zim1@psu.edu . This is a term appointment funded for one year from date of hire with possibility of renewal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging\u00a0that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the\u00a0educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the\u00a0community thrive.\u00a0 We value belonging as a core strength and an\u00a0essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service\u00a0mission. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Open-rank-Faculty-Position-in-Quantitative-Methods--Department-of-Human-Development-and-Family-Studies_REQ_0000074379-1": {"title": "Open-rank Faculty Position in Quantitative Methods, Department of Human Development and Family Studies", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Penn State Department of Human Development and Family Studies , located in the College of Health and Human Development , is actively seeking applications for an open-rank, tenure-track or tenured faculty position in quantitative developmental and family systems methods. Competitive candidates will have expertise in measurement, latent variable modeling, or novel data integration approaches. Particular attention will be given to applicants whose major area(s) of research coincides with one of the followings: The development of novel methods to strengthen the measurement and analysis of multi-system, multi-scale processes (e.g., models of within-person change and variability in human development and family processes across the lifespan; multilevel methods that integrate individual and community differences across contexts) Methods for large data sets Latent variable modeling Computational models of psychological processes, health decision processes, and human dynamics The use of advanced longitudinal methodologies to analyze intensive data streams, including mobile sensor data, social media, and ecological momentary assessment data The use of models as measurement instruments The selected candidate will contribute to advancing scholarship in quantitative methodology and data science in social and behavioral sciences within the Department, College, and University. Mid-career or senior candidates should also address their potential to serve in a leadership capacity in these areas.\u00a0Responsibilities also include teaching undergraduate and graduate level courses as well as directing theses/dissertations. Key Qualifications of the Candidate: The successful candidate at each rank will have an earned doctorate in quantitative, developmental, behavioral, social science, or related field prior to beginning at Penn State. The candidate must have a clear program of research, a strong publication record, and evidence of or potential for receiving extramural funding, commensurate with rank. The candidate must show evidence of appropriate teaching and mentorship, commensurate with rank. Human Development and Family Studies (HDFS) Rated #1 in a recent survey of HDFS doctoral programs in North America, Penn State HDFS administers graduate, undergraduate, and research programs in its core, signature areas of individual development, family science, prevention/intervention, and developmental methods. HDFS is a dynamic, multidisciplinary and collaborative department, committed to excellence, innovation and impact in understanding and improving the lives of individuals and families in diverse contexts. The successful faculty member will have opportunities to collaborate with the Department\u2019s superb group of quantitative/developmental ( QuantDev ) research methodologists with expertise in intensive longitudinal data analysis and within-person/within-family methods that assess, analyze, and interpret daily and real-time information about ongoing individual-environment interactions. Centers and training grants in the College of Health and Human Development and Penn State research institutes The College of Health and Human Development provides excellent opportunities for research collaboration, mentoring, and scholarship. The College houses the Edna Bennett Pierce Prevention Research Center ( https://www.prevention.psu.edu / ), the Center for Healthy Aging ( https://healthyaging.psu.edu/), the Center for Childhood Obesity ( https://hhd.psu.edu/ccor ), and the NICHD-funded P50 Capstone Center ( t he Translational Center for Child Maltreatment Studies), In addition, the College is home to three T32 training grants, including the NICHD-funded T32 Fellowship Training Program in Child Maltreatment Science , the NIA-funded T32 Pathways to Healthy Aging training program , and the NIDA-funded Prevention and Methods Training program . In addition, HDFS has extensive links with other key College and University Centers of Excellence, networks, and Institutes that provide research infrastructure and extensive collaboration opportunities. These include the Child Study Center ( https://csc.la.psu.edu/ ), the Population Research Institute ( http://www.pop.psu.edu ), the Penn State Addiction Center for Translation ( https://research.med.psu.edu/addiction/ ), Penn State\u2019s Administrative Data Accelerator http://www.accelerator.psu.edu , and the Social, Life and Engineering Sciences Imaging Center https://www.imaging.psu.edu . The successful faculty hire will also have access to research infrastructure in Penn State\u2019s cross-university research institutes, including the Social Science Research Institute https://ssri.psu.edu/ , the Penn State Clinical and Translational Science Institute http://ctsi.psu.edu/ , the Huck Institutes of Life Sciences https://www.huck.psu.edu/ , the Institute for Computational and Data Science https://www.icds.psu.edu /, the Penn State Cancer Institute https://cancer.psu.edu / , and the Penn State Neuroscience Institute https://hmc.pennstatehealth.org/neuroscience-institute . About Penn State: Penn State is a public, land-grant, research-intensive university with campuses and facilities throughout Pennsylvania. Founded in 1855, the university has a threefold mission of teaching, research, and public service. Its instructional mission includes undergraduate, graduate, professional, and continuing education offered through resident instruction and online delivery. Annual enrollment at its 24 campuses totals more than 100,000 graduate and undergraduate students, making it one of the largest universities in the United States. As an R1 research institution Penn State\u2019s annual research expenditure exceeds $1billion. This rich university environment offers unparalleled opportunities for cross disciplinary partnerships in education, community outreach, and research.\u00a0Of particular note, is Penn State\u2019s unique approach to university-level research institutes. Penn State\u2019s seven well-resourced university-designated research institutes ( https://www.psu.edu/research/interdisciplinary-institutes/ ) are not siloed \u201cclosed shops,\u201d but entities that exist principally to strategically disseminate funding that fosters cross-college, transdisciplinary research collaborations and makes needed shared resources widely available.\u00a0This approach has led to Penn State being recognized as standing out for effective promotion of team research collaboration . HHD maintains robust partnerships with nearly all of these institutes. Penn State\u2019s University Park campus is located in the town of State College in Centre County, Pennsylvania. Employment at Penn State at University Park will allow you to live amid the beauty of the central Pennsylvania outdoors while enjoying all the culture, sports, and entertainment that a large university community can bring.\u00a0More information on the area and all of its amenities can be found here: http://www.visitpennstate.org . Our campuses are located on the original homelands of the Erie, Haudenosaunee (Seneca, Cayuga, Onondaga, Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and Wahzhazhe (Osage) Nations.\u00a0As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and honor the traditional caretakers of these lands and strive to understand and model their responsible stewardship. We also acknowledge the longer history of these lands and our place in that history. Application Submissions Candidates should complete an on-line application at https://hr.psu.edu/careers and upload: a) a cover letter (1 page), b) a statement of research interests (2-3 pages), c) a statement of teaching interests and experiences (1-2 pages), d) a statement of Diversity, Equity, Inclusion and Belonging (1-2 pages), e) a list of names and contact information of three professional references (who will provide letters of recommendation upon request), and f) up to three selected publications or preprints. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials as necessary to meet the 5-document limit. For more information contact Search Chair Sy-Miin Chow (symiin@psu.edu). Review of applications will begin after January 31, 2026, and continue until a suitable candidate is identified. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Researcher_REQ_0000074123-2": {"title": "Researcher", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Come and help define how large-scale genomic data analysis is done from a web browser. We are a friendly, ambitious research group at the Pennsylvania State University working on some of the most popular software in genomics, including Galaxy and AnVIL . These software platforms help thousands of researchers each year solve their data analysis needs. As the size of data and number of files grows, we are actively rethinking and designing new ways for researchers to organize, analyze, and visualize their data. In this Researcher position, you will help design and implement these solutions. You will work with modern web technologies, such as Vue.js, rely on REST APIs, and find solutions on how to scale and enable analysis display of thousands of datasets. We work in small teams that focus on specific tasks so there will be plenty of opportunity to learn and be heard. Job responsibilities: Build responsive, scalable, and beautiful web components that solve pressing challenges in genomic data analysis, Integrate capabilities from multiple systems to create seamless user experience, Help domain researchers and understand their needs to design and implement web-based capabilities that support their use case, Explore new technologies and figure out where to use them, Come up with creative ideas for projects and work through them with your teammates, Keep learning and advancing your skills by reviewing and digging into code, Be a part of a team that\u2019s as excited about your growth and happiness as much as you are about theirs. Education and Experience: Applicants should possess a master's degree, or its equivalent, in computer science, or be an active candidate for a terminal degree, in an academic field related to computer science. Knowledge of a modern JavaScript framework and ecosystem, Bootstrap, Git + GitHub, CI tools is required, as is familiarity with Python and REST APIs. Applicants should possess great communication skills and interest in working with other teammates. Familiarity with the basics of genomics, such as concepts, data types, tools, is preferred. Additional Information: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a curriculum vitae and the names and contact information of three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Assistant-Professor-of-Turfgrass-Science_REQ_0000073749-1": {"title": "Associate/Assistant Professor of Turfgrass Science", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Plant Science in the College of Agriculture Sciences at The Pennsylvania State University is hiring an Assistant/Associate Professor of Turfgrass Science . RESPONSIBILITIES : The Pennsylvania State University is pleased to invite qualified applicants to apply for an Associate/Assistant Professor of Turfgrass Science position. This is a full-time (9-month) tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Plant Science in the College of Agricultural Sciences with a 50% teaching, 25% research and 25% extension appointment. The successful candidate will specialize in turfgrass science and bring expertise that complements and enhances the strengths of the current faculty. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, turfgrass breeding, turf pathology, soil and nutrient management, water management, root biology and physiology, and implementation of agricultural technologies of all types. The candidate will teach four classes in turfgrass science subjects related to their area of expertise to students in the resident baccalaureate program, as well as online classes through Penn State\u2019s World Campus. Courses may include Introduction to Turfgrass Science, Turfgrass Cultural Systems, Turfgrass Physiology, and Pest Management. Additional courses that contribute to the departmental teaching program in areas related to the candidate\u2019s disciplinary strengths may also be taught. Recruitment and advising of undergraduate and graduate students, as well as interaction with the turfgrass industry through an extension program that addresses practitioner needs, are expected. The successful candidate will engage in collaborative and interdisciplinary projects with other faculty at Penn State, as well as with plant scientists at regional and national levels, to develop a research program supported by extramural funding. This research program should lead to improved and sustainable turfgrass systems that foster environmental and economic resilience. QUALIFICATIONS: A Ph.D. in turfgrass science, soil science, plant physiology, or a related field is required. The candidate must demonstrate disciplinary expertise in a field relevant to turfgrass science, with the ability and desire to address problems within the context of turfgrass systems. Candidates must possess effective communication skills (verbal and written), teaching skills, interpersonal skills, and the ability to build effective working relationships with colleagues and clientele. The candidate must be organized and capable of managing multiple projects simultaneously. An ability to engage professionally with our population of faculty, staff, and students across the university is required. SALARY:\u00a0 Commensurate with qualifications and experience.\u00a0 An excellent benefits package includes health, dental, and retirement contributions. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS : Candidates should apply online at https://hr.psu.edu/careers . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Candidates should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, the names and contact information for three references, three representative publications, a statement of research experiences/future interests, and a statement of teaching pedagogy/interests. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. START DATE: August 2026 or as negotiated. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Instructor---Undergraduate-General-Education-Course-in-Workforce-Financial-Skills_REQ_0000073943-1": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor \u2013 Undergraduate General Education Course in Workforce Financial Skills", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-01\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS Position Summary The Workforce Education and Development (WFED) program seeks qualified adjunct instructors to teach undergraduate general education courses related to personal financial planning, financial literacy, and money management for the workforce. These courses serve students across all academic backgrounds and are designed to build foundational financial knowledge and quantitative reasoning skills relevant to career entry and long-term financial well-being. Courses may focus on topics such as personal financial planning, financial decision-making for working adults, financial well-being for the workforce, and related subject areas. Courses are expected to be delivered in-person at University Park , with hybrid delivery possible depending on departmental needs. Primary Responsibilities- Deliver weekly in-person and/or hybrid instruction following approved course syllabus and objectives. Support student learning of core financial concepts, quantitative reasoning, and practical financial skills. Develop and facilitate applied learning activities including calculations, analysis, and scenario-based work. Evaluate student progress through assignments, quizzes, exams, and projects. Maintain timely student grading and records through Canvas. Hold weekly office hours, in person or via Zoom. Submit final grades according to university policies. Example Topic Areas- Budgeting fundamentals and cash flow planning Income, taxation, and cost-of-living comparisons Banking, saving, and financial services Credit, borrowing, and debt strategy Insurance and risk management Retirement accounts and planning options Investment fundamentals Financial decision-making for education and careers Required Qualifications- Master\u2019s degree in: \u2022 Personal finance \u2022 Finance \u2022 Accounting \u2022 Business \u2022 Workforce development / workforce education \u2022 or closely related field Experience teaching or training young adults or adults. Preferred Qualifications- Certified Financial Planner (CFP) designation preferred. Professional experience in financial advising, financial coaching, accounting, HR benefits, retirement planning, or related areas. Experience teaching undergraduate or general education courses. Experience teaching quantitative subjects. Familiarity with Canvas. Appointment Terms- This is a part-time wage appointment , assigned for a single academic semester and contingent upon student enrollment and available funding. Reappointment may be possible based on enrollment needs, performance, and departmental priorities. Delivery is expected to be in-person or hybrid . For questions, please contact: Hyung Joon Yoon, Ph.D., Professor-in-Charge, Workforce Education and Development Program (huy114@psu.edu). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Department-of-Kinesiology-Part-Time-Adjunct-Instructors--KPAP-_REQ_0000073753-1": {"title": "Department of Kinesiology Part-Time Adjunct Instructors (KPAP)", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-20\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Kinesiology Physical Activity Program (KPAP) in the Department of Kinesiology invites applications for part-time instructors to teach academically focused physical activity and/or fitness for life classes. These are one semester, non-tenure track appointments with the possibility of reappointment. Candidates should have an interest and skills in lifetime sport and exercise activities (e.g. fitness conditioning, yoga). A minimum of a Master\u2019s degree in an appropriate discipline and/or advanced certification/expertise in a specialized field, and a commitment to quality teaching is required. Previous teaching experience is preferred. Applications will be reviewed beginning immediately and continue to be reviewed until needed positions are filled. To be considered for this position, applications must be submitted online electronically and should include a cover letter, C.V., and three references. Please include strengths and preferences in specific areas (i.e. yoga, fitness conditioning, wellness, racquet sports, ballroom dance, etc.). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/General-Chemistry-Lecture-Coordinator_REQ_0000073132-2": {"title": "General Chemistry Lecture Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-11\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University Chemistry Department, University Park Campus, seeks to fill a position at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor , Associate Teaching Professor , or Teaching Professor , dependent upon qualifications. Responsibilities will include serving as General Chemistry Lecture Coordinator, which includes, but not limited to: 1. Curriculum development 2. Selection, hiring, training, and supervision of teaching assistants (TAs) and related administrative work 3. Selection, training, and supervision of undergraduate learning assistants (LAs) 4. Organization of graded assignments, including exam planning across multiple sections of general chemistry 5. Course administration 6. Faculty mentoring In addition, the candidate is expected to coordinate with other faculty teaching related courses, such as the general chemistry laboratory director, and teach general chemistry courses and other courses as needed. Our General Chemistry lectures are built around a 2-course sequence, and involve 12 faculty, over 30 TAs, and serve more than 3,000 students per semester. The ideal candidate will have demonstrated experience with teaching large lecture courses, coordinating the efforts of several teaching staff, and coordinating teaching assistants and faculty across multiple sections of a course. The position will begin in the fall semester of 2026. Assistant Teaching Professor candidates should possess a terminal degree or its equivalent in an academic field related to his/her teaching specialization; alternatively, the assistant teaching professor without a terminal degree should possess at least a master's degree or its equivalent in an academic field related to their teaching specialization; must have demonstrated ability as a teacher and adviser; and must have shown evidence of professional growth, scholarship, and/or mastery of subject matter. Associate Teaching Professor candidates should possess a terminal degree in an academic field related to their teaching specialization; must have demonstrated ability as a teacher and adviser; and must have shown evidence of professional growth, scholarship, and/or mastery of subject matter. Alternatively, the associate teaching professor without a terminal degree should possess at least a master's degree or its equivalent in an academic field related to their teaching specialization; must have demonstrated exceptional ability as a teacher and adviser while in the rank of senior lecturer or instructor; and must have shown evidence of professional growth, scholarship, and/or mastery of subject matter at a level of distinction beyond that of the assistant teaching professor. Teaching Professor candidates should possess a terminal degree in an academic field related to their teaching specialization; must have demonstrated exceptional ability as a teacher and adviser while in the rank of associate teaching professor; and must have shown evidence of professional growth, scholarship, and/or mastery of subject matter at a level of distinction beyond that of the associate teaching professor. In addition to completing a Penn State application , an application must be submitted at https://academicjobsonline.org/ajo/jobs/30937 . The application materials should include a cover letter, current CV, and a statement of teaching philosophy which also addresses teaching within a diverse community of students, staff, and faculty. Applicants will also need to arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to Academic Jobs Online . Review of applications will begin immediately, and the search will continue until the position is filled. For more information on the Penn State Chemistry Department, visit https://science.psu.edu/chem . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Line-Open-Rank-Position---Nursing_REQ_0000062297-1": {"title": "Tenure Line Open Rank Position - Nursing", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Overview: Expanding the bounds of our knowledge base within and surrounding the nursing discipline, we aim to build a robust community of researchers, educators, and scientists. As a result, the Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing at the Pennsylvania State University is searching for tenure-line faculty members to join us at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Faculty Position: Your work at Penn State will have a lasting impact and you will enjoy the benefit of being a part of Penn State\u2019s R1 research community. As an integral research faculty member in the Nese College of Nursing, you will be expected to direct a research program focused on nursing science and its translation to person-centered care across the lifespan and the health/wellness continuum. We welcome applicants whose research incorporates AI-driven methodologies. Our faculty teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses as well as supervise and mentor doctoral students. In addition, we expect our tenure track and tenured faculty to engage in outreach to disseminate research to stakeholders, including policymakers, nurses, and other practitioners at national, regional, and local conferences and meetings. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants at the rank of Assistant Professor must have the following at the time of beginning the appointment: Earned\u00a0a doctorate or a degree equivalent to a Ph.D. in the United States, in nursing or a closely related discipline. A valid United States nursing license. A strong record of research and scholarly achievements. Evidence of, or potential for, receiving external research funding. The following clearances: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Applicants at the rank of Associate Professor should possess the same qualifications as Assistant Professor as well as: Must show evidence of expertise in advancing science or theory and/or conducting an independent program of research (including serving as PI of funded grants and dissemination of research through presentations, scholarly publications, and directing research activities of others). May also engage in team science or innovation/entrepreneurship that is aligned with their independent program of research. Team science should be impactful and scientifically rigorous with the same criteria of dissemination noted above. Applicants at the rank of Professor should possess the same qualifications as Associate Professor as well as: Must have demonstrated and sustained productivity in research and scholarly activities, recognized leadership in professional organizations and learned societies, and national recognition as a leader in their area of research. May also engage in or assume a leadership role in team science or innovation/entrepreneurship, as articulated above, and extending to the level of full professorship that is aligned with their program of research. Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing: The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing is one of the most comprehensive nursing colleges in any public university in the United States. With over $17 million in research expenditures since the college\u2019s inception in 2013, the college has been awarded over $8 million for gerontology research, over $4 million for the development of a sexual assault forensic examination telehealth center (SAFE-T Center), and approximately $1.5 million to support clinical and translational science. Recently named a Center of Excellence by the National League for Nursing in recognition of the college\u2019s commitment to the investment in its faculty, Penn State Nursing is poised to support you throughout your time on its faculty and beyond. With over 2,100 undergraduate students and approximately 200 graduate students, our footprint is world-wide with our faculty creating immeasurable experiences for our students around the globe. We offer four undergraduate degree programs as well as six advanced degree programs. The Nese College of Nursing enjoys the distinction of being the only named nursing school in the Big 10. Being fully accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) with programmatic approval from the State Board of Nursing, the Nese College of Nursing is a premier educator for nurses across the Commonwealth. Further, the college is the academic home to the Tressa Nese and Helen Diskevich Center of Geriatric Nursing Excellence, the Sexual Assault Forensic Examination Telehealth (SAFE-T) Center, Age-Friendly Care, PA, and delivers its award-winning curriculum across 12 Penn State Campus locations including Hershey Medical Center. The Nese College of Nursing resides primarily at the University Park Campus. Set in the State College metropolitan area, a university town located in central Pennsylvania, State College offers a vibrant community with outstanding recreational facilities, a low crime rate, and excellent public schools. Further, State College\u2019s proximity to Penn State affords a variety of cultural events and experiences for local residents ensuring a rich, inclusive community. The campus is within a half-day\u2019s drive to Washington D.C., Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City, or Pittsburgh. The State College Regional Airport is served by three major carriers with flights to Philadelphia, Chicago, and Washington, DC. Penn State: The Pennsylvania State University (Penn State) is one of the largest public research and land grant universities in the country, serving over 83,000 students at 24 campuses across the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Penn State consistently ranks as a top twenty-five research university and its research enterprise ranks first nationally, tied with Johns Hopkins University, in the breadth and depth of its expertise. Penn State is a Research I university, a category employed by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education to indicate universities in the United States that engage in the highest levels of research activity. Penn State\u2019s unique educational model spans twenty-five campuses, including World Campus, that educate more than 100,000 students every year and drive innovation and quality of life in communities all over the world. We offer a competitive salary, commensurate with qualifications and experience. An attractive benefits package is available as are startup funds to support the applicant\u2019s research program. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. Application Process: To apply, candidates must submit the following. Incomplete applications will not be considered. A cover letter describing your interest in and qualifications for the position A current curriculum vitae Contact information of three professional references (No references will be contacted until the candidate is consulted) Applicants must submit their application and accompanying materials online at the PSU job site ( https://hr.psu.edu/careers ). Review of applications will be ongoing and will continue until the position is filled. Information on the Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing and its programs can be found at\u00a0 http://www.nursing.psu.edu/ . For more information or questions about this position, please contact: Dr. Sunday Azagba, Search Committee Chair Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing 201 Nursing Sciences Building University Park, PA 16802 E-mail (preferred): spa5695@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---BMB_REQ_0000072298-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - BMB", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The research lab of Dr. Katsu Murakami in the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, the Huck Center for Structural Biology, at Penn State seeks a postdoctoral scholar to study the structure and function of cellular RNA polymerase transcription complexes using cryo-electron microscopy, biophysics, and biochemical methods. Applicants must hold a PhD in biochemistry, biophysics, or molecular biology and have experience in cryo-EM structural analysis of macromolecular complexes or in the study of cellular RNA polymerase transcription. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a curriculum vitae and the names and contact information of two references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Teaching-Support-Specialist--Smeal_REQ_0000073351-1": {"title": "Part-Time Teaching Support Specialist- Smeal", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-06\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Penn State Smeal Professional Graduate Programs is seeking to hire Teaching Support Specialists (TSS) to assist with online course de livery and instruction for the online master's and graduate certificate portfolio spanning a variety of specialty areas including Online MBA ; Accounting Foundations ; Business Analytics ; Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship ; Marketing Analytics and Insights ; Strategic Management and Executive Leadership ; Supply Chain Management ; and Taxation. Media outlets and independent observers regularly rank the Smeal College of Business among the best institutions in the world , and Penn State World Campus has been a recognized institution in U.S. News and World Report \u2019s annual rankings of Best Online Programs since 2017. An overview of the p ortfolio including l ist s of core/advanced courses can be found here: https://www.smeal.psu.edu/pgp . TSSs are professionals in the ir respective fields with the appropriate background needed to assist with engagement of professional students and application of course concepts to contemporary business. Duties include but are not limited to assisting the lead instructor with feedback/grading, facilitation of discussion boards, moderation of live sessions, and course innovation. Additionally, TSSs will assist students with technical and course content issues upon request. The position requires competency in the application of principles and practices essential to modern business . A Master's Degree or equivalent education and experience is required. Individual s who have completed a Penn State online master\u2019s or graduate certificate or similar education are preferred. Teaching Support Specialists have the potential to work remotely within the United States and will typically work 10 -12 hours per week (average) on a contract basis. These positions are one semester , part-time appointments without guarantee of renewal. TSSs are paid based on credit assignment, $4000/semester/3 credit course. Prorated accordingly based on credit hours. Applications will be received and reviewed on an ongoing basis and positions filled as needed. Applicants should submit a cover letter and re sume . In the cover letter, indicate which subject area(s) you are applying for , based on the list of 19 areas noted below. 1. Financial Accounting 2. Marketing Management 3. Supply Chain Management 4. Corporate Finance 5. Statistics/Data Analysis 6. Marketing Analytics 7. Corporate Innovation & Entrepreneurship 8. Economics for Business Strategy 9. Global Strategic Management 10. Organizational Behavior/Leadership 11. Managing in the Digital Economy 12. Business Negotiation 13. Corporate Sustainability 14. Team Performance 15. Leadership Communications/Change Management 16. Ethics & Responsible Leadership 17. Taxation 18. Strategic Management and Executive Leadership 19. Real Estate Law and Valuation \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Electromagnetic-Effects---Applications-Department-Head--Faculty-_REQ_0000073024-1": {"title": "Electromagnetic Effects & Applications Department Head (Faculty)", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-04\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are seeking a Department Head for the Electromagnetic Effects and Applications Department to join our team within the Spectrum and Signatures Solutions (S3) Division at the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State. \u00a0 You will report directly to the Spectrum and Signatures Solutions Division Head and direct a team of research engineers, scientists, technicians, and support personnel in architecture, design, integration, and testing of RF and Microwave systems for multiple Department of Defense (DoD) and Intelligence Community (IC) sponsors. \u00a0Technologies include medium-to-high-power RF emitters, waveform design, propagation analysis, RF circuits and radiating systems, and related applications. \u00a0This position can be filled as a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Manage the daily activities of the team, including hiring, training, mentoring, task assignment, and coaching sessions/performance evaluations Lead department operations including strategic planning, budgeting, staffing, facilities, proposal development, and risk mitigation to ensure growth is aligned and sustainable Maintain regular communication with sponsors and associate contractors Lead the technical execution of research, development, prototyping, and implementation of systems for a wide range of customers in the DoD and IC\u00a0 Direct technical excellence, cost control, and on time delivery of work\u00a0 Oversee the development of plans and proposals for new programs Lead and assure the proper execution of sponsored research Lead a high performing and collaborative team across engineering, scientific, and support functions, fostering a culture of excellence, cohesion, and professional growth, and embrace ARL\u2019s mission to discover, demonstrate, transition, and educate Faculty rank will be commensurate with education and experience. Minimally requires a Master's degree in an engineering or science discipline and 1 year related experience. Required skills/experience areas include: Principal investigator, technical lead, program management, or senior contributor on applied and basic research efforts Record of securing and sustaining external funding in technical areas related to electromagnetic propagation modeling and simulation, radio frequency spectrum research, electromagnetic effects, signals processing, and/or general electrical engineering skill sets Development, field-testing, delivery, and integration of technology Proven competence working within 3D EM analysis software (e.g. CST Studio Suite, Remcom EM simulation software) Success in dynamic environments where various forms of communication and organizational skills were crucial to be effective Previous success with collaborations in a multi-disciplinary, team-oriented culture Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Secret level or higher; TS/SCI clearance level is preferred Preferred skills/experience areas include: PHD or Master\u2019s Degree in Electrical Engineering, Applied Physics, or related MBA with Electrical Engineering Research, military, or government environment Designing, orchestrating, and conducting technical design reviews and field tests Security and IT frameworks applied to DoD and IC sponsored programs Active TS/SCI Security Clearance Your working location will be fully on-site, located in State College, PA.\u00a0 This position will require occasional travel to designated sponsor or associate contractor locations within and outside the continental United States.\u00a0 ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Department of Defense (DoD), and the Intel Community (IC).\u00a0 FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our web site at www.arl.psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 All positions at ARL require candidates to\u00a0possess the ability to obtain a government security clearance; you will be notified during the interview process if this position is subject to a government background investigation.\u00a0 You must be a U.S. citizen to apply.\u00a0 Employment with the ARL will require successful completion of a pre-employment drug screen. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Lecturer-Opportunities-for-2025-2026-Academic-Year---Department-of-Mathematics_REQ_0000065347-3": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer Opportunities for 2025/2026 Academic Year - Department of Mathematics", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-04\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Mathematics seeks to hire adjunct lecturers throughout the 2025/2026 academic year. Applications must be submitted electronically and include: Application and Curriculum Vitae and Publication List. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until all positions are filled. Master\u2019s degree or equivalent education and experience required. The required teaching load and course assignments will be allocated by the department . The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Instruction-Positions-with-Integrative-Arts_REQ_0000072998-3": {"title": "Part-Time Instruction Positions with Integrative Arts", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-04\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The College of Arts & Architecture's Integrative Arts program seeks to fill part-time instructional support positions. Hours and wages for each position will vary. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as needed. Job duties will be a combination of the following but may vary day to day: Instruct courses within the Integrative Arts program Instruct general education arts & integrative studies courses Support digital media team in production/post-production Support learning design staff in development of programs/courses \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Pan-Lab_REQ_0000073042": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar- Pan Lab", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-03\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Prof. Dipanjan Pan, Huck Chair Professor in Nanomedicine in the Huck Institute of Life Sciences at Penn State, is seeking a self-motivated, highly skilled Postdoctoral Scholar . The successful candidate will work closely with the PI and other lab members in a multidisciplinary laboratory environment to develop various sensing platforms and other nanomedicine projects. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Design and conduct biomedical experiments. Nanomaterials synthesis and characterization. Extensive experience with electrical engineering, circuit design.\u00a0 Translational science. 3D printing. Hands-on lab benchwork on cell biology, immunology, and animal tumor models is a plus. Generate, analyze, and evaluate data. Present results in an organized manner. Learn new techniques and approaches in state-of-the-art materials characterization techniques. Stay up to date with the latest advancements in the field and integrate them into research. Required and preferred qualifications: A PhD degree in bioengineering or biomedical engineering, cancer biology, molecular biology, immunology, or a related field is required by the start date. Multiple peer-reviewed publications that demonstrate relevant hands-on skills are required. Experience with mentoring junior scientists, graduate students and working within a diverse, multidisciplinary group. Excellent organizational skills, oral and written communication skills, self-motivation, and a strong work ethic are required. The Pan Lab is equipped with state-of-the-art equipment for nanoparticle characterization, and the Postdoctoral Scholar will have access to world class facilities at the Penn State campus. For more information about Prof. Dipanjan Pan\u2019s lab, please visit https://www.dipanjanpanlaboratory.org/ . Interested applicants should submit an updated CV, a cover letter describing their current position and reasons for applying, and contact information of two referees, including the current supervisor. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Dean-for-Undergraduate-Education---Non-Tenured-Position_REQ_0000072937-2": {"title": "Associate Dean for Undergraduate Education \u2013 Non-Tenured Position", "description": "Posted: 2025-11-03\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for Associate Dean for Undergraduate Education to oversee our undergraduate program curriculum, student admissions, progression, outcomes, and faculty development. This position is responsible for BSN curricular activities and ensuring program compliance with state, regional, and national accreditation standards. This is a non- tenured faculty appointment as an Academic Administrator at the rank of Teaching Professor , with an anticipated start date of July 2026 . The start date is negotiable. The position is located at the University Park campus. Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. A startup package to support the successful candidates' research or scholarship program is negotiable. RESPONSIBILITIES: Academic Leadership: Provide strategic oversight and administration of undergraduate nursing programs across all campuses, ensuring academic quality and operational consistency. Lead curriculum development, evaluation, and continuous improvement to maintain alignment with accreditation and licensure standards. Ensure full compliance with state and national regulatory and accrediting bodies governing nursing education. Collaborate with Undergraduate Assistant Deans, Campus Directors, and Campus Administrators to recruit and retain highly qualified faculty. Supervise teaching faculty and staff, including hiring, onboarding, mentoring, and conducting performance evaluations. Manage the procurement, renewal, and oversight of healthcare partnership agreements to support student clinical education needs. Coordinate clinical placements and maintain effective, collaborative relationships with healthcare facilities and community partners. Oversee and support the academic promotion process for non-tenure line teaching faculty within the college. Student Success: Collaborate in the design and execution of strategic initiatives to recruit and retain high-caliber undergraduate nursing students. Provide leadership for student recruitment, retention, and success efforts across all campuses. Oversee the operations of the Student Success Center and the Simulation Laboratory to ensure they effectively support student learning, academic achievement, and clinical skill development. Monitor student academic progress and address concerns related to academics, compliances, and clinical performance. Participate in the review, development, and oversight of academic policies to ensure equitable and consistent application. Promote the nursing program across the Commonwealth through active student engagement, recruitment efforts, and outreach initiatives. Cultivate and maintain strategic partnerships with hospitals, clinics, educational institutions, and peer universities within the Commonwealth and beyond. Administrative and Strategic Planning: Prepare, manage, and oversee the undergraduate nursing program budget to ensure efficient use of resources. Collect, analyze, and interpret program data to support ongoing evaluation, accreditation, and strategic planning efforts. Represent the undergraduate nursing program in college-wide and external meetings, serving as a liaison with internal and external stakeholders. Coordinate scheduling of courses and clinical rotations to optimize faculty workload, student needs, and clinical site availability. Accreditation and Compliance: Ensure the undergraduate nursing program consistently meets or exceeds standards established by national and state accrediting and regulatory agencies. Prepare and submit required documentation for faculty approvals, curriculum changes, and licensure of graduates. Remain current with emerging educational technologies and pedagogical best practices, integrating innovative tools to enhance teaching and learning. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: A doctorate in nursing or a closely related field. Candidates will have attained the rank of Teaching Professor before their appointment start date in Nursing. Candidates must hold a current U.S. registered nurse license and eligibility for licensure in Pennsylvania . Experience: Experience in academic administration with undergraduate nursing education programs. Leadership experience in undergraduate curricular development, program development, implementation, and evaluation. A keen understanding of the key issues and opportunities in the nursing profession and nursing education, coupled with knowledge of current trends in innovative undergraduate education. Demonstrated ability to motivate faculty and lead teams in a dynamic environment. Evidence of interprofessional collaboration and a track record of educational program funding preferred. Scholarship in various aspects of nursing education, such as innovative and interprofessional teaching methodologies. Fiscal experience in terms of developing and monitoring budgets and other resources for academic affairs. Experience in developing strategic plans and providing visionary leadership for academic programs. Documented experience in professional scholarship and presentation. Possess an understanding of management challenges that present themselves in highly complex academic environments. Personal Characteristics: Strong communication and interpersonal skills with demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and academic leaders across the University. Self-motivated, approachable, and visible leader who has an open-door policy and empowers others. A highly professional, inclusive, and mature individual who is trustworthy and exemplifies honesty and integrity. An open, articulate, engaging, approachable, and innovative leader who offers clarity and inspires respect and credibility. The candidate will generate enthusiasm and passion for this work. Demonstrates creative problem-solving skills with the willingness to take the initiative in leading and managing change. An effective consensus builder and consummate team player who has a proven history of providing timely follow-up. Has strong negotiation and persuasion skills and the ability to work with multiple individuals to bring about a broad perspective. A well-organized, analytical, politically savvy, self-directed individual with excellent time management skills. Possesses a high level of diplomacy and maintains a culture of integrity. Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing: The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing is one of the most comprehensive colleges of nursing in any public university in the country. With over $17 million in research expenditures since the college\u2019s inception in 2013, the college has been awarded over $8 million for gerontology research, over $4 million for the development of a sexual assault forensic examination telehealth center (SAFE-T Center), and approximately $1.5 million to support clinical and translational science. Recently, named a Center of Excellence by the National League for Nursing in recognition of the college\u2019s commitment to the investment in its faculty, Penn State Nursing is poised to support you throughout your time on its faculty and beyond. With over 2,100 undergraduate students and approximately 200 graduate students , our footprint is worldwide, with our faculty creating immeasurable experiences for our students around the globe. We offer four undergraduate program options as well as six advanced degree programs. The Nese College of Nursing enjoys the distinction of being the only named nursing school in the Big 10. Being fully accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) with programmatic approval from the State Board of Nursing, the Nese College of Nursing is a premier educator for nurses across the Commonwealth, delivering its award-winning curriculum across 12 Penn State Campus locations , including Hershey Medical Center. The Nese College of Nursing resides primarily at the University Park Campus . Set in the State College metropolitan area, a university town located in central Pennsylvania, State College offers a vibrant community with outstanding recreational facilities, a low crime rate, and excellent public schools. Further, State College\u2019s proximity to Penn State affords a variety of cultural events and experiences for local residents ensuring a rich, inclusive community. The campus is within a half-day\u2019s drive to Washington D.C., Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City, or Pittsburgh. The University Park Airport is served by three major carriers with flights to Washington D.C., Philadelphia, Chicago, and Detroit. Penn State: The Pennsylvania State University is one of the largest public research and land grant universities in the country, serving over 83,000 students at 24 campuses across the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Penn State consistently ranks as a top twenty-five research university and its research enterprise ranks first nationally, tied with Johns Hopkins University, in the breadth and depth of its expertise. Penn State is a Research 1 university , a category employed by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education to indicate universities in the United States that engage in the highest levels of research activity. Penn State\u2019s unique educational model spans twenty-five campuses, including World Campus, that educate more than 100,000 students every year and drive innovation and quality of life in communities all over the world. Application Process: To apply, candidates must electronically submit the following. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Cover letter describing interest in and qualification for the position Current curriculum vitae Contact information of four professional references (References will not be contacted without prior consultation with the candidate.) Applicants must submit their application and accompanying materials online at the PSU job site ( https://hr.psu.edu/careers ). Review of applications will begin on November 21, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Information on the Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing and its programs can be found at http://www.nursing.psu.edu/ . For more information or questions about this position, please contact: Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing 201 Nursing Sciences Building University Park, PA 16802 Dr. Vinciya Pandian, Search Chair Email: vpandian@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Dean-for-Undergraduate-Education---Tenured-Position_REQ_0000072936-1": {"title": "Associate Dean for Undergraduate Education - Tenured Position", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-27\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for Associate Dean for Undergraduate Education to oversee our undergraduate program curriculum, student admissions, progression, outcomes, and faculty development. This position is responsible for BSN curricular activities and ensuring program compliance with state, regional, and national accreditation standards. This is a tenured faculty appointment as an Academic Administrator at the rank of Professor , with an anticipated start date of July 2026 . The start date is negotiable. The position is located at the University Park campus. Penn State offers a comprehensive benefits package for full-time employees, designed to support both personal and professional well-being. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. A startup package to support the successful candidates' research or scholarship program is negotiable. RESPONSIBILITIES: Academic Leadership: Provide strategic oversight and administration of undergraduate nursing programs across all campuses, ensuring academic quality and operational consistency. Lead curriculum development, evaluation, and continuous improvement to maintain alignment with accreditation and licensure standards. Ensure full compliance with state and national regulatory and accrediting bodies governing nursing education. Collaborate with Undergraduate Assistant Deans, Campus Directors, and Campus Administrators to recruit and retain highly qualified faculty. Supervise teaching faculty and staff, including hiring, onboarding, mentoring, and conducting performance evaluations. Manage the procurement, renewal, and oversight of healthcare partnership agreements to support student clinical education needs. Coordinate clinical placements and maintain effective, collaborative relationships with healthcare facilities and community partners. Oversee and support the academic promotion process for non-tenure line teaching faculty within the college. Student Success: Collaborate in the design and execution of strategic initiatives to recruit and retain high-caliber undergraduate nursing students. Provide leadership for student recruitment, retention, and success efforts across all campuses. Oversee the operations of the Student Success Center and the Simulation Laboratory to ensure they effectively support student learning, academic achievement, and clinical skill development. Monitor student academic progress and address concerns related to academics, compliances, and clinical performance. Participate in the review, development, and oversight of academic policies to ensure equitable and consistent application. Promote the nursing program across the Commonwealth through active student engagement, recruitment efforts, and outreach initiatives. Cultivate and maintain strategic partnerships with hospitals, clinics, educational institutions, and peer universities within the Commonwealth and beyond. Administrative and Strategic Planning: Prepare, manage, and oversee the undergraduate nursing program budget to ensure efficient use of resources. Collect, analyze, and interpret program data to support ongoing evaluation, accreditation, and strategic planning efforts. Represent the undergraduate nursing program in college-wide and external meetings, serving as a liaison with internal and external stakeholders. Coordinate scheduling of courses and clinical rotations to optimize faculty workload, student needs, and clinical site availability. Accreditation and Compliance: Ensure the undergraduate nursing program consistently meets or exceeds standards established by national and state accrediting and regulatory agencies. Prepare and submit required documentation for faculty approvals, curriculum changes, and licensure of graduates. Remain current with emerging educational technologies and pedagogical best practices, integrating innovative tools to enhance teaching and learning. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: A doctorate in nursing or a closely related field. Candidates will have attained the full rank of Professor before their appointment start date in Nursing. Candidates must hold a current U.S. registered nurse license and eligibility for licensure in Pennsylvania . Experience: Experience in academic administration with undergraduate nursing education programs. Leadership experience in undergraduate curricular development, program development, implementation, and evaluation. A keen understanding of the key issues and opportunities in the nursing profession and nursing education, coupled with knowledge of current trends in innovative undergraduate education. Demonstrated ability to motivate faculty and lead teams in a dynamic environment. Evidence of interprofessional collaboration and a track record of educational program funding preferred. Scholarship in various aspects of nursing education, such as innovative and interprofessional teaching methodologies. Fiscal experience in terms of developing and monitoring budgets and other resources for academic affairs. Experience in developing strategic plans and providing visionary leadership for academic programs. Documented experience in professional scholarship and presentation. Possess an understanding of management challenges that present themselves in highly complex academic environments. Personal Characteristics: Strong communication and interpersonal skills with demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and academic leaders across the University. Self-motivated, approachable, and visible leader who has an open-door policy and empowers others. A highly professional, inclusive, and mature individual who is trustworthy and exemplifies honesty and integrity. An open, articulate, engaging, approachable, and innovative leader who offers clarity and inspires respect and credibility. The candidate will generate enthusiasm and passion for this work. Demonstrates creative problem-solving skills with the willingness to take the initiative in leading and managing change. An effective consensus builder and consummate team player who has a proven history of providing timely follow-up. Has strong negotiation and persuasion skills and the ability to work with multiple individuals to bring about a broad perspective. A well-organized, analytical, politically savvy, self-directed individual with excellent time management skills. Possesses a high level of diplomacy and maintains a culture of integrity. Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing: The Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing is one of the most comprehensive colleges of nursing in any public university in the country. With over $17 million in research expenditures since the college\u2019s inception in 2013, the college has been awarded over $8 million for gerontology research, over $4 million for the development of a sexual assault forensic examination telehealth center (SAFE-T Center), and approximately $1.5 million to support clinical and translational science. Recently, named a Center of Excellence by the National League for Nursing in recognition of the college\u2019s commitment to the investment in its faculty, Penn State Nursing is poised to support you throughout your time on its faculty and beyond. With over 2,100 undergraduate students and approximately 200 graduate students , our footprint is worldwide, with our faculty creating immeasurable experiences for our students around the globe. We offer four undergraduate program options as well as six advanced degree programs. The Nese College of Nursing enjoys the distinction of being the only named nursing school in the Big 10. Being fully accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) with programmatic approval from the State Board of Nursing, the Nese College of Nursing is a premier educator for nurses across the Commonwealth, delivering its award-winning curriculum across 12 Penn State Campus locations , including Hershey Medical Center. The Nese College of Nursing resides primarily at the University Park Campus . Set in the State College metropolitan area, a university town located in central Pennsylvania, State College offers a vibrant community with outstanding recreational facilities, a low crime rate, and excellent public schools. Further, State College\u2019s proximity to Penn State affords a variety of cultural events and experiences for local residents ensuring a rich, inclusive community. The campus is within a half-day\u2019s drive to Washington D.C., Baltimore, Philadelphia, New York City, or Pittsburgh. The University Park Airport is served by three major carriers with flights to Washington D.C., Philadelphia, Chicago, and Detroit. Penn State: The Pennsylvania State University is one of the largest public research and land grant universities in the country, serving over 83,000 students at 24 campuses across the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Penn State consistently ranks as a top twenty-five research university and its research enterprise ranks first nationally, tied with Johns Hopkins University, in the breadth and depth of its expertise. Penn State is a Research 1 university , a category employed by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education to indicate universities in the United States that engage in the highest levels of research activity. Penn State\u2019s unique educational model spans twenty-five campuses, including World Campus, that educate more than 100,000 students every year and drive innovation and quality of life in communities all over the world. Application Process: To apply, candidates must electronically submit the following. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Cover letter describing interest in and qualification for the position Current curriculum vitae (CV) Contact information of four professional references (References will not be contacted without prior consultation with the candidate.) Applicants must submit their application and accompanying materials online at the PSU job site ( https://hr.psu.edu/careers ). Review of applications will begin on November 21, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Information on the Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing and its programs can be found at http://www.nursing.psu.edu/ . For more information or questions about this position, please contact: Ross and Carol Nese College of Nursing 201 Nursing Sciences Building University Park, PA 16802 Dr. Vinciya Pandian, Search Chair Email: vpandian@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Theoretical-High-Energy-Physics_REQ_0000072840-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Theoretical High Energy Physics", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill multiple post-doctoral positions in theoretical high energy physics, to start between July 2026 and October 2026. These positions are primarily for work on scattering amplitudes in gauge and gravity theories\u2014understanding their mathematical form, developing tools for their computation and representation, and applying new results to particle physics, gravitational wave physics, gauge/string duality, integrability or various related topics. \u00a0 The elementary-particle theory faculty at Penn State consists of Carlos Blanco, Jacob Bourjaily, John Collins (emeritus), Murat Gunaydin (emeritus), Irina Mocioiu, Kohta Murase, Radu Roiban, Sarah Shandera, Anna Stasto and Mark Strikman. There are experimental groups active in astroparticle physics, dark matter and neutrino mass measurement. There are also active programs in theoretical gravitational physics, gravitational wave physics and cosmology. Postdoctoral scholars will be members of the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos at Penn State. \u00a0 Requirements include a Ph.D. in Physics. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to physicsapply@psu.edu indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line (REQ_0000072840). \u00a0 Applicants\u2019 questions may be sent to: Prof. Jacob Bourjaily or Prof. Radu Roiban, Physics Department, The Pennsylvania State University, 104 Davey Laboratory, University Park, PA 16802, U.S.A. E-mail: bourjaily@psu.edu or radu@phys.psu.edu \u00a0 Applications should be received by December 15, 2025 for full consideration. However, applications will be considered until the positions is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Open-Rank-Tenure-Track-Faculty-in-Industrial-Engineering_REQ_0000071761-1": {"title": "Open Rank Tenure-Track Faculty in Industrial Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Harold and Inge Marcus Department of Industrial and Manufacturing Engineering (IME) in the College of Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, PA, is pleased to announce a search for one outstanding tenure track faculty position in the area of Operations Research (OR). This position will be filled at the rank of Assistant , Associate or Full Professor , depending on the successful candidate\u2019s qualifications. Candidates for Assistant Professor must have demonstrated ability as a teacher or research worker and must have shown definite evidence of growth in scholarly or professional achievement. The Associate Professor should possess the same qualifications as the Assistant Professor but must also provide evidence of an established reputation in scholarly or professional achievement. The Professor should possess the same qualifications as the Associate Professor but must also provide evidence of a substantial record of advanced research and/or creative work, and of leadership in their field of specialization.\u00a0 The Operations Research (OR) area is foundational to the IME Department at Penn State. Roughly two-thirds of our current PhD students are in the area of OR and related applications. We welcome candidates who can build a strong methodological research base in areas of Operations Research, including optimization, stochastics, simulation, machine learning and artificial intelligence. Applicants at all ranks must have a Ph.D. in Industrial Engineering, Operations Research, or closely related discipline (or near completion of their doctoral studies) with demonstrated research potential by the appointment date. They must also possess excellent verbal and written communication skills. Candidates are expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, establish and lead an innovative research program, supervise graduate students, pursue external funding opportunities, and provide service to the University. The anticipated start date for this faculty position is August 2026. About the Department: The Harold and Inge Marcus Department of Industrial and Manufacturing Engineering at Penn State was founded in 1908 \u00a0as the first industrial engineering program in the world. Our department has a history of excellence in educating the next generation of industrial engineers while providing new solutions for industry through innovative research, interdisciplinary projects, and hands-on experience in our state-of-the-art facilities. With approximately 30 faculty members, 10 support staff, 400 undergraduate students, and 200 graduate students, we are a diverse department with research interests in many areas including: additive manufacturing processes, human factors in transportation and healthcare, supply chain management, service systems engineering, and healthcare systems engineering\u2014just to name a few. We offer the\u00a0 B.S. degree \u00a0and\u00a0 graduate degrees (Master of Science, Master of Engineering, and Doctorate) \u00a0in industrial engineering as well as dual-graduate degrees in industrial engineering and operations research. Both our undergraduate and graduate programs consistently rank highly in the\u00a0U.S. News & World Report\u00a0surveys, thanks in large part to our world-class faculty, the students they mentor, and our excellent support staff. Applicants should submit an online application including a cover letter, a Curriculum Vitae, a summary of research and teaching (no more than 5 pages), a statement on proposed contributions to the Penn State Values ( https://universityethics.psu.edu/penn-state-values ) and a list of 3-5 professional references combined as one PDF file not to exceed 5MB, due to system limitations. The summary should contain plans to establish a research program and their vision for collaborating within the department as well as across Penn State. Additionally, the summary should articulate the applicant\u2019s interest in supporting our graduate and undergraduate programs through teaching and mentoring students. Early applications are encouraged, as consideration will begin once applications are received. This requisition will remain open until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Huck-Institutes---Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000072682-2": {"title": "Huck Institutes - Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-14\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences seeks an outstanding scientist to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in the research group of Dr Vidhi Pareek. Our lab studies how cells organize their metabolism through enzyme complexes and their interaction with cellular organelles. We combine mass spectrometry imaging, biochemistry, structural biology, and cell biology to examine metabolism in single cells, tissues, and animal models. Our current projects focus on metabolic heterogeneity and pathological drivers in cancer. Education and Experience: We're looking for someone who brings both technical expertise and creative thinking to the lab. The ideal candidate will have earned their Ph.D. in Medicinal Chemistry, Pharmaceutical Sciences, Chemistry, Biochemistry or a closely related field. Your doctoral work should demonstrate a strong focus on developing methods and workflows for mass spectrometry imaging, particularly as applied to single cells, tissues, or organoids. Expertise in post-acquisition analysis is essential. If you also bring experience in cell culture, tissue micro-dissection, or fluorescence imaging, these skills would be valuable additions to our team. We're particularly interested in candidates who can demonstrate a track record of solving complex analytical challenges and working collaboratively. About the Position: The successful candidate will take a leading role in method development, data analysis, and publication of results, while also having opportunities to mentor students and contribute to grant writing. Working in our lab, you'll have access to state-of-the-art facilities at Penn State University and be part of a supportive research environment that encourages innovation and professional growth. Salary will be commensurate with your experience and qualifications, reflecting the importance of this role in our research program. Essential job function: Design and implement research protocols; design safety procedures; adapt new procedures, methods or instrumentation related to research procedures. Collect, prepare, and analyze research data; experience in collecting and analyzing HPLC and proteomics and mass spectrometry data is required. Design and execute mass spectrometry imaging experiments. Develop and optimize sample preparation protocols including flash freezing/ chemical fixation of samples and cryo-sectioning. Process and analyze complex spatial metabolomics datasets. Lead manuscript preparation and present findings at conferences. Contribute to grant writing and research proposals. Excellent communication with collaborators. Keep a detailed notebook summarizing experiments and recording research data; maintain computer database of research data. Supervise other personnel in the laboratory to coordinate research efforts for increased efficiency; participate in training of fellows, students and volunteer workers as needed. Assist with ordering and procurement of supplies and equipment and with general maintenance of laboratory. Application: In addition to submitting an application in Workday, interested candidates must share: Your detailed CV A cover letter describing how your research experience and interests align with the position Contact information for three professional references PDF copies of two relevant publications that showcase your work System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Questions can be directed to Dr Vidhi Pareek at [ vup9@psu.edu ]. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---School-of-Hospitality-Management---Adjunct-Instructor_REQ_0000072463-2": {"title": "Part-Time \u2013 School of Hospitality Management - Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-03\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS Penn State University, located in State College, PA, is seeking a part-time instructor to teach Hospitality Management courses in person during the spring, summer, and/or fall semesters. Duties may include: Assisting with content development and instruction Preparation of learning materials and activities Presentation of specific subjects, assessments of student learning Leading learning course activities in accordance with assigned course description and prescribed learning objectives Adjunct instructors typically teach one to two courses Following appropriate protocols in the instance of student illness/injury or emergency during class trips Communication with hiring department and with Penn State propriety systems including Penn State email, LionPath, and Starfish systems. To be considered for this opening, applications must be submitted electronically and include a letter of application detailing relevant qualifications for this job and a curriculum vitae. Applications will be accepted until positions are filled. Requirements and Qualifications The minimum qualifications include a Master's degree in related field or Bachelor\u2019s degree with appropriate years of work experience in the related field. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Chemistry-Department-_REQ_0000070979-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (Chemistry Department)", "description": "Posted: 2025-09-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratory of Associate Professor Mark Hedglin in the Chemistry Department at The Pennsylvania State University seeks to fill a postdoctoral research position to work in the areas of molecular biology, biochemistry and biophysical chemistry. \u00a0 The position requires a PhD in Chemistry (or an equivalent doctorate in an appropriate field) with a focus on cryogenic electron microscopy (Cryo-EM) and/or single molecule optical tweezers-fluorescence microscopy. \u00a0Researchers with training/expertise in expressing and purifying recombinant proteins from the baculovirus/insect cell expression system are highly-preferred, but individuals trained in other methods of protein expression and purification are welcome to apply. \u00a0 Interested and qualified applicants should submit applications electronically and include a CV with their research history and a complete list of publications. \u00a0Following a screening of initial application materials, appropriate candidates will be contacted by email and asked to arrange for letters of recommendation to be sent so that they might be considered further.\u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Instructor-Department-of-Educational-Psychology--Counseling--and-Special-Education_REQ_0000070559-3": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor Department of Educational Psychology, Counseling, and Special Education", "description": "Posted: 2025-08-14\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Educational Psychology, Counseling, and Special Education is seeking to hire part-time instructors to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Educational Psychology, Counselor Education, School Psychology, Rehabilitation Human Services, and Special Education. Required qualifications include evidence of an earned Doctorate or Master's degree, a commitment to excellence in teaching, including use of current technology, evidence of a commitment to working collegially and with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and reviewed as need arises throughout the academic year. The positions are dependent on class enrollments, low enrollments may necessitate canceling the class and position. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Instructor_REQ_0000069988-1": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2025-08-04\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The College of Agricultural Sciences seeks an adjunct instructor to assist with teaching lectures and barn sections of ERM 151 in Fall 2025. A Masters degree or equivalent education and experience is required. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Research-Professor_REQ_0000069746-1": {"title": "Adjunct Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2025-07-23\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Penn State Center of Excellence in Directed Energy (CEDE: mri.psu.edu/cede ) in conjunction with the Computational Electromagnetics and Antennas Research Lab (CEARL: ( https://sites.google.com/psu.edu/cearl/ ) in the Department of Electrical Engineering, is seeking a highly qualified individual for an exempt part time adjunct research professor position. Job Duties to Include: The primary responsibilities of the position will be assisting the director, Prof. Doug Werner, to manage the daily operation of CEDE and CEARL as well as to collaborate with other faculty, researchers, and the students. The successful candidate is expected to interact with government and/or industry program sponsors, participate in funded research projects, assist in the writing of proposals and prepare technical reports as well as other duties as directed. Requirements: The Researcher should possess a postgraduate degree (Ph.D. preferred) in Engineering (preferably Electrical Engineering). The successful candidate must also have United States Citizenship. Preferred Qualifications: Industrial experience. Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Comfortable presenting information to team members and group leaders. Capable of accomplishing efforts in a timely manner with high quality and with a positive attitude. Required Application Materials: Cover letter Academic CV Three references \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor_REQ_0000068828-1": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2025-06-26\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University, College of Health and Human Development, Department, of Human Development and Family Studies is seeking candidates for an Assistant Research Professor. The successful candidate should have expertise in the area of behavioral neuroscience, a focus on development is preferred.\u00a0The candidate should have demonstrated expertise in EEG research (experience with collecting, processing, analyzing, and publishing neuroscience data with EEG).\u00a0 Responsibilities Primary job responsibilities of this position include: (include teaching/research/service/administrative duties) Provide instrumental support to ongoing research using EEG assessments to examine treatment responsiveness among children diagnosed with ADHD. Support will include verifying the accuracy of the equipment and experimental setup, facilitating a pipeline for data transfer and storage from the medical school to the University Park campus, assisting in the development of the data processing pipeline, supervising graduate student and research assistant tasks. Lead and contribute to the publication of empirical research using archival and newly collected EEG data. Lead and contribute to the development of grant applications for external funding. Opportunities for teaching and mentoring within the Social Behavioral Neuroscience doctoral dual-title program. Qualifications Candidates must possess a Ph.D., or terminal degree at the time of hire. A degree in Neuroscience, Psychology, or closely related field is preferred/required. Demonstrated experience in research management and scientific publication is essential. Competencies critical to success include the ability to work with minimal supervision, effective verbal and communication skills needed to coordinate across and within a large collaborative research environment. Application Instructions To apply, please upload a curriculum vitae, a cover letter outlining your interest in the position and summarizing goals for independent projects, as well as a DEI Statement which addresses how your values and experiences advance diversity, equity, and inclusion in your work, and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications with begin on July 1st and will continue until a suitable candidate is identified. Questions related to the position can be addressed to Lisa Gatzke-Kopp, Ph.D.\u00a0at lmk18@psu.edu .\u00a0 About the College The College of Health and Human Development offers a robust program of eight interdisciplinary programs that share one common goal: enriching the lives of others. We continually examine contemporary issues facing people in today\u2019s changing times, and we develop cutting-edge solutions for addressing them. Our impact extends from our classrooms, across communities and industries, and around the globe. About the Department/Hiring Unit Human Development and Family Studies is an interdisciplinary department with a shared focus on understanding lifespan development within context, and across levels of analysis. HDFS is an intellectually vibrant academic environment, with approximately 25 faculty members engaged in externally funded research, and a doctoral training program of approximately 50 students.\u00a0 Land Acknowledgement Our campuses are located on the original homelands of the Erie, Haudenosaunee (Seneca, Cayuga, Onondaga, Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and Wahzhazhe (Osage) Nations. As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and honor the traditional caretakers of these lands and strive to understand and model their responsible stewardship. We also acknowledge the longer history of these lands and our place in that history. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---Psychology---Adjunct-Lecturer_REQ_0000068830-2": {"title": "Part Time - Psychology - Adjunct Lecturer", "description": "Posted: 2025-06-24\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Psychology at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for the opening of Adjunct Lecturers of Psychology for the semester starting Fall, 2025 . The opening require teaching undergraduate research methods courses, introductory statistics, or courses in clinical, cognitive, developmental, industrial-organizational, or social psychology. Candidates should be available for both on-line and classroom teaching assignments. Requirements and Qualifications Previous teaching experience and fit to the department\u2019s teaching needs are critical. In addition, successful candidates must either have demonstrated a commitment to building an inclusive, equitable, and diverse campus community, or describe one or more ways they would envision doing so, given the opportunity. Ph.D. preferred and at least ABD status required. The initial contract period is one semester, with a good chance of continuing renewal depending on funding. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until the vacancies are filled . Candidates should submit a letter of application, including concise statements of teaching experience and interests, and a CV. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Electrical-Engineering_REQ_0000068533-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Electrical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2025-06-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Electrical Engineering is looking for a Postdoctoral Scholar to join Dr. Yan Li's research group at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park Campus. Candidates with a background in one or more of the following areas: dynamics analysis of power systems, machine learning, cybersecurity, renewable energy, microgrids, hands-on experiences on hardware-in-the-loop projects, are needed. A Ph.D. in power systems or a closely related field is required by the start date. The successful applicant must have the ability to work independently and participate in teamwork. He/She is expected to document the research results in refereed journal publications, present them at seminars and conferences, assist with grant applications, and be involved in the supervision of research of graduate students. Applicants should send their CV to Dr. Yan Li at YQL5925@psu.edu. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Lecturer--Part-Time_REQ_0000068638-1": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Part-Time", "description": "Posted: 2025-06-13\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Biomedical Engineering in the College of Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for part-time, non-tenure track positions for the fall 2025 and spring 2026 semesters. These appointments will be part-time, non-tenure track appointments without benefits and no guarantee of renewal. Duties will include teaching lecture-based and/or laboratory classes, advising students and helping to assess course learning outcomes. A Ph.D. or master\u2019s degree in biomedical engineering or a closely related field is required. Preferred areas of expertise include, but are not limited to engineering design, thermodynamics, numerical simulation, biomechanics, instrumentation, and medical imaging. Previous teaching experience is preferred. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until all positions are filled. Interested applicants should upload a cover letter and resume. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Deputy-Division-Head---Applied-Sustainment-Technology-Division--Faculty-_REQ_0000068511-1": {"title": "Deputy Division Head - Applied Sustainment Technology Division (Faculty)", "description": "Posted: 2025-06-12\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS We are searching for a Deputy Division Head to join our Applied Sustainment Division (AST) Division of the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) at Penn State.\u00a0\u00a0The AST Division is an interdisciplinary group of engineers, software developers, functional business process experts, and IT professionals who collaborate to develop technologies for logistics, maintenance, and lifecycle asset sustainment for DoD systems. We conduct applied R&D efforts focused on acquiring data, turning data into information and knowledge, and securely delivering that data, information and knowledge to the right warfighter at the right time to support logistics and maintenance. Our research spans the spectrum from the warfighter edge to the heart of the enterprise.\u00a0 This position may be filled as either a Research and Development Engineer or a non-tenure Research Faculty. ARL is an authorized DoD SkillBridge partner and welcomes all transitioning military members to apply. You will: Lead a group of engineers and scientists in business development activities that include strategic planning for identifying new business opportunities, developing activity plans for meeting with new potential sponsors, and creating business development presentation material\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Lead and/or assist in the development of proposals and projects that further our knowledge and expertise in the area of Applied Sustainment Technologies Lead a group of engineers, scientists, and support staff that are engaged in the development of technologies critical to the advancement of the Applied Sustainment Technologies Division Mentor and encourage creativity in innovative technologies and research Support labor planning activities to ensure all departmental staff and faculty are appropriately and sufficiently tasked at all times Work with Division Head to review and analyze Division level financial project and overhead funding/expenditure data to enable data driven decision making for managing the Division Assist with recruitment and retaining, and define performance expectations of department head staff and faculty Assist with evaluating the professional growth and performance of Department Heads through performance reviews and coaching conversations Faculty rank will be commensurate with education and experience. Minimally requires a Master's degree in an engineering or science discipline and 1 year related experience. A Doctorate degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering or Aerospace Engineering is preferred. Required skills/experience areas include: Demonstrated success leading a team of engineers/scientists, and collaborating with large teams on multi-organization, multi-disciplinary projects Demonstrated success developing new business, including proposal writing and technical presentation skills Preferred skills/experience areas include: Current eligibility for access to classified information at the Secret level or higher and may be subject to a government background investigation to upgrade clearance eligibility, if required Previous management and technical leadership in the development, engineering, and sustainment technologies Your working location will be in State College, PA. ARL\u2019s purpose is to research and develop innovative solutions to challenging scientific, engineering, and technology problems in support of the Navy, the Department of Defense (DoD), and the Intel Community (IC).\u00a0 FOR FURTHER INFORMATION on ARL, visit our web site at www.arl.psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 All positions at ARL require candidates to\u00a0possess the ability to obtain a government security clearance; you will be notified during the interview process if this position is subject to a government background investigation.\u00a0 You must be a U.S. citizen to apply.\u00a0 Employment with the ARL will require successful completion of a pre-employment drug screen. \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our \u00a0 Benefits Page. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---Earth-and-Mineral-Sciences---Adjunct-Instructor_REQ_0000067620-1": {"title": "Part Time - Earth and Mineral Sciences - Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2025-05-15\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The College of Earth and Mineral Sciences is seeking Part-Time Instructors for its online geospatial education programs. Instructors teach on a semester-by-semester basis for the academic year.\u00a0 Requirements and Qualifications Applicants will be evaluated based on education and experience, with typical requirements including a Master`s degree and some classroom teaching experience in a college environment.\u00a0 The review of applications will be ongoing through the 2025-2026 academic year as needed. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-time-Instructor--CI-385-395601-DC-Social-Justice-in-Education_REQ_0000066172-2": {"title": "Part-time Instructor- CI 385-395.601 DC Social Justice in Education", "description": "Posted: 2025-04-18\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: Conferences and Institutes is hiring individuals as part-time drivers and chaperones for courses that have off-site learning components. Duties include driving undergraduate students and equipment to off-site locations and acting as the designated chaperone for all class trip activities. Other course duties may be assigned, as warranted by course instructor.\u00a0\u00a0 This job requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid US\u00a0driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required\u00a0in addition to standard background checks. Drivers will be requested to drive a variety of vehicles up to the size of a 15-passenger van. Additional training may be required.\u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing\u00a0 diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual\u00a0 uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity\u00a0 initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and\u00a0 nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core\u00a0 strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Teaching-Opportunities-in-Nutritional-Sciences_REQ_0000065420-1": {"title": "Part-Time Teaching Opportunities in Nutritional Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2025-03-24\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Nutritional Sciences (Nutr) seeks candidates for potential part-time teaching positions. Candidates must hold a Master\u2019s degree or Doctoral degree in nutrition or closely related field. Teaching opportunities may include: Nutr 100 (Contemporary Nutrition Concerns, 3 credits), Nutr 251 (Introductory Principle of Nutrition, 3 credits), and other courses which may require an MS/RD or RD/PhD to teach. A full listing of undergraduate courses is available at: https://bulletins.psu.edu/university-course-descriptions/undergraduate/nutr/.\u00a0 Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Reappointment in subsequent years is possible pending continuing need. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue to be accepted until all positions are filled. To be considered, interested candidates must complete an on-line application and upload a cover letter (with a list of courses you are interested in teaching), curriculum vitae, and the names of three professional references (with complete contact information, including mailing/email addresses, and telephone number). The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Biochemistry-and-Molecular-Biology_REQ_0000065496-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Biochemistry and Molecular Biology", "description": "Posted: 2025-03-21\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: Postdoctoral Position working on single molecule imaging and gene regulation One Postdoctoral Position is available in the lab of Dr. Manyu Du at The Pennsylvania State University. The Du lab is interested in understanding how transcription machineries and regulatory DNA elements organize in 3D in the nucleus to regulate gene expression. We leverage single-molecule super-resolution imaging, advanced lattice light sheet microscopy and other state of the art biophysical approaches to study molecular mechanisms of transcription, genome organization and bio-molecular condensation in live cells. We are using mouse embryonic stem cells and mouse erythroid leukemia cells to investigate the dynamics and function of transcriptional condensates in health and disease. Other than imaging, we are also interested in biochemical, genetic and sequencing approaches to understand gene regulation. This position is open immediately and initially funded for two years.\u00a0 YOUR TASKS: Your role at the lab is to investigate the behavior of individual molecules and bio-molecular condensates in living cells. You will use and develop the imaging and computational methods that to visualize dynamic molecule clusters during gene expression to study the formation and function of these assemblies in gene regulation. We want to recruit postdoc who is familiar with any of the following topics: Prior background in studying bio-molecular condensates using a combination of biochemistry, fluorescence and quantitative modeling methods is highly desired.\u00a0\u00a0 Prior backgrounds in single-molecule imaging, as well as DNA/RNA imaging in live mammalian cells are highly desired. YOUR QUALIFICATIONS: We are looking for independent, creative and highly motivated post-doctoral scientists interested in exploring biophysical principles that regulate genomic processes. Applicants should have a PhD in molecular biophysics, biochemistry or a related discipline. The ability to work effectively in a team and possess good communication skills. APPLICATION DEADLINE: Please apply with your complete application documents (letter of motivation, curriculum vitae) including a statement of research interests via our Workday portal by June 1st, 2025. At the same time, please ask three of your referees to send recommendation letters to mxd451@psu.edu. This is a\u00a0term\u00a0appointment initially funded for two years from date of hire with possibility of refunding. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports both broad and specific equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Center-for-Healthy-Aging_REQ_0000052408": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Center for Healthy Aging", "description": "Posted: 2025-03-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Center for Healthy Aging within the College of Health and Human Development at Penn State seeks a Postdoctoral Scholar to join an interdisciplinary team focusing on mobile health phenotyping and environmental influences. This position will be directly involved in a diverse range of participant, lab, and university-facing activities across multiple teams to support success amongst projects. \u00a0 The primary job functions and responsibilities may include: Project throughput and data monitoring. Data processing, analyses, and documentation. Contribute and lead team meetings to evaluate the progress of writing projects. Project closeout and dissemination, including dataset preparation and manuscript submission procedures. Eligible candidates are those with a Ph.D. in the behavioral and/or social sciences. The successful candidate must evidence interest and commitment to a research career focused on aging. The candidate must be able to work independently as well as contribute to research labs in the center consisting of graduate students as well as other postdoctoral researchers and faculty. This position is funded for one year from the start date, with the possibility of renewal. Salary and benefits follow NIH guidelines; more information on benefits for postdoctoral scholars can be found at https://www.research.psu.edu/opa/benefits . The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in\u202fall of\u202fits forms.\u202fWe embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusive excellence that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusive excellence as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Department-of-Chemistry_REQ_0000056762-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Department of Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2025-03-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The laboratory of Professor Tae-Hee Lee in the Chemistry Department at the Pennsylvania State University seeks to fill postdoctoral research positions to work in the area of single-molecule biophysics of the nucleosome, RNA polymerase II, and chromatin remodelers. The position requires a Ph.D. in an area of physical or biological sciences or equivalent doctorate in an appropriate field. Researchers trained in the field of nucleosome biophysics, chromatin or eukaryotic transcription biochemistry and molecular biology are preferred, but individuals trained in other fields of molecular/structural biology and biochemistry are also welcome to apply. Interested and qualified applicants should submit applications electronically and include a CV which includes a list of publications. Following a screening of these initial application materials, appropriate candidates will be contacted by email and asked to arrange for letters of recommendation to be sent so that they might be considered further. This is a term position funded for one year from date of hire with possibility of refunding. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-time-Adjunct-Instructor--Organization-Development-and-Change_REQ_0000064746-3": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Instructor, Organization Development and Change", "description": "Posted: 2025-02-20\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Learning and Performance Systems is seeking to hire part-time Instructors to teach occasional courses in its online Master of Professional Studies in Organization Development and Change. These courses are offered through Penn State\u2019s World Campus, and the intended audience is working professionals in business and industry. The preferred qualifications for applicants are a PhD in Organization Development or closely related field, at least ten years of related business and industry experience at the managerial level, demonstrated success in teaching online courses, knowledge of Canvas, Penn State\u2019s course management system, and the flexibility to interact with students on a daily basis. Applicants should submit a letter of application documenting qualifications for teaching courses within the program, a current curriculum vitae/resume, and teaching evaluations The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Lecturer-in-Graphic-Design_REQ_0000064582-1": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Lecturer in Graphic Design", "description": "Posted: 2025-02-14\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Graphic Design Department within the Stuckeman School of Architecture and Landscape Architecture in the College of Arts and Architecture seeks to hire various part-time faculty appointments throughout the academic year. These appointments will be semester-by-semester or year-long, non-tenure track academic appointments without benefits and no guarantee of renewal.\u00a0 Positions require:\u00a0 Bachelor`s degree, Master`s degree or Ph.D. and teaching experience at the University level.\u00a0 Education requirements vary depending on the specific position and usually are required in the related field or discipline of Graphic Design.\u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants should apply by submitting a short letter of interest with their qualifications and current Curriculum Vita (CV).\u00a0 Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as the need arises. Degree will be verified at the time of the offer. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Adjunct-Lecturer-in-Architecture_REQ_0000064549-2": {"title": "Part-Time Adjunct Lecturer in Architecture", "description": "Posted: 2025-02-12\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Architecture Department within the Stuckeman School of Architecture and Landscape Architecture in the College of Arts and Architecture seeks to hire various part-time faculty appointments throughout the academic year. These appointments will be semester-by-semester or year-long, non-tenure track academic appointments without benefits and no guarantee of renewal.\u00a0 Positions require:\u00a0 Bachelor`s degree, Master`s degree or Ph.D. and teaching experience at the University level.\u00a0 Education requirements vary depending on the specific position and usually are required in the related field or discipline of Architecture. Applicants should apply by submitting a short letter of interest with their qualifications and current Curriculum Vita (CV).\u00a0 Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as the need arises. Degree will be verified at the time of the offer. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Multifunctional-Landscapes_REQ_0000062848-1": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Multifunctional Landscapes", "description": "Posted: 2025-02-06\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Ecosystem Science and Management at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor of Multifunctional Landscapes. This is a tenure-line position with a 75% research and 25% teaching appointment. The position comes with a competitive start-up package and salary based on 36-weeks of service annually, which can be supplemented with additional salary up to a total of 48 weeks from external competitive grants and contracts and/or from endowment funds . \u00a0 The position will be filled at the Assistant or Associate level, commensurate with experience. \u00a0 \u00a0 The successful candidate\u2019s research will focus on balancing diverse human needs (e.g., food, water, energy, timber , recreation) with the needs of fish, wildlife, and other non-human species (e.g., habitat, water availability , healthy soils) at landscape scales. While any area of landscape-scale research will be considered, some areas of particular interest include managing forested landscapes to optimize the water-energy-food nexus, designing landscapes that maximize carbon storage and serve as buffers against natural disasters (e.g., fires, floods), and land use strategies to conserve fish and wildlife habitat while meeting human needs. Teaching responsibilities will include an undergraduate course in r emote s ensing and s patial d ata a nalysis and a graduate course in remote sensing applied multifunctional landscapes . This hire is part of departmental effort to build expertise in Biological Solutions to Climate Change , which seeks to make ecosystems more adaptive and resilient in the face of environmental change, while promoting sustainability and mitigat ing the worst impacts of climate change on humanity . \u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications . Individuals must have a Ph.D. (or equivalent) in Forestry, Soil Science, Environmental Science , Ecology, Environmental Engineering, Landscape Architecture, or related field with degree requirements complete by the application date. A strong publication record is required , as is evidence of (or potential for) securing extramural research funding from local, federal, and international agencies. The ideal candidate will work at regional, national, and/or global spatial scales using tools in remote sensing, GIS, mobile platforms (planes, drones, gliders, etc.), spatial statistics, and/or landscape modeling. The position is open to those who study any type of ecosystem; however, those with emphas i s on forested systems will receive preference. The ability to engage professionally with a diverse population of faculty, staff, and students across the University is required . \u00a0 \u00a0 Application . Interested individuals are invited to apply at REQ_0000062848 at https://hr.psu.edu/careers . Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, names and contact information for three references, three representative publications, statement of research experiences/future interests, statement of teaching pedagogy/interests, and a reflection of diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging document . Applicants are also encouraged to weave evidence of their commitment to fostering inclusivity throughout their application material. Questions about the application process should be directed to Mary Jo Schillings at mjs9@psu.edu .\u00a0 Review of applications will begin March 14 th , 2025 . \u00a0 \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University \u00a0 Office of Human Resources -\u202f http://www.ohr.psu.edu \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Public-Health-Entomology_REQ_0000063563": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health Entomology", "description": "Posted: 2025-01-17\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: POSITION DESCRIPTION:\u00a0 The Department of Entomology at The Pennsylvania State University seeks applications for a full-time, 9-month tenure track\u00a0 Assistant/Associate Professor of Public Health Entomology \u00a0with 70% research, 30% Extension assignment. Candidates with expertise in arthropods affecting humans including such pests as ticks, bedbugs, mosquitoes, and/or arthropods that contribute to allergies/asthma are encouraged to apply.\u00a0\u00a0Research focus could include, but is not limited to, pest management, pesticide resistance, population dynamics, behavioral/chemical ecological interactions, interactions of arthropods with pathogens and symbionts, and/or epidemiology.\u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES :\u00a0 The successful applicant will establish a strong externally funded research program, conduct independent high-quality research, publish in leading scholarly journals, and mentor graduate students.\u00a0Extension responsibilities include interacting with other specialists, county educators, and relevant stakeholder groups (especially urban clientele) around the state, region and nation; and developing a comprehensive extension education program with a variety of outputs.\u00a0The ability to engage a diverse population of faculty, staff, and students at the Departmental, College, and University levels is an important aspect of this academic appointment.\u00a0 REQUIREMENTS: \u00a0An earned Ph.D. in Entomology, Ecology, Epidemiology, Public Health, Microbiology/Parasitology, or related discipline; a record of excellent scholarship commensurate with their career stage as demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications; and potential to be successful in securing funding for research on arthropods of human or animal health significance. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. SALARY:\u00a0\u00a0 Commensurate with qualifications and experience.\u00a0 An excellent benefits package includes health, dental, and retirement contributions. APPLICATION REQUIREMENTS:\u00a0 Candidates should apply online at\u00a0 https://hr.psu.edu/careers . Review of applications will begin on April 10, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Candidates should provide a cover letter, curriculum vitae, the names and contact information for three references, three representative publications, a statement of research experiences/future interests, and a statement of teaching pedagogy/interests. Applicants should provide evidence, either woven through their application materials or as a separate diversity statement, of a commitment to fostering diversity, equity, inclusive excellence, and belonging and of engagement that creates an inclusive environment in their classroom, Department, and the University. START DATE : July 1, 2025 or as negotiated. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver\u2019s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks.\u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. We particularly welcome applicants who can contribute to such an environment through their scholarship of teaching, research, and professional service. We strongly encourage historically underrepresented groups in academia to apply. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Electrical-Engineering-Wooram-Lee-Group_REQ_0000062625-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Electrical Engineering Wooram Lee Group", "description": "Posted: 2024-12-03\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Electrical Engineering at Penn State University is seeking to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in RF & mmWave integrated circuits (ICs) and systems to start in the Spring of 2025. The postdoc will work on topics related to sub-THz circuits, beamformer design, heterogenous integration, and antenna-in-package under the supervision of Prof. Wooram Lee. The postdoctoral scholar is expected to work in a highly collaborative environment where packaging, thermal, and electromagnetics engineers will collaborate to develop the next generation of microelectronics. More information about our research can be found on: High-Speed Integrated Circuits Lab \u2013 Professor Wooram Lee \u00a0 Requirements Applicants must have a PhD in electrical engineering by the start date with a strong focus in analog and RF integrated circuits. The candidates must have expertise in mmWave circuit design using advanced CMOS or SiGe process, electromagnetic simulations using HFSS and EMX, antenna design, and beamformers. This is a term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire, with additional years of funding available if there is mutual interest. To apply, please submit an online application, a CV, and contact information of three references. Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Electrical-Engineering_REQ_0000062613-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Electrical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2024-12-03\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Electrical Engineering at Penn State is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar. The successful candidate will work on Phased Arrays and Power Convertors. The Postdoctoral Scholar will also mentor graduate students working in the area of semiconductor packaging. The successful candidate will be part of the JUMP 2.0 Center, namely the Center for Heterogeneous Integration of Micro Electronics Systems (CHIMES). For additional information about CHIMES, please click here . Requirements and Qualifications: A PhD in Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline is required by the start date. The successful candidate should have clean room experience, along with a background in semiconductor packaging. Additional Information: To apply, please submit an online application, a CV, and contact information of three references. This is a term appointment, funded for one year from date of hire, with an excellent possibility of renewal depending on satisfactory performance. Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Department-of-Physics---Postdoctoral-Scholar---LIGO_REQ_0000062439-1": {"title": "Department of Physics - Postdoctoral Scholar - LIGO", "description": "Posted: 2024-12-02\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Eberly College of Science, Department of Physics LIGO group is seeking to fill a postdoctoral scholar position in Laser Interferometer Gravitational-wave Observatory. This person will work under Chad Hanna, and their responsibilities include leading projects in real-time gravitational wave detection and parameter inference of neutron stars and black holes to support multimessenger astrophysics. They will also develop new methods and contribute to the ever-growing catalog of LIGO discoveries. \u00a0 The ideal candidate is expected to develop infrastructure to support the production of the CBC catalog. The successful candidate is expected to have strong analytical skills and experience with signal processing, Bayesian statistics and machine learning. Exemplary software engineering skills are also required.\u00a0Most importantly we are looking for a clear scientific leader with tremendous capacity to advance the field. This position has ample opportunity for mentoring students and for collaborative work within the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos and the Institute for Computational and Data Science.\u00a0 The candidate must have a PhD in Physics, Astronomy or a closely related field. \u00a0This is a term position funded for one year from date of hire with possibility of re-funding. \u00a0 Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Research-Scholar--Zhou-Lab_REQ_0000061023-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Research Scholar--Zhou Lab", "description": "Posted: 2024-10-09\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Zhou research team in the College of Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a highly motivated and skilled Postdoctoral Scholar to join our lab in the field of Biodevices and Biomaterials . The candidate will work in a highly interdisciplinary environment at the intersection of engineering, materials science, biology, electronics, where we are motivated by a goal to improve human health. The position will involve development/synthesis of biomaterials and fabrication of biodevices . More information about the PI and the lab can be found here: https://www.esm.psu.edu/department/directory-detail-g.aspx?q=tzz5199 Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: 1. Develop novel materials and devices 2. Lead projects related to biodevices/biomaterials 3. Write manuscripts and publish findings in peer-reviewed journals 4. Support in the mentorship of junior scholars Requirements: The applicant must have recently received, or be scheduled to receive, a Ph.D. in an area broadly relevant to our research by the time employment starts, such as Biomedical Engineering, Material Science, Electrical Engineering, Polymer Science, Chemistry, Biology, or related field. Experience with one or more of the following techniques would be preferred: polymer synthesis, device fabrication, animal experiments, wireless circuits. Term This is a term appointment funded for one year from date of hire with possibility of re-funding\u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral_REQ_0000058449-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral", "description": "Posted: 2024-09-05\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: A postdoctoral position is available in Dr. Paul Babitzke\u2019s research lab within the Center for RNA Molecular Biology and the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology at Penn State. The candidate in this position will study transcription and/or post-transcriptional regulatory mechanisms in B. subtilis and E. coli . Experience in gene regulation, in vitro transcription, RNA biochemistry, protein-RNA interaction, protein-protein interaction, and/or bioinformatics analysis of transcriptomics data is required. The successful candidate will explore fundamental mechanisms that control RNA polymerase pausing and termination, regulation of gene expression by transcription attenuation and translational control mechanisms, structural studies of RNA polymerase using cryo-EM, and/or genome-wide approaches to identify novel RNA-based regulatory mechanisms using RNET-seq, Term-seq, and Structure-seq. Applicants must have recently received their Ph.D. in the Life Sciences. Applications must be submitted electronically at https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic \u00a0Search:0000058449 and include a cover letter containing a description of past accomplishments, research interests and goals, as well as a curriculum vita (CV) that includes a list of publications, conference presentations, and contact information for three referees. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This is a \u00a0 term \u00a0 appointment funded for one year from date of hire. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Amphibian-Diseases-and-Microbial-Ecology_REQ_0000057682-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar- Amphibian Diseases and Microbial Ecology", "description": "Posted: 2024-07-15\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Bletz Lab at Penn State is seeking to hire a postdoctoral scholar.\u00a0The position start dates are flexible, with an ideal start date in Fall 2024. Research in the Bletz Lab lies\u00a0at the intersection of disease ecology, microbial ecology, and wildlife conservation. We ask both fundamental and applied ecological questions using field surveys, laboratory and field-based experiments, microbial culturing and functional bioassays, and multi-omics approaches. We use amphibian-chytrid systems (Bd & Bsal) to understand, \u201chow do host defenses, host microbiomes and the environment interact to shape host-pathogen dynamics and disease outcomes?\u201d and then, use this information, to answer, \u201chow can we modulate these relationships to shift disease outcomes and promote survival?\u201d The postdoctoral scholar will contribute by: initiating research projects within our research sphere, wrapping up existing manuscripts, mentoring students, and assisting with lab management activities. The aims of the position will be tailored to the expertise of the successful applicant and complement the lab\u2019s broad interests in amphibian disease, microbiomes, and host immunity. This position has the potential to include (1) contributing to an NSF-funded research aimed at understanding disease dynamics in wildlife trade using amphibians as a model system, (2) leading research to investigate microbial contributions to immune system development and disease protection in amphibians, and (3) leading functional genomics work on host-associated microbes. Research will likely include field and/or lab-based experiments, culture assays and molecular work, multi-omics techniques, and establishing bioinformatic pipelines for data analysis. The ideal candidate will demonstrate the ability to integrate across biological disciplines, be excited to help jumpstart our new lab, and use the appointment to develop and pursue novel, exciting questions. Individuals who have an interest in data analysis, writing and coordinating/managing lab activities are strongly encouraged to apply. Duties : work closely with the PI, collaborators, and lab personnel to lead research in the lab and/or the field. perform molecular techniques including: DNA extractions, PCR, qPCR for pathogen diagnostics, 16S rRNA library prep, and other methods of high-throughput sequencing. prepare, process, and analyze amplicon sequencing and metagenomic data. compile, manage, and analyze datasets with appropriate statistical methods including univariate and multivariate methods. lead preparation and publication of peer-reviewed manuscripts. present research findings at conferences. contribute to lab management activities: coordinate lab equipment use, curate lab databases, coordinate lab ordering. Eligibility :\u00a0 PhD in ecology, biology, microbiology, or other related field. Applicants are required to have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in an appropriate field and be able to provide evidence that all requirements have been met for completion of the Ph.D. prior to the effective date of hire. Preferred Qualities: The information listed below is meant to capture the breadth of skills that would help applicants succeed in this position; however, I do not expect individual applicants to possess all of these skills a background in or interest in microbial ecology, amphibian disease, conservation, and omics approaches collaborative mindset and attitude strong organization and time management skills enjoyment in both independent and collaborative work\u00a0 interest in preparing scientific publications ability to design and execute experimental studies, including pathogen exposure experiments experience with molecular techniques experience analyzing barcoded amplicon sequencing and/or metagenomic data experience with statistical modeling (general linear models, network analysis, etc.) experience with culturing microorganisms (fungi and/or bacteria) experience with R and/or other programming languages familiarity with bioinformatics and modeling approaches for microbiome datasets ability to bridge fields, including microbial ecology, genomics/transcriptomics, statistics, immunology experience or interest in supervising students Location: This position will be located at The Pennsylvania State University in University Park in State College, Pennsylvania. Application: I highly encourage applicants from historically underrepresented groups in science or non-traditional backgrounds to apply for this position. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references to REQ_0000057682 at https://hr.psu.edu/careers . The cover letter should be 1\u20132 pages describing: research interests and background why you are interested in this position career goals availability for starting this position experience and/or enthusiasm for learning about the dimensions outlined in the position description and preferred qualities Informal inquiries are welcome \u2013 contact Dr. Molly Bletz (molly.bletz@psu.edu) Salary/Benefits The position salary will be commensurate with the applicant\u2019s experience and includes benefits. Initial contracts will be 1 year contracts and renewed based on performance for a second year with the potential for continuation for additional years. Application Deadline: accepting applications until the positions are filled. Review of applications will begin immediately. Position Start Date: Fall 2024\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Contact: Dr. Molly Bletz (molly.bletz@psu.edu) CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Experimental-Condensed-Matter-Physics-_REQ_0000050105": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (Experimental Condensed Matter Physics)", "description": "Posted: 2024-07-10\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The \u00a0 Eberly College of Science, Department of Physics \u00a0 at \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University \u00a0 is seeking to fill \u00a0 two Postdoctoral Scholar positions \u00a0 in \u00a0 Experimental Condensed Matter Physics .\u202fThe successful candidates will participate in the research program of \u00a0 Prof. Cui-Zu Chang\u2019s group to investigate the quantum phenomena in molecular beam epitaxy (MBE)-grown films/heterostructures. The project involves molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) growth, angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES), scanning tunneling microscopy and spectroscopy (STM/S), nanoscale device fabrication, mechanical exfoliation, and dilution electrical transport measurements. The ideal candidates should have experience in at least one of these areas.\u00a0 Education and Experience Requirements include a \u00a0 Ph.D. in Physics or related fields. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a \u00a0 cover letter, CV, and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for \u00a0 three reference letters \u00a0 to be submitted to physicsapply@psu.edu , indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. Additional Information These are \u00a0 term appointments , \u00a0 funded for one year from the date of hire, with the possibility of re-funding. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found.\u202f\u202f The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-Mechanical-Engineering_REQ_0000055576-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Radiation Effects on Electronics", "description": "Posted: 2024-06-21\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar to perform research under the direction of Professor Aman Haque (Mechanical Engineering) & Professor Doug Wolfe (Materials Science & Engineering). Job Duties: Perform electrical characterization on semiconductor devices as function of radiation exposure. The specimens are discrete wide bandgap devices (diodes and transistors), as well as larger systems (field programmable gate arrays, memory). Collaborate with national lab(s) to perform experiments that mimic ionizing radiation. Perform modeling and/or experimental analysis (microscopy, spectroscopy) to investigate the fundamentals of radiation effects in electronics. Analyze data. Disseminate findings in journals and conferences. Qualifications and Requirements: Must have Ph.D. by the start of the appointment in Electrical/Computer/Mechanical/Materials/Nuclear Engineering or a related discipline. Must be a US citizen. Must pass the Sandia National Lab Screening and receive approval to the National Lab. Excellent foundation on semiconductor device physics, reliability. Hands on experience with device and system (FPGA, memory) characterization. Excellent written/oral communication skills. Experience in radiation effects (single event, total ionize dose, displacement damage) is very helpful. Additional Information: Interested applicants should submit a cover letter describing their interest in the position, a CV including a publication list, and names & contact information of up to three references. This is a term appointment, funded for one year from the date of hire, with a possibility of renewal. Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Exploring-Quantum-Phenomena_REQ_0000056784-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Experimental Condensed Matter Physics", "description": "Posted: 2024-06-06\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Eberly College of Science, Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill two postdoctoral positions in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics.\u202fThe successful candidate will actively engage in Prof. Cui-Zu Chang\u2019s research program ( https://sites.psu.edu/changresearch/ ), which focuses on exploring quantum phenomena in films and heterostructures grown by molecular beam epitaxy (MBE). The projects in Cui-Zu's group encompass a range of techniques, including MBE growth, angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy (ARPES), scanning tunneling microscopy and spectroscopy (STM/S), nanoscale device fabrication, mechanical exfoliation, and dilution electrical transport measurements. We are seeking an ideal candidate with expertise in at least one of these areas. Requirements include a Ph.D. in Physics or related fields. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV, and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to physicsapply@psu.edu\u202findicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. \u202fThis is a limited term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire, with the possibility of refunding. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found.\u202f\u202f The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time---Accounting---Adjunct-Instructor_REQ_0000056250-1": {"title": "Part Time - Accounting - Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2024-05-20\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Accounting Department within the Smeal College of Business seeks to hire a Part-Time Instructor to teach courses in the online Masters of Taxation program. Applicants should have detailed knowledge of the tax law in subjects such as corporate taxation (including reorganizations and consolidated tax returns); tax research, writing & analysis; partnerships; estate & gift tax; exempt organizations; and/or state & local taxation. A Master's degree or equivalent education and experience is required. \u00a0 The successful candidate will be expected to design and present course material in an asynchronous format that teaches students how to resolve tax law questions in support of economic decision making and tax return position defense. Courses provide an in-depth understanding of the ethical constructs that guide and limit the practice of taxation. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000051878": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2024-04-29\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The laboratory of Associate Professor Joseph Cotruvo, Jr . in the Department of Chemistry at The Pennsylvania State University , seeks to fill a postdoctoral research position focused on rare earth element biochemistry and technology development. Projects will involve development of novel approaches using biological ligands to recover, separate, and detect rare earth elements. Education and Experience The ideal postdoctoral candidate will have extensive experience in one or more of the following fields: f-element chemistry, protein biochemistry, bioinorganic spectroscopy, chemical biology and molecular biology methods, and chemical engineering. The applicant must have recently received, or be scheduled to receive, a Ph.D. in an area broadly relevant to our research program by the time employment starts. The individual should be highly self-motivated and is expected to lead their own individual projects as well as contribute to collaborative research efforts. Additional Information Interested and qualified applicants must submit applications electronically to include a cover letter describing your background, prior training, and research interests, as well as a CV which includes a list of publications. Following a screening of these initial application materials, appropriate candidates will be contacted by email for letters of reference. This is a term appointment funded for one-year from the date of hire with excellent possibility of renewal. All applicants will be encouraged to apply for independent funding. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Our lab is committed to advancing diversity and inclusion efforts at Penn State and we encourage individuals who identify as members of groups historically underrepresented in STEM to apply. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Northeast-Center-of-Excellence-for-Pavement-Technology_REQ_0000054902-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Northeast Center of Excellence for Pavement Technology", "description": "Posted: 2024-04-16\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Penn State University Northeast Center of Excellence for Pavement Technology (NECEPT) is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar to assist with supervision of research projects related to pavement materials. NECEPT is a center under the Larson Transportation Institute , within the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Penn State's College of Engineering .\u00a0NECEPT conducts pavement materials research, as well as the technician certification programs and related training courses for Pennsylvania Department of Transportation, in the areas of asphalt and concrete pavements and aggregates. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Supervising and mentoring research conducted by graduate students. Data analysis. Writing technical reports to research project sponsors. Developing novel and innovative research papers. Developing collaborative research with Penn State faculty. Writing research grant proposals.\u00a0 Requirements and Qualifications: The Postdoctoral Scholar must have PhD in Civil Engineering, with focus on asphalt pavement materials research. In addition, the successful candidate must have demonstrated sufficient knowledge and experience with performance testing, sustainability, and recycling through well-established journal publications. The Postdoctoral Scholar must have a strong knowledge of asphalt mixtures, asphalt binders, and characterization techniques and testing of pavement materials. Excellent verbal and written communication skills and excellent presentation skills are also required. Additional Information: This is a term appointment, funded for one year from date of hire. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusive excellence that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusive excellence as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission.\u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000053661": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2024-03-18\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Social Science Research Institute at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park) seeks two Postdoctoral Scholars to work with Dr. Jonathan Daw (Associate Professor of Sociology and Demography) and collaborators (at Penn State University Park and College of Medicine, Duke University, ENSAE Paris, Florida State University, Georgia Southern University, Johns Hopkins University, and Temple University), on projects related to the demography of kidney disease and transplantation. Position 1: This position is funded by an R01 research grant from the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, will help investigate the role of county-level measures of structural racism in racial/ethnic disparities in end-stage kidney disease incidence, treatment, and patient mortality. Key duties will include managing and analyzing large, complex datasets such as the United States Renal Data System, the National Health Interview Study, US Census and American Community Survey data, and area-level administrative and survey data used to construct an index of structural racism. The successful applicant will collaborate on and lead the design and implementation of quantitative research and co-author the resulting manuscripts for academic publication. Position 2: This position has greater flexibility in research topics so long as they are related to the social determinants of kidney disease and transplantation and are conducted in collaboration with Dr. Daw. Interest in analyzing existing (survey, administrative, text, and/or medical record) data or fielding novel data collection and analysis to address research questions at the intersection of social science and medicine is the primary qualification, along with excellent data analysis and academic writing skills and a relevant doctorate. The successful applicant will be expected to collaborate and lead the development of manuscripts in the relevant topic area. Education and Experience: The following education and work experience are required: A Ph.D. in sociology, demography, public health, medicine, biostatistics by the effective date of employment Expertise in at least one programming language for data analysis (Stata, R, or SAS preferred) Prior academic publication experience The successful candidate for both positions will have strong research skills experience, as well as experience working in multidisciplinary teams, good writing skills, and strong training in quantitative research. Both positions will reserve time to author publications resulting from the applicant\u2019s independent research, and successful applicants will be co-mentored by Dr. Daw and other research team members. They will be encouraged and supported in initiating and developing new independent lines of research and/or funding as well. Overall, it is expected the scholar will spend 70% of their time working on collaborative research and 30% of their time on their own independent research. Application: To apply, please include a CV, names and contact details of three references, and a cover letter explaining which position most interests you, why, and your relevant experience. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The expected start date is June 1, 2024. This is a limited-term appointment funded for one year with a high likelihood of renewal contingent on successful work. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusive excellence that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusive excellence as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. Penn State offers competitive benefits for Postdoctoral Scholars, including medical, dental, vision, and retirement plans. Please visit https://www.research.psu.edu/opa/benefits for more detailed information. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000053155-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2024-03-01\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Statistics at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for one Postdoctoral Scholar working with Dr. Michael Schweinberger. The postdoctoral scholar is expected to work on a set of statistical-theoretical problems concerned with networks, space, time, or causal inference based on discrete and dependent data, either Bayesian or n on-Bayesian. If desired, the postdoctoral scholar may teach one course in the Department of Statistics per year, but teaching is not expected. \u00a0 Education and Experience A Ph.D. in statistical science or data science is required at the time of appointment.\u00a0Successful applicants will be expected to have a strong statistical background, research experience showing independence and innovation, and demonstrated academic writing skills.\u00a0 Additional Information Applicants must complete both the Penn State application and an application through Mathjobs.org at https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/24362 The following materials must be submitted: (1) Curriculum Vitae; (2) Statement of Research, Experience and Interests; (3) Names and Contact Information for three references. The initial appointment is\u00a0funded for one year from the date of hire with a possibility of refunding. \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until\u00a0the positions are filled. Following a screening of initial application materials, candidates will be contacted by email asking for letters of reference to be sent. Informal inquiries about this search may be directed to Dr. Michael Schweinberger (michael.schweinberger@psu.edu). Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with\u00a0University\u00a0polices. \u00a0 The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in\u202fall of\u202fits forms.\u202fWe embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusive excellence that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusive excellence as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission.\u202f\u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000051842-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2024-01-11\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Biomolecular and Biomimetic Materials Laboratory in the Biomedical Engineering Department is seeking to hire two Postdoctoral Scholars to conduct independent research under the direction of Dr. Yong Wang. Working in a collaborative multidisciplinary team, the postdoctoral candidate will conduct extensive research to develop biomimetic extracellular matrices and cell walls using aptamers and hydrogels for protein and cell delivery. Responsibilities of the position include developing novel aptamer-based biomaterials or drug delivery systems for regenerative medicine, cancer immunotherapy, genome editing, and cell regulation. \u00a0 \u00a0 Education and Experience: The position requires a doctoral (Ph.D.) degree in Biomedical Engineering or related discipline by the time of appointment. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in biomaterials, cell biology and genome editing. Appointment duration is for one year, renewal possible depending on the performance of the candidate and availability of funds. Candidates must have excellent interpersonal and communication skills to work with colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Application Requirements: Qualified candidates should apply online and include the following two documents: (1) a one-page cover letter detailing their research expertise, scientific interests and career goals; and (2) a complete curriculum vitae that includes a list of education, publications, work experience, and a list of references. For additional information contact Dr. Yong Wang, yxw30@psu.edu . Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Academic-Instructor_REQ_0000046834-3": {"title": "Part-Time Academic Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2023-09-25\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Department of Educational Psychology, Counseling, and Special Education is seeking to hire part-time instructors to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Educational Psychology, Counselor Education, School Psychology, Rehabilitation Human Services, and Special Education. Required qualifications include evidence of an earned Doctorate or Master's degree, a commitment to excellence in teaching, including use of current technology, evidence of a commitment to working collegially and with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and reviewed as need arises throughout the academic year. The positions are dependent on class enrollments, low enrollments may necessitate canceling the class and position. The Pennsylvania State University is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, inclusion, and sustainability in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity in society and nature, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Experimental-Ultrahigh-Energy-Neutrino---PUEO-Experiment_REQ_0000043392-2": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Experimental Ultrahigh Energy Neutrino - PUEO Experiment", "description": "Posted: 2023-08-31\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Particle Astrophysics group at Penn State is seeking a postdoctoral researcher to work with Professor Stephanie Wissel on experimental searches for the highest energy neutrinos, multi-messenger, and particle astrophysics. Researchers in the Wissel Lab work on several experiments deployed around the world including in Antarctica, Greenland, and high elevation mountains. Experiments such as the Askaryan Radio Array (ARA) and the future radio component of IceCube-Gen2 at the South Pole and the Radio Neutrino Observatory in Greenland (RNO-G) search for EeV-scale neutrinos with antennas deployed in polar ice. Balloon-borne experiments like the Payload for Ultra-high-Energy Observations (PUEO) search for neutrino interactions in the ice and upgoing tau neutrinos from a high altitude. Researchers in the Wissel lab are also exploring novel concepts like the Beamforming Elevated Array for Cosmic Neutrinos which searches for upgoing tau neutrinos from a high-elevation mountain. Previous experience in these experiments or related experiments is advantageous, but not required. \u00a0 The postdoctoral scholar will conduct research on PUEO, which is expected to launch from McMurdo in 2024. For PUEO, the Penn State group is responsible for a deployable array of antenna and calibration systems. The payload will be integrated in Chicago and in Palestine, Tx prior to launch and the postdoc will be expected to contribute to building and testing instrumentation on the PUEO instrument. They will also travel to contribute to integration activities and\u00a0 may conduct field work in Antarctica. As a member of the PUEO team, they will contribute to searches for the highest energy neutrinos in the flight data. Penn State is a vibrant and stimulating environment for particle and multi-messenger astrophysics with ample opportunities for collaboration and career development. The postdoctoral scholar will be embedded within the Particle Astrophysics group and the\u00a0Center for Multi-Messenger Astrophysics (CMA) at the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos (IGC). Penn State is a leading institution in multi-messenger astrophysics. PSU hosts the Astrophysical Multi-Messenger Observatory Network, strong experimental groups in LIGO, HAWC, Auger, HELIX, LZ, Project8, IceCube, GRAND, and Swift, as well as leading theoretical groups in particle astrophysics, gravitation, and cosmology.\u00a0 Education and Experience Applications will be considered from Ph.D. physicists and astronomers with strong backgrounds in particle astrophysics, multi-messenger astrophysics, particle physics, cosmic ray physics,\u00a0 and related fields.\u00a0 Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include a CV and brief statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to physicsapply@psu.edu indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. This is a term appointment funded for one year from date of hire, with possibility of yearly renewal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, \u00a0 equity , and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Department-of-Physics---Wissel-Research-Group_REQ_0000045022-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Department of Physics - Wissel Research Group", "description": "Posted: 2023-08-25\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The Particle Astrophysics group at Penn State is seeking a postdoctoral researcher to work with Prof. Stephanie Wissel on experimental searches for the highest energy neutrinos, multi-messenger, and particle astrophysics. Researchers in the Wissel Lab work on several experiments deployed around the world including in Antarctica, Greenland, and high elevation mountains. Experiments such as the Askaryan Radio Array (ARA) and the future radio component of IceCube-Gen2 at the South Pole and the Radio Neutrino Observatory in Greenland (RNO-G) search for EeV-scale neutrinos with antennas deployed in polar ice. Balloon-borne experiments like the Payload for Ultra-high-Energy Observations (PUEO) search for neutrino interactions in the ice and upgoing tau neutrinos from a high altitude. Researchers in the Wissel lab are also exploring novel concepts like the Beamforming Elevated Array for COsmic Neutrinos which searches for upgoing tau neutrinos from a high-elevation mountain. Previous experience in these experiments or related experiments is advantageous, but not required. \u00a0 The postdoctoral scholar will conduct research on RNO-G, which is under rapid expansion to cover a full 40 km^2. For RNO-G, the Penn State group is responsible for integration, testing, and validation of the data acquisitions systems and contributes to event filtering, both at the hardware and software level.\u00a0As a part of the RNO-G team, they will contribute to searches for the highest energy neutrinos in the the data as well as instrument calibration and monitoring. The successful candidate may contribute to field deployment, installing and commissioning new stations for the experiment. Penn State is a vibrant and stimulating environment for particle and multi-messenger astrophysics with ample opportunities for collaboration and career development. The postdoctoral scholar will be embedded within the Particle Astrophysics group and the\u00a0 Center for Multi-Messenger Astrophysics (CMA) at the Institute for Gravitation and the Cosmos (IGC). Penn State is a leading institution in multi-messenger astrophysics. PSU hosts the Astrophysical Multi-Messenger Observatory Network, strong experimental groups in LIGO, HAWC, Auger, HELIX, LZ, Project8, IceCube, GRAND, and Swift, as well as leading theoretical groups in particle astrophysics, gravitation, and cosmology.\u00a0 Education and Experience Applications will be considered from Ph.D. physicists and astronomers with strong backgrounds in particle astrophysics, multi-messenger astrophysics, particle physics, cosmic ray physics,\u00a0 and related fields.\u00a0 Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include a CV and brief statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to physicsapply@psu.edu indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. This is a term appointment funded for one year from date of hire, with possibility of yearly renewal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Our lab is committed to advancing \u00a0 diversity \u00a0 and inclusion efforts at Penn State and we encourage individuals who identify as members of groups historically underrepresented in STEM to apply. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000041070-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2023-08-08\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The laboratory of Assistant Professor Danielle Reifsnyder Hickey, in the Departments of Chemistry and of Materials Science and Engineering , at The Pennsylvania State University , seeks to fill a postdoctoral research position in aberration-corrected scanning transmission electron microscopy (STEM). Projects will involve the structure and properties of nanomaterials. Education and Experience The postdoctoral candidate should have extensive experience in nanomaterials and aberration-corrected STEM.\u00a0An applicant must possess a Ph.D. (or be scheduled to receive one) in a relevant research area before the start date of employment. Self-motivation is essential because the selected individual will be expected to lead independent research projects. Strong communication skills and a collaborative mindset are also necessary to work in this highly collaborative environment. Additional Information Applicants who are interested and qualified must submit an application electronically as a single pdf that includes: 1. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 A cover letter describing your background and prior training 2. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 A CV which includes a list of publications 3. \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 A brief statement (1-2 pages) of research interests.\u00a0 Following a screening of these initial application materials, appropriate candidates will be contacted by email for letters of reference.\u00a0 This is a limited-term appointment funded for one-year from the date of hire with a possibility of re-funding. All applicants are encouraged to apply for independent funding.\u00a0Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Our lab is committed to advancing diversity and inclusion efforts at Penn State and we encourage individuals who identify as members of groups historically underrepresented in STEM to apply. \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Part-Time-Teaching-Positions--SEDTAPP-_REQ_0000015731-3": {"title": "Part-Time Teaching Positions (SEDTAPP)", "description": "Posted: 2023-08-08\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS: The School of Engineering Design and Innovation (SEDI) within the College of Engineering is seeking individuals for part-time teaching positions. A Master\u2019s Degree, in engineering or a closely related field, or similar education and experience required . Applicants should be interested in teaching as part of programs that are offered by the School. These include: 1. Engineering Design (EDSGN) Program Courses within the program, particularly the cornerstone engineering design course, assists students in learning design processes, methods, and decision-making tools while engaged in team-based design projects. Effective use of communication skills and computer-aided analysis tools are an integral part of the cornerstone engineering design course. 2. Entrepreneurship and Innovation (ENTI) Minor Courses are taught in support of the Technology-Based Entrepreneurship or the Social Entrepreneurship cluster within the Entrepreneurship and Innovation (ENTI) Minor that assist students in obtaining skills attributed to entrepreneurial behavior and innovative thinking. 3. Engineering Leadership Development (ELD) Program Courses in engineering leadership provide students with the understanding of individual, team, and organizational leadership; business acumen, global competencies and multicultural awareness; and innovation and management. 4. Law, Policy, and Engineering (LPE) Program Courses in Law, Policy, and Engineering aim to provide new cross-disciplinary perspectives and tools required to solve complex multidisciplinary problems and address societal changes. Students will be versed in science and technology policy, legal and regulatory policy, complex systems design, and anticipating technology trends. 5. Other courses as part of SEDTAPP\u2019s growing portfolio. Experience teaching online/remotely is a plus. More information of the School\u2019s programs may be found at www.sedi.psu.edu Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion in all of its forms. We embrace individual uniqueness, foster a culture of inclusion that supports both broad and specific diversity initiatives, leverage the educational and institutional benefits of diversity, and engage all individuals to help them thrive. We value inclusion as a core strength and an essential element of our public service mission. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS: Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.\u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Affirmative Action Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines University Park, PA"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Lecturer-of-Art-History_REQ_0000083776-1": {"title": "Adjunct Lecturer of Art History", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Art History invites applications for a part-time academic position for Spring 2027 to teach an undergraduate course. Position requires a Master's degree or PhD in Art History. Applicants should apply by submitting a cover letter and current Curriculum Vita (CV). This is a one semester, non tenure track appointment with the possibility of reappointment. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the opening has been filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Mucosal-Immunology_REQ_0000083238-1": {"title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor of Mucosal Immunology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Assistant/Associate/Professor of Mucosal Immunology The Department of Veterinary and Biomedical Sciences (VBS) in the College of Agricultural Sciences, and the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for an open rank, tenure track faculty position in Mucosal Immunology. This is a 9-month position and has a 75 percent research and 25 percent teaching appointment. Rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants must hold a doctoral degree (PhD and/or MD) in Immunology, microbiology, metabolomics, or a related discipline. Postdoctoral training with a strong record of peer reviewed publications is expected for candidates at the assistant professor level. For appointment at the Associate or Full Professor level, candidates must have established a national/international reputable, extramurally funded research program with a strong track record of high impact publications. We strongly encourage applicants focused on immune cell development and function at the mucosal surface and their metabolism with research programs that incorporate animal models and/or clinical studies. In addition, candidates with interdisciplinary research programs investigating the molecular mechanisms by which mucosal immune cells interact and respond to diverse internal and external cues, including microbiome, pathogens, dietary components, and environmental toxins will also be considered. The candidate may employ computational, statistical, or data driven approaches as part of their research program but are expected to maintain a clear connection to experimental biology and mechanistic insight through wet laboratory, biochemical, molecular approaches, and translation to human and/or animal health. The candidates must demonstrate strong potential for securing extramural funding, excellence in research and teaching, effective communication skills, and the ability to work collegially within an inclusive academic environment. Candidates must have a strong commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring. Teaching responsibilities will include teaching in the undergraduate Immunology and Infectious Disease major and participation in graduate education in Immunology. The successful candidate will be a part of a collaborative research ecosystem created by the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences.\u00a0 The Huck Institutes serve as a hub for life sciences research at Penn State, bringing together scientists from across the University to address fundamental questions and societal challenges. \u00a0The Huck Institutes supports Centers, including the One Health Microbiome Center (OHMC), the Center for Molecular Immunology (CMI), and the Center for Environmental Health Sciences.; graduate programs, including the Interdisciplinary Graduate Degree Programs in Integrative and Biomedical Physiology; and manages shared and core facilities with instrumentation and expertise in genomics, metabolomics, imaging, and other technologies. \u00a0The candidate will have access to gnotobiotic facilities and ABSL-3 capabilities. The department has strong ties with other research units at Penn State including the Penn State Cancer Institute and the Institute of Energy and the Environment. \u00a0 Qualifications Candidates must have a PhD, MD, DVM/VMD, or equivalent degree in a relevant discipline and have an outstanding record of scientific ability as demonstrated by a strong publication record. Applicants should apply at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically: Cover letter that includes research area, qualifications, and contact information Curriculum vitae A statement of research interests (3-pages maximum) A statement of Teaching interests Three confidential letters of recommendation upon request. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact K. Sandeep Prabhu, Professor and Head of the Department of Veterinary & Biomedical Sciences, Penn State University, by email at ksp4@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Accounting-Adjunct-Professor_REQ_0000083699": {"title": "Accounting Adjunct Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Accounting Department within the Smeal College of Business seeks to hire a Part-Time Instructor(s) to teach undergraduate accounting courses in person at University Park. Typical qualifications include advanced degrees (particularly in accounting or tax) and relevant work experience. \u00a0 Applicants must submit an online application that includes a curriculum vitae (CV) and may include additional supporting materials. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching undergraduate courses for a variety of accounting subjects, including preparing and delivering course material, evaluating student work, maintaining appropriate course records, and fulfilling other instructional responsibilities associated with the assigned course(s). \u00a0 Appointments are contingent upon departmental instructional needs and available funding. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000083440-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Paulson Lab at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a motivated\u00a0 Postdoctoral Scholar \u00a0to investigate the cellular and molecular mechanisms regulating\u00a0 stress erythropoiesis and inflammatory anemia . Our research focuses on how inflammatory signaling and the hematopoietic microenvironment regulate erythroid progenitor development and recovery from anemia. Current projects examine interactions between\u00a0 erythroid progenitors, monocytes/macrophages, and inflammatory signaling pathways \u00a0using mouse models of inflammatory anemia and complementary ex vivo approaches. The successful candidate will have opportunities to develop independent projects and gain experience in\u00a0 hematopoiesis, immunology, erythroid biology, multicolor flow cytometry, primary cell culture, molecular assays, and in vivo mouse models . Qualifications PhD in immunology, hematology, molecular/cell biology, biochemistry, or a related field Experience with cell and molecular biology techniques Experience with flow cytometry, primary cell culture, and/or mouse models is preferred Strong interest in hematopoiesis, erythropoiesis, or inflammation Ability to work independently and collaboratively The position is based at\u00a0 Penn State University in University Park, Pennsylvania. Interested candidates must submit an online application at Penn State\u2019s Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically: CV, brief description of research interests, and contact information for references . Inquiries may be directed to rfp5@psu.edu \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Line-Faculty-Position--College-of-Engineering--Department-of-Aerospace-Engineering-and-National-Security-Institute_REQ_0000083587-1": {"title": "Tenure-Line Faculty Position, College of Engineering, Department of Aerospace Engineering and National Security Institute", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The National Security Institute (NSI) and the Department of Aerospace Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University in Uiversity Park, PA, invite applications for a full-time tenure-line faculty position in Autonomous and Resilient Space Operations. The successful candidate\u2019s academic and tenure home will be the Department of Aerospace Engineering, and the faculty member will be expected to contribute actively in NSI\u2019s research pillar on Aeronautics, Hypersonics, and Space. The position supports Penn State\u2019s growing efforts in next-generation space technologies spanning advanced sensing, autonomous and AI-enabled systems, resilient space architectures, and in-space operations in complex and contested environments. We seek candidates whose research advances the future of autonomous and resilient space operations. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, distributed spacecraft systems and coordination; space domain awareness across Earth-orbit and cislunar environments; onboard perception, navigation, guidance, and control for rendezvous and proximity operations; resilient spacecraft autonomy and decision-making; space robotics; and in-space servicing, assembly, and manufacturing (ISAM). Particular interest is in researchers developing integrated approaches that combine robotics, sensing, onboard intelligence, spacecraft systems, and mission design to enable sustained orbital and cislunar operations. The successful candidate is expected to establish an externally funded, internationally recognized research program; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in aerospace engineering; develop new courses where appropriate; advise undergraduate and graduate students; contribute service to the Department, NSI, University, and profession; and contribute to an inclusive community of faculty, staff, and students. The candidate will contribute to Penn State\u2019s broader vision of building interdisciplinary research and workforce-development programs spanning space technologies, autonomous systems, and national security applications. Research that connects foundational science and computational methods with experimental validation and operationally relevant engineering is especially encouraged. Penn State offers a highly collaborative environment with strong institutional capabilities across the Department of Aerospace Engineering, the College of Engineering, NSI, the Applied Research Laboratory (ARL), and other interdisciplinary research institutes and centers. The position is expected to play a foundational role in shaping Penn State\u2019s long-term leadership in space domain awareness, autonomous and resilient space systems, future space infrastructure, and sustained operations beyond Earth orbit. Qualifications Candidates at each rank should have an earned doctorate in aerospace engineering or a closely related field by the start date. The assistant professor must have demonstrated ability as a teacher or research worker; and must have shown definite evidence of growth in scholarly, artistic, or professional achievement. The associate professor should possess the same qualifications as the assistant professor, but must also provide evidence of an established reputation in scholarly, artistic, or professional achievement. The professor should possess the same qualifications as the associate professor, but must also provide evidence of a substantial record of advanced research and/or creative work, and of leadership in their field of specialization. This rank should be reserved for persons of proven stature in teaching and/or research. Application Materials Applications should be submitted on the Penn State site. Applicants should submit electronically: (1) a complete curriculum vitae; (2) a research statement summarizing their prior research contributions and articulating the research program they plan to pursue after joining Penn State, including opportunities for collaboration with Aerospace Engineering, NSI, and other Penn State units; (3) a teaching statement describing their teaching experience and approach and clearly identifying specific courses in the current Penn State Aerospace Engineering undergraduate and graduate curricula that they are prepared to teach, as well as potential new courses they could develop; and (4) the names and contact information of three professional references. For full consideration, applications must be received by November 6, 2026. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Puneet Singla (psingla@psu.edu). About the Department of Aerospace Engineering The Penn State Department of Aerospace Engineering, established in 1961 and the only aerospace engineering department in Pennsylvania, is an international leader in aerospace education, research, and engagement. Its undergraduate and graduate programs prepare students across the core disciplines and integrative systems of aerospace engineering, and the department has growing strengths in astrodynamics, space systems, autonomy, sensing, guidance and control, propulsion, aerodynamics, structures, and vertical lift. The department\u2019s community includes approximately 20 tenure-line faculty, five teaching faculty, and active research and emeritus faculty, together with collaborators across the College of Engineering and ARL. The department moved into the Engineering Collaborative Research and Education (ECoRE) Building in 2024, which provides modern research laboratories, dedicated capstone design space, and innovative classrooms. The department supports B.S., M.Eng., M.S., and Ph.D. programs in aerospace engineering and emphasizes collegiality, rigorous engineering practice, and collaboration across disciplinary boundaries. More information is available at aero.psu.edu. About the National Security Institute Penn State\u2019s National Security Institute advances national security solutions through interdisciplinary research and strategic partnerships with government and industry. NSI is a research-driven institute focused on accelerating the translation of academic breakthroughs into mission-ready solutions while developing the next generation of security-focused researchers and leaders. Its Aeronautics, Hypersonics, and Space pillar brings together expertise in aerospace engineering, propulsion, autonomy, flight systems, sensing, controls, and space systems to address critical national security challenges. NSI complements and collaborates with Penn State\u2019s Applied Research Laboratory and connects researchers across colleges, campuses, government agencies, national laboratories, and industry. More information is available at nsi.psu.edu. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Adjunct-Instructor-of-Supply-Chain-Management_REQ_0000083671-1": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor of Supply Chain Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS The Department of Supply Chain and Information Systems at Penn State University Park invites applications for one part-time adjunct instructor to start in January 2027. The successful candidate will teach one to two sections of SCM 301: Supply Chain Management at Penn State World Campus . The successful candidate will be committed to active and collaborative learning and the instructional use of technology in a student-centered online environment. \u00a0 Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree or equivalent education and experience in the field of supply chain management At least 15 years of experience in the field of supply chain management Teaching experience at the college level \u00a0 To be considered for this opening, applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for at least three professional references. \u00a0 Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as the need arises. This is a one semester, non-tenure track appointment with the possibility of reappointment. \u00a0 Candidates with questions may contact the department assistant, Autumn Knepp, at adh5253@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Department-Head--Health-Policy-and-Administration_REQ_0000083470-1": {"title": "Department Head, Health Policy and Administration", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Job Description The Department of Health Policy and Administration (HPA), located in the College of Health and Human Development (HHD) at The Pennsylvania State University (Penn State), University Park, invites applications for the position of Department Head. About the Department The Department of Health Policy and Administration (HPA) in the Penn State College of Health and Human Development is a nationally recognized academic unit focused on improving health care delivery, health outcomes, public health, and health policy through excellence in teaching, research, and outreach. The department prepares future health care leaders, administrators, researchers, and policymakers through a multidisciplinary curriculum that integrates health services management, health policy, economics, public health, and health services research. HPA offers more than 400 undergraduate and graduate students a comprehensive portfolio of academic programs, including the residential and online Bachelor of Science in Health Policy and Administration, the residential and online Master of Health Administration (M.H.A.) programs, and graduate programs leading to the M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Health Policy and Administration. In Fall 2026, the department added an undergraduate Bachelor of Science in Public Health to the curriculum. Through collaboration with health care organizations, government agencies, and community partners, HPA advances innovative solutions to some of the most pressing challenges facing health systems today, including health care access, quality, cost, population health, and workforce development.\u00a0 The department is home to 13 tenured and tenure-track faculty members and 18 teaching and research faculty members who contribute to a vibrant culture of scholarship, student mentorship, and professional engagement. Faculty expertise spans health services research, health economics, health policy, population health, health care management, organizational leadership, and rural health. Academic leadership within the department includes oversight of undergraduate education, graduate education, online learning initiatives, research activities, and extensive community and professional partnerships. The department is supported by a team of staff members and includes a robust network of adjunct faculty, preceptors, alumni, and health system partners who contribute to its educational and professional mission. The Department Head serves as the chief academic and administrative officer for the department, providing strategic leadership for faculty, staff, students, academic programs, research initiatives, and external engagement activities across both residential and online educational environments.\u00a0 The Department Head oversees an active research portfolio in the department, including NIH, state, and foundation grants. Department faculty also collaborate with the College\u2019s three research centers and with Penn State\u2019s multidisciplinary research institutes, including the Social Science Research Institute (SSRI), the Penn State Cancer Institute, and the Clinical and Translational Science Institute (CTSI). The department provides administrative oversight for the Pennsylvania Office of Rural Health (PORH), whose director reports directly to the Department Head. As Pennsylvania's designated state office of rural health, PORH is recognized nationally for its leadership in advancing rural health through research, education, technical assistance, workforce development, policy initiatives, and community partnerships. Collaborating with health care providers, public agencies, and community organizations throughout the Commonwealth, PORH extends the department's impact well beyond the University and exemplifies Penn State's land-grant mission of service and outreach.\u00a0 The Department Head also provides oversight for Penn State's emerging undergraduate public health initiative, which includes the new undergraduate degree in public health and reflects the University's commitment to addressing evolving population health challenges and workforce needs, and offers substantial opportunity for collaboration with the Department of Public Health Sciences in the College of Medicine and the Demography program in the College of Liberal Arts, including through a dual doctoral degree option. Together, the department's academic programs, research enterprise, online education portfolio, outreach organizations, and public health initiatives create a dynamic and collaborative environment that serves students, communities, health care organizations, and policymakers across Pennsylvania and beyond. The successful candidate will lead a department with a strong tradition of academic excellence, interdisciplinary collaboration, student success, impactful research, and meaningful engagement with the health systems and communities it serves.\u00a0 About the College HPA is one of eight academic units in the College of Health and Human Development (HHD), which focuses on providing interdisciplinary programs sharing a common goal of enriching the lives of others. We continually examine contemporary issues facing people in today\u2019s changing times and develop cutting-edge solutions for addressing them.\u00a0 The College of HHD is home to approximately 4,200 undergraduates and 350 graduate students at the University Park (UP) campus. HHD also serves nearly 1,000 additional students through Penn State\u2019s nationally recognized online World Campus and collaborates on educational programming with several of Penn State\u2019s other physical campus locations throughout the Commonwealth.\u202fWith annual extramural funding in the $70-$80 million range, HHD is one of the most research-active colleges at UP.\u202fThe college is home to three multidisciplinary research centers, including the Child Health Research Center, the Center for Healthy Aging, and the Edna Bennett Pierce Prevention Research Center. These centers support a vibrant research climate within HHD, facilitate cross-department collaboration, and house several interdisciplinary T31/32 training grants. Under the College leadership of Dean Craig Newschaffer, the college has outlined an innovative vision and strategic plan that emphasizes creating an environment to support student success while in college and beyond and growing the impact of the college\u2019s research scholarship. The Head of the Department of Health Policy and Administration, as a member of the college\u2019s leadership team, plays a critical role in the realization of the college\u2019s strategic vision and goals and ensuring that the Department of HPA efforts align with and support these goals.\u00a0 Primary Job Responsibilities\u00a0 Reporting to the Dean of the College, the Head of Health Policy and Administration provides strategic leadership for the department's academic, research, operational, and outreach missions. The Department Head is responsible for visioning and strategic planning; oversight of academic and research programs; management of departmental operations, finances, faculty, and staff affairs; cultivation of external partnerships; and fundraising in support of the department's priorities and aspirations. The Head is expected to further strengthen a cohesive and multidisciplinary department that leverages the strengths of its diverse programs, advances diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging, fosters interdisciplinary collaboration, and supports innovation and creativity across educational, research, and outreach activities. Additionally, the Head is responsible for recruiting, developing, and retaining outstanding faculty and staff, advocating for the department, enhancing its visibility and reputation, and promoting a culture that values well-being and work-life balance. As a key academic leader within the College and University, the Department Head is expected to advance the strategic priorities of both institutions by fostering research productivity, teaching excellence, interdisciplinary scholarship, and external engagement. The Head will encourage and support faculty in securing external funding, expanding collaborative research initiatives, and translating scholarship into meaningful impact for health systems, communities, and policymakers. The successful candidate will have administrative responsibility for all operational, fiscal, and procedural matters within the department, including oversight of fundraising and development activities. The Head will also be encouraged to maintain an active program of scholarship and mentor graduate student research. In addition, the position requires identifying and advancing new opportunities in undergraduate, graduate, and online education. The new Head will cultivate an environment in which innovation, creativity, and collaboration thrive, while fostering a positive and inclusive culture that inspires confidence and trust among students, faculty, and staff through strong interpersonal skills and a compassionate, community-oriented leadership style. Qualifications\u00a0 Candidates must possess an earned doctorate, evidence of an active and focused program of research in health services research, health administration/management, population health or a related field, and previous teaching experience. The successful candidate must also possess the scholarly credentials necessary to merit appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor in the College of Health and Human Development. Candidates should possess the vision, energy, and leadership ability to advance and grow this nationally and internationally recognized department, promoting excellence across the teaching, research, outreach, and service missions of a comprehensive, land-grant, and research-intensive university. The next Department Head must be a collaborative, transparent, and inclusive leader with strong strategic thinking skills and an innovative spirit to advance the department's vision and goals. Successful candidates will demonstrate: Experience with undergraduate and graduate education programs, including significant exposure to degree programs in health policy and administration and public health. Experience and aptitude for building relationships and partnerships with key constituencies both within and beyond the University, including faculty colleagues, Penn State Health, other health systems, organizations engaged in public health practice, community partners, and alumni. Commitment to fostering a positive organizational culture that emphasizes inclusivity, transparency, collaboration, and engagement among faculty, staff, and students. Recognition of the importance of both undergraduate and graduate education and a willingness to support innovation and continuous improvement across educational programs and delivery modalities. An established record of scholarly excellence and success in developing, sustaining, and managing a robust, externally visible research program. Demonstrated administrative and leadership experience in an academic, research, outreach, or similarly complex organizational setting, including responsibility for strategic planning, personnel management, budgeting, program development, and resource stewardship. The ability to articulate and advance a compelling vision for the department's future that leverages its strengths across research, education, outreach, partnerships, and emerging opportunities. Strong interpersonal, communication, and consensus-building skills, with a demonstrated ability to build support among diverse stakeholders and enhance the department's visibility, reputation, and external partnerships. Experience working effectively within a large, complex university environment is desirable; experience with performance-based budgeting or similar resource-allocation models is preferred but not required. Please direct nominations and inquiries to the Search Committee Chair, Dennis Shea, via e-mail at dgs4@psu.edu . To receive full consideration, candidates should submit the following by November 15th, 2026, for priority review: A cover letter (up to 3 pages) detailing the applicant\u2019s interest in the position. Please highlight relevant experiences in leadership positions, a leadership vision, and a description of personal leadership style and values, including how they resonate with Penn State Values. \u00a0Please also describe your vision for teaching and scholarship and your approach to integrating the teaching, research and service priorities of the department. Curriculum vitae. Names and contact information for 5 individuals willing to serve as references (to be contacted only prior to invitations for on-campus interviews). About Penn State Penn State is a public, land-grant, research-intensive university with campuses and facilities throughout Pennsylvania. Founded in 1855, the university has a threefold mission of teaching, research, and public service. Its instructional mission includes undergraduate, graduate, professional, and continuing education offered through resident instruction and online delivery. Annual enrollment at its 24 physical campuses totals more than 100,000 graduate and undergraduate students, making it one of the largest universities in the United States. As an R1 research institution, Penn State\u2019s annual research expenditure exceeds $1 billion. This rich university environment offers unparalleled opportunities for cross-disciplinary partnerships in education, community outreach, and research.\u202fOf particular note is Penn State\u2019s unique approach to university-level research institutes. Penn State\u2019s well-resourced university-designated research institutes ( https://www.psu.edu/research/interdisciplinary-institutes/ ) are not siloed \u201cclosed shops,\u201d but entities that exist principally to strategically disseminate funding that fosters cross-college, transdisciplinary research collaborations and makes needed shared resources widely available.\u202fThis approach has led to Penn State being recognized as standing out for effective promotion of team research collaboration . HHD maintains robust partnerships with nearly all of these institutes. Penn State\u2019s University Park campus is located in the town of State College in Centre County, Pennsylvania. Employment at Penn State at University Park will allow you to live amid the beauty of the central Pennsylvania outdoors while enjoying all the culture, sports, and entertainment that a large university community can bring.\u202fMore information on the area and all of its amenities can be found here: http://www.visitpennstate.org . Our campuses are located on the original homelands of the Erie, Haudenosaunee (Seneca, Cayuga, Onondaga, Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and Wahzhazhe (Osage) Nations. As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and honor the traditional caretakers of these lands and strive to understand and model their responsible stewardship. We also acknowledge the long history of these lands and our place in that history. Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with university policies. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/OPEN-RANK-FACULTY-Position-in-Environmental-Health-Science-at-Penn-State-s-College-of-Health-and-Human-Development_REQ_0000083542-2": {"title": "OPEN RANK FACULTY Position in Environmental Health Science at Penn State's College of Health and Human Development", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University\u2019s College of Health and Human Development invites applications for an open-rank tenure-track position under its ongoing program area in environmental health sciences initiative.\u00a0Applicants should have research interests that align with one or both of the following priority areas: \u00a0 1) Built environment and health outcomes - the study of the influence of human-made surroundings on health and well-being of populations. Our principal interest is in population-level inquiry that involves (or spans) epidemiologic or computational (digital twins, agent-based modelling) approaches to assessing the influence of the chemical and material, biologic, physical, and geospatial exposures related to the built environment on health outcomes. Outcomes of interest should relate to other college research priorities including physical activity, mental health and well-being, substance misuse, cognitive decline, nutritional status, chronic disease etc. Scholars who bring an environmental health policy perspective to these issues are also welcome to apply. Successful candidate\u2019s formal training background could be from a range of disciplines including, but not limited to environmental health science, epidemiology, environmental/health policy, human biology, urban planning, architectural engineering.\u00a0 \u00a0 2)\u00a0Extreme weather and health outcomes - the study of the influence of extreme weather (e.g., drought, extreme heat, flooding, hurricanes) and associated events on health and well-being of populations, such as but not limited to birth and developmental outcomes, nutritional outcomes, epigenetics, aging outcomes, physical activity, stress and inflammation, mental health, cardiometabolic health, etc. Our principal interest is in population-level inquiry that is consistent with the priorities in NIH\u2019s Health and Extreme Weather Strategic Framework . However, researchers focused on mechanisms underlying the above associations (e.g., thermoregulation impacts on physiology) are also welcome to apply. Successful candidate\u2019s formal training background could be from a range of disciplines including, but not limited to environmental health science, epidemiology, human biology, meteorology, or climate science.\u00a0 \u00a0 Successful candidates will be expected to build research programs involving collaboration across multiple disciplines to both capitalize on the broad range of scientific expertise at Penn State University and to promote an understanding of environmental influences on health that considers interactions with social, behavioral, and physiological determinants. Tenure track faculty members at Penn State are also expected to teach, mentor trainees, and engage in service to the university and profession. \u00a0 The primary academic appointment for this position will be in one of the College of Health and Human Development\u2019s eight academic units , including but not limited to the departments of Biobehavioral Health, Kinesiology, Nutrition Sciences, Human Development and Family Science, and Recreation, Park, and Tourism Management.\u00a0HHD is one of the larger academic units at the University, home to approximately 160 full-time faculty and 200 staff members who serve approximately 4,300 undergraduate and 300 graduate students in-residence at its University Park campus, as well as 600 online students at Penn State\u2019s World Campus.\u00a0In addition to its eight academic units, the college houses three research centers, and the college\u2019s investigators lead projects generating ~$80 million in externally supported research expenditures.\u00a0 \u00a0 As appropriate, offered positions may also be supported by one (or more) of the following university-level research institutes: Institute of Energy and the Environment (IEE), the Social Sciences Research Institute (SSRI), or the Cocoziello Institute of Real Estate Innovation as well as academic units in other colleges. Successful candidates co-funded by these institutes would attract extramural funding, publish in top journals, be collaborative and promote and enhance excellence and innovation in interdisciplinary research.\u00a0For IEE, the focus would be on Institute\u2019s Health and the Environment theme (one of IEE\u2019s five key research themes). For SSRI, the candidate would emphasize research in social and behavioral sciences and be involved in broader University-wide activities, including those Penn State\u2019s land grant mission. For Cocoziello, the research would center on how buildings and infrastructure are designed, constructed, and operated, how these structures create healthy, sustainable, and affordable housing solutions, and how they enhance living environments and accessibility for diverse communities. Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. Our campuses are located on the original homelands of the Erie, Haudenosaunee (Seneca, Cayuga, Onondaga, Oneida, Mohawk, and Tuscarora), Lenape (Delaware Nation, Delaware Tribe, Stockbridge-Munsee), Monongahela, Shawnee (Absentee, Eastern, and Oklahoma), Susquehannock, and Wahzhazhe (Osage) Nations. As a land grant institution, we acknowledge and honor the traditional caretakers of these lands and strive to understand and model their responsible stewardship. We also acknowledge the long history of these lands and our place in that history. \u00a0 TO APPLY - Applicants must demonstrate excellence in research, a strong publication record, and interest in collaboration across disciplines. Candidates must hold a PhD in one of the fields listed above. Established researchers should have demonstrated a track record of external grant funding and a commitment to mentoring students or early career researchers with early career researchers demonstrating the potential to achieve the above. An online application should be completed and upload, including: 1) a cover letter (3 pages max), which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications, discusses which department(s) would be suitable as the tenure home, current and future research interests (including highlighting key publications and current/future funding plans), and how they would interact with one or more of the co-funding institutes, teaching philosophy, and a commitment to fostering diversity, equity, and inclusive excellence), 2) curriculum vitae, and 3) contact information for three (3) professional references who will be providing letters if applying at the assistant professor level or four (4) if applying at the associate or full professor level. We will request reference letters, with a short timeframe for response, only for applicants undergoing further consideration. Applications received by November 20 will be given full consideration, but applications will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. Employment will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with university policies. \u00a0 Inquiries about the position may be directed to\u00a0Dr. Asher Rosinger, Associate Professor of Biobehavioral Health and Anthropology, Environmental Health Sciences Program Area Leader, and Search Committee Chair, at axr579@psu.edu or 814-865-5220.\u00a0 \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Post-doctoral-Associate-in-Socioecological-Outcomes-and-Monitoring-of-Restoration-in-Dryland-Ecosystems_REQ_0000078390": {"title": "Post-doctoral Associate in Socioecological Outcomes and Monitoring of Restoration in Dryland Ecosystems", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS Duties Place The primary work location will be the University Park Campus of Penn State University, PA. Approximately 10% of the work will require travel for research collaboration (e.g. potentially to other universities in the US involved in this project including University of Minnesota and Duke University, as well as to meetings in Southern Africa as needed). The position is in-person , with Penn State as duty location; however, some flexibility may be considered. While part of the work can be performed virtually with a flexible work location, Penn State University policy requires employees to live primarily in Pennsylvania. \u00a0 Job Duties We are recruiting a postdoctoral associate who will work on an NSF DISES-funded project titled \u201cSocioecological Outcomes of Restoration: Discovering the interplay among biophysical, socioeconomic, and institutional dimensions of dryland forest-grassland landscapes\u201d. This is a collaborative research project between Penn State (Ida Djenontin and Erica Smithwick), Duke University (Tong Qiu), University of Minnesota (Forrest Fleischman), University of Witswatersrand (Wayne Twine) and LUANAR (Judith Kamoto). The postdoctoral associate will report to Ida Djenontin (main mentor) while benefiting from a co-mentorship arrangement across disciplines to strengthen applications and further learning of integrative methods. The initial term of appointment will be for 1 year , with possibility of renewal for an additional year contingent on performance and funding availability. The postdoctoral associate will focus on analyzing the socio-ecological impacts of ecosystem restoration in mosaic forest-grassland ecosystems and design appropriate monitoring frameworks, in collaboration with scientists located at several institutions in the US, Africa, and beyond whose goals include understanding tradeoffs in social and ecological outcomes.\u00a0 The work will involve analyzing empirical primary social and ecological data on ecosystem restoration processes and outcomes collected in Malawi and South Africa from (i) household and community surveys, (ii) semi-structured qualitative interviews, (iii) ecological surveys from forests and farms, (iv) remote sensing of land cover change, and (v) other secondary data. The specific expertise, skills, and interest of the candidate will further determine this process. Deliverables expected from this position include the generation of both integrative scientific research publications and practical policy insights. The incumbent will also coordinate with other members of the research team and engage in outreach. The postdoctoral associate will receive training in scientific publication, grant-writing and outreach, relevant research techniques and skills, and have opportunities to build connections with broader networks of scholars studying restoration social science in general, and particularly the network of ecosystem restoration scientists collaborating on this project. (75%) Analyzing data on ecosystem restoration and synthesizing secondary data and information to produce research products including scientific publications and policy briefs. (10%) support overall planning and logistics of the team to develop and gain leadership skills. This includes assisting with meeting coordination, meeting minutes, and supporting the development of the annual technical report. (10%) Support engagement efforts with a broader research community funded by this grant, organizing and assisting with science-policy outreach efforts (including peer training), presenting research and & presentations across Africa and the US related to this research. (5%) As scholars in advanced training status, Post-Doctoral Associates devote five percent of their effort to pursue professional and career development opportunities (e.g., seminars, workshops) outside the scope of their assigned research responsibilities. The nature and content of professional and career development opportunities is at the discretion of the Post-Doctoral Associate who can seek advice from the direct mentor and other project team members. Required Qualifications Ph.D. degree with expertise in at least two of the following areas: human-environment geography, landscape ecology, land system science, remote sensing/GIS science, data science, or related field. Demonstrated interdisciplinary background, with experience in the integration of social and ecological theories, methods, and data, with interest in advancing these skills for data integration. Demonstrated ability to engage with both quantitative and qualitative analysis of data (e.g., household surveys, spatial data, interviews, and ecological data), including statistical methods to account for trade-offs and co-benefits. Publication record that demonstrates the ability to publish integrative social-ecological research. Preferred/Desired Qualifications Demonstrated understanding of ecosystem restoration and its policy dynamics linking biodiversity, climate, and human well-being goals. Substantive experience studying landscapes with mixed land uses and ecosystems. Substantive experience with policy related to rural smallholder livelihoods. Demonstrated ability to coordinate complex team-based projects, including working successfully with a varied mix of internal and external partners from diverse communities and cultures using tact, diplomacy, initiative, and sound judgement. Application Instructions Applications must be submitted online. To be considered for this position, please click the Apply button and follow the instructions. You will have the opportunity to complete an online application for the position and attach a cover letter and a CV. Applications must include the following: Academic CV, emphasizing socio-ecological analytical skills Cover letter that describes the applicant\u2019s interest in the position and specifies how the applicant meets the required and preferred qualifications (1-2 pages) Two representative publications Names and contact information for three professional references. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Documents may be attached after application by accessing your \"My Job Applications\" page and uploading documents in the \"My Cover Letters and Attachments\" section.\u00a0Make sure to combine all parts of the application into a single document before uploading\u201d In instances where the Search Committee is unable to ascertain from a candidate\u2019s application materials whether they meet any of the qualifications, they will be evaluated as not meeting such qualifications.\u00a0This position will remain open until it is filled. Application review as soon as they are received. Questions about the position can be directed to Ida Djenontin ( ind5050@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/MINDSET-Postdoctoral-Scholar_REQ_0000083496-1": {"title": "MINDSET Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Informatics and Intelligent Systems Department at the Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a full-time postdoctoral scholar position in Informatics and Applied Cognition, working with Teaching Professor Robert Thomson. This is a limited-term appointment hybrid position with an initial appointment for one year from date of hire with strong possibility of renewal. The position is available immediately. The successful candidate will conduct research on the development and generalization of cognitive models integrating analyses to capture expert behavior and strategies for vulnerability analysis. Responsibilities include developing algorithmic techniques, establishing performance benchmarks, designing experiments, collaborating with faculty and graduate students, and disseminating research through journal publications and conference proceedings. Applicants must possess a doctoral degree in Human Factors, Cognitive Science, Computer Science, or a related discipline by the appointment start date. Candidates should have strong analytical skills, expertise in human study design and analysis, a demonstrated record of research relevant to the position, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. The applicant must demonstrate strong written communication skills and have the ability and willingness to mentor students. The postdoctoral scholar will be mentored toward an academic or research career, with opportunities to publish and present research results, develop grant proposals, and collaborate with partner researchers on the project. The position fully focuses on research with no expectation of teaching. However, should the scholar want to teach, arrangements can be made to build teaching experience. The objective of this position is to enhance the researcher\u2019s skills and record for a placement in a leading university or research laboratory at the end of the post-doctoral position. Penn State is a premier Research I university in the northeastern United States situated in a university town, State College, that is within three to four hours by car from New York, Washington, D.C., Philadelphia, Cleveland, Pittsburgh, Baltimore, etc. Situated in a valley surrounded by mountains, State College has a low cost of living and small university town charm. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please submit an application consisting of a CV, a statement of research interests, and names of three references. Any questions can be emailed to Teaching Professor Robert Thomson ( robert.thomson@psu.edu ). \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Reinhart-Group---Materials-Science-and-Engineering_REQ_0000082292-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Reinhart Group - Materials Science and Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences is searching for a postdoctoral scholar. The position will involve machine learning for autonomous thin-film materials synthesis, including representation learning for scientific data, multimodal data fusion, and real-time predictive modeling. This work will be performed as part of LATTICE (Layered and Thin Film Technologies with Intelligent Cloud Experimentation), a National Science Foundation Programmable Cloud Laboratory at the Pennsylvania State University\u2019s University Park campus. The postdoctoral scholar will develop specialized machine learning models that enable AI systems to interpret scientific data from instruments including atomic force microscopy, reflection high-energy electron diffraction, spectroscopic ellipsometry, X-ray diffraction, and similar characterization methods. These models serve as the perceptual layer for a multi-agent AI framework that will guide autonomous materials synthesis and interact with robotic systems. The models will be trained, calibrated, and validated against the specific data modalities produced by LATTICE instrumentation. The scholar will deploy these models on edge-computing infrastructure for real-time feedback during deposition and integrate them with the Lifetime Sample Tracking data platform. The position requires close collaboration with LATTICE domain scientists in thin-film growth and characterization, AI researchers developing the agentic workflow framework, and future users of the LATTICE framework. Requirements Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field, plus a strong record of research experience in applied machine learning, computer vision, and/or scientific data analysis. Preferred Experience with one or more of the following is strongly preferred: deep learning for image analysis, multimodal or multi-task learning, or deployment of ML models in real-time or edge-computing environments. Domain knowledge of materials science, chemistry, or physics will be an advantage. Extensive programming experience in Python is required, and familiarity with PyTorch or JAX is preferred. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Chemo-Mechanical-Modeling-of-Porous-Materials_REQ_0000083444-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar-Chemo-Mechanical Modeling of Porous Materials", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The College of EMS is seeking to hire one postdoctoral scholar to develop novel computational methods for modeling the coupling between chemical reactions, mechanical deformation, and failure in porous materials. Volume-changing reactions can fracture the solids that host them, and the resulting damage governs performance across a wide range of settings. These include geologic CO2 storage and mineralization, cement and concrete degradation, in-situ hydrogen generation, nuclear waste isolation, geothermal energy extraction, and electrochemical energy storage. The successful candidate will build models that resolve these processes at the pore scale and connect them to engineering-scale behavior. The position is computational. The candidate will lead model formulation, algorithm development, and software implementation, and will work closely with the PI and with graduate students conducting companion laboratory experiments. There will be opportunities to mentor students, co-lead a conference workshop, and release open-source software and benchmark data to the research community. Required: A PhD in engineering, applied mathematics, geosciences, physics, computer science, or a closely related field is required by the date of hire, along with demonstrated experience implementing numerical methods for partial differential equations in research code written by the candidate, rather than solely through commercial finite-element, fluid-dynamics, or multiphysics packages. Desired: Experience in one or more of the following is desired: computational solid and fracture mechanics, particularly phase-field or other diffuse-interface formulations; reactive transport and flow in porous media; poromechanics and continuum thermodynamics; discretization schemes for coupled multiphysics systems (FVM, FEM, XFEM); scientific programming (MATLAB, C++, Python); and high-performance computing. Experience bridging modeling and experiments is valued but not required. Application materials : Applicants should upload: (1) a current CV including a list of publications; (2) a statement of research interest and experience in the context of the qualifications above; and (3) the names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is funded for one year from the date of hire, with renewal for a second year anticipated upon satisfactory performance. The expected start date is Spring or Summer 2027 and is negotiable for the right candidate. About the group: Yashar Mehmani is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Energy and Mineral Engineering (EME) at The Pennsylvania State University, and a co-funded faculty member in the Institutes of Energy and the Environment (IEE). He received a BSc from Sharif University of Technology, Iran, followed by a PhD from the University of Texas at Austin. He was then a Postdoctoral Fellow and later a Research Scientist in the Department of Energy Science & Engineering at Stanford University. His lab focuses on the fundamental physics of fluid flow and mechanical deformation of porous materials, with a special emphasis on computing and scale translation. Further information about the lab is found at: www.mehmaniresearchgroup.com . Informal inquiries are welcome and may be sent to Yashar Mehmani at yzm5192@psu.edu. Please begin the subject line with \"Postdoc 2027 \u2013 \" followed by your surname. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--NERCRD_REQ_0000083448-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar, NERCRD", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Northeast Regional Center for Rural Development (NERCRD) is located in the Department of Agricultural Economics, Sociology and Education within Penn State\u2019s College of Agricultural Sciences. Our mission is to work on a range of issues with land grant universities and other partners in the Northeast as well as nationally in support of regional economic growth and rural development goals. The Center has a strong track record of publishing peer-reviewed articles. \u00a0 The NERCRD seeks applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar position. This is a limited-term position funded for one year with good possibility of renewal subject to funding availability. The post-doc will be responsible for conducting economic and statistical analyses on a wide range of rural development topics, as determined by the Center\u2019s emerging needs and priorities. There is a strong expectation that this research will contribute both to the science base as well as to informing U.S. rural economic development policy. Examples of topics to be studied range from policy impact assessments; the interdependence of rural and urban areas, as well as agricultural and non-agricultural industries; to the determinants and impacts of local economic well-being and health, including that of farmers and small businesses. The opportunity exists to work within Penn State\u2019s Federal Statistical Research Data Center. \u00a0 The Center offers a competitive salary along with benefits, and the opportunity to collaborate with scholars in the region, nationally, and internationally. Opportunities also exist for attending conferences to support networking activities. This position is required to work at University Park, PA. \u00a0 Primary Responsibilities Design and execute rigorous empirical research on regional and rural economic development topics. Manage and analyze large, complex datasets, including administrative records, federal statistical microdata, and novel big data sources. Prepare high-quality manuscripts for submission to peer-reviewed journals. Present research findings at national and international conferences and contribute to NERCRD research reports and policy briefs. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams, graduate students, and regional Extension partners. \u00a0 Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in Agricultural Economics, Applied Economics, Economics, Regional Science, Public Policy, or related fields by the effective date of hire. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. Extensive training in applied econometrics, causal inference, and spatial statistics. Demonstrated proficiency in modern statistical and computational tools (e.g., R, Stata, Python). Experience working with large-scale administrative, survey, or big data sets. Strong written and oral communication skills, evidenced by peer-reviewed publications, working papers, or a strong dissertation portfolio. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative, multidisciplinary research team. \u00a0 Preferred Qualifications Experience with, or interest in, Large Language Models (LLMs) and automated computational pipelines. Experience or familiarity with Federal Statistical Research Data Center (FSRDC) data environments or restricted-use datasets. \u00a0 Screening of applications will begin November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date for the position is December 1, 2026, with flexibility. \u00a0 To ensure full consideration, applicants must submit the following materials electronically through the Penn State Careers Portal: \u00a0 Cover Letter: A 1\u20132 page letter describing your research background, qualifications, career goals, and specific interest/fit with the NERCRD. Curriculum Vitae (CV): Detailed CV including educational background, publication record, working papers, software proficiency, and research experience. Research Statement: A brief statement (1\u20132 pages) outlining your current research interests, methodological expertise, and future research plans. Writing Sample(s): One or two representative research papers (e.g., job market paper, dissertation chapter, or published journal article). Professional References: Contact information (full name, title, institution, email address, and phone number) for three professional references. (Letters of recommendation will be requested for shortlisted candidates). \u00a0 System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. Applicants are welcome to direct inquiries regarding the position, qualifications, research opportunities, or the application process to Dr. Zheng Tian at ztian@psu.edu . \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-Computational-Optoelectronics-and-Applied-Mathematics_REQ_0000083327-1": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Computational Optoelectronics and Applied Mathematics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Lakhtakia research team in the College of Engineering (Department of Engineering Science and Mechanics) at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking a highly motivated and skilled Postdoctoral Scholar to join a collaborative research program in computational optoelectronics, mathematical modeling, and numerical simulation of integrated energy microgenerators (IEMGs) containing \u00a0compound semiconductors. The postdoctoral scholar will work under the direction of Prof. Akhlesh Lakhtakia in cooperation with Prof. Anna Mazzucato (Mathematics at Penn State), Prof. Peter B. Monk (Mathematics at University of Delaware), and a postdoctoral scholar at University of Delaware. The position will involve developing and analyzing two- and three-dimensional optical and electronic models; implementing high-order numerical methods for semiconductor drift-diffusion and Maxwell systems; modeling grain boundaries, defects, and interfaces; and optimizing material, geometric, and illumination-dependent designs for efficient IEMGs. Education Requirement: Qualified individuals will hold a Ph.D.\u00a0 by the time of appointment in applied mathematics, computational mathematics, electrical engineering, engineering science, physics, computational science, or a closely related field.\u00a0 \u00a0 Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Implement and improve high-order finite-element and discontinuous-Galerkin software in Python and related scientific-computing environments, including robust solvers, error assessment, and computational validation. Investigate the effects of grain boundaries, defects, interfaces, material properties, and illumination conditions on carrier transport, recombination, and device performance. Perform mathematical analysis and computational optimization of bandgap profiles, layer thicknesses, device geometry, and tandem IEMG configurations using gradient-based and derivative-free methods. Collaborate with the faculty investigators and graduate students; prepare manuscripts, conference presentations, technical documentation, and research software for dissemination. Develop, analyze, verify, and document two- and three-dimensional numerical models for coupled optical and electronic processes in IEMGs, including semiconductor drift-diffusion and Maxwell equations. \u00a0 It is preferred that the successful candidate will possess: Demonstrated experience in numerical analysis, scientific computing, partial differential equations, finite-element or discontinuous-Galerkin methods, and computational modeling. Experience with semiconductor models, drift-diffusion systems, Maxwell equations, optoelectronics, photovoltaics, optimization, or machine learning is highly desirable. Proficiency in Python and familiarity with version control and high-performance computing are preferred. Excellent written and oral communication skills; ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team; demonstrated initiative, organization, problem-solving ability, and commitment to reproducible research. Record of publications, historical work, etc.: A record of peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, dissertations, software, or other scholarly work demonstrating research capability in a relevant area. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenure-Track-Faculty-in-the-Department-of-Biomedical-Engineering_REQ_0000083387-1": {"title": "Tenure-Track Faculty in the Department of Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Biomedical Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University in University Park, PA, is pleased to invite applications for a tenure-line position Assistant or Associate Professor in the area\u00a0of cell therapy, immune cell therapy, tissue engineering with an emphasis on immune modulation\u00a0approaches to advance fundamental understanding or translational biomedical technologies. The candidate will have the opportunity to interact with an interdisciplinary team of engineering faculty and others in related fields at Penn State. The position will include an expectation for active participation in focused mentoring and professional development opportunities. The Department of Biomedical Engineering is home to 34 faculty, ~100 graduate students, and ~400 undergraduate students. The faculty conduct in excess of $17M per year of research across a broad spectrum of traditional and emerging areas in biomedical engineering. Penn State actively encourages and provides resources for interdisciplinary research collaboration through university-level institutes in the areas of healthcare, materials and data science/computation.\u00a0The Department offers separate B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degree programs in biomedical engineering.\u00a0 The Department has a dedicated faculty and staff forming a strong sense of community and fostering a welcoming culture.\u00a0Further information on the Department can be found at:\u00a0 https://www.bme.psu.edu . The BME department has strong relationships with the School of Medicine, Materials Research Institute ( https://www.mri.psu.edu ), Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences ( https://www.huck.psu.edu ), and the Institute for Computational and Data Sciences ( https://www.icds.psu.edu ). This position will potentially be supported in part by the Penn State Huck Institutes of Life Sciences ( https://www.huck.psu.edu/ ) and is expected to collaborate closely with the Centers and expertise in the Huck. Qualification for the position at each rank is a doctorate in engineering or a related field that must be completed by the start date in the position. The successful applicant at each rank will have demonstrated outstanding scholarly research, and will have a strong track record in engineering education, as well as a commitment to inclusivity. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses at both undergraduate and graduate levels, to develop an internationally recognized, externally-funded research program, and to contribute to the operation and promotion of the department, college, university, and profession through service. Nominations and applications will be considered until the position is filled. Screening of applicants will begin on November 15th. Applicants should submit the following documents: Cover letter; curriculum\u00a0vitae; separate statements on research and teaching that are aligned with the Penn State Values of integrity, respect, responsibility, discovery, excellence, and community\u00a0 https://universityethics.psu.edu/penn-state-values ; copies of 3 key publications; and names and addresses of five professional references.\u00a0 Application materials should be uploaded as two PDFs: one PDF containing all application materials in the order listed, without journal publications, and a second PDF only containing the two selected journal publications. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials as requested above to meet the 5-document limit. The Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences (Huck) serves as Penn State\u2019s primary engine for interdisciplinary research across the life sciences, creating connections among researchers, technologies, and shared infrastructure that span traditional disciplinary and college boundaries. Through its research centers, graduate programs, core facilities, and cross-college faculty networks, Huck provides an especially strong environment for research at the interface of engineering, cell biology, immunology, genomics, and translational biomedicine. For this position, particularly relevant Huck strengths and opportunities for collaboration include: Center for Cellular Dynamics , which brings together expertise in cell biology, molecular mechanisms, advanced imaging, and quantitative approaches to understanding cellular organization and function\u2014providing a strong foundation for research in cell engineering, tissue engineering, and cell-based therapies. Center for Molecular Immunology and Infectious Disease , which connects faculty working across immunology, host\u2013pathogen interactions, inflammation, and immune responses and offers opportunities for collaboration in immune-cell engineering and immune-modulation approaches. Huck core facilities and advanced technology platforms , including capabilities in genomics, proteomics, metabolomics, microscopy and imaging, flow cytometry, and other molecular and cellular characterization approaches that can support mechanistic and translational research in engineered cells and tissues. Cross-institute opportunities at the life sciences\u2013engineering interface , particularly through Huck's connections with the Materials Research Institute, Institute for Computational and Data Sciences, and Penn State College of Medicine. These relationships create opportunities to integrate biomaterials, advanced manufacturing, computation and AI, molecular and cellular biology, and clinical perspectives in the development of next-generation biomedical technologies. The successful candidate would also strengthen Penn State's interdisciplinary graduate education through participation in relevant Huck Intercollege Graduate Degree Programs, including\u00a0 Molecular, Cellular and Integrative Biosciences, Bioinformatics and Genomics, Neuroscience, and related programs , providing opportunities to mentor students and build collaborations across colleges and disciplines. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor_REQ_0000083374-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Edna Bennett Pierce Prevention Research Center (PRC), housed in the College of Health and Human Development at The Pennsylvania State University, invites applications for an Assistant Research Professor position. The PRC seeks a collaborative and highly motivated prevention scientist who is committed to advancing research that improves the health and well-being of children, families, and communities. We are particularly interested in candidates who are enthusiastic about developing and contributing to externally funded research , writing competitive grant proposals, and building a program of scholarship within the broad field of prevention science. Areas of research interest may include, but are not limited to: Development, implementation, and evaluation of preventive interventions Etiology and the study of risk and protective factors Community-based and population-level prevention Implementation and dissemination science Research-to-practice and research-to-policy translation Prevention of behavioral health problems, substance use, violence, and other adverse outcomes Promotion of child, family, and community health and well-being Economic evaluation and assessment of the societal impact of prevention programs and policies Innovative methods, data science, and emerging technologies applied to prevention research We welcome candidates whose work complements and expands the Center's existing research portfolio and who are interested in collaborating across disciplines and projects. The successful candidate will be expected to participate actively in the intellectual life of the PRC and to contribute to the development of new research initiatives and funding opportunities. Successful applicants should demonstrate: A clear and developing program of prevention research A strong and growing record of peer-reviewed scholarship Demonstrated interest and experience in developing grant proposals The capacity to contribute to and, over time, lead externally funded research projects A commitment to collaborative, interdisciplinary research Strong methodological and scientific skills relevant to prevention research An earned doctorate in a relevant behavioral, social, public health, or related discipline is required. Relevant fields may include human development and family studies, psychology, public health, social work, sociology, education, prevention science, health policy, or related disciplines. Candidates should demonstrate the potential for outstanding scholarly accomplishments and the development of a sustainable externally funded research program. The Edna Bennett Pierce Prevention Research Center is an interdisciplinary research center dedicated to advancing the science of prevention and improving the health and well-being of children, families, and communities. The Center brings together faculty, research scientists, staff, students, policymakers, practitioners, and community partners to develop, evaluate, implement, and disseminate effective approaches to prevention. The PRC supports a diverse portfolio of research spanning intervention development and evaluation, implementation science, community-based prevention, behavioral health, research translation, policy, economic evaluation, and innovative applications of data and technology. Center investigators lead and collaborate on projects supported by federal agencies, including the National Institutes of Health and National Science Foundation, as well as foundations, state and federal government agencies, and other partners. A central goal of this position is to expand the PRC's research portfolio. Accordingly, we are especially interested in candidates who are motivated to write grants, pursue new funding opportunities, develop collaborative research teams, and establish an externally funded program of prevention research . Review of applications and nominations will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Research-Professor_REQ_0000083162-1": {"title": "Associate Research Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Informatics and Intelligent Systems in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for an Associate Research Professor position in Artificial Intelligence and Applications, beginning in January or July 2027 at the University Park campus in State College, Pennsylvania. This is a non-tenure-line, one-year appointment with a mix of research and teaching responsibilities. Fully remote appointments are not permitted for this position. \u00a0 The faculty member hired for this position will be expected to teach two courses in the College of IST each semester and conduct research contributing to an NSF-funded project developing machine-learning methods for segmenting stomata and surrounding cells in 3D plant microscopy images. \u00a0 Candidates must have a Ph.D. in computer science, electrical engineering, or a related field, with expertise in machine learning, computer vision, and image analysis. Experience with 3D biomedical imaging and scientific machine learning is preferred. Candidates should provide evidence of excellence in teaching at the university level. A commitment to teaching learners at all levels and from all backgrounds is essential.\u00a0 \u00a0 Applicants should include the following materials with their application: (i) a cover letter detailing their qualifications for the position; (ii) a curriculum vitae; and (iii) contact information for at least three professional references. In the cover letter, please indicate the specific courses from the Artificial Intelligence Methods and Applications and Data Science programs that you would be excited to teach. Please upload one document that combines the above materials into a single PDF. \u00a0 Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Neutrino-Astrophysics--Phenomenology--and-Data-Analysis_REQ_0000077646-2": {"title": "Assistant Research Professor - Neutrino Astrophysics, Phenomenology, and Data Analysis", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Physics at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking to fill an Assistant Research Professor position in the area high-energy neutrino astrophysics. The successful candidate will lead phenomenological and data-driven research efforts in the astrophysics of ultra-high\u00a0energy neutrinos, cosmic rays, and dark matter.\u00a0 Additionally, this position involves close and constant collaboration\u00a0with existing experimental efforts at Penn State including IceCube,\u00a0as well as other radio detection techniques and\u00a0next generation neutrino experiments.\u00a0 Requirements include a Ph.D. in Physics, materials or device physics. Applications must be submitted electronically and include a cover letter, CV and statement of research interests. Applicants should arrange for three reference letters to be submitted to szw5718@psu.edu indicating the appropriate job number in the subject line. \u00a0 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a suitable candidate is found. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Clinical-or-Teaching-Professor-of-Finance_REQ_0000083280-2": {"title": "Clinical or Teaching Professor of Finance", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Finance at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park) seeks to fill up to three non-tenure-track faculty members (rank and salary commensurate with experience) beginning in August 2027 to support curriculum needs across corporate finance, investments, financial institutions, FinTech, Wealth Management, and related areas. Teaching responsibilities will be predominantly at the undergraduate level, with potential opportunities to teach graduate courses. We seek candidates dedicated to delivering excellent teaching across rigorous courses that incorporate experiential elements, such as case discussions and projects presented to industry partners or alumni. Candidates should also be open to service commitments required of teaching and clinical faculty, such as mentoring students, serving on department or school committees, or managing corporate partner relationships. We seek individuals who will work effectively with our talented faculty and students and contribute to our vibrant and collegial environment. JOB QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must hold a minimum of a master\u2019s degree in finance or a closely related field at the time of hiring. A PhD in finance is preferred. We encourage applications from experienced teaching professors, recent Ph.D. graduates, Ph.D. candidates who will complete their degree before August 2027, and individuals with terminal degrees and substantial industry experience. \u00a0 APPLICATION PROCEDURE: \u00a0 To apply for this position, candidates are to apply directly on the PSU site and submit the following documents as PDF files: vita teaching evaluations (when applicable) names of at least three (3) references \u00a0 A minimum of three reference letters should be emailed directly from reference providers to this address : finance.recruiting@psu.edu \u00a0 Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. More information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at www.smeal.psu.edu/finance .\u00a0 For questions about the application process and portal, please contact Kayla Horting ( keo131@psu.edu ), 814-863-0486. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Associate-Research-Professor-in-the-Department-of-Mechanical-Engineering_REQ_0000083144-1": {"title": "Associate Research Professor in the Department of Mechanical Engineering", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click \u201cApply\u201d and complete the application process for external applicants . \u00a0 Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location.\u00a0For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see\u00a0 Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term\u00a0length\u00a0discussed will\u00a0be\u00a0based\u00a0on\u00a0university\u00a0need,\u00a0performance,\u00a0and/or\u00a0availability\u00a0of\u00a0funding. \u00a0 POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Penn State is seeking a highly motivated Associate Research Professor . Job Description: Conduct externally funded research projects involving high-temperature, high-pressure, transient two-phase flow and heat transfer with liquid-vapor phase change taking place in different two-phase flow regimes leading to the occurrence of dryout at the CHF point Investigate pre-dryout and post dryout heat transfer Explore the impact of droplet dynamics on the resulting heat transfer Design new test facility needed to quantify specific features Train graduate students in relevant research areas and teach classes in thermal sciences Qualifications Required: Must hold an active security clearance PhD in Mechanical, Nuclear, or Chemical Engineering (or equivalent) by the appointment start date Experience performing high temperature rod bundle experiments under a variety of reflood conditions Clear understanding of fundamental two-phase heat transfer under DFFB and IAFB conditions Familiar with measurement of liquid droplets under high pressure high temperature conditions Ten or more years of experience in experimental studies Interested candidates should upload the following application materials: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information. \u00a0 BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children. \u00a0 For more detailed information, please visit our\u00a0 Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.) \u00a0 CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here . \u00a0 EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473. \u00a0 Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university\u2019s teaching, research, and service mission. \u00a0 Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"}}, "rows": {"https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenured-Tenure-line-Positions-in-Interdisciplinary-Research--and--Quantum--ICDS-Co-hire-_REQ_0000083511-1": {"school_id": 1219, "posting_url": "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Tenured-Tenure-line-Positions-in-Interdisciplinary-Research--and--Quantum--ICDS-Co-hire-_REQ_0000083511-1", "job_title_in_post": "Tenured/Tenure line Positions in Interdisciplinary Research \"and\" Quantum (ICDS Co-hire)", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Institute for Computational and Data Sciences", "area_key_words": "mathematics of quantum computing; numerical analysis", "deadline_of_application": "January 3, 2027", "posted_date": "2026-10-19", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Faculty-Position-in-Biomechanics-and-Biorobotics_REQ_0000083086-1": {"school_id": 1219, "posting_url": "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/PSU_Academic/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Faculty-Position-in-Biomechanics-and-Biorobotics_REQ_0000083086-1", "job_title_in_post": "Faculty Position in Biomechanics and Biorobotics", "position_type": "Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Center for Movement Science and Technology", "area_key_words": "Biomechanics and Biorobotics; cardiovascular physiology; environmental physiology", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-10-19", "position_s